const PASSAGES = [{"id":"27ST_E_03_01","difficulty":"보통","title":"인간의 미기후 조절","sentences":["Even outdoors, although climate (including temperature) is usually regarded as beyond the control of man, localized temperature control is sometimes effective on a microclimate scale.","Vancouver, Canada, is a few miles north of the 49th parallel, about 60 miles farther north than Minot, North Dakota, with its legendary harsh winter temperatures.","When I had a garden there in the late 1940s, a neighbor used to say that I \"cheated God\" to bring in my lettuce and tomatoes earlier than anyone else.","The bed in which the vegetables grew was banked toward the south at approximately 50 degrees, and the area between the plants was covered with flat stones, gathered from the nearby beach, to maximize soil heating from the weak late winter-early spring sun."],"abstract":"Human beings can manipulate localized environmental conditions to overcome climate limitations, as demonstrated by deliberate gardening techniques that maximize heat absorption.","topic_options":["human manipulation of local climate conditions for agricultural benefit","the geographic factors that determine regional temperature patterns","the unpredictability of outdoor temperature control methods","natural wind systems and their influence on coastal weather","the history of gardening techniques in cold northern regions"],"topic_answer":1,"blank_sentence_index":0,"blank_target":"localized temperature control is sometimes effective on a microclimate scale","blank_options":["localized temperature control is sometimes effective on a microclimate scale","regional climate is determined entirely by latitude","human beings have no ability to alter natural conditions","outdoor temperatures are too unpredictable to control","large-scale patterns override all small-scale interventions"],"blank_answer":1,"order_given_index":0,"order_blocks":[],"order_options":["(B)-(A)-(C)","(A)-(B)-(C)","(B)-(C)-(A)","(C)-(B)-(A)","(A)-(C)-(B)"],"order_answer":2,"insert_sentence":null,"insert_answer":null,"summary_template":"Although climate is generally considered beyond human ________(A)________, people can deliberately alter ________(B)________ conditions to their advantage.","summary_A_options":["prediction","awareness","human","intervention","beings"],"summary_A_answer":4,"summary_B_options":["effective","seasonal","geological","localized","stable"],"summary_B_answer":4,"implication_sentence_index":2,"implication_keyword":"cheated God","implication_options":["achieved results that seemed to defy the natural limits of the environment","acted dishonestly toward a religious figure to gain personal advantage","violated the rules of farming accepted by the local community","relied on supernatural forces to improve agricultural outcomes","ignored scientific principles in favor of personal belief"],"implication_answer":1,"irrelevant_sentence_index":3},{"id":"27ST_E_03_02","difficulty":"높음","title":"진정한 충성심의 원천","sentences":["Energy can always be injected into an organization to motivate people to do things.","Bonuses, promotions, other carrots, and even a few sticks can get people to work harder, for sure, but the gains are, like all manipulations, short-term.","Over time, such tactics cost more money and increase stress for employee and employer alike, and eventually will become the main reason people show up for work every day.","That's not loyalty.","That's the employee version of repeat business.","Loyalty among employees is when they turn down more money or benefits to continue working at the same company.","Loyalty to a company trumps pay and benefits.","It's the cause that we come to work for.","We don't want to come to work to build a wall; we want to come to work to build a cathedral."],"abstract":"Genuine employee loyalty cannot be manufactured through external incentives but emerges from a deeper sense of shared purpose and meaning in one's work.","topic_options":["the insufficiency of material rewards in cultivating true organizational commitment","the effectiveness of financial incentives in improving short-term productivity","the relationship between workplace stress and employee turnover rates","strategies for designing competitive compensation packages in organizations","the importance of clear job descriptions in maintaining employee motivation"],"topic_answer":1,"blank_sentence_index":1,"blank_target":"short-term","blank_options":["short-term","long-lasting","beneficial","predictable","motivating"],"blank_answer":1,"order_given_index":0,"order_blocks":[{"label":"B","sentence_indices":[1,2,3]},{"label":"C","sentence_indices":[4,5,6]},{"label":"D","sentence_indices":[7,8]}],"order_options":["(A)-(B)-(C)","(B)-(C)-(A)","(C)-(A)-(B)","(B)-(A)-(C)","(A)-(C)-(B)"],"order_answer":1,"insert_sentence":"It's the cause that we come to work for.","insert_answer":7,"summary_template":"External ________(A)________ can boost short-term effort but fail to generate the genuine ________(B)________ that keeps employees committed to an organization.","summary_A_options":["pressures","evaluations","incentives","genuine","employee"],"summary_A_answer":3,"summary_B_options":["compliance","productivity","dedication","effective","stable"],"summary_B_answer":3,"implication_sentence_index":8,"implication_keyword":"build a cathedral","implication_options":["contribute to a meaningful and lasting purpose beyond routine tasks","engage in large-scale construction projects that require collective effort","follow a religious calling that gives spiritual meaning to daily work","pursue ambitious goals that require years of technical training","focus on visible achievements that can be recognized by others"],"implication_answer":1,"irrelevant_sentence_index":7},{"id":"27ST_E_03_03","difficulty":"높음","title":"DNA와 생물학적 역사","sentences":["In the early 1960s the great American writer James Baldwin wrote: \"People are trapped in history, and history is trapped in them.\"","But the statement is equally true if the word 'people' is replaced with 'all of life on Earth, present and past,' for each strand of DNA, in each of our cells, is an ancient record of biological history, written in simple code and passed down from generation to generation.","One could say that DNA is nothing but history, one with a physical manifestation that was slowly blended and accumulated over countless eons by the most pitiless of all phenomena — natural selection.","DNA is a history that is inside us — and yet one that is our master as well, the blueprint for our bodies, and dictator of what we will pass on to our children, gifts that can be blessings — or deadly time bombs.","We are indeed trapped in this particular vehicle of history as much as it is trapped in us."],"abstract":"DNA functions simultaneously as a record of biological history inherited across generations and as a deterministic force that governs what living organisms are and what they transmit to their descendants.","topic_options":["the dual nature of DNA as both a record and a controller of biological inheritance","the influence of racial history on the formation of human genetic identity","the process by which natural selection gradually shapes genetic diversity","the role of literary metaphor in explaining complex scientific phenomena","the ethical implications of passing genetic information to future generations"],"topic_answer":1,"blank_sentence_index":2,"blank_target":"the most pitiless of all phenomena — natural selection","blank_options":["the most pitiless of all phenomena — natural selection","the most creative force in biological history","a random series of environmental accidents","the most ancient process in science","a cooperative mechanism between organisms"],"blank_answer":1,"order_given_index":0,"order_blocks":[{"label":"B","sentence_indices":[1]},{"label":"C","sentence_indices":[2]},{"label":"D","sentence_indices":[3,4]}],"order_options":["(A)-(B)-(C)","(B)-(C)-(A)","(C)-(A)-(B)","(B)-(A)-(C)","(A)-(C)-(B)"],"order_answer":1,"insert_sentence":null,"insert_answer":null,"summary_template":"DNA serves as a permanent ________(A)________ of evolutionary history that simultaneously acts as a ________(B)________ over the biological traits transmitted to future generations.","summary_A_options":["archive","barrier","symbol","functions","simultaneously"],"summary_A_answer":1,"summary_B_options":["governing force","variation","variation","effective","stable"],"summary_B_answer":1,"implication_sentence_index":3,"implication_keyword":"deadly time bombs","implication_options":["inherited genetic traits that may cause serious harm to future generations","explosive substances concealed within biological structures of the human body","sudden environmental changes that trigger irreversible genetic mutations","historical events that erupt unpredictably in the lives of descendants","diseases that spread rapidly through populations without warning"],"implication_answer":1,"irrelevant_sentence_index":1},{"id":"27ST_E_03_04","difficulty":"높음","title":"사고의 두려움","sentences":["People may not think critically for a variety of reasons, such as laziness and inability, but fear is a big one.","Why is that?","People don't want to think not just because it's hard, but also because they're afraid it will make them question their long-held beliefs.","But probe even deeper.","Once we start thinking deeply, long-held assumptions are challenged.","Thought makes us worry that we'll lose our balance and have to look at the world in a different way.","We worry about thinking because we care about what we and other people think.","Even the most far-fetched ideas have an effect on the world.","Non-Euclidean geometry and symbolic logic are about as abstract as thinking can get, but you can't understand Einsteinian gravity without the first and run computers without the second.","Thinking is important to us, to others, and to the world we live in.","This is one reason why we are so afraid of it: it shakes us to the core."],"abstract":"The deeper reason people avoid critical thinking is not difficulty alone but a profound fear that genuine thought will destabilize their existing beliefs and force them to see the world differently.","topic_options":["fear of belief disruption as a primary barrier to deep critical thinking","the relationship between abstract academic disciplines and practical technology","methods teachers can use to encourage students to explore controversial topics","the cognitive difficulty of engaging with complex philosophical questions","the social consequences of expressing unconventional ideas in public"],"topic_answer":1,"blank_sentence_index":2,"blank_target":"question their long-held beliefs","blank_options":["question their long-held beliefs","gain recognition from their peers","take on unnecessary responsibilities","solve complex mathematical problems","change their daily habits"],"blank_answer":1,"order_given_index":0,"order_blocks":[{"label":"B","sentence_indices":[1,2]},{"label":"C","sentence_indices":[3,4,5,6]},{"label":"D","sentence_indices":[7,8,9,10]}],"order_options":["(C)-(A)-(B)","(B)-(A)-(C)","(A)-(C)-(B)","(B)-(C)-(A)","(A)-(B)-(C)"],"order_answer":5,"insert_sentence":"But probe even deeper.","insert_answer":3,"summary_template":"People resist deep thinking primarily because it threatens to ________(A)________ their established worldview, even though genuine thought is ________(B)________ to both individuals and society.","summary_A_options":["validate","simplify","deeper","reason","undermine"],"summary_A_answer":5,"summary_B_options":["optional","dangerous","effective","stable","indispensable"],"summary_B_answer":5,"implication_sentence_index":10,"implication_keyword":"shakes us to the core","implication_options":["profoundly disrupts the fundamental assumptions we rely on to understand reality","causes physical discomfort that makes sustained intellectual effort impossible","creates social conflict by exposing the weaknesses of widely accepted ideas","produces emotional instability that prevents rational decision-making","gradually erodes the moral values that guide personal and social behavior"],"implication_answer":1,"irrelevant_sentence_index":3},{"id":"27ST_E_04_01","difficulty":"보통","title":"지식이 만든 식량","sentences":["There's a saying that 'you can't eat information.'","That may be so, but the food we eat today is the fruit of thousands of years of increasingly high-quality information — the knowledge of how to farm — what seeds, what tools and how to use them, what times of year, what irrigation, what sequence of one crop after another on the same land.","What we eat is solar energy, filtered, concentrated, and distilled through the lens of human knowledge.","What's allowed us to flourish is our increasingly sophisticated knowledge of how to capture an ever-growing but still tiny fraction of that energy in a form that can fuel our bodies.","Every step in the advancement of our knowledge has brought with it an increase in the amount of energy we can tap into."],"abstract":"The abundance of food available to modern humans is not the result of more solar energy but of the cumulative growth of agricultural knowledge that has enabled increasingly efficient conversion of that energy.","topic_options":["the role of accumulated human knowledge in transforming solar energy into food","the constant nature of solar energy received by the Earth throughout history","the origins of modern agricultural tools and their impact on crop yield","the relationship between population growth and demand for food production","the environmental costs of converting natural energy into human consumption"],"topic_answer":1,"blank_sentence_index":2,"blank_target":"filtered, concentrated, and distilled through the lens of human knowledge","blank_options":["filtered, concentrated, and distilled through the lens of human knowledge","absorbed and stored naturally through the biological processes of plant growth","converted directly into nutrition through photosynthesis and soil chemistry","measured and distributed according to seasonal and geographic variation","transformed randomly through unpredictable environmental changes"],"blank_answer":1,"order_given_index":0,"order_blocks":[{"label":"B","sentence_indices":[1]},{"label":"C","sentence_indices":[2]},{"label":"D","sentence_indices":[3,4]}],"order_options":["(A)-(C)-(B)","(B)-(A)-(C)","(C)-(B)-(A)","(A)-(B)-(C)","(B)-(C)-(A)"],"order_answer":4,"insert_sentence":null,"insert_answer":null,"summary_template":"Human ________(A)________ has been the key driver behind our ability to convert a fixed supply of solar energy into increasingly greater amounts of ________(B)________.","summary_A_options":["population","geography","energy","knowledge","abundance"],"summary_A_answer":4,"summary_B_options":["sunlight","farmland","effective","nourishment","stable"],"summary_B_answer":4,"implication_sentence_index":2,"implication_keyword":"filtered, concentrated, and distilled through the lens of human knowledge","implication_options":["made accessible and useful to humanity through the application of accumulated understanding","physically purified and processed using advanced agricultural machinery and technology","examined and classified according to scientific principles developed in laboratories","collected and stored systematically through the organized efforts of farming communities","broken down into its basic components through chemical reactions in the digestive system"],"implication_answer":1,"irrelevant_sentence_index":3},{"id":"27ST_E_04_02","difficulty":"높음","title":"시민 저널리즘의 부상","sentences":["Increased community engagement by professional journalists, on their own, will not solve the problem of making the news more relevant to everyone because traditional news organizations already have abandoned many communities, leaving behind news deserts.","In those places, citizens must take up the responsibility for discovering information, holding the powerful accountable, and telling the news for themselves and their neighbors.","The democratization of information — through the disruptions caused by computers and the internet — allows citizens to retake control of local news in ways that never have existed before, and it calls them to take greater care in the gathering and dissemination of what they discover or think they know.","The same technology that has shifted the balance of power toward the people gives them the tools to act as broadcasters and publishers of information essential to their immediate community — and, more critically, to serve as gatekeepers to information for other people around them."],"abstract":"The withdrawal of professional journalism from underserved communities has created a necessity for citizen-led information gathering, enabled and demanded by digital technology that redistributes the power to report and control the flow of news.","topic_options":["the transfer of journalistic responsibility to citizens driven by digital democratization","the decline of traditional media organizations due to increasing financial pressures","the need for professional journalists to increase their presence in local communities","the risks of unverified information spreading through citizen-run media platforms","the historical development of press freedom and its impact on democratic societies"],"topic_answer":1,"blank_sentence_index":0,"blank_target":"leaving behind news deserts","blank_options":["leaving behind news deserts","producing more profitable content strategies","increasing reader engagement and loyalty","strengthening their editorial independence","expanding into digital platforms"],"blank_answer":1,"order_given_index":0,"order_blocks":[{"label":"B","sentence_indices":[1]},{"label":"C","sentence_indices":[2]},{"label":"D","sentence_indices":[3]}],"order_options":["(B)-(C)-(A)","(B)-(A)-(C)","(A)-(B)-(C)","(C)-(A)-(B)","(A)-(C)-(B)"],"order_answer":3,"insert_sentence":null,"insert_answer":null,"summary_template":"As professional journalism ________(A)________ many communities, digital technology has empowered citizens to assume the role of information ________(B)________ for their local areas.","summary_A_options":["reforms","dominates","withdrawal","professional","abandons"],"summary_A_answer":5,"summary_B_options":["critics","consumers","effective","stable","providers"],"summary_B_answer":5,"implication_sentence_index":3,"implication_keyword":"gatekeepers to information","implication_options":["individuals who control what information others in their community can access and trust","security personnel responsible for preventing unauthorized access to sensitive data","editors employed by news organizations to verify facts before publication","government officials who regulate the content broadcast by media outlets","technology experts who design algorithms to filter online content"],"implication_answer":1,"irrelevant_sentence_index":2},{"id":"27ST_E_04_03","difficulty":"높음","title":"과학적 사고와 증거","sentences":["It is a myth that all ideas are equally valid, even those with little or no objective proof.","The existence of science is the commitment to objective truth.","After all, science is true: fire is hot, the wheel is efficient, birds and planes can fly, we've landed on a comet and traveled to the Moon, antibiotics treat illness, and immunizations keep us from getting sick.","These accomplishments are made possible by objective truths.","However, an intuition must be followed with testing that confirms or disproves its veracity.","If a theory is disproved, one should consider it as a reason to reject or alter the hypothesis, not a justification to just keep firmly holding to the hypothesis because you are instinctively wedded to it.","Critical thinking is an absolute must, and we must respect evidence.","It's the only reason for anyone to trust anything about reality.","Without testing and evidence, intuition is useful, but it is never the ultimate word."],"abstract":"While intuition may initiate scientific inquiry, genuine scientific progress depends on rigorous evidence-based testing and the willingness to revise or abandon hypotheses that fail to withstand scrutiny.","topic_options":["the indispensable role of evidence and critical scrutiny in validating scientific claims","the process by which plausible theories gradually gain acceptance in the scientific community","the superiority of empirical science over philosophical reasoning in understanding reality","the historical achievements made possible by the application of scientific knowledge","the dangers of relying on personal intuition when forming judgments about complex issues"],"topic_answer":1,"blank_sentence_index":5,"blank_target":"reject or alter the hypothesis","blank_options":["reject or alter the hypothesis","confirm and strengthen the original theory","seek additional funding for research","publish results in academic journals","defend the hypothesis against criticism"],"blank_answer":1,"order_given_index":0,"order_blocks":[{"label":"B","sentence_indices":[1,2,3]},{"label":"C","sentence_indices":[4,5]},{"label":"D","sentence_indices":[6,7,8]}],"order_options":["(C)-(A)-(B)","(A)-(B)-(C)","(A)-(C)-(B)","(B)-(A)-(C)","(B)-(C)-(A)"],"order_answer":2,"insert_sentence":"However, an intuition must be followed with testing that confirms or disproves its veracity.","insert_answer":4,"summary_template":"Scientific advancement requires not only the generation of ________(A)________ ideas but also the rigorous ________(B)________ of those ideas through objective testing and evidence.","summary_A_options":["revolutionary","popular","plausible","scientific","while"],"summary_A_answer":3,"summary_B_options":["promotion","rejection","validation","effective","stable"],"summary_B_answer":3,"implication_sentence_index":5,"implication_keyword":"instinctively wedded to it","implication_options":["emotionally committed to a belief regardless of contradicting evidence","legally obligated to defend a hypothesis in a formal academic setting","naturally inclined to explore ideas that align with established scientific norms","professionally required to maintain consistency in one's published research","subconsciously drawn toward theories that reflect personal moral values"],"implication_answer":1,"irrelevant_sentence_index":4},{"id":"27ST_E_04_04","difficulty":"보통","title":"불안의 긍정적 전환","sentences":["If you suffer from social angst, awkwardness, or dread, know that this is a perfectly normal response.","No matter what it looks like, a lot of people are dealing with internal anxiety in social situations.","But it is actually possible to build your social muscle and use it to boost your connections — and your anxiety is giving you clues to what icebreakers and lifelines other people might be grateful for you to extend.","Truly listen to what your anxiety is signaling to you about where you feel uncertain or insecure, and practice empathy by offering a hand to others who might be in the same boat.","Remember that flipping anxiety into compassion is something inherent in you — it is, in fact, what your anxiety was designed to do for you.","You can use your anxiety to be more outward-facing.","The outcome? The spread of compassion for your fellow human beings, other species, and the planet!"],"abstract":"Social anxiety, rather than being merely a personal burden, can be consciously redirected into empathy and compassion that strengthens connections with others.","topic_options":["the potential to transform social anxiety into empathy and outward compassion","the medical treatments available for individuals suffering from chronic social anxiety","the negative effects of unaddressed anxiety on personal and professional relationships","the neurological mechanisms that trigger feelings of fear in social environments","the role of community support systems in reducing anxiety among young people"],"topic_answer":1,"blank_sentence_index":2,"blank_target":"icebreakers and lifelines","blank_options":["icebreakers and lifelines","obstacles and burdens","strategies and techniques","warnings and signals","questions and challenges"],"blank_answer":1,"order_given_index":0,"order_blocks":[{"label":"B","sentence_indices":[1,2]},{"label":"C","sentence_indices":[3,4]},{"label":"D","sentence_indices":[5,6]}],"order_options":["(C)-(B)-(A)","(A)-(B)-(C)","(B)-(A)-(C)","(A)-(C)-(B)","(B)-(C)-(A)"],"order_answer":2,"insert_sentence":"You can use your anxiety to be more outward-facing.","insert_answer":5,"summary_template":"Social anxiety can be ________(A)________ into a positive force by channeling it toward ________(B)________ with and for others.","summary_A_options":["suppressed","diagnosed","social","reframed","anxiety"],"summary_A_answer":4,"summary_B_options":["competition","isolation","effective","empathy","stable"],"summary_B_answer":4,"implication_sentence_index":2,"implication_keyword":"social muscle","implication_options":["the capacity for confident and empathetic interaction that can be developed through practice","the physical strength required to maintain composure in stressful social encounters","the natural charm and charisma that some individuals possess from birth","the ability to suppress emotional responses in order to appear socially competent","the mental resilience built through years of professional training in communication"],"implication_answer":1,"irrelevant_sentence_index":4},{"id":"27ST_E_05_01","difficulty":"보통","title":"위기의 분할 관리","sentences":["Many crises today, such as the Great Recession, are simply too big and too overwhelming for you to completely comprehend, much less control.","Crises of this ilk are precisely the kind that can easily engulf you with destructive reactions that interfere with your ability to overcome them.","Focusing on these oversized crises will exacerbate the natural psychological, emotional, and physical reactions you are going to experience.","With these sorts of crises, your best chance is to identify those aspects that are within your control.","For example, think back to the Great Recession.","Although you probably didn't have the ability to influence economic policy, you were able to revisit the distribution of your investments and choose to create a more diverse portfolio."],"abstract":"When facing an overwhelming crisis, the most effective approach is to focus on controllable elements and break the larger problem into smaller, actionable components.","topic_options":["the strategy of focusing on controllable aspects to manage overwhelming crises","the psychological damage caused by large-scale economic crises on individuals","the importance of diversifying financial investments during periods of instability","the role of government policy in preventing and resolving national economic crises","the physical and emotional toll that prolonged exposure to crisis situations inflicts"],"topic_answer":1,"blank_sentence_index":0,"blank_target":"too big and too overwhelming for you to completely comprehend, much less control","blank_options":["too big and too overwhelming for you to completely comprehend, much less control","too distant and abstract for ordinary citizens to feel affected by","too slow-moving for most people to recognize until too late","too complex for any single government to address effectively","too deeply rooted in inequality for short-term solutions"],"blank_answer":1,"order_given_index":0,"order_blocks":[{"label":"B","sentence_indices":[1,2]},{"label":"C","sentence_indices":[3]},{"label":"D","sentence_indices":[4,5]}],"order_options":["(B)-(A)-(C)","(A)-(B)-(C)","(A)-(C)-(B)","(C)-(A)-(B)","(B)-(C)-(A)"],"order_answer":2,"insert_sentence":"For example, think back to the Great Recession.","insert_answer":4,"summary_template":"Rather than being overwhelmed by a crisis beyond one's ________(A)________, individuals should identify manageable aspects and channel their energy toward ________(B)________ solutions.","summary_A_options":["experience","awareness","control","facing","overwhelming"],"summary_A_answer":3,"summary_B_options":["comprehensive","theoretical","actionable","effective","stable"],"summary_B_answer":3,"implication_sentence_index":1,"implication_keyword":"engulf you with destructive reactions","implication_options":["overwhelm you with responses that undermine your capacity to cope effectively","physically surround you with the visible consequences of economic collapse","expose you to the destructive behavior of others who have lost control","force you to confront the full scale of damage caused by the crisis","trap you in a cycle of negative thinking that is difficult to escape"],"implication_answer":1,"irrelevant_sentence_index":5},{"id":"27ST_E_05_02","difficulty":"보통","title":"건강정보와 신뢰성","sentences":["Consumer surveys indicate that the majority of Americans (91%) believe they have some control over their health, and 72% believe that food and nutrition play the greatest role.","However, 75% of consumers rely on media outlets including the Internet as their major sources of health and nutrition information, and only half use medical sources.","A Google search for 'nutrition listservs' yielded over 100,000 sites, but it is likely that many of these writings are not reviewed by nutrition experts.","Internet sites marketing herbs, drugs, and health devices are not monitored by government regulatory agencies and often contain misleading information.","Reputable food companies provide helpful facts about the nutrient content of their products, but commercial sites devoted to sales often post misleading health claims."],"abstract":"Despite widespread public interest in managing personal health through nutrition, most people obtain health information from unreliable online sources rather than evidence-based institutions.","topic_options":["the gap between public reliance on unreliable online health information and the availability of credible sources","the increasing awareness among Americans of the connection between diet and personal health","the failure of government agencies to monitor misleading health claims on commercial websites","the role of reputable food companies in providing accurate nutritional information to consumers","the growing volume of health-related content available through internet search engines"],"topic_answer":1,"blank_sentence_index":1,"blank_target":"only half use medical sources","blank_options":["only half use medical sources","most prefer to rely on personal experience","few trust commercially sponsored websites","the majority ignore government recommendations","nearly all consult licensed dietitians regularly"],"blank_answer":1,"order_given_index":0,"order_blocks":[{"label":"B","sentence_indices":[1]},{"label":"C","sentence_indices":[2,3]},{"label":"D","sentence_indices":[4]}],"order_options":["(A)-(B)-(C)","(B)-(C)-(A)","(C)-(A)-(B)","(A)-(C)-(B)","(B)-(A)-(C)"],"order_answer":1,"insert_sentence":null,"insert_answer":null,"summary_template":"Although most Americans believe they can ________(A)________ their own health, the majority depend on ________(B)________ online sources rather than professionally verified information.","summary_A_options":["manage","predict","improve","health","despite"],"summary_A_answer":1,"summary_B_options":["unverified","outdated","effective","commercial","stable"],"summary_B_answer":1,"implication_sentence_index":3,"implication_keyword":"not monitored by government regulatory agencies","implication_options":["left without official oversight and therefore potentially unreliable","carefully reviewed by medical experts before being published online","required to meet strict standards set by health authorities","consistently accurate due to their commercial reputation","regularly updated to reflect the latest scientific research"],"implication_answer":1,"irrelevant_sentence_index":4},{"id":"27ST_E_05_03","difficulty":"보통","title":"서번트 리더십의 실천","sentences":["My business partner Charles and I embraced the servant leader's way of doing things.","In other words, nothing was beneath us.","We led by example and did the work.","When any new salesman came into the store, he would look around, notice Charles polishing some corner of the floor and me covered in flour, and assume the decision-maker was not present.","He'd then hand off whatever he was selling to me and say, 'Can you give this to the owner?'","It's more about modeling what's important.","If cleanliness and details are important, be sure you aren't above doing the work and pitching in.","Come into your workspace and ask how you can help.","If it's clear your team is in the weeds, jump in without asking."],"abstract":"Effective leadership involves demonstrating the values of an organization through direct personal participation in all levels of work, rather than maintaining a distance from hands-on tasks.","topic_options":["the importance of leaders personally modeling the values they expect their team to uphold","the risks of leaders spending excessive time on operational tasks instead of strategic planning","the impact of a humble workplace appearance on how outsiders perceive a business","the role of cleanliness and attention to detail in maintaining a professional work environment","the challenges of balancing hands-on involvement with the need for organizational growth"],"topic_answer":1,"blank_sentence_index":0,"blank_target":"embraced the servant leader's way of doing things","blank_options":["embraced the servant leader's way of doing things","prioritized profit over the well-being of employees","focused exclusively on expanding market share","delegated all routine tasks to lower-level staff","emphasized formal authority and hierarchy"],"blank_answer":1,"order_given_index":0,"order_blocks":[{"label":"B","sentence_indices":[1,2,3]},{"label":"C","sentence_indices":[4,5]},{"label":"D","sentence_indices":[6,7,8]}],"order_options":["(A)-(C)-(B)","(B)-(A)-(C)","(C)-(A)-(B)","(B)-(C)-(A)","(A)-(B)-(C)"],"order_answer":5,"insert_sentence":"It's more about modeling what's important.","insert_answer":5,"summary_template":"True leadership means ________(A)________ the values of the organization through direct action, so that team members see their leader as someone who genuinely ________(B)________ in shared work.","summary_A_options":["documenting","promoting","embodying","effective","leadership"],"summary_A_answer":3,"summary_B_options":["believes","invests","participates","stable","flexible"],"summary_B_answer":3,"implication_sentence_index":8,"implication_keyword":"in the weeds","implication_options":["overwhelmed by tasks and struggling to keep up with the demands of the situation","working outdoors in an unkempt environment that requires physical maintenance","confused by unclear instructions and unable to proceed without guidance","engaged in tasks that fall outside their defined professional responsibilities","distracted by minor details that prevent them from seeing the bigger picture"],"implication_answer":1,"irrelevant_sentence_index":5},{"id":"27ST_E_05_04","difficulty":"높음","title":"호흡과 각성 조절","sentences":["Training and competition naturally speed the breath, which activates the sympathetic nervous system.","In performance, this is acceptable because an athlete wants to produce adrenaline and compete and train in an aroused state.","However, it is equally important for an athlete to learn how to mentally and physically downshift from the acute sympathetic activity experienced in sport, and outside of performance focus their attention on slow breathing to reduce the sympathetic activity and resolve the fight-or-flight state.","In a performance realm, this means athletes can use breathing pace to manage their state of arousal.","During training and competition, the breathing rate increases with the introduction of adrenaline, and athletes must be able to control this to be able to adapt and recover.","One way is to practice slower breathing protocols outside of training and competition."],"abstract":"While rapid breathing during athletic performance serves a necessary physiological function, athletes must also develop the capacity to deliberately slow their breathing outside competition in order to regulate arousal and promote recovery.","topic_options":["the need for athletes to actively regulate their breathing to manage arousal both during and after performance","the physiological mechanisms through which adrenaline affects athletic performance and endurance","the role of brain activation patterns in determining an athlete's response to competitive pressure","the benefits of slow breathing techniques in treating anxiety disorders in non-athletic populations","the relationship between sympathetic nervous system activity and long-term cardiovascular health"],"topic_answer":1,"blank_sentence_index":2,"blank_target":"downshift from the acute sympathetic activity experienced in sport","blank_options":["downshift from the acute sympathetic activity experienced in sport","maintain peak performance levels throughout competition","suppress all emotional responses during high-pressure situations","increase oxygen consumption to enhance endurance","override the body's natural fatigue signals during training"],"blank_answer":1,"order_given_index":0,"order_blocks":[{"label":"B","sentence_indices":[1,2]},{"label":"C","sentence_indices":[3]},{"label":"D","sentence_indices":[4,5]}],"order_options":["(B)-(C)-(A)","(C)-(A)-(B)","(A)-(C)-(B)","(A)-(B)-(C)","(B)-(A)-(C)"],"order_answer":4,"insert_sentence":"In a performance realm, this means athletes can use breathing pace to manage their state of arousal.","insert_answer":3,"summary_template":"Athletes need to not only embrace elevated ________(A)________ during performance but also practice deliberate ________(B)________ techniques to restore balance and support recovery.","summary_A_options":["focus","arousal","endurance","breathing","while"],"summary_A_answer":2,"summary_B_options":["visualization","technique","effective","rapid","relaxation"],"summary_B_answer":2,"implication_sentence_index":2,"implication_keyword":"fight-or-flight state","implication_options":["a heightened physiological condition of stress that the body must be guided out of through deliberate calming","a competitive mindset in which athletes choose between aggression and retreat during a game","a psychological response that enables athletes to make split-second decisions under pressure","a state of physical exhaustion that follows intense training and requires extended rest","a survival instinct that improves reaction time during high-stakes athletic competitions"],"implication_answer":1,"irrelevant_sentence_index":3},{"id":"27ST_E_06_01","difficulty":"높음","title":"거주와 민주적 참정권","sentences":["In the United States, the practice of permitting aliens to vote could be seen as compatible with the idea of an exclusionary citizenship, but that is a hard balance to maintain.","If the vote, of all rights, is in the hands of noncitizens, why should they not count as citizens, and the entire distinction between resident alien and citizen be abandoned?","But no theory of 'active' democracy can countenance this distinction: the laws concerning our common life must be made by all those who are taking part in it, and residence is the only convincing test of whether someone is taking part — as is understood almost universally when it comes to questions of which citizens should have a voice in local government."],"abstract":"A genuinely democratic system cannot coherently deny voting rights to long-term residents, because participation in shared civic life, not formal citizenship status, is the most defensible basis for political inclusion.","topic_options":["the incompatibility of residence-based exclusion with the foundational logic of active democratic participation","the historical reasons behind the elimination of alien voting rights in the United States after 1920","the legal distinctions between resident aliens and naturalized citizens in American constitutional law","the practical difficulties of maintaining a clear boundary between citizenship and permanent residency","the global trend toward expanding suffrage to non-citizen residents in modern democratic nations"],"topic_answer":1,"blank_sentence_index":2,"blank_target":"residence is the only convincing test of whether someone is taking part","blank_options":["residence is the only convincing test of whether someone is taking part","citizenship is the only reliable indicator of national loyalty","voting rights must be restricted to those born in the territory","legal status determines the extent of civic participation","cultural assimilation should precede granting democratic rights"],"blank_answer":1,"order_given_index":0,"order_blocks":[],"order_options":["(B)-(A)-(C)","(B)-(C)-(A)","(A)-(B)-(C)","(C)-(A)-(B)","(A)-(C)-(B)"],"order_answer":3,"insert_sentence":null,"insert_answer":null,"summary_template":"The logic of active democracy demands that the right to vote be extended to all who ________(A)________ in shared civic life, making ________(B)________ a more defensible basis for suffrage than formal legal status.","summary_A_options":["participate","reside","contribute","genuinely","democratic"],"summary_A_answer":1,"summary_B_options":["residence","engagement","integration","effective","stable"],"summary_B_answer":1,"implication_sentence_index":2,"implication_keyword":"countenance this distinction","implication_options":["accept or justify the separation between those who live under the law and those who make it","recognize the physical differences between citizens and non-citizens in a legal document","formally acknowledge the historical origins of the boundary between aliens and nationals","permit government institutions to enforce different rules for different categories of residents","tolerate the visible inequality created by unequal access to public services and benefits"],"implication_answer":1,"irrelevant_sentence_index":1},{"id":"27ST_E_06_02","difficulty":"보통","title":"맥락이 만드는 의미","sentences":["When people are asked what any painting hanging on a gallery wall means, no matter how strange it might appear, as is the case with most abstract-expressionist paintings, they tend to find meaning in it because it is located in a gallery.","Consider a soda can found thrown away on a city street.","But if we saw the very same object on a pedestal, displayed in an art gallery, signed by some artist, and given a title such as 'Waste,' then we would interpret its meaning in a vastly different way.","We would, in fact, be inclined to interpret it as an artistic form, descrying a throw-away or materialistic society.","Clearly, the can's location on a sidewalk versus its display on a pedestal in an art gallery will influence how we will interpret it."],"abstract":"The meaning we assign to an object is not inherent in the object itself but is fundamentally shaped by the context in which it is encountered.","topic_options":["the determining role of contextual setting in shaping how people interpret the meaning of objects","the criteria used by art critics to distinguish genuine artistic works from ordinary consumer goods","the psychological tendency of gallery visitors to find meaning in all displayed works regardless of quality","the influence of artist reputation and title on the commercial value of contemporary art","the evolution of abstract expressionism as a movement challenging traditional definitions of art"],"topic_answer":1,"blank_sentence_index":2,"blank_target":"interpret its meaning in a vastly different way","blank_options":["interpret its meaning in a vastly different way","question the artist's intentions and motivations","recognize it immediately as a worthless item","evaluate it based solely on its material composition","dismiss it as an inappropriate use of gallery space"],"blank_answer":1,"order_given_index":0,"order_blocks":[{"label":"B","sentence_indices":[1]},{"label":"C","sentence_indices":[2]},{"label":"D","sentence_indices":[3,4]}],"order_options":["(B)-(C)-(A)","(B)-(A)-(C)","(A)-(B)-(C)","(C)-(A)-(B)","(A)-(C)-(B)"],"order_answer":3,"insert_sentence":null,"insert_answer":null,"summary_template":"The ________(A)________ in which an object is placed fundamentally determines how observers ________(B)________ its significance, regardless of the object's inherent qualities.","summary_A_options":["context","title","origin","object","meaning"],"summary_A_answer":1,"summary_B_options":["interpret","question","overlook","effective","stable"],"summary_B_answer":1,"implication_sentence_index":3,"implication_keyword":"descrying a throw-away or materialistic society","implication_options":["critically exposing the values of a culture that prioritizes consumption over lasting meaning","physically disposing of objects that have no further use in a consumer-driven economy","identifying and cataloging items discarded by members of an affluent urban population","celebrating the creativity of artists who transform everyday waste into decorative objects","warning viewers about the environmental consequences of excessive industrial production"],"implication_answer":1,"irrelevant_sentence_index":1},{"id":"27ST_E_06_03","difficulty":"높음","title":"컴퓨터 비유의 한계","sentences":["The reliance on the computer as a model for the operations of the human mind may well prove to be as limited as an earlier fascination with behaviorism.","Psychologists have already begun to recognize the flaws of the mind-as-computer metaphor.","Others, such as Jerome Bruner, one of the founders of cognitive psychology, find that the computer analogy carries with it an unfortunate shift 'from the construction of meaning to the processing of information.'","Bruner's reflections on the limits of the machine model lead him back to a humanistic emphasis on narrative and story-telling as essential ingredients in understanding human cognition, a fascinating intellectual journey that reveals both the power and the limits of computers as guides to the way we think."],"abstract":"The computer metaphor for the human mind is increasingly recognized as inadequate, prompting psychologists to seek richer frameworks that restore the centrality of meaning-making, narrative, and cultural context in understanding human thought.","topic_options":["the growing inadequacy of the computer metaphor for human cognition and the search for richer alternatives","the historical development of cognitive psychology and its relationship to computer science","the specific contributions of Jerome Bruner to the field of narrative psychology","the reasons why behaviorism was replaced by information-processing models in academic psychology","the role of cultural anthropology in expanding the scope of psychological research methods"],"topic_answer":1,"blank_sentence_index":0,"blank_target":"as limited as an earlier fascination with behaviorism","blank_options":["as limited as an earlier fascination with behaviorism","more productive than traditional approaches to cognitive science","as groundbreaking as the discovery of neuroplasticity","less useful than philosophical approaches to the mind","as controversial as current debates in evolutionary psychology"],"blank_answer":1,"order_given_index":0,"order_blocks":[],"order_options":["(C)-(A)-(B)","(A)-(C)-(B)","(B)-(A)-(C)","(B)-(C)-(A)","(A)-(B)-(C)"],"order_answer":5,"insert_sentence":null,"insert_answer":null,"summary_template":"The computer model of the mind is seen as insufficient because it reduces human cognition to ________(A)________ processing while neglecting the role of ________(B)________ in how people understand the world.","summary_A_options":["behavioral","logical","human","computer","information"],"summary_A_answer":5,"summary_B_options":["memory","perception","effective","stable","meaning-making"],"summary_B_answer":5,"implication_sentence_index":0,"implication_keyword":"as limited as an earlier fascination with behaviorism","implication_options":["destined to eventually reveal its explanatory boundaries just as a once-dominant theory did before it","equally as scientifically rigorous as the experimental methods developed by behavioral psychologists","likely to produce the same degree of controversy that surrounded the rise of behavioral science","just as useful in practical educational settings as behaviorist techniques proved to be historically","as widely accepted among researchers today as behaviorism was during its peak popularity"],"implication_answer":1,"irrelevant_sentence_index":2},{"id":"27ST_E_06_04","difficulty":"높음","title":"문학과 상상력의 활성화","sentences":["In the escape that reading literature provides through vicarious identification and comparison with other lives, places, and times, we activate our imagination, that uniquely human ability to explore an alternative set of ideas and experiences that are outside our present environment and that may not even be real.","As opposed to perception that receives and processes information from the outside world — light, sound, shape — and finds meaning in it — a sunset, a symphony, a house — in imagination, the process is reversed.","For example, we read 'house' and picture a representation of a house from memory.","It is our imagination, the complex interweaving of perception and memory that literature activates, releasing a latent creativity that pleases.","The writer may provide the blueprint, but the reader builds literature's many rooms, and like any satisfying occupation, literature gratifies our imaginative and creative abilities."],"abstract":"Reading literature activates the imagination by reversing the direction of meaning-making — drawing on memory and inner imagery rather than external input — and in doing so releases a distinctly human creative capacity.","topic_options":["the way literary reading uniquely engages imagination by constructing meaning from within rather than from external reality","the cognitive differences between perception and imagination as studied in experimental psychology","the role of memory in enabling readers to visualize fictional settings described in literary texts","the relationship between the quality of a writer's style and the depth of the reader's imaginative response","the therapeutic value of reading fiction for individuals seeking escape from difficult circumstances"],"topic_answer":1,"blank_sentence_index":3,"blank_target":"the complex interweaving of perception and memory","blank_options":["the complex interweaving of perception and memory","the straightforward processing of visual and auditory input","the passive reception of information from the external world","the simple retrieval of stored facts and learned vocabulary","the direct translation of words into their dictionary meanings"],"blank_answer":1,"order_given_index":0,"order_blocks":[{"label":"B","sentence_indices":[1]},{"label":"C","sentence_indices":[2]},{"label":"D","sentence_indices":[3,4]}],"order_options":["(B)-(C)-(A)","(B)-(A)-(C)","(A)-(C)-(B)","(A)-(B)-(C)","(C)-(A)-(B)"],"order_answer":4,"insert_sentence":null,"insert_answer":null,"summary_template":"Literary reading ________(A)________ the imagination by requiring readers to draw on memory and inner experience, thereby releasing a creative capacity that is ________(B)________ to human beings.","summary_A_options":["activates","suppresses","replaces","reading","literature"],"summary_A_answer":1,"summary_B_options":["unique","limited","common","effective","stable"],"summary_B_answer":1,"implication_sentence_index":4,"implication_keyword":"The writer may provide the blueprint","implication_options":["the author supplies only the structural outline while the reader creates the full experiential meaning","the writer is responsible for designing the physical layout of the narrative before publication","authors must plan their works in advance using detailed structural frameworks and outlines","the technical craft of writing serves as a guide for readers who lack literary training","writers communicate their intentions clearly so that readers can follow them precisely"],"implication_answer":1,"irrelevant_sentence_index":3},{"id":"27ST_E_07_01","difficulty":"보통","title":"전문성의 다중 요인","sentences":["You've probably heard that it takes about ten thousand hours of practice to become an expert in anything — a musical instrument, a sport, chess, cooking, or a foreign language.","The research by K. Anders Ericsson on this topic has been written about many times, and it was made even more famous when Malcolm Gladwell described it in his bestselling book Outliers.","Specifically, there is nothing particularly special about ten thousand hours, and while practice is clearly important to boost performance, other factors may play an even more important role.","What are those other factors that get us to expert levels of performance?","Pure innate talent? Intelligence? Luck of the draw? Perseverance? Hard work?","Yes, it's all of that... and more.","Age, experience, and environment all play a role.","In other words, there's no one certain factor that can predict or ensure mastery or optimal performance of anything."],"abstract":"Contrary to the popular ten-thousand-hour rule, expertise is the product of multiple interacting factors rather than practice time alone.","topic_options":["the multifactorial nature of expertise beyond the limitations of the ten-thousand-hour rule","the academic controversy surrounding Malcolm Gladwell's popularization of Ericsson's research","the specific role of innate talent in determining long-term performance outcomes","the reasons why practice remains the single most important factor in skill development","the historical development of research on expert performance in competitive fields"],"topic_answer":1,"blank_sentence_index":2,"blank_target":"other factors may play an even more important role","blank_options":["other factors may play an even more important role","practice alone is sufficient to guarantee expert performance","talent is entirely innate and cannot be developed","the amount of time spent matters more than quality","success depends primarily on access to good teachers"],"blank_answer":1,"order_given_index":0,"order_blocks":[{"label":"B","sentence_indices":[1,2]},{"label":"C","sentence_indices":[3,4]},{"label":"D","sentence_indices":[5,6,7]}],"order_options":["(B)-(C)-(A)","(A)-(C)-(B)","(B)-(A)-(C)","(C)-(A)-(B)","(A)-(B)-(C)"],"order_answer":5,"insert_sentence":"What are those other factors that get us to expert levels of performance?","insert_answer":3,"summary_template":"The ten-thousand-hour rule oversimplifies expertise by ignoring the range of ________(A)________ that interact with practice to shape an individual's path toward ________(B)________.","summary_A_options":["disciplines","habits","contrary","factors","popular"],"summary_A_answer":4,"summary_B_options":["recognition","improvement","effective","mastery","stable"],"summary_B_answer":4,"implication_sentence_index":7,"implication_keyword":"there's no one certain factor","implication_options":["mastery cannot be guaranteed by any single deterministic variable","practice alone is the most reliable predictor of expert performance","innate talent is the primary determinant of achievement in any field","the amount of time invested always determines the level of skill attained","environmental factors are more important than personal effort in reaching excellence"],"implication_answer":1,"irrelevant_sentence_index":5},{"id":"27ST_E_07_02","difficulty":"높음","title":"이념적 맥락의 협상","sentences":["In the old Soviet Union, a famous U.S. beverage company wanted to set up a bottling plant and distribution network.","The prevailing ideology in the old Soviet Union at the time stressed the importance of the group over the individual and the need to develop industrial capacity at the expense of consumer goods.","Soft drinks hardly seemed to fit the country's ideological priorities.","Indeed, one government official dismissed the product as a 'useless drink.'","Eventually, the two sides struck a deal, but not on the basis that the drink would quench the local population's thirst.","They restructured the project to include a heavy training component for local workers and managers, as well as a farm that would grow certain of the drink's ingredients.","In addition, the company promised to make efforts to persuade other American companies to consider investments in the country."],"abstract":"Successful negotiation in an ideologically opposed environment requires reframing a proposal in terms that align with the counterpart's values rather than one's own commercial interests.","topic_options":["the necessity of reframing proposals to align with the ideological priorities of the opposing party","the economic benefits that American companies gained from entering the Soviet consumer market","the role of government officials in blocking foreign commercial ventures on ideological grounds","the historical context of U.S.-Soviet trade relations during the Cold War era","the strategies companies use to adapt their products for ideologically restrictive markets"],"topic_answer":1,"blank_sentence_index":1,"blank_target":"at the expense of consumer goods","blank_options":["at the expense of consumer goods","in support of individual economic freedoms","through the promotion of foreign trade","by means of democratic political reforms","with a focus on agricultural modernization"],"blank_answer":1,"order_given_index":0,"order_blocks":[{"label":"B","sentence_indices":[1,2]},{"label":"C","sentence_indices":[3,4]},{"label":"D","sentence_indices":[5,6]}],"order_options":["(A)-(C)-(B)","(B)-(A)-(C)","(A)-(B)-(C)","(C)-(A)-(B)","(B)-(C)-(A)"],"order_answer":3,"insert_sentence":"They restructured the project to include a heavy training component for local workers and managers, as well as a farm that would grow certain of the drink's ingredients.","insert_answer":5,"summary_template":"When facing ideological ________(A)________, effective negotiators succeed by repositioning their proposal as a contribution to the other party's ________(B)________ rather than their own goals.","summary_A_options":["competition","uncertainty","resistance","successful","negotiation"],"summary_A_answer":3,"summary_B_options":["demands","interests","priorities","effective","stable"],"summary_B_answer":3,"implication_sentence_index":3,"implication_keyword":"useless drink","implication_options":["a product entirely incompatible with the values the state was committed to advancing","a beverage with no nutritional value that failed to meet basic health standards","a foreign commodity that posed a direct threat to domestic manufacturing industries","a consumer item that was too expensive for the average Soviet citizen to afford","a product that lacked the technical sophistication expected by Soviet officials"],"implication_answer":1,"irrelevant_sentence_index":2},{"id":"27ST_E_07_03","difficulty":"높음","title":"CAD와 창의성의 상실","sentences":["In 2012, the Yale School of Architecture held a symposium called 'Is Drawing Dead?'","The bold title reflects a growing sense that the architect's freehand sketch is being displaced by the computer.","The transition from sketchpad to screen entails, many architects believe, a loss of creativity, of adventurousness.","Thanks to the precision and apparent completeness of screen renderings, a designer working at a computer has a tendency to lock in, visually and cognitively, on a design at an early stage.","Researchers term this phenomenon 'premature fixation' and trace its cause to 'the disincentive for design changes once a large amount of detail and interconnectedness is built too quickly into a CAD model.'","The designer at the computer also tends to emphasize formal experimentation at the expense of expressiveness.","By weakening an architect's 'personal, emotional connection with the work,' a renowned American architect and designer Michael Graves argues, CAD software produces designs that, 'while complex and interesting in their own way,' often 'lack the emotional content of a design derived from hand.'"],"abstract":"The shift from hand-drawn sketching to computer-aided design tends to suppress architectural creativity by encouraging premature commitment to a design and weakening the emotional expressiveness that emerges from the uncertainty of manual drawing.","topic_options":["the ways in which CAD software undermines architectural creativity by promoting premature fixation and reducing emotional expressiveness","the historical debate within architecture schools over whether hand drawing should remain part of the curriculum","the technical advantages of computer-aided design in improving the precision of architectural plans","the role of uncertainty and ambiguity in generating innovative solutions across creative disciplines","the reasons why architects increasingly prefer digital tools despite their known creative limitations"],"topic_answer":1,"blank_sentence_index":2,"blank_target":"a loss of creativity, of adventurousness","blank_options":["a loss of creativity, of adventurousness","an increase in precision and technical accuracy","a shift toward more collaborative design processes","a reduction in the time required for completion","an improvement in the quality of presentations"],"blank_answer":1,"order_given_index":0,"order_blocks":[{"label":"B","sentence_indices":[1,2]},{"label":"C","sentence_indices":[3]},{"label":"D","sentence_indices":[4,5,6]}],"order_options":["(A)-(C)-(B)","(A)-(B)-(C)","(B)-(C)-(A)","(B)-(A)-(C)","(C)-(A)-(B)"],"order_answer":2,"insert_sentence":"Researchers term this phenomenon 'premature fixation' and trace its cause to 'the disincentive for design changes once a large amount of detail and interconnectedness is built too quickly into a CAD model.'","insert_answer":4,"summary_template":"CAD software encourages ________(A)________ commitment to early design decisions, thereby reducing the exploratory freedom that hand drawing provides and diminishing the ________(B)________ depth of architectural work.","summary_A_options":["flexible","deliberate","design","shift","premature"],"summary_A_answer":5,"summary_B_options":["structural","technical","effective","stable","emotional"],"summary_B_answer":5,"implication_sentence_index":4,"implication_keyword":"premature fixation","implication_options":["locking onto a design too early before fully exploring creative possibilities","making repairs to a design only after the construction phase has begun","abandoning a design concept before it has been properly developed","spending too much time on the decorative aspects of an architectural plan","presenting a completed design to clients before receiving their initial feedback"],"implication_answer":1,"irrelevant_sentence_index":6},{"id":"27ST_E_07_04","difficulty":"보통","title":"리미티드 애니메이션의 가치","sentences":["Limited animation is a process of making animated cartoons that does not follow a 'realistic' approach.","However, this style of animation is very time-consuming and expensive.","Limited animation creates an image that uses abstract art, symbolism, and limited movement to create the same effect, but at a much lower production cost.","This style of animation depends more upon suspension of disbelief to tell a story; the story exists more in the viewer's imagination.","It also encourages the animators to indulge in artistic styles that are not necessarily bound to the limits of the real world.","The result is a new artistic style that could not have developed if animation was solely devoted to producing simulations of reality.","Without limited animation, such ground-breaking films as Yellow Submarine, Chuck Jones' The Dot and the Line, and many others could never have been produced."],"abstract":"By departing from realistic representation and embracing abstraction, limited animation opened a space for entirely new forms of artistic expression that would have been impossible within the constraints of full animation.","topic_options":["the artistic and creative possibilities unlocked by abandoning realism in limited animation","the economic advantages that made limited animation a practical alternative to full animation","the historical legacy of Walt Disney's realistic animation style in shaping the industry","the technical methods used in limited animation to reduce production time and cost","the audience reception of abstract animation compared to realistic animated feature films"],"topic_answer":1,"blank_sentence_index":2,"blank_target":"abstract art, symbolism, and limited movement","blank_options":["abstract art, symbolism, and limited movement","photorealistic imagery, detailed backgrounds, and fluid motion","traditional painting techniques and elaborate visual narratives","computer-generated graphics and three-dimensional rendering","documentary footage and realistic character proportions"],"blank_answer":1,"order_given_index":0,"order_blocks":[{"label":"B","sentence_indices":[1]},{"label":"C","sentence_indices":[2,3]},{"label":"D","sentence_indices":[4,5,6]}],"order_options":["(A)-(B)-(C)","(A)-(C)-(B)","(C)-(A)-(B)","(B)-(A)-(C)","(B)-(C)-(A)"],"order_answer":1,"insert_sentence":"However, this style of animation is very time-consuming and expensive.","insert_answer":1,"summary_template":"Limited animation, by rejecting ________(A)________ representation and embracing abstraction, enabled animators to develop entirely new artistic styles that ________(B)________ the boundaries of the real world.","summary_A_options":["realistic","detailed","traditional","animation","departing"],"summary_A_answer":1,"summary_B_options":["transcend","challenge","reflect","effective","stable"],"summary_B_answer":1,"implication_sentence_index":5,"implication_keyword":"could not have developed if animation was solely devoted to producing simulations of reality","implication_options":["an exclusive focus on realism would have permanently closed off the creative possibilities that abstraction opened","animators who prioritized accuracy over creativity were unable to produce commercially successful films","the technology required for realistic animation made it impossible to experiment with abstract styles","studios that committed to full animation were financially unable to explore alternative artistic approaches","audiences raised on realistic animation would have rejected abstract styles if introduced too early"],"implication_answer":1,"irrelevant_sentence_index":1},{"id":"27ST_E_11_01","difficulty":"보통","title":"슈퍼마켓 비유 읽기법","sentences":["Here's an application of metaphors to research papers: Below-grade-level readers in my urban middle school have a great deal of difficulty doing research.","Their answer when assigned to do 'a report' is to come to the media center and copy verbatim everything in the encyclopedia article or whatever source they have located, be it Internet, print, or whatever.","To try to get the students to understand why it isn't necessary to copy everything in the articles, I use a comparison to a supermarket.","I ask them if everything in the supermarket is useful, and we discuss this, with the usual conclusion being that it is, but we don't buy everything all the time.","Then I ask them why they don't buy everything each time they go and how they determine what to buy when they go with their parents.","From that point on, I lead a discussion about how whatever their teachers have asked for is their 'shopping list' for their research, and they should just read for that information and write it down in note format.","It sometimes helps them to understand that copying everything is a wasteful endeavor."],"abstract":"By comparing selective research reading to shopping with a list, a teacher helps students understand that effective information gathering requires purposeful selection rather than indiscriminate copying.","topic_options":["the use of a familiar analogy to help students develop more purposeful and selective research habits","the challenges faced by below-grade-level readers when navigating academic research tasks","the role of encyclopedias and internet sources in shaping the research habits of middle school students","the importance of note-taking formats in improving the quality of student research reports","the effectiveness of class discussion as a method for teaching critical reading skills"],"topic_answer":1,"blank_sentence_index":0,"blank_target":"have a great deal of difficulty doing research","blank_options":["have a great deal of difficulty doing research","show remarkable creativity when given open-ended assignments","prefer hands-on activities over traditional academic tasks","struggle to concentrate during extended instruction","excel at memorizing facts but fail to apply them critically"],"blank_answer":1,"order_given_index":0,"order_blocks":[{"label":"B","sentence_indices":[1,2]},{"label":"C","sentence_indices":[3,4]},{"label":"D","sentence_indices":[5,6]}],"order_options":["(C)-(A)-(B)","(A)-(C)-(B)","(B)-(C)-(A)","(A)-(B)-(C)","(B)-(A)-(C)"],"order_answer":4,"insert_sentence":"From that point on, I lead a discussion about how whatever their teachers have asked for is their 'shopping list' for their research, and they should just read for that information and write it down in note format.","insert_answer":5,"summary_template":"A teacher uses a supermarket ________(A)________ to help struggling students recognize that research requires ________(B)________ selection of relevant information rather than copying everything available.","summary_A_options":["exercise","example","analogy","comparing","selective"],"summary_A_answer":3,"summary_B_options":["thorough","creative","purposeful","effective","stable"],"summary_B_answer":3,"implication_sentence_index":6,"implication_keyword":"copying everything is a wasteful endeavor","implication_options":["reproducing all available information without discrimination defeats the purpose of focused inquiry","students who copy from sources without understanding waste the time they could spend writing","teachers who assign open-ended research tasks place an unfair burden on struggling learners","relying on encyclopedias rather than original sources produces reports of inferior quality","spending too much time in the media center reduces the time available for actual writing"],"implication_answer":1,"irrelevant_sentence_index":4},{"id":"27ST_E_11_02","difficulty":"높음","title":"시장 논리의 한계","sentences":["Reformist approaches assume that markets could operate in more equitable and environmentally reasonable ways, and that a market is the most efficient option available.","Yet the logic of market efficiencies generally rotates on purely monetary calculations, effectively reasoning in a hall of mirrors and marginalising real social and environmental values.","Familiar examples are conventional food retailers, such as supermarkets, which purchase fruit and vegetables as cheaply as possible.","Inexpensive produce might be grown using soil- and water-damaging fertilisers, by poorly paid illegal migrant workers, and transported long distances using more cheap labour and environmentally damaging practices.","By its very nature, one never manages to escape the conundrums that production for trade entails.","Real social and environmental values involved in caring for people and Earth highlight the inequities and damage of market-oriented activities."],"abstract":"Market-based logic, by reducing value to monetary terms, systematically excludes social and environmental costs, making it incapable of addressing the inequities it generates.","topic_options":["the structural incapacity of market logic to account for genuine social and environmental values","the potential for reformist economic policies to make markets more equitable and sustainable","the role of organic farming in providing an ethical alternative to conventional food production","the challenges faced by low-income consumers in accessing environmentally responsible products","the ways in which government regulation can correct the social failures of free market systems"],"topic_answer":1,"blank_sentence_index":1,"blank_target":"reasoning in a hall of mirrors","blank_options":["reasoning in a hall of mirrors","operating within a transparent and accountable framework","responding effectively to real social and environmental needs","aligning economic incentives with ecological sustainability","promoting fair distribution of wealth across all sectors"],"blank_answer":1,"order_given_index":0,"order_blocks":[{"label":"B","sentence_indices":[1,2]},{"label":"C","sentence_indices":[3]},{"label":"D","sentence_indices":[4,5]}],"order_options":["(B)-(C)-(A)","(A)-(C)-(B)","(A)-(B)-(C)","(C)-(A)-(B)","(B)-(A)-(C)"],"order_answer":3,"insert_sentence":"By its very nature, one never manages to escape the conundrums that production for trade entails.","insert_answer":4,"summary_template":"Market efficiency, defined purely in ________(A)________ terms, inevitably ________(B)________ the social and environmental costs that fall outside its calculative framework.","summary_A_options":["competitive","productive","monetary","market","based"],"summary_A_answer":3,"summary_B_options":["conceals","exaggerates","marginalizes","effective","stable"],"summary_B_answer":3,"implication_sentence_index":1,"implication_keyword":"reasoning in a hall of mirrors","implication_options":["operating within a self-referential system that only reflects its own assumptions and never confronts external reality","making calculations so complex that even trained economists struggle to understand their implications","presenting economic data in a way that deliberately misleads policymakers and the general public","producing analyses that appear rigorous but rely on assumptions that have never been empirically tested","creating policies that seem transparent on the surface but conceal hidden contradictions"],"implication_answer":1,"irrelevant_sentence_index":2},{"id":"27ST_E_11_03","difficulty":"보통","title":"인종의 사회적 구성","sentences":["There is no scientific basis for the term 'race.'","Most humans are genetically very similar and there is so little variation amongst us that it is not possible to draw neat boundaries around people and label them as a distinct racial group.","Race is an example of social construction, which social processes create something that essentially does not exist but takes on real force in people's lives.","Sociologists prefer to call these processes 'racialization.'","For example, in ancient Rome there were various leading figures, such as Emperor Septimius Severus, who were black.","Little is said of their skin colour in accounts written at the time, because the ancient Romans did not think it made any difference.","They thought more in terms of judging people as being civilized or a barbarian."],"abstract":"Race has no scientific foundation and is instead a social construct, as demonstrated by historical evidence showing that skin colour was not always treated as a meaningful category of human difference.","topic_options":["the socially constructed nature of race and the historical evidence that it was not always a meaningful category","the genetic research confirming that human populations share far more similarities than differences","the role of sociologists in challenging the biological definitions of race in academic discourse","the political uses of racial categorization in modern democratic societies","the ways ancient Roman society differed from modern societies in its approach to ethnic diversity"],"topic_answer":1,"blank_sentence_index":2,"blank_target":"something that essentially does not exist but takes on real force in people's lives","blank_options":["something that essentially does not exist but takes on real force in people's lives","a biological reality that can be measured through genetic analysis","a permanent feature of human societies across all cultures","a scientific category that accurately reflects natural human variation","an inherited characteristic that determines individual potential"],"blank_answer":1,"order_given_index":0,"order_blocks":[{"label":"B","sentence_indices":[1,2]},{"label":"C","sentence_indices":[3]},{"label":"D","sentence_indices":[4,5,6]}],"order_options":["(B)-(C)-(A)","(A)-(B)-(C)","(A)-(C)-(B)","(B)-(A)-(C)","(C)-(A)-(B)"],"order_answer":2,"insert_sentence":"For example, in ancient Rome there were various leading figures, such as Emperor Septimius Severus, who were black.","insert_answer":4,"summary_template":"Race lacks any ________(A)________ basis and functions instead as a social construct whose significance is ________(B)________ by historical and cultural processes rather than biological reality.","summary_A_options":["historical","legal","scientific","race","foundation"],"summary_A_answer":3,"summary_B_options":["disputed","inherited","constructed","effective","stable"],"summary_B_answer":3,"implication_sentence_index":2,"implication_keyword":"social construction","implication_options":["a category created and sustained by human practices and beliefs rather than grounded in objective reality","a physical structure built by communities to reinforce shared cultural values and group identity","a theoretical framework developed by sociologists to study patterns of inequality in modern societies","an ideological tool deliberately designed by ruling classes to maintain control over subordinate groups","a natural tendency among humans to form group boundaries based on observable physical characteristics"],"implication_answer":1,"irrelevant_sentence_index":4},{"id":"27ST_E_11_04","difficulty":"보통","title":"음식 분량과 비만","sentences":["Many factors contribute to Americans' growing waistlines, but one observation in particular cannot be overlooked: The incidence of obesity has increased in parallel with increasing portion sizes.","Consider this: Adults today consume an average of 300 more calories per day than they did in the year 1985.","Is this just a coincidence, or do larger portion sizes have something to do with it?","In almost every eating situation, we are now confronted by huge portions, which are perceived as 'normal' or 'a great value.'","Americans have created the perception that large portion sizes are appropriate, creating an environment of portion distortion.","We find portion distortions in restaurants, where the jumbo-sized portions are consistently 250 percent larger than the regular portions.","Research shows that people unintentionally consume more calories when offered larger portions.","Consuming larger portion sizes can contribute to positive energy balance, which, over time, leads to weight gain and ultimately can result in obesity."],"abstract":"The normalization of oversized food portions in American culture has created an environment in which people systematically consume more calories than necessary, contributing significantly to the rise in obesity.","topic_options":["the cultural normalization of excessive portion sizes as a key driver of rising obesity rates","the caloric differences between restaurant meals and home-cooked food in the modern American diet","the role of dishware and kitchenware design in unconsciously influencing eating behavior","the relationship between food marketing strategies and consumer perceptions of appropriate serving sizes","the public health interventions needed to address the growing epidemic of obesity in the United States"],"topic_answer":1,"blank_sentence_index":0,"blank_target":"increased in parallel with increasing portion sizes","blank_options":["increased in parallel with increasing portion sizes","declined steadily as nutritional awareness has improved","varied significantly across different demographic groups","remained stable despite changes in dietary guidelines","risen sharply due to reduced physical activity levels"],"blank_answer":1,"order_given_index":0,"order_blocks":[{"label":"B","sentence_indices":[1,2]},{"label":"C","sentence_indices":[3,4,5]},{"label":"D","sentence_indices":[6,7]}],"order_options":["(C)-(A)-(B)","(A)-(C)-(B)","(B)-(C)-(A)","(B)-(A)-(C)","(A)-(B)-(C)"],"order_answer":5,"insert_sentence":"Research shows that people unintentionally consume more calories when offered larger portions.","insert_answer":6,"summary_template":"The widespread ________(A)________ of oversized portions has conditioned Americans to perceive excess as normal, leading to unintentional overconsumption and a steady rise in ________(B)________.","summary_A_options":["promotion","availability","normalization","oversized","food"],"summary_A_answer":3,"summary_B_options":["consumption","expenditure","obesity","effective","stable"],"summary_B_answer":3,"implication_sentence_index":1,"implication_keyword":"300 more calories per day","implication_options":["a consistent and measurable increase in daily energy intake that compounds into significant weight gain over time","a temporary dietary change caused by the introduction of new food products in the American market","a difference in caloric intake that nutritionists consider acceptable within normal variation","an increase driven primarily by changes in food quality rather than the amount of food consumed","a statistical anomaly that reflects changes in how calories are measured rather than actual eating behavior"],"implication_answer":1,"irrelevant_sentence_index":2},{"id":"27ST_E_12_01","difficulty":"높음","title":"도덕적 분노의 기능","sentences":["Moral outrage is the psychological tool that motivates people to punish wrongdoers, even at cost or risk to themselves.","It is a 'commitment device,' something that commits people to punishment, even though trying to punish someone can be dangerous.","When we witness unjust harm, whether someone committing interpersonal violence or obvious cheating, we have an embodied physical reaction.","We get angry, our blood pressure spikes, our heart beats faster; we thirst for retribution.","In any single situation, there is rarely an immediate personal benefit for meting out punishment, and often there is real risk, because the person you are serving justice against could lash out at you or get revenge in the future.","But the powerful feeling of outrage leads us to momentarily forget this unfavorable evaluation and get involved in a situation we would be better off avoiding, and science reveals how this feeling and forgetting is essential for maintaining a cooperative society."],"abstract":"Moral outrage functions as a psychological mechanism that overrides rational self-interest and compels individuals to punish wrongdoing, a capacity that is ultimately indispensable for sustaining social cooperation.","topic_options":["the socially essential role of moral outrage in overcoming self-interested rationality to enforce punishment","the physiological symptoms of anger that arise when individuals witness acts of interpersonal violence","the personal risks that individuals face when they choose to intervene in situations of injustice","the evolutionary origins of retributive impulses in human communities and social hierarchies","the ways in which emotional reactions to injustice undermine an individual's capacity for rational judgment"],"topic_answer":1,"blank_sentence_index":0,"blank_target":"even at cost or risk to themselves","blank_options":["even at cost or risk to themselves","only when there is a clear personal benefit involved","provided that legal authorities have already intervened","whenever social norms explicitly require such action","as long as punishment can be carried out anonymously"],"blank_answer":1,"order_given_index":0,"order_blocks":[{"label":"B","sentence_indices":[1,2]},{"label":"C","sentence_indices":[3]},{"label":"D","sentence_indices":[4,5]}],"order_options":["(B)-(A)-(C)","(A)-(C)-(B)","(A)-(B)-(C)","(C)-(A)-(B)","(B)-(C)-(A)"],"order_answer":3,"insert_sentence":"In any single situation, there is rarely an immediate personal benefit for meting out punishment, and often there is real risk, because the person you are serving justice against could lash out at you or get revenge in the future.","insert_answer":4,"summary_template":"Moral outrage acts as a ________(A)________ that overrides rational calculation and pushes individuals to punish wrongdoers despite personal risk, making it ________(B)________ to the maintenance of cooperative social life.","summary_A_options":["moral device","commitment device","social device","behavioral tool","rational mechanism"],"summary_A_answer":2,"summary_B_options":["optional","indispensable","outrage","flexible","redundant"],"summary_B_answer":2,"implication_sentence_index":5,"implication_keyword":"a situation we would be better off avoiding","implication_options":["an intervention that carries personal risk but serves a broader social function beyond individual benefit","a conflict that rational individuals would recognize as too dangerous to enter under any circumstances","a confrontation that emotionally unstable individuals are unable to resist despite knowing the consequences","a social obligation that most people fulfill only when they are certain of support from their community","a scenario in which the emotional satisfaction of punishment outweighs the realistic assessment of harm"],"implication_answer":1,"irrelevant_sentence_index":3},{"id":"27ST_E_12_02","difficulty":"높음","title":"자연 제품 선호의 기원","sentences":["Why do humans have the counterproductive instinct to favor natural products in the absence of knowledge of their benefits or their potential for harm?","The answer likely lies in our genes.","Our species, through most of its evolutionary history, relied heavily upon experience to judge whether ingestion of something was beneficial versus whether it was dangerous.","We evolved the instinct to avoid plants that made us sick and favored those that made us well.","Treating unknowns with great caution provided a terrific survival advantage.","But those pills coming off a pharmaceutical production line look nothing like what our instincts tell us is safe to eat.","The ingredients remind us of a high school chemistry lab.","Yet we are expected to consume them.","Thus, we treat them with caution just as our distant ancestors regarded a new plant.","When in need of a remedy, we are drawn to derivatives of our food, plant products, which we perceive to be safe, and not artificial products of science."],"abstract":"The human preference for natural over synthetic products is not a rational judgment but an evolutionarily inherited instinct that once protected our ancestors from poisonous plants but now misleads us in evaluating modern medicine.","topic_options":["the evolutionary origin of the instinct to prefer natural products over synthetic ones despite lacking rational justification","the medical dangers of relying on plant-based remedies instead of clinically tested pharmaceutical drugs","the role of genetic inheritance in determining individual differences in response to natural versus artificial substances","the ways in which the pharmaceutical industry can address consumer distrust of synthetic medications","the historical evidence showing that ancient humans successfully used plant-based medicine to treat disease"],"topic_answer":1,"blank_sentence_index":4,"blank_target":"a terrific survival advantage","blank_options":["a terrific survival advantage","an unnecessary restriction on dietary choices","a significant obstacle to medical progress","an outdated response to modern food safety","a harmful bias against pharmaceutical treatments"],"blank_answer":1,"order_given_index":0,"order_blocks":[{"label":"B","sentence_indices":[1,2,3]},{"label":"C","sentence_indices":[4,5]},{"label":"D","sentence_indices":[6,7,8,9]}],"order_options":["(B)-(C)-(A)","(C)-(A)-(B)","(A)-(C)-(B)","(A)-(B)-(C)","(B)-(A)-(C)"],"order_answer":4,"insert_sentence":"But those pills coming off a pharmaceutical production line look nothing like what our instincts tell us is safe to eat.","insert_answer":5,"summary_template":"The human tendency to favor natural over synthetic products stems from an ________(A)________ instinct that once aided survival but now produces ________(B)________ judgments about the safety of modern medicine.","summary_A_options":["rational","cultural","human","evolutionary","preference"],"summary_A_answer":4,"summary_B_options":["effective","inconsistent","cautious","irrational","stable"],"summary_B_answer":4,"implication_sentence_index":5,"implication_keyword":"look nothing like what our instincts tell us is safe to eat","implication_options":["bear no resemblance to the familiar natural forms our evolved intuitions associate with safety","fail to meet the aesthetic standards that consumers expect from products they are willing to purchase","lack the visual cues that medical professionals use to distinguish effective from ineffective treatments","appear too uniform and artificially produced to inspire confidence in their nutritional value","do not match the descriptions of safe foods found in traditional medical and dietary knowledge"],"implication_answer":1,"irrelevant_sentence_index":7},{"id":"27ST_E_12_03","difficulty":"보통","title":"보조식품과 의약품 규제","sentences":["Dietary supplements are not drugs.","A drug is intended to diagnose, cure, mitigate, treat, or prevent disease.","Before marketing, drugs must undergo extensive studies of effectiveness, safety, interactions with other substances, and dosing.","The FDA gives formal premarket approval to a drug and monitors its safety after the drug is on the market.","If a drug is subsequently shown to be dangerous, the FDA can act quickly to have it removed from the market.","None of this is true for dietary supplements.","The current law gives the FDA only limited authority over supplements.","This makes it difficult for the government to remove unsafe supplements from the marketplace.","There are some legislators in Congress who want to improve the law by requiring supplement makers to put safer products on the shelves and label products more clearly.","The objective is to ensure that consumers can tell the difference between dietary supplements that are safe and those that have potentially serious side effects or drug interactions."],"abstract":"Unlike pharmaceutical drugs, dietary supplements operate under far weaker regulatory oversight, leaving consumers without adequate protection from potentially unsafe products.","topic_options":["the regulatory gap between pharmaceutical drugs and dietary supplements that leaves consumers inadequately protected","the rigorous approval process that the FDA applies to pharmaceutical drugs before they reach the market","the legislative efforts in Congress to reform the law governing the marketing of dietary supplements","the health risks that consumers face when they substitute dietary supplements for prescribed medications","the role of labeling requirements in helping consumers make informed choices about nutritional products"],"topic_answer":1,"blank_sentence_index":2,"blank_target":"extensive studies of effectiveness, safety, interactions with other substances, and dosing","blank_options":["extensive studies of effectiveness, safety, interactions with other substances, and dosing","a brief review of manufacturing practices and ingredient labeling","informal surveys of consumer satisfaction and reported side effects","a simple check to ensure basic hygiene standards are maintained","voluntary self-reporting by companies about known risks"],"blank_answer":1,"order_given_index":0,"order_blocks":[{"label":"B","sentence_indices":[1,2,3]},{"label":"C","sentence_indices":[4,5,6]},{"label":"D","sentence_indices":[7,8,9]}],"order_options":["(A)-(B)-(C)","(B)-(A)-(C)","(B)-(C)-(A)","(A)-(C)-(B)","(C)-(A)-(B)"],"order_answer":1,"insert_sentence":"There are some legislators in Congress who want to improve the law by requiring supplement makers to put safer products on the shelves and label products more clearly.","insert_answer":8,"summary_template":"While pharmaceutical drugs must pass ________(A)________ regulatory review before reaching consumers, dietary supplements face minimal oversight, creating a serious gap in ________(B)________ protection.","summary_A_options":["expedited","voluntary","unlike","pharmaceutical","rigorous"],"summary_A_answer":5,"summary_B_options":["environmental","commercial","effective","stable","consumer"],"summary_B_answer":5,"implication_sentence_index":7,"implication_keyword":"difficult for the government to remove unsafe supplements from the marketplace","implication_options":["the regulatory framework lacks sufficient authority to swiftly act against harmful products already in circulation","government agencies are unwilling to enforce existing laws due to political pressure from the supplement industry","consumers are unlikely to report adverse effects from supplements because they consider them natural and safe","the legal definition of dietary supplements makes it impossible to distinguish them from regulated medications","removing products from sale requires evidence of harm that is rarely available before widespread distribution"],"implication_answer":1,"irrelevant_sentence_index":9},{"id":"27ST_E_12_04","difficulty":"높음","title":"문학의 가변적 의미","sentences":["Literature is not a disposable carrier of nuggets of information.","Literature invites us back again and again to re-experience what it offers and to reassess its meanings.","Literature continues to communicate meaning and significance over time, and, most remarkably, to shift its meaning based on our perspective.","We have all had the experience of taking up a classic work of literature after several years and finding in it details and significance we missed the first time through.","One's perception of Shakespeare's grand drama on aging under existential threat, King Lear, is a different experience read in one's twenties than it is in one's seventies.","This is true because reading literature, as opposed to everyday reading, requires full reader participation, activating not just our informational processing skills but our analysis, imagination, and emotions.","These change over time in every person, and those changes explain how works of literature are more variable than everyday reading."],"abstract":"Literature's meaning is not fixed but evolves with the reader's accumulated experience, because genuine literary engagement activates the full range of human faculties that change as we grow.","topic_options":["the reader-dependent variability of literary meaning arising from the full engagement of changing human faculties","the superiority of classic literature over contemporary writing in conveying enduring emotional truths","the role of rereading in helping students develop deeper analytical and critical thinking skills","the contrast between the fixed informational content of non-fiction and the open-ended nature of fiction","the ways in which a writer's biography influences how readers interpret the themes of literary works"],"topic_answer":1,"blank_sentence_index":5,"blank_target":"full reader participation","blank_options":["full reader participation","passive reception of factual information","a basic understanding of narrative structure","professional literary training and expertise","repeated exposure to academic criticism"],"blank_answer":1,"order_given_index":0,"order_blocks":[{"label":"B","sentence_indices":[1,2]},{"label":"C","sentence_indices":[3]},{"label":"D","sentence_indices":[4,5,6]}],"order_options":["(B)-(C)-(A)","(C)-(A)-(B)","(B)-(A)-(C)","(A)-(B)-(C)","(A)-(C)-(B)"],"order_answer":4,"insert_sentence":"One's perception of Shakespeare's grand drama on aging under existential threat, King Lear, is a different experience read in one's twenties than it is in one's seventies.","insert_answer":4,"summary_template":"Unlike informational texts, literature generates ________(A)________ meaning because it demands the engagement of faculties — analysis, imagination, and emotion — that ________(B)________ as a person's life experience deepens.","summary_A_options":["fixed","variable","abstract","literature","meaning"],"summary_A_answer":2,"summary_B_options":["stabilize","evolve","diminish","effective","stable"],"summary_B_answer":2,"implication_sentence_index":0,"implication_keyword":"disposable carrier of nuggets of information","implication_options":["a temporary medium whose only function is to transmit facts that can be extracted and discarded once understood","a low-quality publication designed for mass consumption without regard for artistic or intellectual value","a format that loses its relevance quickly because the information it contains becomes outdated","a text whose meaning is entirely determined by the author and remains unchanged regardless of the reader","a medium that appeals primarily to readers who lack the patience for sustained analytical engagement"],"implication_answer":1,"irrelevant_sentence_index":4},{"id":"27ST_E_13_01","difficulty":"높음","title":"아리스토텔레스의 목적인","sentences":["In the Physics, Aristotle asks whether nature acts for the sake of something.","He offers an account of rain as water that rises when heated by the Sun, then cools, condenses, and falls to Earth, but is not particularly concerned with explaining rain as such.","Rather, he addresses a more general question: how to account for natural objects, events, and processes that appear with regularity.","The sharpness of front teeth allows them to tear while the bluntness of those in the back enables them to crush food; both are useful for eating.","In Aristotle's view, all natural things happen in a given way and occur for the sake of something; that is the final cause."],"abstract":"Aristotle argues that the regular patterns observed in nature are not coincidental but purposeful, and that understanding natural phenomena requires identifying the end or goal — the final cause — toward which they are directed.","topic_options":["Aristotle's argument that natural regularity reflects purposefulness and is best understood through the concept of final cause","the scientific accuracy of Aristotle's account of meteorological phenomena such as the water cycle","the contrast between Aristotle's teleological view of nature and modern mechanistic explanations","the role of anatomical observation in supporting Aristotle's broader philosophical claims about the natural world","the historical influence of Aristotle's Physics on the development of biology and natural science"],"topic_answer":1,"blank_sentence_index":4,"blank_target":"for the sake of something; that is the final cause","blank_options":["for the sake of something; that is the final cause","by chance; that is the accidental nature of evolution","through random variation; that is the basis of natural selection","according to fixed laws; that is the deterministic view of science","in response to external pressures; that is the adaptive mechanism"],"blank_answer":1,"order_given_index":0,"order_blocks":[{"label":"B","sentence_indices":[1]},{"label":"C","sentence_indices":[2]},{"label":"D","sentence_indices":[3,4]}],"order_options":["(C)-(A)-(B)","(A)-(C)-(B)","(B)-(C)-(A)","(A)-(B)-(C)","(B)-(A)-(C)"],"order_answer":4,"insert_sentence":null,"insert_answer":null,"summary_template":"Aristotle contends that the ________(A)________ of natural phenomena is not accidental but reflects an inherent ________(B)________ that constitutes the final cause of all natural things.","summary_A_options":["diversity","complexity","aristotle","argues","regularity"],"summary_A_answer":5,"summary_B_options":["simplicity","effective","symmetry","stable","purposefulness"],"summary_B_answer":5,"implication_sentence_index":4,"implication_keyword":"occur for the sake of something","implication_options":["are directed toward an end that gives them their proper function and explains why they exist in the form they do","are caused by external forces that act intentionally upon passive natural materials","are produced by the deliberate choices of living organisms seeking to satisfy biological needs","are the result of divine intervention that assigns each natural object its appropriate role","are shaped by the cumulative effects of environmental pressures acting over long periods of time"],"implication_answer":1,"irrelevant_sentence_index":1},{"id":"27ST_E_13_02","difficulty":"보통","title":"아이디어의 양과 질","sentences":["AI is a prolific idea generator.","Human brainstorming groups tend to focus on the quality of creative ideas and almost immediately lean into variations of first suggestions, but good ideas are more likely when groups focus first on quantity.","As Linus Pauling put it, 'The best way to have a good idea is to have lots of ideas.'","Many studies have confirmed that creative quality comes from quantity of ideas, and one Stanford study pegged the number of ideas that distinguish a successful product from a failure at more than two thousand.","This is why design thinking and innovation are so focused on the processes of creating possibilities without judgment."],"abstract":"Creative quality is more reliably produced by maximizing the quantity of ideas generated than by focusing prematurely on quality, a principle confirmed by research and embodied in design thinking practice.","topic_options":["the evidence-based principle that generating a large volume of ideas is the most reliable path to creative quality","the competitive advantage that AI holds over human brainstorming groups in generating novel concepts","the role of the equal odds rule in guiding professional designers toward more innovative product outcomes","the reasons why most human brainstorming sessions fail to produce ideas of sufficient originality","the specific numerical threshold of ideas required to ensure the success of a new product or innovation"],"topic_answer":1,"blank_sentence_index":0,"blank_target":"a prolific idea generator","blank_options":["a prolific idea generator","a reliable substitute for human creativity","an accurate predictor of market success","a tool for eliminating subjective bias","a system for organizing existing knowledge"],"blank_answer":1,"order_given_index":0,"order_blocks":[{"label":"B","sentence_indices":[1]},{"label":"C","sentence_indices":[2]},{"label":"D","sentence_indices":[3,4]}],"order_options":["(B)-(C)-(A)","(A)-(B)-(C)","(B)-(A)-(C)","(C)-(A)-(B)","(A)-(C)-(B)"],"order_answer":2,"insert_sentence":null,"insert_answer":null,"summary_template":"Research consistently shows that creative ________(A)________ depends on generating a high ________(B)________ of ideas rather than focusing prematurely on selecting the best ones.","summary_A_options":["diversity","quality","originality","creative","reliably"],"summary_A_answer":2,"summary_B_options":["frequency","quantity","variety","effective","stable"],"summary_B_answer":2,"implication_sentence_index":2,"implication_keyword":"The best way to have a good idea is to have lots of ideas","implication_options":["excellence in creative output is a probabilistic outcome that becomes more likely as the total number of attempts increases","people who generate more ideas than their peers are naturally more intelligent and creatively gifted","the quality of an idea can only be judged after it has been tested against a large number of alternatives","creative thinkers should avoid refining individual ideas and instead move on to generating new ones immediately","the pressure to produce good ideas quickly leads to the selection of conventional rather than innovative solutions"],"implication_answer":1,"irrelevant_sentence_index":4},{"id":"27ST_E_13_03","difficulty":"높음","title":"신체와 감정적 공감","sentences":["Becoming aware of our internal sensations can help us handle our own emotions.","Perhaps more surprisingly, the body's interoceptive faculty can also bring us into closer contact with other people's emotions.","That's because the brain, on its own, has no direct access to the contents of other people's minds, no way to feel what others are feeling.","Interpreting others' spoken words and facial expressions may yield only a coolly abstract sense of the emotions that stir within.","The body acts as a critical conduit, supplying the brain with the visceral information it lacks.","It does so in this way: When interacting with other people, we subtly and unconsciously mimic their facial expressions, gestures, posture, and vocal pitch.","We bring other people's feelings onboard, and the body is the bridge.","In an act similar to taking a bite off our partner's plate, or borrowing an earbud to hear the song our friend is listening to, we are sampling their emotions."],"abstract":"Empathy is not achieved through intellectual interpretation alone but through the body's unconscious mimicry of others' physical signals, which allows us to experience others' emotions as our own through interoception.","topic_options":["the body's role as an indispensable mediator of empathy through unconscious mimicry and interoceptive feedback","the limitations of verbal and facial communication in conveying the full range of human emotional experience","the neurological mechanisms that enable the brain to process and store emotional memories from social interactions","the relationship between self-awareness of internal sensations and the ability to regulate one's own emotional responses","the ways in which cultural differences in body language complicate cross-cultural emotional understanding"],"topic_answer":1,"blank_sentence_index":1,"blank_target":"bring us into closer contact with other people's emotions","blank_options":["bring us into closer contact with other people's emotions","improve our ability to suppress unwanted emotional responses","help us maintain emotional distance in stressful situations","enable us to communicate our own feelings more accurately","allow us to make more rational decisions under pressure"],"blank_answer":1,"order_given_index":0,"order_blocks":[{"label":"B","sentence_indices":[1,2]},{"label":"C","sentence_indices":[3,4,5]},{"label":"D","sentence_indices":[6,7]}],"order_options":["(B)-(C)-(A)","(A)-(C)-(B)","(C)-(A)-(B)","(B)-(A)-(C)","(A)-(B)-(C)"],"order_answer":5,"insert_sentence":"We bring other people's feelings onboard, and the body is the bridge.","insert_answer":6,"summary_template":"The body serves as the essential ________(A)________ of empathy by unconsciously mirroring others' physical signals and feeding that information back to the brain through ________(B)________, allowing us to feel what others feel.","summary_A_options":["medium","source","filter","others","empathy"],"summary_A_answer":1,"summary_B_options":["interoception","cognition","perception","effective","stable"],"summary_B_answer":1,"implication_sentence_index":7,"implication_keyword":"sampling their emotions","implication_options":["briefly and partially experiencing others' feelings through bodily resonance rather than purely intellectual understanding","consciously selecting which of another person's emotional states to respond to based on personal relevance","collecting data about others' emotional patterns in order to predict their future behavior more accurately","testing the reliability of one's emotional responses by comparing them against those of other people","absorbing the full range of another person's emotional experience through sustained close interaction"],"implication_answer":1,"irrelevant_sentence_index":4},{"id":"27ST_E_13_04","difficulty":"높음","title":"기술 확장과 인간 퇴화","sentences":["The strongest criticisms of the overextension of technology involve claims of dehumanization, and these arguments are not new.","Canadian philosopher of the electronic age, Marshall McLuhan was primarily a techno-utopian, but he was also a critical thinker, who cautioned decades ago against too much human extension into technology.","McLuhan famously claimed that every media extension of man is an amputation.","For example, once we have a car, we don't walk to the shops any more; once we have a computer hard-drive, we don't have to remember things; and now that we have personal GPS on our cell phones, no one can find their way about without it.","It is thus possible that extensions of human faculties, through techno- and bio-enhancement, will bring about arrested development in the natural evolution of higher human faculties."],"abstract":"Following McLuhan's argument that technological extension of human capacities inevitably atrophies the natural faculties it replaces, excessive reliance on technology risks stunting the development of distinctly human cognitive abilities.","topic_options":["the risk that technological enhancement of human capabilities may arrest the natural development of the faculties it replaces","the historical debate between techno-utopianism and techno-pessimism in modern philosophical thought","the specific ways in which GPS technology has diminished human spatial reasoning and navigational skill","Marshall McLuhan's broader contributions to media theory and their ongoing relevance to digital culture","the scientific evidence for cognitive decline in populations that rely heavily on digital devices"],"topic_answer":1,"blank_sentence_index":2,"blank_target":"every media extension of man is an amputation","blank_options":["every media extension of man is an amputation","technology always enhances human cognitive abilities","digital tools strengthen our connection to the natural world","modern media has made communication more meaningful","every new invention improves the quality of human life"],"blank_answer":1,"order_given_index":0,"order_blocks":[{"label":"B","sentence_indices":[1]},{"label":"C","sentence_indices":[2,3]},{"label":"D","sentence_indices":[4]}],"order_options":["(B)-(C)-(A)","(C)-(A)-(B)","(A)-(B)-(C)","(B)-(A)-(C)","(A)-(C)-(B)"],"order_answer":3,"insert_sentence":null,"insert_answer":null,"summary_template":"McLuhan's insight that technological ________(A)________ of human faculties functions as an amputation suggests that over-reliance on technology may lead to the ________(B)________ of the natural cognitive capacities it replaces.","summary_A_options":["simulation","extension","promotion","human","following"],"summary_A_answer":2,"summary_B_options":["transformation","atrophy","isolation","effective","stable"],"summary_B_answer":2,"implication_sentence_index":2,"implication_keyword":"every media extension of man is an amputation","implication_options":["each gain in technological capability is simultaneously a loss of a natural human faculty that the technology displaces","the adoption of new media physically injures users by replacing organic cognitive processes with mechanical ones","technological tools that extend human reach inevitably cause irreversible damage to the body's nervous system","the spread of digital media severs the social bonds that hold communities together over generations","media technologies remove individuals from their cultural roots by replacing tradition with artificial substitutes"],"implication_answer":1,"irrelevant_sentence_index":3},{"id":"27ST_E_14_01","difficulty":"보통","title":"경험 공유와 의미 차이","sentences":["Sharing meanings and experiences is not a simple, automatic process: whenever two or more people observe or participate in the same ongoing event they experience it from different perspectives, with different histories, with different background knowledge.","These differences are most glaring when the individuals involved include an infant or very young child and an adult, although an adult arranging an event for an infant may find it difficult to keep these differences in mind.","When giving a bath, for example, a parent whose experience with water play has been fun, whose knowledge about the source of the water and its disposition provides confidence, and whose body control ensures that the baby is safely held and not in danger, expects the infant to enjoy splashing water.","Yet the baby may make it clear that her perspective is quite different from that of the adult."],"abstract":"Even when two people participate in the same event, they do not necessarily share the same meaning, because each brings a distinct personal history, knowledge, and perspective to that experience.","topic_options":["the inevitable divergence of meaning even in shared experiences due to differences in perspective and background","the challenges adults face in accurately anticipating an infant's emotional responses to new experiences","the role of prior positive experience in shaping an individual's expectations about familiar activities","the ways in which physical safety and bodily control influence a parent's enjoyment of childcare tasks","the developmental gap between infants and adults in their capacity to derive meaning from sensory experiences"],"topic_answer":1,"blank_sentence_index":0,"blank_target":"not a simple, automatic process","blank_options":["not a simple, automatic process","a shared and intuitive experience","easily resolved through communication","consistent across cultures and ages","primarily shaped by biological factors"],"blank_answer":1,"order_given_index":0,"order_blocks":[{"label":"B","sentence_indices":[1]},{"label":"C","sentence_indices":[2,3]},{"label":"D","sentence_indices":[4]}],"order_options":["(A)-(C)-(B)","(B)-(A)-(C)","(A)-(B)-(C)","(B)-(C)-(A)","(C)-(A)-(B)"],"order_answer":3,"insert_sentence":null,"insert_answer":null,"summary_template":"Participating in the same event does not guarantee a ________(A)________ understanding, because each person's unique history and knowledge shapes how they ________(B)________ what they experience.","summary_A_options":["accurate","clear","shared","same","people"],"summary_A_answer":3,"summary_B_options":["remember","describe","interpret","effective","stable"],"summary_B_answer":3,"implication_sentence_index":3,"implication_keyword":"her perspective is quite different from that of the adult","implication_options":["the baby and the adult experience the same event in fundamentally different ways","adults always succeed in communicating their intentions clearly to infants","shared experiences naturally lead to shared meanings between people","differences in perspective always cause conflict between adults and children","infants are unable to form any meaningful understanding of their environment"],"implication_answer":1,"irrelevant_sentence_index":2},{"id":"27ST_E_14_02","difficulty":"높음","title":"과학적 공로와 경쟁","sentences":["A detailed anthropological study of daily scientific practice in the Salk Institute laboratory in La Jolla, California shows how difficult it is to assign credit and dates.","Bruno Latour describes how scientists arrived at the elucidation of TRF, a hormone that is secreted by the brain.","The final consensus formulation of TRF emerged some time between January 1968 and January 1970.","Half of the Nobel Prize in Medicine for 1977 for this discovery was shared between the Salk group and another competing group in New Orleans, but each of these two competing groups strongly felt that they deserved sole credit and that the other did not deserve even a share of the award."],"abstract":"An anthropological study of real scientific practice reveals that scientific discovery is not the orderly, logical process it appears from the outside but a messy, contested struggle from which questions of credit and priority are never cleanly resolved.","topic_options":["the disorderly and contested nature of scientific practice that contradicts its outwardly rational appearance","the methodological contributions of anthropological research to understanding how science actually functions","the role of institutional rivalry in motivating scientists to accelerate their research toward major discoveries","the difficulty of assigning Nobel Prizes fairly when multiple groups contribute to a single scientific breakthrough","the gap between the public image of science as objective and the personal ambitions that drive researchers"],"topic_answer":1,"blank_sentence_index":0,"blank_target":"how difficult it is to assign credit and dates","blank_options":["how difficult it is to assign credit and dates","how efficiently scientists collaborate on shared research goals","how clearly defined the boundaries of scientific disciplines are","how straightforward the peer review process can be","how quickly scientific knowledge is accumulated and verified"],"blank_answer":1,"order_given_index":0,"order_blocks":[],"order_options":["(B)-(A)-(C)","(A)-(B)-(C)","(A)-(C)-(B)","(C)-(A)-(B)","(B)-(C)-(A)"],"order_answer":2,"insert_sentence":null,"insert_answer":null,"summary_template":"Close observation of real scientific practice reveals that it is far more ________(A)________ than it appears, and that questions of ________(B)________ for discoveries are rarely settled without dispute.","summary_A_options":["creative","collaborative","scientific","disorderly","anthropological"],"summary_A_answer":4,"summary_B_options":["accuracy","funding","effective","credit","stable"],"summary_B_answer":4,"implication_sentence_index":2,"implication_keyword":"final consensus formulation","implication_options":["the agreed-upon scientific conclusion reached after years of contested research","the initial hypothesis proposed at the beginning of a scientific investigation","the official government policy on the regulation of medical research","the personal opinion of the lead researcher published in an academic journal","the preliminary finding presented before any experimental testing has occurred"],"implication_answer":1,"irrelevant_sentence_index":3},{"id":"27ST_E_14_03","difficulty":"보통","title":"음악 지휘의 비가시성","sentences":["The idea of music direction, in the sense of someone shaping and leading a musical performance, goes back to the beginnings of music.","Even the gamelans of ancient Indonesia had leaders who would signal to the group changes of meter and tempo, beginnings and endings, and transitions from piece to piece.","Yet listening audiences are rarely aware of any musical leadership, and for good aesthetic reason.","An audience is better off, for the most part, taking in the whole of a stage work rather than being party to the techniques that go into realizing it.","This is not to say that when an orchestra plays alone the audience members' eyes are not fixed on the conductor for the majority of the time; they probably are.","When music is accompanying something happening on stage, however, all eyes turn to the stage, and so do everyone's ears, too."],"abstract":"Although musical leadership is essential to performance, effective direction works best when it remains invisible to the audience, whose experience is enriched by engaging with the whole rather than the technical means behind it.","topic_options":["the aesthetic value of invisible musical leadership in allowing audiences to engage fully with the performance as a whole","the historical origins of musical direction and its continued presence across diverse cultural traditions","the contrast between the conductor's visible role in orchestral concerts and their hidden role in stage performances","the techniques that experienced conductors use to signal changes in tempo and meter without distracting the audience","the reasons why modern audiences have become less aware of musical leadership than audiences in earlier periods"],"topic_answer":1,"blank_sentence_index":4,"blank_target":"the audience members' eyes are not fixed on the conductor for the majority of the time","blank_options":["the audience members' eyes are not fixed on the conductor for the majority of the time","the musicians are entirely dependent on the conductor for timing","the music flows without any visible sign of coordination","the conductor's role is more important than the performers","listeners pay close attention to every gesture the conductor makes"],"blank_answer":1,"order_given_index":0,"order_blocks":[{"label":"B","sentence_indices":[1,2]},{"label":"C","sentence_indices":[3]},{"label":"D","sentence_indices":[4,5]}],"order_options":["(B)-(A)-(C)","(B)-(C)-(A)","(A)-(C)-(B)","(A)-(B)-(C)","(C)-(A)-(B)"],"order_answer":4,"insert_sentence":"An audience is better off, for the most part, taking in the whole of a stage work rather than being party to the techniques that go into realizing it.","insert_answer":3,"summary_template":"Effective musical direction is most valuable when it remains ________(A)________ to the audience, allowing them to experience the performance as a unified whole rather than as a collection of ________(B)________ techniques.","summary_A_options":["consistent","minimal","invisible","although","musical"],"summary_A_answer":3,"summary_B_options":["competing","rehearsed","technical","effective","stable"],"summary_B_answer":3,"implication_sentence_index":3,"implication_keyword":"being party to the techniques that go into realizing it","implication_options":["being made consciously aware of the craft and method behind the performance rather than simply experiencing its effect","participating actively in the production process alongside the performers and technical staff","understanding the theoretical principles of music well enough to evaluate the quality of the performance","sharing responsibility with the performers for the success or failure of the overall production","gaining insider knowledge about how musical decisions are made during rehearsal and preparation"],"implication_answer":1,"irrelevant_sentence_index":5},{"id":"27ST_E_14_04","difficulty":"보통","title":"배경지식과 독해력","sentences":["The importance of what a reader brings to the page is highlighted in a study discussed by Hirsch in The Knowledge Deficit.","This study consisted of two groups of students who were asked to read a passage about baseball.","The first group was made up of strong readers who knew little about baseball.","The second group was composed of struggling readers who were knowledgeable about baseball.","After reading the passage, students in each group had their comprehension tested.","Guess which group scored higher? The struggling readers.","Though the second group of readers were not strong readers, their prior knowledge enabled them to outscore readers with far better abilities.","Prior knowledge, or, in the case of the good readers, the lack of prior knowledge, was the x-factor."],"abstract":"A study comparing strong readers with poor readers on a topic-specific passage demonstrates that prior knowledge of the subject matter can outweigh technical reading ability in determining reading comprehension.","topic_options":["the decisive role of topic-specific prior knowledge in reading comprehension, surpassing technical reading skill","the limitations of conventional reading instruction that focuses on decoding skills rather than content knowledge","the reasons why baseball is a particularly effective topic for testing the relationship between knowledge and reading","the methods researchers use to isolate the effects of background knowledge from general reading ability","the implications of Hirsch's research for designing reading curricula that address knowledge deficits in students"],"topic_answer":1,"blank_sentence_index":7,"blank_target":"the x-factor","blank_options":["the x-factor","a minor advantage","a fixed limitation","an irrelevant variable","a temporary obstacle"],"blank_answer":1,"order_given_index":0,"order_blocks":[{"label":"B","sentence_indices":[1,2]},{"label":"C","sentence_indices":[3,4,5]},{"label":"D","sentence_indices":[6,7]}],"order_options":["(C)-(A)-(B)","(B)-(C)-(A)","(A)-(B)-(C)","(B)-(A)-(C)","(A)-(C)-(B)"],"order_answer":3,"insert_sentence":"Though the second group of readers were not strong readers, their prior knowledge enabled them to outscore readers with far better abilities.","insert_answer":6,"summary_template":"A study on baseball reading comprehension reveals that ________(A)________ knowledge of a topic can compensate for weaker reading skills, making it a more ________(B)________ factor in comprehension than technical reading ability alone.","summary_A_options":["general","prior","cultural","readers","reading"],"summary_A_answer":2,"summary_B_options":["reliable","decisive","consistent","effective","stable"],"summary_B_answer":2,"implication_sentence_index":7,"implication_keyword":"the x-factor","implication_options":["the hidden but decisive variable that explains an outcome that technical skill alone cannot account for","an unknown quantity that researchers were unable to measure despite its obvious influence on the results","a controversial element that some researchers believe is relevant while others dismiss it as insignificant","a factor unique to this particular study that cannot be generalized to other reading comprehension contexts","an unpredictable force that occasionally determines outcomes in ways that defy systematic explanation"],"implication_answer":1,"irrelevant_sentence_index":5},{"id":"27ST_E_15_01","difficulty":"보통","title":"운동과 감정 활용","sentences":["The use of emotion may be important in exercise, particularly among exercise instructors.","It has been established that exercise enjoyment is associated with increased exercise adherence.","An instructor might aim to foster enjoyment in his participants as a means of increasing their program adherence.","An instructor also might use emotion to elicit greater effort from her students.","Conversely, a yoga instructor could use positive emotions or emotion-related states such as compassion to get her students in the proper mindset for their practice.","Evidently, there are a number of ways emotions could be used to enhance performance in sport and exercise."],"abstract":"Exercise instructors can strategically harness a range of emotions — both positive and negative — to increase participants' adherence to programs and improve their physical performance.","topic_options":["the strategic use of diverse emotional states by exercise instructors to improve adherence and performance","the physiological connection between emotional arousal and the intensity of physical effort during exercise","the specific benefits of fostering enjoyment in exercise classes for long-term participant retention","the contrast between the emotional demands of high-intensity exercise and those of mindfulness-based practices","the professional responsibilities of exercise instructors in managing the emotional well-being of their students"],"topic_answer":1,"blank_sentence_index":1,"blank_target":"associated with increased exercise adherence","blank_options":["associated with increased exercise adherence","linked to greater physical strength and endurance","considered irrelevant to long-term fitness outcomes","found to reduce the effectiveness of training programs","shown to interfere with proper form and technique"],"blank_answer":1,"order_given_index":0,"order_blocks":[{"label":"B","sentence_indices":[1,2]},{"label":"C","sentence_indices":[3]},{"label":"D","sentence_indices":[4,5]}],"order_options":["(A)-(B)-(C)","(B)-(C)-(A)","(A)-(C)-(B)","(B)-(A)-(C)","(C)-(A)-(B)"],"order_answer":1,"insert_sentence":"Conversely, a yoga instructor could use positive emotions or emotion-related states such as compassion to get her students in the proper mindset for their practice.","insert_answer":4,"summary_template":"Exercise instructors can deliberately ________(A)________ a variety of emotions to boost both participant ________(B)________ and the quality of physical effort during training.","summary_A_options":["harness","suppress","observe","exercise","instructors"],"summary_A_answer":1,"summary_B_options":["adherence","awareness","effective","stable","confidence"],"summary_B_answer":1,"implication_sentence_index":4,"implication_keyword":"proper mindset for their practice","implication_options":["the optimal mental and emotional state needed to engage in yoga effectively","the physical posture required to perform yoga exercises without injury","the strict dietary rules that yoga students must follow before class","the formal certification that qualifies a student to teach yoga professionally","the set of technical skills needed to advance to more difficult yoga poses"],"implication_answer":1,"irrelevant_sentence_index":4},{"id":"27ST_E_15_02","difficulty":"보통","title":"측정 기기의 정밀도","sentences":["The most fundamental rule regarding the use of any measuring device is that the device should always be read to its optimum capability with regard to precision.","Precision is reflected in the number of digits in a measurement; the more digits this measurement has, the more precise it is.","If it is possible to obtain the first digit to the right of the decimal point from a device, then that digit should be recorded; if it is possible to obtain the second digit to the right of a decimal point, then that digit should be recorded, and so on.","Thus, a laboratory worker should endeavor to obtain the most digits possible from whatever device is being used whether it is digital or nondigital."],"abstract":"The fundamental principle of using measuring devices is to always record measurements to the maximum precision the instrument allows, extracting as many significant digits as possible.","topic_options":["the principle of maximizing measurement precision by recording the greatest number of digits a device can yield","the differences in precision between digital and nondigital measuring devices used in laboratory settings","the role of decimal notation in representing the degree of accuracy achieved in scientific measurements","the standards that laboratory workers must follow when selecting the most appropriate measuring device for a task","the relationship between the number of significant digits in a measurement and the reliability of experimental results"],"topic_answer":1,"blank_sentence_index":0,"blank_target":"to its optimum capability with regard to precision","blank_options":["to its optimum capability with regard to precision","in accordance with the manufacturer's recommended settings","using the simplest method available to the technician","only when absolute accuracy is required for safety reasons","after ensuring the device has been properly calibrated"],"blank_answer":1,"order_given_index":0,"order_blocks":[],"order_options":["(A)-(B)-(C)","(C)-(A)-(B)","(A)-(C)-(B)","(B)-(A)-(C)","(B)-(C)-(A)"],"order_answer":1,"insert_sentence":null,"insert_answer":null,"summary_template":"The core rule of measurement practice is to always capture the ________(A)________ number of digits a device can produce, since more digits directly reflect greater ________(B)________ in the recorded measurement.","summary_A_options":["maximum","average","minimum","fundamental","principle"],"summary_A_answer":1,"summary_B_options":["precision","accuracy","reliability","effective","stable"],"summary_B_answer":1,"implication_sentence_index":1,"implication_keyword":"the more digits this measurement has, the more precise it is","implication_options":["a greater number of recorded digits indicates that finer distinctions between values have been captured","measurements with more digits are more likely to be correct because they have been verified more thoroughly","longer numerical representations are easier for laboratory workers to interpret and compare across experiments","adding more digits to a measurement increases its credibility when submitted for peer review","precision increases automatically as the number of decimal places in a recorded value grows"],"implication_answer":1,"irrelevant_sentence_index":3},{"id":"27ST_E_15_03","difficulty":"높음","title":"수학의 추상화 원리","sentences":["The standard school mathematics curriculum doesn't stress enough that mathematics is all about abstraction.","Mathematicians study specific objects but, usually, they aim to cluster them together and study them all at the same time.","This saves huge amounts of time and effort because they must prove properties only once, for the whole class of objects, instead of studying each object individually.","Often, when mathematicians want to prove that an important object behaves in a particular way, they prove instead that it belongs to a class already known to have this property.","We reason similarly in everyday life: since all fruits have seeds, and an apple is a fruit, then an apple must have seeds."],"abstract":"The power of mathematical abstraction lies in its ability to establish properties for entire classes of objects at once, eliminating the need to examine each object individually and guaranteeing results even for objects not yet encountered.","topic_options":["the efficiency and generative power of mathematical abstraction in establishing properties across entire classes of objects","the failure of school mathematics education to convey the true nature and purpose of abstract mathematical thinking","the role of class membership in allowing mathematicians to prove properties without examining individual objects","the parallels between abstract mathematical reasoning and the logical inferences people make in everyday situations","the advantages of studying mathematics through specific examples before progressing to more abstract generalizations"],"topic_answer":1,"blank_sentence_index":0,"blank_target":"all about abstraction","blank_options":["all about abstraction","primarily a set of memorized rules and procedures","best learned through repetitive calculation and drills","essentially a tool for solving practical engineering problems","mainly concerned with measuring and counting physical quantities"],"blank_answer":1,"order_given_index":0,"order_blocks":[{"label":"B","sentence_indices":[1]},{"label":"C","sentence_indices":[2]},{"label":"D","sentence_indices":[3,4]}],"order_options":["(B)-(A)-(C)","(A)-(B)-(C)","(B)-(C)-(A)","(A)-(C)-(B)","(C)-(A)-(B)"],"order_answer":2,"insert_sentence":null,"insert_answer":null,"summary_template":"Mathematical abstraction allows properties to be established for ________(A)________ classes of objects simultaneously, making it far more efficient than studying individual cases and ensuring results apply even to ________(B)________ objects.","summary_A_options":["familiar","specific","objects","entire","power"],"summary_A_answer":4,"summary_B_options":["abstract","complex","effective","undefined","stable"],"summary_B_answer":4,"implication_sentence_index":3,"implication_keyword":"prove instead that it belongs to a class already known to have this property","implication_options":["demonstrate that the object shares membership in a category whose defining characteristics have already been established","show that the object was incorrectly classified and should be reassigned to a different mathematical category","confirm that the object's behavior matches what was predicted by a previously published mathematical theorem","establish that the object can be transformed into a simpler form that is easier to analyze directly","verify that the object satisfies the conditions required to apply a specific computational formula"],"implication_answer":1,"irrelevant_sentence_index":3},{"id":"27ST_E_15_04","difficulty":"높음","title":"공개적 플라시보 효과","sentences":["Because belief is so crucial in the placebo effect, it would seem that deception is necessary in order to trigger a patient's trust in the actual drug he might be taking.","But Ted Kaptchuk, a leading placebo researcher at Harvard, is investigating the possibility of doing away with the element of deception.","In one trial with irritable bowel syndrome, it was found that roughly 59 percent of those on an open placebo treatment reported improvements, as compared with 35 percent of the control group that received no treatment.","The results may seem modest, but they make the point that giving a placebo isn't the same as doing nothing."],"abstract":"Research by Ted Kaptchuk suggests that the placebo effect can operate even without deception, as openly administered placebos still produce meaningful therapeutic outcomes when patients are informed about their potential effectiveness.","topic_options":["the surprising finding that openly administered placebos can produce real therapeutic effects without requiring patient deception","the ethical debate surrounding the use of deception in placebo-controlled clinical trials","the neurological mechanisms through which belief and expectation generate measurable changes in patient outcomes","the implications of open-label placebo research for reforming the standards of informed consent in medicine","the specific conditions under which placebo effects are strongest and most reliably replicated across patient populations"],"topic_answer":1,"blank_sentence_index":0,"blank_target":"deception is necessary in order to trigger a patient's trust","blank_options":["deception is necessary in order to trigger a patient's trust","the strength of a placebo depends on its physical appearance","patients must be kept completely unaware of their treatment","open communication between doctor and patient reduces effectiveness","the placebo effect only works for psychological conditions"],"blank_answer":1,"order_given_index":0,"order_blocks":[],"order_options":["(B)-(C)-(A)","(C)-(A)-(B)","(B)-(A)-(C)","(A)-(B)-(C)","(A)-(C)-(B)"],"order_answer":4,"insert_sentence":null,"insert_answer":null,"summary_template":"Contrary to the assumption that ________(A)________ is essential to the placebo effect, research shows that openly administered placebos still produce ________(B)________ improvements in patient outcomes.","summary_A_options":["deception","belief","suggestion","research","kaptchuk"],"summary_A_answer":1,"summary_B_options":["measurable","consistent","dramatic","effective","stable"],"summary_B_answer":1,"implication_sentence_index":3,"implication_keyword":"giving a placebo isn't the same as doing nothing","implication_options":["administering a placebo produces a genuine therapeutic effect that cannot be dismissed as mere absence of treatment","prescribing a placebo requires the same level of medical expertise as prescribing an active pharmaceutical drug","patients who receive placebos experience the same degree of recovery as those who receive standard treatments","the act of giving any treatment, regardless of its active ingredients, is sufficient to produce positive health outcomes","doctors who prescribe placebos are fulfilling their professional obligation to offer patients some form of care"],"implication_answer":1,"irrelevant_sentence_index":3},{"id":"27ST_E_16_01","difficulty":"보통","title":"온라인 글쓰기의 역피라미드","sentences":["In academia, you are taught to write up your results thus: I came up with a hypothesis, then I did this experiment, and then I did another experiment, then I tested my ideas some more, and so on until ta-da! I proved this.","If you wrote this way online, very few of your readers would make it to your dramatic conclusion, no matter how exciting or groundbreaking it was.","Online, we don't have the patience to wait for your big reveal at the end.","Instead, you need to tell us up front: I proved this! And here's how I know it...","Your readership may still dwindle and trail off over the course of your writing, but at least the vast majority know what it is you've achieved from the very beginning.","If you grab their attention early, you can more likely convince more readers to stay for the whole story."],"abstract":"Online writing demands the opposite structure of academic writing: the conclusion must come first, followed by supporting evidence, because digital readers lack the patience to follow a slow build toward a reveal.","topic_options":["the necessity of presenting conclusions first in online writing to retain readers who lack patience for gradual reveals","the differences in writing conventions between academic journals and popular science communication","the techniques journalists use to craft compelling opening lines that attract and hold readers' attention","the reasons why online audiences are less capable of sustained reading than academic readers","the role of structural clarity in determining whether a piece of writing achieves its intended persuasive effect"],"topic_answer":1,"blank_sentence_index":1,"blank_target":"very few of your readers would make it to your dramatic conclusion","blank_options":["very few of your readers would make it to your dramatic conclusion","most readers would appreciate the logical structure of your argument","your audience would be impressed by your thorough methodology","readers would find the detailed experimental process engaging","the majority would share your work with their professional networks"],"blank_answer":1,"order_given_index":0,"order_blocks":[{"label":"B","sentence_indices":[1,2]},{"label":"C","sentence_indices":[3,4]},{"label":"D","sentence_indices":[5]}],"order_options":["(B)-(A)-(C)","(A)-(B)-(C)","(B)-(C)-(A)","(C)-(A)-(B)","(A)-(C)-(B)"],"order_answer":2,"insert_sentence":"If you grab their attention early, you can more likely convince more readers to stay for the whole story.","insert_answer":5,"summary_template":"Unlike academic writing, effective online writing requires placing the ________(A)________ at the beginning and using the opening line as a ________(B)________ to prevent readers from abandoning the text.","summary_A_options":["conclusion","evidence","hypothesis","writing","online"],"summary_A_answer":1,"summary_B_options":["hook","summary","effective","stable","transition"],"summary_B_answer":1,"implication_sentence_index":0,"implication_keyword":"ta-da! I proved this","implication_options":["the dramatic final revelation that academic writing builds toward but that online readers will never wait to reach","the moment of triumph that motivates researchers to endure the long and uncertain process of experimentation","the conclusive statement that distinguishes genuine scientific proof from preliminary or speculative findings","the climactic announcement that marks the transition from methodology to results in a research paper","the surprise ending that makes academic writing entertaining and memorable for non-specialist audiences"],"implication_answer":1,"irrelevant_sentence_index":5},{"id":"27ST_E_16_02","difficulty":"높음","title":"뇌의 대리적 기능","sentences":["The human perceptual system is designed to recognize objects under changing illuminations, situations, and contexts.","It is extraordinarily adapted to a constantly changing world.","To deal with this uncertainty, the brain uses not one, but multiple routes.","This immense flexibility of the brain to rely on changing cues, according to whatever is available, is known as vicarious functioning.","It can be found in most biological systems.","For instance, migrating birds fly thousands of miles and may rely on the stars to navigate.","But if it's a cloudy day, they may instead rely on landmarks or their magnetic sense.","Similarly, the brain can recognize a face by the shape of the eyes, nose, and mouth.","In extreme cases, only a few lines are sufficient, as when we recognize the face of a celebrity in caricatures made with just a few pencil strokes.","Face recognition also functions even when parts of a face are covered and internal features such as eyes are hardly visible.","In this case, the brain relies on external features such as hair and head shape."],"abstract":"The brain's perceptual system achieves remarkable adaptability by switching flexibly between multiple available cues when any single route to recognition is blocked, a capacity known as vicarious functioning.","topic_options":["the brain's adaptive use of alternative perceptual cues when primary routes to recognition are unavailable","the evolutionary advantages of flexible sensory processing in animals living in unpredictable environments","the specific neural pathways involved in facial recognition under varying lighting and contextual conditions","the parallels between human perceptual flexibility and navigational strategies observed in migratory birds","the role of external facial features in compensating for the brain's inability to process partially obscured faces"],"topic_answer":1,"blank_sentence_index":3,"blank_target":"vicarious functioning","blank_options":["vicarious functioning","selective perception","sensory deprivation","cognitive overload","neural specialization"],"blank_answer":1,"order_given_index":0,"order_blocks":[{"label":"B","sentence_indices":[1,2]},{"label":"C","sentence_indices":[3,4,5,6]},{"label":"D","sentence_indices":[7,8,9,10]}],"order_options":["(C)-(A)-(B)","(B)-(C)-(A)","(B)-(A)-(C)","(A)-(C)-(B)","(A)-(B)-(C)"],"order_answer":5,"insert_sentence":"This immense flexibility of the brain to rely on changing cues, according to whatever is available, is known as vicarious functioning.","insert_answer":3,"summary_template":"The brain's ________(A)________ functioning allows it to switch between available perceptual cues when primary routes are blocked, enabling reliable recognition across a wide range of ________(B)________ conditions.","summary_A_options":["predictive","vicarious","selective","brain","perceptual"],"summary_A_answer":2,"summary_B_options":["extreme","changing","familiar","effective","stable"],"summary_B_answer":2,"implication_sentence_index":8,"implication_keyword":"only a few lines are sufficient","implication_options":["minimal visual information can trigger full recognition when the brain draws on stored patterns and expectations","simplified drawings are easier for the brain to process than realistic images because they reduce visual noise","the brain processes caricatures faster than photographs because they emphasize the most distinctive features","artists who use few lines are more skilled at capturing likeness than those who rely on detailed rendering","recognition of famous faces requires less cognitive effort than recognition of unfamiliar individuals"],"implication_answer":1,"irrelevant_sentence_index":6},{"id":"27ST_E_16_03","difficulty":"보통","title":"비르 타윌의 역설","sentences":["Bir Tawil is a strange place.","In January 1899, administrators of the British Empire decided to finalize a border between the countries of Egypt and Sudan.","In colonial fashion, they decided to use the conveniently straight line of the twenty-second parallel of latitude.","Unsurprisingly, this new international border arbitrarily tore through local tribes and communities, and in 1902, the British drew a new line to reflect tribal territories.","The combination of these two intersecting lines brought about the creation of two new areas: the large, inhabitable coastal area called the Hala'ib Triangle and an empty, landlocked patch of desert, which is Bir Tawil.","The strange result of this long-standing conflict is that, to this day, both countries refuse to claim Bir Tawil, an area of land roughly the size of London, as it would mean giving up a greater prize.","This makes Bir Tawil the largest — perhaps the only — piece of land that no country wants."],"abstract":"Bir Tawil remains unclaimed by any nation because each of the two countries that could claim it can only do so by surrendering its claim to the far more valuable Hala'ib Triangle, creating a unique geopolitical paradox.","topic_options":["the geopolitical paradox by which competing territorial claims over a valuable area leave an adjacent land permanently unclaimed","the historical consequences of the British Empire's arbitrary use of geometric lines to draw colonial borders","the reasons why uninhabited desert regions are generally less strategically important than coastal territories","the long-standing diplomatic dispute between Egypt and Sudan over the legal validity of competing border agreements","the environmental characteristics that make Bir Tawil inhospitable and therefore unattractive to both neighboring nations"],"topic_answer":1,"blank_sentence_index":5,"blank_target":"both countries refuse to claim Bir Tawil","blank_options":["both countries refuse to claim Bir Tawil","both nations have signed a formal treaty to resolve the dispute","the United Nations has been asked to administer the territory","the land has attracted international investment and development","local residents have established an independent governing authority"],"blank_answer":1,"order_given_index":0,"order_blocks":[{"label":"B","sentence_indices":[1,2]},{"label":"C","sentence_indices":[3,4]},{"label":"D","sentence_indices":[5,6]}],"order_options":["(C)-(A)-(B)","(A)-(C)-(B)","(A)-(B)-(C)","(B)-(C)-(A)","(B)-(A)-(C)"],"order_answer":3,"insert_sentence":"The strange result of this long-standing conflict is that, to this day, both countries refuse to claim Bir Tawil, an area of land roughly the size of London, as it would mean giving up a greater prize.","insert_answer":5,"summary_template":"Because claiming Bir Tawil would require each country to ________(A)________ its right to the more valuable Hala'ib Triangle, both nations strategically ________(B)________ the territory, leaving it without any sovereign owner.","summary_A_options":["defend","negotiate","surrender","claim","tawil"],"summary_A_answer":3,"summary_B_options":["contest","ignore","renounce","effective","stable"],"summary_B_answer":3,"implication_sentence_index":6,"implication_keyword":"the largest — perhaps the only — piece of land that no country wants","implication_options":["a territory uniquely rendered worthless not by its inherent qualities but by the strategic logic of the competing claims surrounding it","an uninhabitable region that has been formally excluded from the international system of sovereign states","a desert area so remote and resource-poor that no government has ever considered it worth the cost of administration","a disputed zone that international law has been unable to assign to any nation due to the complexity of the competing claims","a piece of land whose ownership has been deliberately obscured by both countries to avoid triggering a military conflict"],"implication_answer":1,"irrelevant_sentence_index":2},{"id":"27ST_E_16_04","difficulty":"높음","title":"준거집단의 자기평가 효과","sentences":["An in-group can become a reference group, a group that is used as the frame of reference for evaluating one's own behavior.","Members of a volunteer organization, for example, may evaluate themselves by the standards of the group and feel proud about their contribution to a community service project.","This positive self-evaluation reflects the normative effect of a reference group whose members share the same view of themselves.","If other members of your reference group (say, your parents) have high self-esteem, you, too, are likely to share that norm and have high self-esteem.","However, reference groups can also have comparison effects and associative effects on self-appraisals.","If most of your classmates shine in academic achievement, you are likely to compare yourself with them.","As a result, you may have a negative self-evaluation, feeling that your academic performance is not up to par.","Being associated with the brilliant group, though, makes you feel proud of yourself, basking in reflected glory."],"abstract":"Reference groups shape self-evaluation through three distinct mechanisms — normative, comparative, and associative effects — each of which can produce different and sometimes contradictory outcomes for an individual's self-appraisal.","topic_options":["the three distinct ways reference groups influence self-evaluation through normative, comparative, and associative effects","the psychological tendency of individuals to adopt the self-esteem norms of the groups they identify with most closely","the negative impact of academic competition on students' self-perception in high-achieving peer environments","the role of voluntary organizations in providing members with a positive and stable sense of personal identity","the contrast between the motivating effects of upward social comparison and the comfort of downward comparison"],"topic_answer":1,"blank_sentence_index":7,"blank_target":"basking in reflected glory","blank_options":["basking in reflected glory","feeling pressured to maintain their high standards","experiencing anxiety about your own academic performance","distancing yourself from the group to protect your self-esteem","working harder to close the gap between you and your peers"],"blank_answer":1,"order_given_index":0,"order_blocks":[{"label":"B","sentence_indices":[1,2]},{"label":"C","sentence_indices":[3,4]},{"label":"D","sentence_indices":[5,6,7]}],"order_options":["(C)-(A)-(B)","(B)-(C)-(A)","(A)-(C)-(B)","(B)-(A)-(C)","(A)-(B)-(C)"],"order_answer":5,"insert_sentence":"However, reference groups can also have comparison effects and associative effects on self-appraisals.","insert_answer":4,"summary_template":"Reference groups affect self-evaluation through ________(A)________ effects, where group norms are imitated, ________(B)________ effects, where one feels inadequate beside high achievers, and associative effects, where group membership generates pride.","summary_A_options":["normative","social","psychological","self","reference"],"summary_A_answer":1,"summary_B_options":["comparison","negative","competitive","effective","stable"],"summary_B_answer":1,"implication_sentence_index":7,"implication_keyword":"basking in reflected glory","implication_options":["deriving personal pride from one's association with a high-status group rather than from one's own individual achievements","enjoying the recognition that comes from having personally contributed to a group's celebrated accomplishments","feeling satisfied with one's performance by comparing it favorably to the lower achievements of others","experiencing a sense of superiority by remaining passively connected to a group without actively contributing","gaining confidence from the positive feedback that group members offer each other in supportive communities"],"implication_answer":1,"irrelevant_sentence_index":4},{"id":"27ST_E_16_05","difficulty":"높음","title":"음악에서 근접성 그룹화","sentences":["In music, proximity may refer to elements' being close together in pitch, time, or space.","For example, notes that are similar in pitch may be grouped together.","Notes are also grouped together if they are played together in time or if they come from the same instrument or section of a larger musical group.","To get a sense of the idea of proximity, imagine a person playing a piano.","Typically, the right hand plays notes that are higher in pitch than the left hand.","Even though all of the notes are played in close spatial proximity and at approximately the same time, we hear the notes from the right hand emerging as melody because they are grouped together with respect to pitch.","Similarly, in some of Bach's famous solo music for violin, the violinist essentially creates two streams of music by simultaneously playing both high and lower notes.","Perceptually, we group the high notes together and group the low notes together, so we hear it as polyphonic or as two lines of music."],"abstract":"In music perception, proximity in pitch, time, or space causes listeners to group sounds together into distinct streams, enabling the auditory system to distinguish separate melodic lines even when they are physically interwoven.","topic_options":["the perceptual principle of proximity by which the auditory system groups musical sounds into distinct melodic streams","the technical differences between melody and accompaniment in keyboard and string music","the role of spatial separation between instruments in helping listeners identify individual voices in ensemble music","the ways in which Bach's compositional techniques challenge the conventional boundaries of solo instrument performance","the relationship between physical proximity of notes on a musical instrument and their perceptual grouping by listeners"],"topic_answer":1,"blank_sentence_index":0,"blank_target":"close together in pitch, time, or space","blank_options":["close together in pitch, time, or space","repeated in identical patterns throughout a composition","produced by the same instrument in an ensemble","played at the same volume and dynamic level","written in the same key and rhythmic pattern"],"blank_answer":1,"order_given_index":0,"order_blocks":[{"label":"B","sentence_indices":[1,2]},{"label":"C","sentence_indices":[3,4]},{"label":"D","sentence_indices":[5,6,7]}],"order_options":["(B)-(C)-(A)","(A)-(B)-(C)","(B)-(A)-(C)","(A)-(C)-(B)","(C)-(A)-(B)"],"order_answer":2,"insert_sentence":"Even though all of the notes are played in close spatial proximity and at approximately the same time, we hear the notes from the right hand emerging as melody because they are grouped together with respect to pitch.","insert_answer":5,"summary_template":"Musical ________(A)________ in pitch, time, or space leads the auditory system to automatically bundle sounds into distinct perceptual ________(B)________, enabling listeners to perceive multiple simultaneous lines of music.","summary_A_options":["similarity","contrast","proximity","music","perception"],"summary_A_answer":3,"summary_B_options":["layers","patterns","streams","effective","stable"],"summary_B_answer":3,"implication_sentence_index":7,"implication_keyword":"polyphonic or as two lines of music","implication_options":["perceptually distinct voices that the auditory system separates and tracks independently despite emerging from a single source","two separate instruments performing simultaneously to create the illusion of a single unified musical texture","a compositional technique in which two melodies of equal importance are woven together throughout a piece","two streams of sound that alternate in dominance depending on the listener's level of musical training","a form of musical complexity that can only be fully appreciated by listeners with advanced theoretical knowledge"],"implication_answer":1,"irrelevant_sentence_index":6},{"id":"27ST_E_16_06","difficulty":"높음","title":"공공재의 시장 과소평가","sentences":["Public goods are undervalued in markets, which exist for private goods but rarely for public goods.","For example, aquatic habitats such as wetlands provide diverse benefits that are often public goods, including breeding or refuge for unique species, recreation, hunting and tourism, or purification of water supplies.","These benefits are enjoyed simultaneously by many people and are provided to them for free by the natural functioning of the wetlands.","But the actual value of these services is not zero.","Because many people benefit from these services, their value is the total additional benefits of all individuals who enjoy provision of these services by wetlands.","This value could be huge, even though there is no apparent market price for these wetland services.","This gap between the (zero) price for wetland services and their actual value to all beneficiaries indicates how much these public goods are undervalued in markets."],"abstract":"Public goods like wetland services are systematically undervalued in markets because the absence of a price mechanism obscures their true collective value, which is the sum of all individual benefits derived from them.","topic_options":["the systematic undervaluation of public goods in markets due to the absence of a price that reflects their true collective benefit","the ecological importance of wetland habitats in providing essential services to both wildlife and human communities","the reasons why governments must intervene in markets to ensure that public goods are adequately funded and maintained","the distinction between the market price of natural resources and the economic value of the ecosystem services they provide","the challenge of measuring the total social benefit of public goods when that benefit is distributed across many individuals"],"topic_answer":1,"blank_sentence_index":0,"blank_target":"undervalued in markets, which exist for private goods but rarely for public goods","blank_options":["undervalued in markets, which exist for private goods but rarely for public goods","protected effectively by government regulations and environmental laws","overestimated by developers who fail to account for ecological costs","accurately priced through competitive bidding and market mechanisms","recognized as national assets and included in economic statistics"],"blank_answer":1,"order_given_index":0,"order_blocks":[{"label":"B","sentence_indices":[1,2]},{"label":"C","sentence_indices":[3]},{"label":"D","sentence_indices":[4,5,6]}],"order_options":["(B)-(A)-(C)","(C)-(A)-(B)","(A)-(C)-(B)","(B)-(C)-(A)","(A)-(B)-(C)"],"order_answer":5,"insert_sentence":"But the actual value of these services is not zero.","insert_answer":3,"summary_template":"Because public goods like wetland services are provided ________(A)________ and lack a market price, their true value — the ________(B)________ of all individual benefits — is systematically ignored by market mechanisms.","summary_A_options":["collectively","freely","naturally","public","goods"],"summary_A_answer":2,"summary_B_options":["estimate","sum","average","effective","stable"],"summary_B_answer":2,"implication_sentence_index":6,"implication_keyword":"This gap between the (zero) price for wetland services and their actual value to all beneficiaries indicates how much these public goods are undervalued in markets.","implication_options":["the failure of market pricing to capture the genuine worth of goods that benefit many people simultaneously at no charge","the difference between the cost of maintaining wetlands and the revenue generated by their commercial exploitation","the discrepancy between what governments pay to protect wetlands and what environmental scientists say they are worth","the distance between public awareness of wetland value and political willingness to fund their conservation","the contrast between the financial returns from wetland tourism and the broader ecological services they provide"],"implication_answer":1,"irrelevant_sentence_index":5},{"id":"27ST_E_17_01","difficulty":"보통","title":"심층 작업과 얕은 작업","sentences":["Deep work is when you perform an activity with deep concentration that pushes your cognitive capabilities, and by doing so create new value and improve your skills.","These efforts are hard to replicate; and to be able to do deep work, we need a distraction-free environment.","For many people though, we spend far too much time on the other end of the scale, doing what is referred to as shallow work.","This style of working is not cognitively demanding but is rather an execution of logical-type tasks that rarely create new value.","We often perform these tasks while we are distracted.","The problem with too much shallow work is that we feel busy, maybe even stressed, but we rarely see any output reflecting our experienced effort."],"abstract":"While deep work demands full concentration and generates genuine value, excessive reliance on shallow work creates the illusion of productivity without producing meaningful output.","topic_options":["the contrast between deep and shallow work and the danger of mistaking the busyness of shallow tasks for genuine productivity","the practical strategies individuals can use to create the distraction-free conditions required for deep cognitive work","the types of professional tasks that qualify as deep work and those that fall into the category of shallow work","the relationship between cognitive demand and the degree of personal satisfaction derived from completing a task","the role of routine work in maintaining organizational function while deeper creative work is being undertaken"],"topic_answer":1,"blank_sentence_index":0,"blank_target":"create new value and improve your skills","blank_options":["create new value and improve your skills","complete assigned tasks within the given deadline","satisfy the expectations of your supervisor or employer","maintain a consistent level of output throughout the day","demonstrate your productivity to colleagues and managers"],"blank_answer":1,"order_given_index":0,"order_blocks":[{"label":"B","sentence_indices":[1,2]},{"label":"C","sentence_indices":[3,4]},{"label":"D","sentence_indices":[5]}],"order_options":["(A)-(B)-(C)","(B)-(C)-(A)","(A)-(C)-(B)","(B)-(A)-(C)","(C)-(A)-(B)"],"order_answer":1,"insert_sentence":"The problem with too much shallow work is that we feel busy, maybe even stressed, but we rarely see any output reflecting our experienced effort.","insert_answer":5,"summary_template":"Deep work creates genuine ________(A)________ through focused cognitive effort, while excessive shallow work generates only the appearance of productivity without producing ________(B)________ results.","summary_A_options":["value","output","satisfaction","work","while"],"summary_A_answer":1,"summary_B_options":["meaningful","consistent","measurable","effective","stable"],"summary_B_answer":1,"implication_sentence_index":0,"implication_keyword":"pushes your cognitive capabilities","implication_options":["demands a level of mental engagement that stretches beyond routine thinking and drives the development of new skills","requires individuals to work at a pace that exceeds their normal capacity and risks causing mental fatigue","forces the brain to abandon familiar strategies and adopt entirely new approaches to familiar problems","challenges people to compete intellectually with others at a higher level of expertise or knowledge","compels workers to confront the limits of their current abilities and seek external support to overcome them"],"implication_answer":1,"irrelevant_sentence_index":4},{"id":"27ST_E_17_02","difficulty":"높음","title":"상징과 주관적 현실","sentences":["Symbols are instrumental in helping people derive meanings from social situations.","In social encounters, each person's interpretation or definition of a given situation becomes a subjective reality from that person's viewpoint.","We often assume that what we consider to be reality is shared by others; however, this assumption is often incorrect.","Subjective reality is acquired and shared through agreed-upon symbols, especially language.","If a person shouts Fire! in a crowded movie theater, for example, that language produces the same response in all of those who hear and understand it.","How people interpret the messages they receive and the situations they encounter becomes their subjective reality and may strongly influence their behavior."],"abstract":"Shared symbols, especially language, are what allow individuals' subjective interpretations of social situations to align, making coordinated behavior possible — and their absence or misalignment is a direct source of confusion and miscommunication.","topic_options":["the role of shared symbols and language in enabling individuals to construct aligned subjective realities that coordinate social behavior","the psychological tendency of people to assume that their personal interpretation of events is universally shared by others","the ways in which language barriers between social groups lead to misunderstandings in high-stakes public situations","the relationship between the meaning of symbols and the social norms that govern how people respond to them","the process by which individuals gradually internalize the symbolic meanings accepted by their cultural community"],"topic_answer":1,"blank_sentence_index":3,"blank_target":"agreed-upon symbols, especially language","blank_options":["agreed-upon symbols, especially language","individual reasoning and personal logic","universal biological instincts and reflexes","emotional intuition and nonverbal cues","formal education and academic training"],"blank_answer":1,"order_given_index":0,"order_blocks":[{"label":"B","sentence_indices":[1,2]},{"label":"C","sentence_indices":[3,4]},{"label":"D","sentence_indices":[5]}],"order_options":["(A)-(C)-(B)","(A)-(B)-(C)","(C)-(A)-(B)","(B)-(A)-(C)","(B)-(C)-(A)"],"order_answer":2,"insert_sentence":"How people interpret the messages they receive and the situations they encounter becomes their subjective reality and may strongly influence their behavior.","insert_answer":5,"summary_template":"Because each person's interpretation of a situation constitutes their ________(A)________ reality, shared symbols — especially language — are essential for aligning these individual realities and enabling ________(B)________ social interaction.","summary_A_options":["constructed","personal","subjective","shared","symbols"],"summary_A_answer":3,"summary_B_options":["meaningful","predictable","coordinated","effective","stable"],"summary_B_answer":3,"implication_sentence_index":4,"implication_keyword":"that language produces the same response in all of those who hear and understand it","implication_options":["a shared symbolic meaning triggers identical behavioral reactions across all individuals who have internalized it","the emotional impact of a warning depends on the volume and urgency with which the speaker delivers it","language that carries a clear threat automatically overrides individual differences in personality and temperament","the speed of a group's response to a verbal warning is determined by how familiar members are with the speaker","a widely understood word can serve as a reliable coordination signal even in the absence of prior social agreement"],"implication_answer":1,"irrelevant_sentence_index":4},{"id":"27ST_E_17_03","difficulty":"높음","title":"우울증의 복합적 본질","sentences":["Depression is terrible, and it is common.","Roughly one in seven people will experience at least one full-blown depressive episode in their lifetime.","It is a tragedy on an individual and a societal level, yet we — and by we, I mean all of us, including doctors — struggle to grasp it.","This is because depression is not one disease; it is a collection of symptoms that appears similar across sufferers, despite resulting from a melting pot of diverse causes and mechanisms.","There is no single reason for depression: one person's depressive episode seems to clearly stem from recent life events, another from historic trauma and loss, yet another out of the blue, with no clear psychological or social cause whatsoever.","Perhaps understandably, there is no one treatment for this condition, either.","Antidepressants lead to improvement in roughly a third of patients, offer some kind of improvement in another third, while a final third remain completely unaffected."],"abstract":"Depression resists simple understanding and uniform treatment because it is not a single disease but a heterogeneous cluster of symptoms arising from a wide diversity of causes, mechanisms, and presentations.","topic_options":["the fundamental heterogeneity of depression in terms of causes, presentations, and treatment responses that makes it exceptionally difficult to define and treat","the prevalence of depression as a global health crisis and the inadequacy of current medical responses to its scale","the reasons why antidepressants are effective for some patients but entirely without effect for a significant proportion","the distinction between depression triggered by identifiable life events and that which arises without any apparent cause","the challenge of developing a universal diagnostic standard for a condition that manifests so differently across individuals"],"topic_answer":1,"blank_sentence_index":3,"blank_target":"a melting pot of diverse causes and mechanisms","blank_options":["a melting pot of diverse causes and mechanisms","a single identifiable biochemical imbalance in the brain","a consistent pattern of symptoms across all age groups","a well-understood neurological disorder with clear treatments","a predictable response to traumatic life experiences"],"blank_answer":1,"order_given_index":0,"order_blocks":[{"label":"B","sentence_indices":[1,2]},{"label":"C","sentence_indices":[3,4]},{"label":"D","sentence_indices":[5,6]}],"order_options":["(A)-(C)-(B)","(C)-(A)-(B)","(B)-(A)-(C)","(B)-(C)-(A)","(A)-(B)-(C)"],"order_answer":5,"insert_sentence":"Perhaps understandably, there is no one treatment for this condition, either.","insert_answer":5,"summary_template":"Depression is best understood not as a single ________(A)________ but as a heterogeneous cluster of symptoms arising from diverse causes, which is why no single ________(B)________ approach works for all patients.","summary_A_options":["disease","condition","symptom","depression","resists"],"summary_A_answer":1,"summary_B_options":["treatment","diagnostic","effective","preventive","stable"],"summary_B_answer":1,"implication_sentence_index":3,"implication_keyword":"a melting pot of diverse causes and mechanisms","implication_options":["a complex mixture of entirely different biological, psychological, and social origins that cannot be reduced to one explanation","a cultural environment in which multiple competing theories of mental illness have been combined without resolution","a research tradition that has drawn on many different disciplines without producing a unified scientific consensus","a therapeutic framework that combines elements from different treatment traditions to address complex cases","a diagnostic category that has been expanded over time to incorporate previously unrelated psychological conditions"],"implication_answer":1,"irrelevant_sentence_index":5},{"id":"27ST_E_17_04","difficulty":"높음","title":"철학에서 유추의 두 기능","sentences":["Analogies can serve two different functions in philosophy.","Sometimes, as seems often the case in Plato, for example, they serve simply to illustrate.","When Socrates compares the Good with the sun, he may simply be using the image of the sun to help bring to life his arguments about the Good.","On other occasions, however, the analogy can be an integral part of an argument.","Consider one of the most popular arguments for the existence of God, the argument from design, which has been advanced by many thinkers, from the ancient Stoics to British theologian William Paley.","The argument holds that just as an artefact such as a watch implies the existence of an artisan, so the universe implies the existence of a divine creator.","Rather, the analogy is supposed to show why we should conclude that the universe has a creator."],"abstract":"In philosophical reasoning, analogies function either as illustrative devices that make abstract ideas vivid or as structural components of an argument from which a substantive conclusion is drawn.","topic_options":["the distinction between analogies used merely to illustrate philosophical ideas and those that function as the core of an argument","the historical use of analogical reasoning in arguments for the existence of God from Plato to William Paley","the reasons why the argument from design has been considered one of the most persuasive theistic arguments in philosophy","the difference between Plato's use of metaphor in the Republic and Aristotle's more systematic analogical reasoning","the logical limitations of analogical arguments and the conditions under which they can be considered valid"],"topic_answer":1,"blank_sentence_index":0,"blank_target":"two different functions","blank_options":["two different functions","a single unified purpose","several unrelated roles","only a decorative purpose","primarily a logical structure"],"blank_answer":1,"order_given_index":0,"order_blocks":[{"label":"B","sentence_indices":[1,2]},{"label":"C","sentence_indices":[3,4]},{"label":"D","sentence_indices":[5,6]}],"order_options":["(A)-(C)-(B)","(B)-(A)-(C)","(A)-(B)-(C)","(B)-(C)-(A)","(C)-(A)-(B)"],"order_answer":3,"insert_sentence":"Rather, the analogy is supposed to show why we should conclude that the universe has a creator.","insert_answer":6,"summary_template":"Philosophical analogies can function either as ________(A)________ tools that clarify abstract concepts or as ________(B)________ components of an argument from which a substantive conclusion logically follows.","summary_A_options":["explanatory","rhetorical","philosophical","reasoning","illustrative"],"summary_A_answer":5,"summary_B_options":["essential","structural","effective","stable","argumentative"],"summary_B_answer":5,"implication_sentence_index":5,"implication_keyword":"just as an artefact such as a watch implies the existence of an artisan","implication_options":["the presence of complex purposeful design in an object is taken as sufficient evidence that an intelligent agent created it","the mechanical complexity of a watch is used to demonstrate that natural objects are superior in design to human creations","a comparison between human craftsmanship and divine creation is used to establish the limits of human understanding","the reliability and precision of a watch serves as a model for the kind of order that God imposes on the universe","an object's usefulness and elegance are treated as proof that its creator possessed both skill and intentionality"],"implication_answer":1,"irrelevant_sentence_index":4},{"id":"27ST_E_17_05","difficulty":"높음","title":"회복의 과정과 결과","sentences":["Recovery can be considered a process as well as an outcome.","Recovery as an outcome refers to one's physiological and psychological state after a certain recovery period, which can be, for instance, at the end of the day, after engaging in a certain activity, or after waking up.","Physiological recovery outcomes involve the restoration of physiological resources such as muscle strength, heart rate, and the absence of physical fatigue.","Psychological recovery outcomes relate to the restoration of mental resources such as attention, motivation, mental energy, and mood.","As such, one's physiological and psychological states act as a resource that functions as a stress-buffer for upcoming activities as well.","Recovery as a process refers to those activities and experiences that result in a change in one's physiological and psychological state.","Regarding recovery processes, physical inactivity is generally considered the most effective way to restore physiological resources."],"abstract":"Recovery encompasses both the activities and experiences that restore physiological and psychological resources and the resultant states of restoration, with the former determining whether the latter is adequately achieved.","topic_options":["the conceptual distinction between recovery as a restorative process and recovery as a measurable outcome of that process","the physiological indicators used to assess whether an individual has achieved adequate recovery after physical exertion","the role of psychological resources such as attention and motivation in determining resilience to work-related stress","the relative effectiveness of active and passive recovery strategies for restoring muscle strength and cardiovascular function","the relationship between sleep quality and the restoration of both physical and mental resources after demanding activities"],"topic_answer":1,"blank_sentence_index":6,"blank_target":"physical inactivity is generally considered the most effective way to restore physiological resources","blank_options":["physical inactivity is generally considered the most effective way to restore physiological resources","intense exercise is recommended for accelerating psychological recovery","social interaction is the primary means of restoring mental energy","nutritional supplementation plays the most significant role in recovery","sleep quality matters far more than the total duration of rest"],"blank_answer":1,"order_given_index":0,"order_blocks":[{"label":"B","sentence_indices":[1,2]},{"label":"C","sentence_indices":[3,4]},{"label":"D","sentence_indices":[5,6]}],"order_options":["(B)-(C)-(A)","(A)-(C)-(B)","(C)-(A)-(B)","(B)-(A)-(C)","(A)-(B)-(C)"],"order_answer":5,"insert_sentence":"Regarding recovery processes, physical inactivity is generally considered the most effective way to restore physiological resources.","insert_answer":6,"summary_template":"Recovery encompasses both the ________(A)________ that restore physiological and psychological resources and the resultant ________(B)________ of restoration, with the former directly shaping the quality of the latter.","summary_A_options":["behaviors","strategies","recovery","encompasses","processes"],"summary_A_answer":5,"summary_B_options":["conditions","effective","states","stable","outcomes"],"summary_B_answer":5,"implication_sentence_index":4,"implication_keyword":"functions as a stress-buffer for upcoming activities","implication_options":["serves as a protective reserve of physiological and psychological capacity that absorbs the demands of future challenges","acts as a warning signal that alerts individuals to the risk of overexertion before they begin a new activity","provides a temporary period of reduced cognitive demand that allows the brain to consolidate learning","creates an emotional shield that prevents individuals from feeling the full psychological impact of stressful tasks","generates a stable baseline of energy that ensures consistent performance regardless of the difficulty of the task"],"implication_answer":1,"irrelevant_sentence_index":4},{"id":"27ST_E_17_06","difficulty":"높음","title":"고통과 삶의 의미","sentences":["The difficult times that we endure play a key role in helping us to lead more meaningful lives.","As Jean-Paul Sartre put it, Human life begins on the far side of despair.","That is, many of the ways people feel their lives are meaningful are grounded in the sufferings they have experienced.","One research project investigated the differences between people who found their lives to be happy and those who found them to be meaningful.","While, on average, happy lives and meaningful lives overlap a great deal, the researchers focused on those aspects of a meaningful life that were distinct from happiness.","And, remarkably, they found that people who had more meaningful lives reported that they had more experience suffering through past negative events.","On the other hand, these past experiences with suffering tended to reduce people's overall levels of happiness.","Our sufferings, then, seem to help to provide people with the sense that their lives are more meaningful, even if these events are associated with lower feelings of happiness."],"abstract":"Research supports the paradoxical finding that suffering contributes to a sense of meaningfulness in life even as it reduces happiness, suggesting that meaning and happiness are distinct and sometimes opposed dimensions of human experience.","topic_options":["the paradoxical finding that suffering enhances the sense of life's meaningfulness even while reducing overall happiness","the philosophical basis for Jean-Paul Sartre's claim that genuine human life is only possible beyond despair","the methodological differences between research on happiness and research on meaning in positive psychology","the reasons why people who have experienced trauma often report a stronger sense of purpose than those who have not","the relationship between stress and resilience and the long-term benefits of enduring difficult life experiences"],"topic_answer":1,"blank_sentence_index":2,"blank_target":"grounded in the sufferings they have experienced","blank_options":["grounded in the sufferings they have experienced","derived from the achievements and successes they celebrate","shaped by the relationships they have built over time","determined by the material comfort they have accumulated","based on the positive emotions they experience daily"],"blank_answer":1,"order_given_index":0,"order_blocks":[{"label":"B","sentence_indices":[1,2]},{"label":"C","sentence_indices":[3,4,5]},{"label":"D","sentence_indices":[6,7]}],"order_options":["(B)-(C)-(A)","(C)-(A)-(B)","(A)-(C)-(B)","(B)-(A)-(C)","(A)-(B)-(C)"],"order_answer":5,"insert_sentence":"On the other hand, these past experiences with suffering tended to reduce people's overall levels of happiness.","insert_answer":6,"summary_template":"Research shows that ________(A)________ through negative experiences contributes to a sense of life's ________(B)________, even as those same experiences tend to lower overall happiness — revealing that meaning and happiness are distinct dimensions of a good life.","summary_A_options":["persisting","reflecting","suffering","happiness","research"],"summary_A_answer":3,"summary_B_options":["depth","resilience","meaningfulness","effective","stable"],"summary_B_answer":3,"implication_sentence_index":1,"implication_keyword":"Human life begins on the far side of despair","implication_options":["authentic and meaningful human existence is only possible after one has passed through and beyond profound suffering","people cannot begin to live fully until they have confronted the possibility that life has no inherent purpose","the most significant moments of personal growth occur in the period immediately following a major life crisis","a life lived in comfort and ease cannot produce the depth of character that genuine humanity requires","the experience of despair is a necessary precondition for developing the emotional capacity to feel joy"],"implication_answer":1,"irrelevant_sentence_index":3},{"id":"27ST_E_18_01","difficulty":"높음","title":"생존 편향과 트랙터","sentences":["There are estimated to be more than 160,000 farms spread across Northern Ireland and the Republic of Ireland combined.","On all of those farms, you will find barns, and in some of those barns, you might be fortunate enough to stumble across a classic tractor like the Massey Ferguson 35.","If you were to strike up a conversation with a farmer who still owns one, she might well give the chassis of her Massey Ferguson 35 an affectionate tap and nostalgically remark, They don't make 'em like that anymore.","The fact that the tractor has survived at least fifty-eight years seems to provide evidence of its superior build quality.","But wait — how long did the other 388,381 Massey Ferguson 35 tractors produced between 1956 and 1964 last before they went for scrap?","Rather than build quality, it might well be the fondness that people in Ireland have for the little red tractor that has led farmers there to hold on to their Massey Fergusons and take care of them as well as they have."],"abstract":"The longevity of surviving tractors does not necessarily reflect superior build quality but may instead reflect a selection bias, as we only observe units that were preserved through sentiment rather than those that were discarded.","topic_options":["the danger of drawing conclusions about quality from surviving examples while ignoring the many that did not last","the historical significance of the Massey Ferguson 35 as an icon of traditional farming culture in Ireland","the relationship between emotional attachment to objects and their likelihood of being maintained and preserved","the ways in which nostalgic bias leads consumers to overestimate the quality of products from earlier eras","the role of community traditions in preserving agricultural heritage through the maintenance of classic machinery"],"topic_answer":1,"blank_sentence_index":3,"blank_target":"its superior build quality","blank_options":["its superior build quality","its low cost and widespread availability","the sentimental attachment of its owners","the favorable agricultural policies of the region","the tractor's compatibility with modern equipment"],"blank_answer":1,"order_given_index":0,"order_blocks":[{"label":"B","sentence_indices":[1,2]},{"label":"C","sentence_indices":[3]},{"label":"D","sentence_indices":[4,5]}],"order_options":["(A)-(C)-(B)","(A)-(B)-(C)","(C)-(A)-(B)","(B)-(A)-(C)","(B)-(C)-(A)"],"order_answer":2,"insert_sentence":"The fact that the tractor has survived at least fifty-eight years seems to provide evidence of its superior build quality.","insert_answer":3,"summary_template":"The longevity of surviving tractors is mistakenly attributed to superior ________(A)________, when in reality the more likely explanation is the ________(B)________ that led their owners to preserve them while others were scrapped.","summary_A_options":["design","engineering","reflect","build quality","longevity"],"summary_A_answer":4,"summary_B_options":["variation","variation","effective","emotional attachment","stable"],"summary_B_answer":4,"implication_sentence_index":2,"implication_keyword":"They don't make 'em like that anymore","implication_options":["a nostalgic belief that surviving old products represent a higher standard of craftsmanship than modern ones","a factual observation that manufacturing technology has deteriorated significantly since the mid-twentieth century","a complaint that modern agricultural equipment lacks the aesthetic charm of classic vintage machinery","a sentimental expression of loyalty to a brand that has been part of a family's farming heritage for generations","a reflection on the environmental cost of replacing durable old machines with new ones that wear out faster"],"implication_answer":1,"irrelevant_sentence_index":2},{"id":"27ST_E_18_02","difficulty":"높음","title":"위기 유형과 미디어 선택","sentences":["During crises that present immediate danger, people seek trusted and verified sources to ease their immediate concerns, thus turning to traditional sources such as television and radio.","For other crisis types, such as public health and political crises, however, people are more likely to turn to social media where they can seek multiple voices and a variety of expert opinions, as, unlike the first set of crises, public health and political crises may be more subjective and less straightforward, and thus necessitate a deeper dive into supplementary information and evidence.","In addition to the type of crisis at hand, Liu, a communication scholar, and colleagues argued that traditional and social media have different effects on different audiences regarding the motivation to follow instructions and recommended behaviors during crises.","Thus, both traditional and social media play a prominent role in delivering important scientific information to the public during crises."],"abstract":"The choice between traditional and social media during a crisis depends on both the nature of the crisis and the characteristics of the audience, with each medium serving different informational needs in different contexts.","topic_options":["the differential role of traditional and social media in crisis communication depending on crisis type and audience characteristics","the superiority of traditional media over social media in delivering accurate and reliable information during emergencies","the reasons why younger audiences have largely abandoned traditional media in favor of social media platforms","the challenges that communication scholars face in measuring the effectiveness of different media during public crises","the role of government institutions in regulating the flow of information through both traditional and social media channels"],"topic_answer":1,"blank_sentence_index":0,"blank_target":"trusted and verified sources","blank_options":["trusted and verified sources","entertaining and engaging content","informal and personal accounts","frequent and rapid updates","visually appealing information"],"blank_answer":1,"order_given_index":0,"order_blocks":[{"label":"B","sentence_indices":[1]},{"label":"C","sentence_indices":[2]},{"label":"D","sentence_indices":[3]}],"order_options":["(B)-(A)-(C)","(B)-(C)-(A)","(A)-(B)-(C)","(A)-(C)-(B)","(C)-(A)-(B)"],"order_answer":3,"insert_sentence":null,"insert_answer":null,"summary_template":"Crisis communication research shows that the ________(A)________ of a crisis determines which media people turn to, while audience ________(B)________ — particularly age — shapes how traditional and social media respectively influence behavior.","summary_A_options":["nature","duration","severity","crisis","different"],"summary_A_answer":1,"summary_B_options":["characteristics","behaviors","preferences","effective","stable"],"summary_B_answer":1,"implication_sentence_index":1,"implication_keyword":"a deeper dive into supplementary information and evidence","implication_options":["a more thorough and wide-ranging search for additional context beyond what a single source can provide","a professional investigation conducted by trained researchers with access to classified government data","a prolonged period of study in which individuals immerse themselves in academic literature on the topic","a deliberate effort to seek out contradictory evidence in order to challenge one's initial assumptions","a systematic comparison of all available sources to determine which one is the most authoritative"],"implication_answer":1,"irrelevant_sentence_index":2},{"id":"27ST_E_18_03","difficulty":"높음","title":"초점과 다중 균형","sentences":["Focal points are the little things that make a big difference — the difference between reaching one equilibrium and reaching another.","If a local soccer team comes to practice near the playground of the park every Saturday morning or a group of stay-at-home parents arranges a regular trip at 3 P.M. on a Wednesday afternoon, that can create a focal point around which others coordinate.","With the team at practice, the park will feel safe from muggers and there will be something to look at, so families will come along to use the park.","A lively park playground can be created by a soccer practice that doesn't even take place any longer.","That is an indication of how whimsically unpredictable these multiple equilibria can be.","Yet while the outcome is whimsical, the causes are rational."],"abstract":"Small, seemingly arbitrary initial events can act as focal points that coordinate behavior and lock in one social equilibrium over another, producing outcomes that are unpredictable in origin but perfectly rational in mechanism.","topic_options":["the way small focal events coordinate behavior into self-sustaining social equilibria whose origins may be arbitrary but whose logic is rational","the role of community activities such as sports practice in transforming unsafe public spaces into welcoming social environments","the reasons why people are more likely to visit public parks when they expect other people to be present there","the unpredictability of social coordination and the difficulty of deliberately engineering a desired community outcome","the contrast between the planned activities of local organizations and the spontaneous behaviors they induce in others"],"topic_answer":1,"blank_sentence_index":4,"blank_target":"how whimsically unpredictable these multiple equilibria can be","blank_options":["how whimsically unpredictable these multiple equilibria can be","how rationally people respond to clearly defined social incentives","how effectively governments can design public spaces for community use","how strongly economic factors determine the success of public areas","how quickly communities abandon established patterns of social behavior"],"blank_answer":1,"order_given_index":0,"order_blocks":[{"label":"B","sentence_indices":[1,2]},{"label":"C","sentence_indices":[3]},{"label":"D","sentence_indices":[4,5]}],"order_options":["(A)-(C)-(B)","(A)-(B)-(C)","(B)-(C)-(A)","(C)-(A)-(B)","(B)-(A)-(C)"],"order_answer":2,"insert_sentence":"A lively park playground can be created by a soccer practice that doesn't even take place any longer.","insert_answer":3,"summary_template":"Focal points — small initial events that coordinate behavior — can lock communities into ________(A)________ equilibria that persist even after the original trigger is gone, producing outcomes that seem ________(B)________ but arise from perfectly rational individual responses.","summary_A_options":["predictable","self-sustaining","desirable","small","seemingly"],"summary_A_answer":2,"summary_B_options":["irrational","whimsical","intentional","effective","stable"],"summary_B_answer":2,"implication_sentence_index":5,"implication_keyword":"while the outcome is whimsical, the causes are rational","implication_options":["the final social pattern appears arbitrary and unpredictable even though each step that produced it followed a logical individual logic","communities choose outcomes that seem playful and spontaneous in order to conceal the deliberate planning behind them","the unpredictability of social life is a consequence of irrational decision-making rather than rational coordination","outcomes that appear to be the result of chance are in fact the product of deliberate collective organization","rational individual choices inevitably produce irrational collective outcomes in complex social environments"],"implication_answer":1,"irrelevant_sentence_index":1},{"id":"27ST_E_18_04","difficulty":"높음","title":"현재의 문화적 비가시성","sentences":["As the set of cultural norms and categories taken for granted at any particular time, the present is normally more or less invisible to those who participate in it.","It is the unthought background of their thought and action, like water to a fish, or air to a dove.","In films, this background can sometimes become visible as a bygone present in a film that is not just historically but culturally dated.","In the culturally dated film, attitudes and ways of behaving that have altered over time and which now appear as quaint, strange, incorrect or problematic, are taken for granted by the characters in the film, and go unquestioned or are even happily endorsed in the film's narrative.","This is something that is doubly evident in dated historical films that read the past in terms of their present, where the anachronisms are themselves reflective of a bygone present."],"abstract":"The cultural assumptions of any era are invisible to those living within them, becoming perceptible only in retrospect — either when old films expose the taken-for-granted attitudes of a past present, or when modern films anachronistically project today's assumptions onto historical settings.","topic_options":["the invisibility of cultural assumptions to those who hold them and the various ways this becomes apparent in retrospect through film","the technical differences between historically accurate films and those that modernize the past for contemporary audiences","the role of cinema in preserving cultural attitudes from earlier periods that would otherwise be forgotten over time","the aesthetic judgments viewers apply when evaluating whether the portrayal of the past in a film feels authentic","the challenge filmmakers face in depicting historical periods without inadvertently projecting their own cultural biases"],"topic_answer":1,"blank_sentence_index":0,"blank_target":"normally more or less invisible to those who participate in it","blank_options":["normally more or less invisible to those who participate in it","constantly analyzed and critiqued by cultural historians and scholars","always recognized and challenged by progressive social movements","carefully preserved and documented for future generations to study","deliberately constructed through media and institutional narratives"],"blank_answer":1,"order_given_index":0,"order_blocks":[{"label":"B","sentence_indices":[1]},{"label":"C","sentence_indices":[2,3]},{"label":"D","sentence_indices":[4]}],"order_options":["(A)-(B)-(C)","(B)-(C)-(A)","(C)-(A)-(B)","(A)-(C)-(B)","(B)-(A)-(C)"],"order_answer":1,"insert_sentence":null,"insert_answer":null,"summary_template":"The cultural norms of any era are ________(A)________ to those living within them, becoming visible only in retrospect — whether through old films that expose past assumptions or modern films that ________(B)________ present attitudes onto historical settings.","summary_A_options":["familiar","implicit","assumptions","invisible","films"],"summary_A_answer":4,"summary_B_options":["variation","variation","effective","anachronistically project","stable"],"summary_B_answer":4,"implication_sentence_index":1,"implication_keyword":"like water to a fish, or air to a dove","implication_options":["so thoroughly surrounding and permeating one's existence that it goes completely unnoticed as a distinct condition","essential for survival but increasingly scarce and therefore treasured by those who depend upon it","natural and comfortable in its proper environment but disorienting when removed from its original context","universally present across all living things and therefore impossible to use as a basis for distinguishing between them","familiar enough to be taken for granted until its sudden absence makes its former presence painfully apparent"],"implication_answer":1,"irrelevant_sentence_index":4},{"id":"27ST_E_19_01","difficulty":"보통","title":"18세기 드레스의 지속가능성","sentences":["Women's dresses from the eighteenth century offered a great opportunity for repurposing, as they were frequently fashioned from long, uncut lengths of fabric.","Textiles were significantly more expensive than the labor it took to alter them, and as a result, most garments were modified numerous times to keep up with changes in fashion.","Sustainability was a way of life.","Indeed, although change is inherent to fashion, remodeling existing clothing, rather than buying new, was a widespread practice.","It is actually rare to find an eighteenth-century dress that does not show some sign of alteration.","The cost of having a gown made, or remade, was only about half the cost of the textile itself and could be significantly less, depending on the type of fabric.","In addition to updated dress silhouettes, accessories and trimmings played an important role in refreshing old clothing styles.","For example, the addition of a row of lace to the upper part of a gown was an economical alternative to a full replacement of the gown.","Many eighteenth-century dresses, particularly those from the first half of the century, were constructed with relatively crude stitches, indicating that the easy alteration of the original gown was a consideration.","Because fabrics retained value even when they were not in fashion, hand-woven silks, cherished for their quality and beauty, were sometimes passed down through generations."],"abstract":"In eighteenth-century fashion, sustainability was not an ideological choice but an economic necessity, as the high cost of textiles relative to labor made repeated alteration and repurposing of garments the standard practice across all social classes.","topic_options":["the economically driven culture of textile reuse and garment alteration that made sustainability a universal practice in eighteenth-century fashion","the role of accessories and trimmings in allowing women of limited means to update their wardrobes without replacing entire garments","the contrast between the fashion practices of the wealthy and those of the poor in eighteenth-century European society","the craftsmanship of eighteenth-century dressmakers and the techniques they used to alter garments for repeated use","the cultural values that led eighteenth-century women to treat clothing as a long-term investment rather than a disposable commodity"],"topic_answer":1,"blank_sentence_index":1,"blank_target":"significantly more expensive than the labor it took to alter them","blank_options":["significantly more expensive than the labor it took to alter them","far less durable than the synthetic materials used today","produced exclusively by skilled artisans for wealthy patrons","largely inaccessible to the working class due to trade restrictions","rarely reused because fashion trends changed too rapidly"],"blank_answer":1,"order_given_index":0,"order_blocks":[{"label":"B","sentence_indices":[1,2]},{"label":"C","sentence_indices":[3,4,5]},{"label":"D","sentence_indices":[6,7,8,9]}],"order_options":["(B)-(C)-(A)","(B)-(A)-(C)","(A)-(B)-(C)","(A)-(C)-(B)","(C)-(A)-(B)"],"order_answer":3,"insert_sentence":"Indeed, although change is inherent to fashion, remodeling existing clothing, rather than buying new, was a widespread practice.","insert_answer":3,"summary_template":"Because textiles were far more ________(A)________ than labor in the eighteenth century, garments were repeatedly altered and repurposed rather than replaced, making ________(B)________ a universal practice across all social classes.","summary_A_options":["scarce","valuable","eighteenth","century","expensive"],"summary_A_answer":5,"summary_B_options":["alteration","reuse","effective","stable","sustainability"],"summary_B_answer":5,"implication_sentence_index":2,"implication_keyword":"Sustainability was a way of life","implication_options":["the careful preservation and reuse of resources was not a conscious environmental choice but an ingrained economic habit","people in the eighteenth century were more environmentally aware than modern consumers who discard clothing after brief use","the practice of reusing materials was considered a moral virtue and was actively promoted by social and religious institutions","sustainable living was a luxury that only the wealthy could afford because it required investment in high-quality durable goods","the concept of sustainability had a different meaning in the eighteenth century than it does in contemporary discourse"],"implication_answer":1,"irrelevant_sentence_index":7},{"id":"27ST_E_19_02","difficulty":"보통","title":"인터넷 뉴스와 신뢰성","sentences":["The rise of internet-based technologies means that news is produced, distributed, and consumed faster than ever before.","However, the reliability of this news is questionable.","Not all organizations or individuals putting out information spend time verifying the details or placing the facts in a wider context.","People are confronted with overwhelming amounts of information not just on a daily basis, but via minute-by-minute updates transmitted to audiences around the globe.","More than ever before, people are involved in organizing and managing the amount and type of news they receive.","The internet means that, regardless of where we are in the world or what time of day it is, news can be accessed from broadcasters located anywhere on the planet.","As new media such as mobile phones, computers, and other portable devices have become more affordable, compact, and embedded in everyday life, they have come to replace television and newspapers.","For younger people, advances in technology form part of the world they were born into.","But the ease of use and affordability of new media mean that they are an integral feature of the lives of people of all ages.","Others fear that new media poses a threat.","Information on the internet is often unregulated, so while it is more accessible than ever before, its reliability is difficult to discern."],"abstract":"While internet-based media have democratized access to news by making it faster, cheaper, and universally available, this same accessibility has come at the cost of reliability, as the absence of regulation makes it difficult to distinguish credible from unreliable information.","topic_options":["the tension between the democratizing potential of internet news and the reliability concerns created by its unregulated nature","the ways in which younger generations have adapted to the information-rich environment created by digital technology","the role of social media platforms in accelerating the spread of misinformation to audiences around the world","the strategies individuals can use to evaluate the credibility of news sources in an age of information overload","the economic factors that have driven the replacement of traditional media by new digital platforms and devices"],"topic_answer":1,"blank_sentence_index":0,"blank_target":"faster than ever before","blank_options":["faster than ever before","more accurately than in previous eras","with greater editorial oversight","with stricter regulatory control","in a more balanced and objective way"],"blank_answer":1,"order_given_index":0,"order_blocks":[{"label":"B","sentence_indices":[1,2,3]},{"label":"C","sentence_indices":[4,5,6,7]},{"label":"D","sentence_indices":[8,9,10]}],"order_options":["(A)-(C)-(B)","(C)-(A)-(B)","(B)-(A)-(C)","(B)-(C)-(A)","(A)-(B)-(C)"],"order_answer":5,"insert_sentence":"Others fear that new media poses a threat.","insert_answer":9,"summary_template":"The internet has made news more ________(A)________ by removing barriers of geography, cost, and age, but this same openness has compromised its ________(B)________, as unregulated content makes it hard to distinguish fact from fiction.","summary_A_options":["abundant","democratic","while","accessible","internet"],"summary_A_answer":4,"summary_B_options":["credibility","effective","accuracy","reliability","stable"],"summary_B_answer":4,"implication_sentence_index":10,"implication_keyword":"its reliability is difficult to discern","implication_options":["the trustworthiness of online information is hard to judge without expertise","internet news is always accurate because it is produced by professional journalists","the speed of online news makes it more reliable than traditional media sources","digital platforms have developed effective tools for filtering out false information","readers are naturally skilled at distinguishing credible from unreliable content"],"implication_answer":1,"irrelevant_sentence_index":9},{"id":"27ST_E_19_03","difficulty":"높음","title":"과로의 구조적 원인","sentences":["Since the 1970s, a combination of forces has made the problem of overwork more widespread.","The service sectors in Western economies have grown dramatically while employment in manufacturing has declined.","The shrinking of labor unions and workplace protections has let employers push for longer hours while global competition, decreased job security, and flat wages have forced workers to work harder to stay in place.","Corporations now shed staff in the course of restructuring and process reengineering, forcing surviving workers to carry heavier workloads.","The 2008 recession and recovery has reinforced a pattern in which companies seek to grow by increasing demands on existing workers rather than hiring new ones.","A few industries have turned into fast-moving, winner-take-all contests: small numbers of people stand to make huge fortunes when their tech company goes public, their hedge fund investment pays off, or their song goes viral.","As a result, many of us are actually working longer hours.","Working hours generally decline with increased productivity, but in the 1970s, increased productivity ceased to yield shorter working hours, despite the expectations of generations of economists.","Since then, this divide has spread to other parts of the world: today, well-off, well-educated people in Western Europe, Australia, and South Korea are also more likely to be overworked, while poorer people struggle to find stable jobs and face chronic underemployment."],"abstract":"Since the 1970s, a convergence of economic forces including weakened labor protections, corporate restructuring, and winner-take-all competition has driven a sustained increase in working hours, particularly among highly educated professionals.","topic_options":["the structural economic forces since the 1970s that have driven an increase in overwork especially among skilled professionals","the historical relationship between productivity growth and working hours and the reasons this relationship broke down","the role of the 2008 financial crisis in accelerating a long-term trend toward longer working hours in developed economies","the growing inequality between overworked high earners and chronically underemployed low-wage workers in Western nations","the ways in which global competition and declining union power have combined to erode workplace protections for all workers"],"topic_answer":1,"blank_sentence_index":2,"blank_target":"forced workers to work harder to stay in place","blank_options":["forced workers to work harder to stay in place","encouraged employers to offer more flexible working arrangements","led to significant improvements in workplace safety standards","resulted in higher wages for workers in competitive industries","prompted governments to introduce stronger labor protection laws"],"blank_answer":1,"order_given_index":0,"order_blocks":[{"label":"B","sentence_indices":[1,2,3]},{"label":"C","sentence_indices":[4,5,6]},{"label":"D","sentence_indices":[7,8]}],"order_options":["(B)-(A)-(C)","(A)-(C)-(B)","(A)-(B)-(C)","(C)-(A)-(B)","(B)-(C)-(A)"],"order_answer":3,"insert_sentence":"Since then, this divide has spread to other parts of the world: today, well-off, well-educated people in Western Europe, Australia, and South Korea are also more likely to be overworked, while poorer people struggle to find stable jobs and face chronic underemployment.","insert_answer":8,"summary_template":"A combination of weakened labor ________(A)________, corporate restructuring, and winner-take-all economic dynamics has driven overwork among skilled professionals, reversing the historical expectation that rising ________(B)________ would lead to shorter working hours.","summary_A_options":["standards","unions","protections","since","convergence"],"summary_A_answer":3,"summary_B_options":["wages","efficiency","productivity","effective","stable"],"summary_B_answer":3,"implication_sentence_index":5,"implication_keyword":"winner-take-all contests","implication_options":["competitions in which the rewards are so heavily concentrated at the top that participants are driven to extreme effort regardless of the odds","economic environments in which firms compete so intensely that only the largest and most efficient survive long term","industries in which success is determined entirely by talent rather than by effort, experience, or institutional support","markets in which a small number of dominant players control pricing and distribution to the exclusion of all others","professional fields in which a single breakthrough achievement can instantly elevate an individual to the highest level"],"implication_answer":1,"irrelevant_sentence_index":5},{"id":"27ST_E_19_04","difficulty":"높음","title":"억제와 갈등나선 관점","sentences":["Political psychologist Philip Tetlock examined the speeches made by policymakers involved in international conflicts.","He noted that, in making important decisions, national leaders often fall back on overly simplified images of the world.","During the Cold War between the United States and the Soviet Union, for example, two very simple images of the conflict were dominant.","One of these was the deterrence view — that any sign of weakness would be taken advantage of by the opponent and that leaders needed to show their willingness to use military force.","People who hold a deterrence view — that demonstrations of weakness would be taken advantage of — are less likely to support nuclear disarmament.","The other prominent view was a conflict spiral view, which presumed that every escalation of international threat leads the opponent to feel more threatened and that leaders need to demonstrate peaceful intentions in order to reduce the opponent's own defensive hostilities.","Tetlock noted that each of these cognitive frames was correct in some circumstances and incorrect in others.","Against an opponent such as Hitler, a deterrence viewpoint might have been more effective than a view that led to conciliation.","On the other hand, international policy experts estimate that the U.S. invasion of Iraq, argued by President G. W. Bush to be the centerpiece of the war on terror, seems to have curbed increases in the membership of Al-Qaeda."],"abstract":"Political leaders tend to rely on simplified cognitive frames when navigating international conflict, but both the deterrence view and the conflict spiral view are only conditionally valid, with each being more appropriate in some contexts than others.","topic_options":["the conditional validity of the deterrence and conflict spiral frames as simplified cognitive tools for navigating international conflict","the psychological research on how national leaders develop and apply mental models when making foreign policy decisions","the historical evidence for the effectiveness of deterrence strategy in preventing major military conflicts during the Cold War","the reasons why political leaders consistently underestimate the complexity of international conflicts they are involved in","the contrast between academic theories of international relations and the simplified images that drive actual policy decisions"],"topic_answer":1,"blank_sentence_index":6,"blank_target":"correct in some circumstances and incorrect in others","blank_options":["correct in some circumstances and incorrect in others","consistently effective regardless of the opponent's behavior","fundamentally flawed because they oversimplify complex conflicts","universally adopted by national leaders across all political systems","proven accurate by the historical outcomes of major conflicts"],"blank_answer":1,"order_given_index":0,"order_blocks":[{"label":"B","sentence_indices":[1,2,3]},{"label":"C","sentence_indices":[4,5]},{"label":"D","sentence_indices":[6,7,8]}],"order_options":["(C)-(A)-(B)","(B)-(A)-(C)","(A)-(B)-(C)","(B)-(C)-(A)","(A)-(C)-(B)"],"order_answer":3,"insert_sentence":"People who hold a deterrence view — that demonstrations of weakness would be taken advantage of — are less likely to support nuclear disarmament.","insert_answer":4,"summary_template":"National leaders facing international conflict tend to rely on simplified ________(A)________ frames such as deterrence or conflict spiral thinking, but Tetlock's research shows that each is only valid in ________(B)________ circumstances rather than as a universal guide.","summary_A_options":["cognitive","strategic","political","conflict","view"],"summary_A_answer":1,"summary_B_options":["specific","predictable","limited","effective","stable"],"summary_B_answer":1,"implication_sentence_index":5,"implication_keyword":"demonstrate peaceful intentions in order to reduce the opponent's own defensive hostilities","implication_options":["signal a willingness to de-escalate in order to break the cycle in which each side's aggression fuels the other's fear","make unilateral concessions to the opponent in exchange for a formal guarantee of non-aggression","publicly renounce the use of military force as a means of resolving international disputes","offer economic incentives to the opposing side as a substitute for the security guarantees they are seeking","initiate diplomatic negotiations only after the opponent has already taken steps to reduce tensions independently"],"implication_answer":1,"irrelevant_sentence_index":5},{"id":"27ST_E_21_01","difficulty":"높음","title":"공간적 데이터 수집의 혁신","sentences":["Perhaps nothing has revolutionized the study of human-environment interactions more than the development of spatially explicit methods for collecting and analyzing data.","Just a few decades ago, most natural and social scientists collected their data without precise spatial referents.","References were made to watersheds, to communities, to villages, to cities, to proximity to rivers, and so on.","While confidentiality remains an important concern when working with human subjects, the extreme to which this was done was largely unjustified.","Everyone knew more or less where these studied communities were, and anyone interested could have found out.","Be that as it may, there was very little interest, except in geography, to precisely locate a study area on a map with coordinates.","Geography persisted, and finally convinced the rest of us, that place was fundamentally important to understand human-environment dynamics."],"abstract":"The development of spatially explicit data collection methods transformed the study of human-environment interactions by establishing precise location as an essential dimension of scientific inquiry rather than an optional detail.","topic_options":["the transformative role of spatially explicit methods in establishing location as essential to understanding human-environment interactions","the historical reasons why social scientists avoided using precise geographic coordinates in their research data","the ethical debates surrounding the protection of research subjects' identities in community-based field studies","the contributions of geography as a discipline to the development of modern spatial analysis techniques","the shift from qualitative to quantitative methods in natural and social science research over recent decades"],"topic_answer":1,"blank_sentence_index":6,"blank_target":"fundamentally important to understand human-environment dynamics","blank_options":["fundamentally important to understand human-environment dynamics","less valuable than broad conceptual frameworks","possible without spatial reference systems","the primary ethical consideration in research","inferior to qualitative approaches in social science"],"blank_answer":1,"order_given_index":0,"order_blocks":[{"label":"B","sentence_indices":[1,2]},{"label":"C","sentence_indices":[3,4]},{"label":"D","sentence_indices":[5,6,7]}],"order_options":["(B)-(C)-(A)","(A)-(C)-(B)","(A)-(B)-(C)","(C)-(A)-(B)","(B)-(A)-(C)"],"order_answer":3,"insert_sentence":"While confidentiality remains an important concern when working with human subjects, the extreme to which this was done was largely unjustified.","insert_answer":3,"summary_template":"Before the rise of spatially explicit methods, scientists collected data without ________(A)________ spatial referents, but geography eventually demonstrated that precise ________(B)________ is fundamental to understanding how humans relate to their environments.","summary_A_options":["reliable","consistent","precise","development","spatially"],"summary_A_answer":3,"summary_B_options":["measurement","mapping","location","effective","stable"],"summary_B_answer":3,"implication_sentence_index":3,"implication_keyword":"the extreme to which this was done was largely unjustified","implication_options":["hiding location data went far beyond what ethical research standards required","protecting research subjects from identification was the most important priority","changing community names was a standard and accepted practice in anthropology","confidentiality concerns made it impossible to conduct meaningful field research","researchers had no obligation to protect the identities of their study participants"],"implication_answer":1,"irrelevant_sentence_index":3},{"id":"27ST_E_21_02","difficulty":"높음","title":"데카르트의 회의와 존재","sentences":["The idea that our senses may be deceiving us was taken up by the French philosopher and mathematician René Descartes.","He realized that sometimes our senses give us a false impression — a straight stick in a glass of water appears to be bent, for example.","It might even be that we are asleep, and that the world we are experiencing is no more than a dream, or that God or some mischievous power is making us believe things that are not really true.","If that is the case, though, we can never know anything for sure.","But Descartes then showed that there was one thing he could be sure of: In order to be deceived, he must exist, and exist as a thing that thinks.","So, although his senses could not be trusted, he could be sure he existed as something that was capable of thinking and reasoning."],"abstract":"Descartes' method of radical doubt, while undermining the reliability of sensory experience entirely, paradoxically yields one indubitable truth: the very act of doubting proves the existence of a thinking subject.","topic_options":["Descartes' argument that systematic doubt about sensory experience leads to the one indubitable certainty of one's own existence as a thinking being","the philosophical tradition of skepticism and the various ways thinkers have challenged the reliability of human perception","the scientific evidence that optical illusions demonstrate the unreliability of sensory data in everyday experience","the relationship between Descartes' mathematical approach to knowledge and his philosophical method of systematic doubt","the reasons why Descartes concluded that God could not be the source of systematic deception in human sensory experience"],"topic_answer":1,"blank_sentence_index":4,"blank_target":"In order to be deceived, he must exist, and exist as a thing that thinks","blank_options":["In order to be deceived, he must exist, and exist as a thing that thinks","the external world could only be known through mathematical reasoning","true knowledge was impossible without the confirmation of divine authority","sensory experience was the only reliable foundation for genuine knowledge","logical deduction was insufficient to establish any form of certainty"],"blank_answer":1,"order_given_index":0,"order_blocks":[{"label":"B","sentence_indices":[1,2]},{"label":"C","sentence_indices":[3]},{"label":"D","sentence_indices":[4,5]}],"order_options":["(A)-(C)-(B)","(A)-(B)-(C)","(B)-(C)-(A)","(B)-(A)-(C)","(C)-(A)-(B)"],"order_answer":2,"insert_sentence":"It might even be that we are asleep, and that the world we are experiencing is no more than a dream, or that God or some mischievous power is making us believe things that are not really true.","insert_answer":2,"summary_template":"Descartes' radical ________(A)________ of all sensory experience ultimately yields one unshakeable certainty: the act of doubting itself proves the existence of a ________(B)________ subject.","summary_A_options":["rejection","analysis","doubt","descartes","method"],"summary_A_answer":3,"summary_B_options":["rational","conscious","thinking","effective","stable"],"summary_B_answer":3,"implication_sentence_index":2,"implication_keyword":"some mischievous power is making us believe things that are not really true","implication_options":["a hypothetical force of systematic deception used to push the limits of doubt to their most extreme possible conclusion","a religious concept of evil that Descartes borrowed from theology to explain the origin of human error and sin","a psychological phenomenon in which people convince themselves of false beliefs through wishful thinking","a reference to the unreliable nature of memory which frequently distorts our recollection of past events","a metaphor for the way social conditioning shapes people's beliefs without their being aware of it"],"implication_answer":1,"irrelevant_sentence_index":3},{"id":"27ST_E_21_03","difficulty":"보통","title":"Ache 부족의 위험 공유","sentences":["Hunters in the Ache tribe, living in the Paraguayan jungle, have a lot of ups and downs in their success at the hunt.","Some days they bring home much more food than they could possibly eat; other days they come home empty-handed.","If a man caught a wild pig and hoarded it for himself and his family, much of it would go to waste.","During unlucky periods, individual hunters and their families would starve.","Instead of living by a philosophy of 'rugged individualism,' however, hunters who have a lucky day share their meat with other families.","In exchange for this generosity, their neighbors share with them on days when the luck runs the other way.","By exchanging resources, particularly those that are unpredictable and uncertain (like meat from the hunt, as opposed to vegetable crops), the group provides a mutual insurance policy against starvation."],"abstract":"The Ache tribe's practice of sharing the majority of their hunt with others functions as a collective risk-pooling strategy that protects all members against the unpredictable variability of food availability.","topic_options":["the collective risk-sharing strategy of the Ache tribe in which generous meat distribution functions as mutual insurance against starvation","the cultural values of generosity and reciprocity that distinguish hunter-gatherer societies from settled agricultural communities","the practical reasons why storing food is more difficult for nomadic jungle hunters than for farmers with fixed settlements","the contrast between the philosophy of individualism in modern Western societies and the communal practices of indigenous groups","the role of reciprocal exchange in building social trust and long-term cooperative relationships within small communities"],"topic_answer":1,"blank_sentence_index":6,"blank_target":"a mutual insurance policy against starvation","blank_options":["a mutual insurance policy against starvation","an efficient system for maximizing individual profit","a competitive strategy for securing the best hunting grounds","a rigid social hierarchy based on hunting ability","a formal agreement to divide resources equally at all times"],"blank_answer":1,"order_given_index":0,"order_blocks":[{"label":"B","sentence_indices":[1,2]},{"label":"C","sentence_indices":[3,4]},{"label":"D","sentence_indices":[5,6]}],"order_options":["(B)-(A)-(C)","(C)-(A)-(B)","(A)-(C)-(B)","(B)-(C)-(A)","(A)-(B)-(C)"],"order_answer":5,"insert_sentence":"In exchange for this generosity, their neighbors share with them on days when the luck runs the other way.","insert_answer":5,"summary_template":"The Ache tribe's practice of sharing up to 90% of their hunt functions as a system of ________(A)________ risk-sharing, in which the unpredictability of hunting outcomes makes ________(B)________ exchange the most rational survival strategy.","summary_A_options":["collective","cultural","voluntary","ache","tribe"],"summary_A_answer":1,"summary_B_options":["reciprocal","communal","generous","effective","stable"],"summary_B_answer":1,"implication_sentence_index":4,"implication_keyword":"rugged individualism","implication_options":["a self-reliant approach in which each person hoards resources for themselves regardless of the cost to others in the group","a competitive philosophy that rewards the strongest and most skilled hunters at the expense of weaker community members","an economic ideology that encourages individuals to accumulate as much wealth as possible without social obligation","a survival strategy based on the belief that personal effort alone is sufficient to overcome any environmental challenge","a cultural value that discourages cooperation and treats dependency on others as a sign of personal weakness"],"implication_answer":1,"irrelevant_sentence_index":2},{"id":"27ST_E_22_01","difficulty":"높음","title":"경관 연결성과 생물 보전","sentences":["Connectivity, the capacity of a landscape to support movement by any given species across the landscape, is of increasing concern for conservation biologists.","As the connectivity of a landscape increases from the human perspective (generally through increases in road networks), connectivity decreases for many other species.","Although we may see many species of animals moving across human landscapes (e.g. deer, wolves, and turtles crossing roads or wandering through our backyards), landscapes substantially altered for human use act as barriers to movement of both animal and plant species.","In other cases, passage is essentially impossible — cities along landscape corridors such as river valleys can effectively eliminate genetic exchange between previously connected plant and animal populations; dams can permanently halt spawning of fish by blocking travel to their breeding grounds.","Thus, lack of connectivity can decrease the conservation value of remaining habitat below what its mapped area might suggest, increasing the impact of fragmentation."],"abstract":"Human modifications to landscapes that increase connectivity for people — such as road networks and urban development — simultaneously reduce it for other species, fragmenting habitats and diminishing the conservation value of remaining areas.","topic_options":["the paradox that human infrastructure increases landscape connectivity for people while decreasing it for other species, reducing the conservation value of remaining habitats","the various methods conservation biologists use to measure and restore connectivity in landscapes fragmented by human development","the specific impact of road networks and dam construction on the migration patterns of terrestrial and aquatic species","the differences between complete and incomplete barriers in landscapes and their respective effects on wildlife movement","the relationship between habitat fragmentation and the long-term viability of isolated animal and plant populations"],"topic_answer":1,"blank_sentence_index":0,"blank_target":"of increasing concern for conservation biologists","blank_options":["of increasing concern for conservation biologists","rarely studied due to the complexity of measuring species movement","considered less important than habitat size in conservation planning","already well understood and effectively managed in most regions","primarily relevant to urban planning and infrastructure development"],"blank_answer":1,"order_given_index":0,"order_blocks":[{"label":"B","sentence_indices":[1]},{"label":"C","sentence_indices":[2]},{"label":"D","sentence_indices":[3,4]}],"order_options":["(A)-(B)-(C)","(B)-(A)-(C)","(A)-(C)-(B)","(B)-(C)-(A)","(C)-(A)-(B)"],"order_answer":1,"insert_sentence":null,"insert_answer":null,"summary_template":"Human landscape modifications that enhance ________(A)________ for people — such as roads and cities — act as barriers for wildlife, reducing ecological ________(B)________ and diminishing the conservation value of habitats that remain.","summary_A_options":["connectivity","accessibility","mobility","human","modifications"],"summary_A_answer":1,"summary_B_options":["flow","diversity","resilience","effective","stable"],"summary_B_answer":1,"implication_sentence_index":1,"implication_keyword":"connectivity decreases for many other species","implication_options":["the same infrastructure that facilitates human movement creates obstacles that prevent wildlife from crossing the landscape","animals that once ranged freely across the landscape are forced to adapt their behavior to avoid human-dominated areas","the ecological value of natural habitats is reduced when they are surrounded by roads and urban development","species that cannot tolerate human presence are gradually excluded from landscapes where human activity is increasing","the expansion of road networks eliminates the natural corridors that animals depend on for seasonal migration"],"implication_answer":1,"irrelevant_sentence_index":3},{"id":"27ST_E_22_02","difficulty":"보통","title":"바이오에너지의 환경적 이점","sentences":["By enhancing energy efficiency and putting waste products to use, biopower helps move utilities and industries in a sustainable direction.","The U.S. forest products industry now obtains half its energy by combusting woody waste and liquid waste from pulp mill processing.","Biopower also benefits human health as it cuts down on pollution; by replacing coal in co-firing and direct combustion, biopower reduces emissions of sulfur dioxide because plant matter, unlike coal, contains no appreciable sulfur content.","In addition, biomass resources tend to be geographically spread out, so using them can help support rural economies and reduce many nations' dependence on imported fuels."],"abstract":"Biopower offers multiple environmental and economic benefits — reducing greenhouse gas emissions, cutting pollution, supporting rural economies, and decreasing reliance on imported fossil fuels — by converting waste biomass into usable energy.","topic_options":["the multiple environmental and economic advantages of biopower as a sustainable energy source derived from waste biomass","the specific technical processes by which the forest products industry converts woody and liquid waste into usable energy","the comparison between biopower and coal in terms of their respective contributions to air pollution and climate change","the role of government policy in encouraging industries to adopt biopower as an alternative to conventional fossil fuels","the geographic distribution of biomass resources and its implications for the decentralization of energy production"],"topic_answer":1,"blank_sentence_index":0,"blank_target":"in a sustainable direction","blank_options":["in a sustainable direction","toward greater dependence on fossil fuels","away from renewable energy investments","into new markets for industrial waste","toward higher short-term profit margins"],"blank_answer":1,"order_given_index":0,"order_blocks":[],"order_options":["(A)-(C)-(B)","(A)-(B)-(C)","(C)-(A)-(B)","(B)-(A)-(C)","(B)-(C)-(A)"],"order_answer":2,"insert_sentence":null,"insert_answer":null,"summary_template":"Biopower advances sustainability by converting ________(A)________ into energy, reducing greenhouse gas and sulfur dioxide emissions, and supporting rural economies by decreasing ________(B)________ on imported fuels.","summary_A_options":["waste biomass","biopower biomass","offers biomass"],"summary_A_answer":1,"summary_B_options":["dependence","biopower","offers"],"summary_B_answer":1,"implication_sentence_index":0,"implication_keyword":"putting waste products to use","implication_options":["converting materials that would otherwise be discarded into a productive energy source that reduces both waste and fuel costs","redesigning industrial processes to eliminate the generation of byproducts that require expensive disposal","creating new markets for materials that industries previously paid to remove and transport to landfill sites","repurposing industrial byproducts as raw materials for other manufacturing processes to reduce overall resource consumption","ensuring that no material produced during energy generation is released into the environment without treatment"],"implication_answer":1,"irrelevant_sentence_index":3},{"id":"27ST_E_22_03","difficulty":"높음","title":"코끼리와 사바나 생태계","sentences":["One example of human interventions modifying the character of savannas is through their effects on savanna-dwelling mammals such as elephants.","They are what is known as a 'keystone species' because they have a strong effect on many aspects of the environment in which they live.","They diversify the ecosystems which they occupy and create a mosaic of habitats by browsing, trampling, and knocking over bushes and trees.","They also spread seeds through their eating and defecating habits and maintain or create water holes by wallowing.","All these roles are beneficial to other species.","Conversely, where human interference prevents elephants from moving freely within their habitats and leads to their numbers exceeding the carrying capacity of the savanna, their effect can be environmentally disastrous.","This will be harmful to other species."],"abstract":"Elephants function as a keystone species whose presence in appropriate numbers maintains savanna biodiversity, but human interference that either overcrowds or depletes elephant populations produces serious ecological harm.","topic_options":["the critical role of elephants as a keystone species in maintaining savanna ecosystems and the damaging consequences of human interference with their populations","the specific mechanisms by which elephants create and maintain the mosaic of habitats that characterizes healthy savanna ecosystems","the conflict between conservation goals and human land use in African savannas and its impact on elephant populations","the differences between the ecological effects of elephant overpopulation and underpopulation in savanna environments","the ways in which keystone species interact with other components of an ecosystem to sustain biodiversity and ecological balance"],"topic_answer":1,"blank_sentence_index":5,"blank_target":"their effect can be environmentally disastrous","blank_options":["their effect can be environmentally disastrous","the ecosystem benefits from the resulting reduction in grazing pressure","other species quickly adapt and fill the ecological roles left vacant","the savanna naturally recovers its biodiversity over a short period","human intervention proves more beneficial than natural regulation"],"blank_answer":1,"order_given_index":0,"order_blocks":[{"label":"B","sentence_indices":[1,2]},{"label":"C","sentence_indices":[3,4]},{"label":"D","sentence_indices":[5,6]}],"order_options":["(B)-(A)-(C)","(A)-(C)-(B)","(C)-(A)-(B)","(A)-(B)-(C)","(B)-(C)-(A)"],"order_answer":4,"insert_sentence":"This will be harmful to other species.","insert_answer":6,"summary_template":"Elephants are a ________(A)________ species whose ecological roles maintain savanna biodiversity, but human interference that disrupts their numbers — whether through overcrowding or ________(B)________ — causes serious harm to the wider ecosystem.","summary_A_options":["dominant","keystone","indicator","elephants","function"],"summary_A_answer":2,"summary_B_options":["displacement","depletion","restriction","effective","stable"],"summary_B_answer":2,"implication_sentence_index":2,"implication_keyword":"create a mosaic of habitats","implication_options":["produce a patchwork of varied ecological conditions that supports a greater diversity of species than a uniform landscape would","construct a series of interconnected territories that different elephant groups use for feeding and breeding at different times","generate a pattern of vegetation that makes the savanna visually distinctive and recognizable from aerial observation","establish boundaries between different habitat types that prevent competition between species with overlapping ecological needs","design a landscape in which each area serves a specific ecological function for one particular group of savanna species"],"implication_answer":1,"irrelevant_sentence_index":4},{"id":"27ST_E_23_01","difficulty":"보통","title":"상대 속도와 운동량","sentences":["There is one important thing to note about momentum.","Since motion is relative, only relative velocities are relevant.","In fact, when you think about it, all velocities are relative.","Thus, on the surface of the earth, we always reckon velocity with respect to the ground — the velocity of the earth itself does not matter.","There is a true story of a French pilot in World War II who stretched his hand out of his small airplane window and caught a bullet.","How is this possible?","The velocity of the bullet must have been about the same as the velocity of his plane.","This can happen, because a bullet slows down to such a velocity toward the end of its flight path due to the action of air drag.","Thus, he would have had little problem in catching the bullet."],"abstract":"Because momentum depends on relative rather than absolute velocity, a pilot traveling at the same speed as a slowing bullet can catch it with his bare hand, as the bullet's momentum relative to him is negligible.","topic_options":["the principle of relative velocity and its practical implication for momentum in real-world situations","the physics of air drag and how it reduces the speed of projectiles over long distances","the historical accounts of extraordinary physical feats recorded during the two World Wars","the difference between absolute and relative measurements in classical mechanics","the role of momentum in determining the danger posed by fast-moving objects"],"topic_answer":1,"blank_sentence_index":1,"blank_target":"only relative velocities are relevant","blank_options":["only relative velocities are relevant","the speed of light sets the upper limit for all motion","the direction of movement is more important than its speed","absolute velocity can be measured against a fixed point in space","the mass of an object determines how it responds to forces"],"blank_answer":1,"order_given_index":0,"order_blocks":[{"label":"B","sentence_indices":[1,2,3]},{"label":"C","sentence_indices":[4,5,6]},{"label":"D","sentence_indices":[7,8]}],"order_options":["(A)-(C)-(B)","(A)-(B)-(C)","(B)-(A)-(C)","(B)-(C)-(A)","(C)-(A)-(B)"],"order_answer":2,"insert_sentence":"Thus, he would have had little problem in catching the bullet.","insert_answer":8,"summary_template":"Because momentum depends on ________(A)________ velocity, a bullet traveling at roughly the same speed as a plane has ________(B)________ momentum relative to the pilot, making it catchable.","summary_A_options":["terminal","absolute","momentum","relative","bullet"],"summary_A_answer":4,"summary_B_options":["effective","maximum","dangerous","negligible","stable"],"summary_B_answer":4,"implication_sentence_index":8,"implication_keyword":"little problem in catching the bullet","implication_options":["the pilot could easily grasp the bullet because their relative speeds were nearly equal","the pilot had exceptional reflexes that allowed him to react faster than the bullet","the bullet had been slowed significantly by external resistance before reaching the plane","the pilot used special equipment designed to intercept projectiles in flight","the low altitude of the plane made it easier for the pilot to catch the bullet"],"implication_answer":1,"irrelevant_sentence_index":4},{"id":"27ST_E_23_02","difficulty":"보통","title":"히파르코스의 천문학적 업적","sentences":["Hipparchus of Nicaea was the most important astronomer of the Hellenistic Age after Aristarchus of Samos.","Unlike Aristarchus, Hipparchus believed in the geocentric universe of Aristotle.","A noted mathematician, Hipparchus gauged the movement of the sun and the moon using an astronomical model devised by Apollonius of Perga.","Hipparchus worked at Alexandria and Rhodes; at the latter city, he created a kind of astronomical research center in which he cataloged the stars according to brightness.","Hipparchus made more accurate measurements than Aristarchus did of the distance of the moon and sun from the earth.","To account for the orbit of the sun around the earth he developed the idea of the eccentric, which Ptolemy of Alexandria would expand upon."],"abstract":"Hipparchus, despite holding a geocentric view of the universe, made landmark contributions to ancient astronomy through precise celestial measurements, star cataloging, and theoretical models that influenced later astronomers.","topic_options":["the landmark astronomical contributions of Hipparchus despite his adherence to the geocentric model","the contrast between the heliocentric and geocentric models of the universe in ancient Greek astronomy","the mathematical methods used by ancient Greek astronomers to calculate the distances of celestial bodies","the influence of Apollonius of Perga on the development of astronomical models in the Hellenistic period","the ways in which Ptolemy of Alexandria built upon and extended the work of earlier Greek astronomers"],"topic_answer":1,"blank_sentence_index":4,"blank_target":"more accurate measurements than Aristarchus did of the distance of the moon and sun from the earth","blank_options":["more accurate measurements than Aristarchus did of the distance of the moon and sun from the earth","the first systematic catalog of planetary movements in the ancient world","a more detailed map of the constellations than any previous astronomer","greater influence on later astronomers than any other figure of his era","a more comprehensive theory of celestial mechanics than Ptolemy"],"blank_answer":1,"order_given_index":0,"order_blocks":[{"label":"B","sentence_indices":[1,2]},{"label":"C","sentence_indices":[3]},{"label":"D","sentence_indices":[4,5]}],"order_options":["(C)-(B)-(A)","(C)-(A)-(B)","(A)-(B)-(C)","(B)-(A)-(C)","(A)-(C)-(B)"],"order_answer":3,"insert_sentence":"Hipparchus made more accurate measurements than Aristarchus did of the distance of the moon and sun from the earth.","insert_answer":4,"summary_template":"Although Hipparchus held a ________(A)________ view of the cosmos, his precise measurements and systematic ________(B)________ of celestial objects established him as the foremost astronomer of the Hellenistic Age.","summary_A_options":["mathematical","heliocentric","geocentric","hipparchus","despite"],"summary_A_answer":3,"summary_B_options":["modelinged","observation","cataloging","effective","stable"],"summary_B_answer":3,"implication_sentence_index":5,"implication_keyword":"the eccentric","implication_options":["a geometric device used to explain the apparent irregularity of the sun's orbit within a geocentric framework","a term for the unusual or unpredictable behavior of celestial bodies observed during solar eclipses","a mathematical concept denoting the deviation of a planetary orbit from a perfect circular path","a theoretical model in which the earth is positioned slightly off-center relative to the sun's circular orbit","a classification for stars located far from the center of the known universe in ancient astronomical charts"],"implication_answer":1,"irrelevant_sentence_index":3},{"id":"27ST_E_23_03","difficulty":"높음","title":"극한 환경의 미생물과 편향된 시각","sentences":["Living things are not confined to the familiar temperate realm of land, water, and sunlight inhabited by plants and plant-eating animals.","They can be found in the darkest depths of the ocean, in hot volcanic mud, in pools beneath the frozen surface of the Antarctic, and buried kilometers deep in the Earth's crust.","The creatures that live in these extreme environments are generally unfamiliar, not only because they are inaccessible, but also because they are mostly microscopic.","In more homely habitats, too, most organisms are too small for us to see without special equipment: they tend to go unnoticed, unless they cause a disease or rot the timbers of our houses.","Studies of bacteria have helped us become familiar with those species of industrial importance, such as those used in breaking down waste materials.","Yet microorganisms make up most of the total mass of living matter on our planet.","Only recently, through new methods of molecular analysis and specifically through the analysis of DNA sequences, have we begun to get a picture of life on Earth that is not grossly distorted by our biased perspective as large animals living on dry land."],"abstract":"Life on Earth is far more diverse and widespread than the limited perspective of large land-dwelling animals suggests, with microorganisms dominating the total biomass and only recently becoming visible through advances in molecular analysis.","topic_options":["the distorted picture of life on Earth that results from our perspective as large land animals and how molecular analysis is correcting it","the extreme environments in which microorganisms survive and the biological adaptations that make this possible","the industrial applications of bacteria that have driven scientific interest in microbial research","the reasons why microorganisms in accessible habitats go unnoticed despite their ecological significance","the historical development of molecular biology and its impact on our understanding of microbial diversity"],"topic_answer":1,"blank_sentence_index":6,"blank_target":"our biased perspective as large animals living on dry land","blank_options":["the inherently limited viewpoint of organisms whose scale and habitat make most of life invisible to them","the cultural tendency of scientists to prioritize the study of species that are economically or medically significant","the methodological constraints of traditional biology that prevented the study of organisms in extreme environments","the overrepresentation of familiar terrestrial ecosystems in scientific literature and biological education","the assumption shared by early biologists that life could only exist in moderate environmental conditions"],"blank_answer":1,"order_given_index":0,"order_blocks":[{"label":"B","sentence_indices":[1,2]},{"label":"C","sentence_indices":[3]},{"label":"D","sentence_indices":[4,5,6]}],"order_options":["(C)-(B)-(A)","(A)-(B)-(C)","(B)-(C)-(A)","(B)-(A)-(C)","(A)-(C)-(B)"],"order_answer":2,"insert_sentence":"In more homely habitats, too, most organisms are too small for us to see without special equipment: they tend to go unnoticed, unless they cause a disease or rot the timbers of our houses.","insert_answer":3,"summary_template":"Most of Earth's living matter consists of ________(A)________ that are invisible to us, and only recent advances in ________(B)________ analysis have allowed us to overcome the distorted view imposed by our perspective as large land animals.","summary_A_options":["microorganisms","extremophiles","bacteria","life","earth"],"summary_A_answer":1,"summary_B_options":["molecular","microscopic","effective","stable","genetic"],"summary_B_answer":1,"implication_sentence_index":6,"implication_keyword":"grossly distorted by our biased perspective as large animals living on dry land","implication_options":["severely skewed by the fact that we can only directly observe life at the scale and in the environments accessible to us","fundamentally flawed because large animals are incapable of understanding the chemistry of microscopic organisms","systematically incomplete because scientists have historically refused to study organisms in inaccessible locations","culturally biased because Western science has always prioritized the study of economically useful species","irreparably limited because the tools needed to study microorganisms were not invented until the twentieth century"],"implication_answer":1,"irrelevant_sentence_index":4},{"id":"27ST_E_24_01","difficulty":"높음","title":"문화관광의 확장과 일상문화","sentences":["Today's cultural tourist is just as likely to be in search of 'popular', 'everyday' or 'street' culture as they are likely to visit a heritage site or a museum.","The museum seems to have lost its dominant role as a factory of meaning in (post)modern society, so cultural tourists have gone in search of meaning elsewhere.","The predominant direction of expansion has been into 'everyday life'.","Cultural tourism is as much based on experiencing as it is on seeing; therefore, Raymond Williams' definitions of culture as a whole way of life as well as the arts and learning are particularly relevant here.","Cultural tourists are also interested in the more experiential aspects of culture.","In an international context, particularly in the context of indigenous or ethnic tourism, the way of life of a people can be a central focus, where the traveller is motivated primarily by first-hand, authentic or intimate contact with people whose ethnic or cultural background is different from their own."],"abstract":"Contemporary cultural tourism has expanded beyond traditional heritage and arts venues to encompass the lived, experiential dimensions of everyday life, reflecting a broader definition of culture as a whole way of living.","topic_options":["the shift in cultural tourism from heritage and arts venues toward the experiential dimensions of everyday life","the declining relevance of museums as institutions capable of generating meaning in postmodern societies","the role of indigenous and ethnic tourism in providing authentic cross-cultural encounters for international travellers","the theoretical frameworks that scholars have used to define and categorize different forms of cultural tourism","the economic consequences of redirecting tourist attention from established heritage sites to street-level culture"],"topic_answer":1,"blank_sentence_index":3,"blank_target":"as much based on experiencing as it is on seeing","blank_options":["as much based on experiencing as it is on seeing","primarily concerned with visiting historical monuments and museums","driven mainly by a desire for passive observation and sightseeing","focused exclusively on the consumption of high culture and fine arts","defined entirely by the economic impact on local tourist destinations"],"blank_answer":1,"order_given_index":0,"order_blocks":[{"label":"B","sentence_indices":[1,2]},{"label":"C","sentence_indices":[3]},{"label":"D","sentence_indices":[4,5]}],"order_options":["(C)-(B)-(A)","(C)-(A)-(B)","(A)-(C)-(B)","(B)-(C)-(A)","(A)-(B)-(C)"],"order_answer":5,"insert_sentence":"Cultural tourists are also interested in the more experiential aspects of culture.","insert_answer":4,"summary_template":"Modern cultural tourism has expanded beyond narrow ________(A)________ tourism to embrace the experiential dimensions of everyday life, driven by tourists seeking ________(B)________ engagement with different ways of living.","summary_A_options":["museum","heritage","artistic","contemporary","cultural"],"summary_A_answer":2,"summary_B_options":["educational","authentic","effective","passive","stable"],"summary_B_answer":2,"implication_sentence_index":1,"implication_keyword":"a factory of meaning","implication_options":["an institution whose primary function was to produce and authorize the cultural significance that visitors were expected to receive","a commercial enterprise that packaged and sold cultural experiences as standardized products for mass consumption","a bureaucratic organization that processed cultural artifacts according to fixed administrative categories","a space in which visitors were passively exposed to predetermined interpretations of historical and artistic works","a system that generated cultural value by acquiring and displaying objects from diverse civilizations"],"implication_answer":1,"irrelevant_sentence_index":1},{"id":"27ST_E_24_02","difficulty":"보통","title":"스포츠와 수치화의 문화","sentences":["Although many U.S. Americans consider mathematics boring and tedious, all forms of standardized rankings involve figures and numbers.","When ranking quarterbacks, for instance, the NFL standardizes the ranking process by defining different numerical categories that cover all aspects of the position.","Each quarterback has certain numbers and figures, ranging from 'percentage of pass completions' to 'interceptions over touchdowns' to 'number of yards passed per game.'","The quarterback's livelihood depends on those numbers.","To negotiate a raise, a quarterback has to improve his numbers, and when a quarterback is benched, it is often due to unsatisfactory numbers.","Similarly, at least 13 million Americans belong to virtual football leagues in which participants select players from different professional teams; at the end of the season, the participant whose virtual team has amassed the most points wins the jackpot."],"abstract":"Despite a cultural aversion to mathematics, Americans routinely use numerical metrics to evaluate athletic performance and structure competitive activities, revealing how deeply quantification is embedded in sports culture.","topic_options":["the pervasive role of numerical metrics in American sports culture despite a general aversion to mathematics","the specific statistical categories used by the NFL to evaluate and compare the performance of quarterbacks","the economic consequences for athletes whose performance statistics fall below league expectations","the growth of fantasy sports leagues and their dependence on real-world player performance data","the contradiction between Americans' dislike of mathematics and their enthusiastic engagement with sport statistics"],"topic_answer":1,"blank_sentence_index":3,"blank_target":"depends on those numbers","blank_options":["depends on those numbers","is unrelated to statistical performance","is determined by the team's overall record","is based on seniority and contract length","is evaluated through public opinion polls"],"blank_answer":1,"order_given_index":0,"order_blocks":[{"label":"B","sentence_indices":[1,2]},{"label":"C","sentence_indices":[3,4]},{"label":"D","sentence_indices":[5]}],"order_options":["(C)-(A)-(B)","(A)-(C)-(B)","(B)-(A)-(C)","(B)-(C)-(A)","(A)-(B)-(C)"],"order_answer":5,"insert_sentence":"Similarly, at least 13 million Americans belong to virtual football leagues in which participants select players from different professional teams; at the end of the season, the participant whose virtual team has amassed the most points wins the jackpot.","insert_answer":5,"summary_template":"In American sports culture, ________(A)________ metrics serve as the primary basis for evaluating athletes and structuring competitions, revealing that quantification is deeply ________(B)________ in everyday life despite a professed dislike of mathematics.","summary_A_options":["performance","statistical","despite","numerical","cultural"],"summary_A_answer":4,"summary_B_options":["valued","accepted","effective","embedded","stable"],"summary_B_answer":4,"implication_sentence_index":3,"implication_keyword":"The quarterback's livelihood depends on those numbers","implication_options":["an athlete's professional survival and financial security are entirely determined by quantitative performance metrics","quarterbacks are paid according to a formula that directly converts statistical output into salary","the pressure of being evaluated numerically motivates quarterbacks to take greater risks during games","athletes whose statistics are poor are immediately released regardless of their contributions to team morale","the NFL's ranking system is designed primarily to serve the financial interests of team owners"],"implication_answer":1,"irrelevant_sentence_index":5},{"id":"27ST_E_25_01","difficulty":"높음","title":"효과적 교육의 질서 요건","sentences":["Teaching reflects what society itself demands; it necessitates that disorder — of students and teachers alike, of mind, behavior, and environment — yield to its opposite.","Effective teaching requires that, failing their own self-imposed order, students experience the imposition of some outer order so that inner order may develop.","This means in practice, for instance, that the goals of classes and courses be clearly set, that they be explained and justified, that the manner of achieving them be clear, that the presentation of materials conducive to reaching them be appropriate, and that all activities be directed somehow to their attainment.","Above all, it implies structured industry — study and activity that are oriented toward a goal and pursued with perseverance and method.","That is, good teaching requires that teachers and students subject themselves to external and internal control so that learning can take place."],"abstract":"Effective teaching depends on the establishment of both external and internal order — clear goals, structured activity, and student self-discipline — as conditions without which genuine learning cannot occur.","topic_options":["the necessity of both external structure and internal discipline as preconditions for effective teaching and learning","the role of clearly stated learning goals in helping students understand the purpose of their coursework","the ways in which teachers can encourage students to develop self-imposed order without external pressure","the relationship between classroom environment and the quality of student participation in learning activities","the social demands that shape the expectations placed on both teachers and students in formal education"],"topic_answer":1,"blank_sentence_index":4,"blank_target":"subject themselves to external and internal control so that learning can take place","blank_options":["subject themselves to external and internal control so that learning can take place","develop creative and independent thinking free from institutional constraints","prioritize personal fulfillment over academic achievement and discipline","challenge existing educational norms and resist standardized curricula","focus on social development rather than academic knowledge acquisition"],"blank_answer":1,"order_given_index":0,"order_blocks":[{"label":"B","sentence_indices":[1]},{"label":"C","sentence_indices":[2]},{"label":"D","sentence_indices":[3,4]}],"order_options":["(A)-(B)-(C)","(A)-(C)-(B)","(C)-(A)-(B)","(B)-(A)-(C)","(B)-(C)-(A)"],"order_answer":1,"insert_sentence":null,"insert_answer":null,"summary_template":"Good teaching requires both ________(A)________ structure — clear goals and organized instruction — and student ________(B)________ so that the conditions necessary for learning can be maintained.","summary_A_options":["flexible","external","minimal","effective","teaching"],"summary_A_answer":2,"summary_B_options":["creativity","self-discipline","motivation","stable","reliable"],"summary_B_answer":2,"implication_sentence_index":3,"implication_keyword":"structured industry","implication_options":["purposeful and methodical effort directed toward a defined learning goal rather than unfocused activity","the organized management of educational institutions in response to economic and social demands","the formal routines and administrative procedures that govern the daily operation of schools","a factory-like model of education in which students are trained to follow instructions without question","a system in which teachers design activities that are efficient enough to cover maximum content in minimum time"],"implication_answer":1,"irrelevant_sentence_index":3},{"id":"27ST_E_25_02","difficulty":"높음","title":"부정어와 뇌의 스트레스 반응","sentences":["When we lecture, scold, yell, or criticize, when we say something positive but in a sarcastic tone, or when we try to make our kids feel guilty, it activates their amygdala, triggering their stress response and putting them into a defensive, rigid, reactive state.","Even more basic, when we say no or don't, it releases stress chemicals in our kids' brains (and in ours) that are associated with fear and anger.","Functional brain imaging research has shown that even seeing the word no on a screen for less than a second while you're lying in an MRI scanner will cause your brain to suddenly release dozens of stress-producing hormones and neurotransmitters.","Conversely, positive words like yes, love, and peace activate systems in the prefrontal cortex that are related to emotional regulation.","The problem is that negative words like no and don't have a more powerful effect on kids than positive words."],"abstract":"Negative words and critical communication trigger powerful stress responses in children's brains that outweigh the effects of positive language, making the tone and word choice of adult communication a critical factor in children's emotional development.","topic_options":["the disproportionately powerful neurological impact of negative words on children compared to positive ones","the physiological mechanisms by which the amygdala processes threatening language in social interactions","the role of parental communication style in shaping the long-term emotional health of children and teenagers","the research findings that challenge common beliefs about the effectiveness of positive reinforcement in parenting","the ways in which stress hormones released during conflict interfere with children's capacity for rational thought"],"topic_answer":1,"blank_sentence_index":4,"blank_target":"a more powerful effect on kids than positive words","blank_options":["a more powerful effect on kids than positive words","a weaker impact than encouraging language on behavior","an equal influence compared to positive emotional cues","a beneficial long-term effect on self-regulation","a less significant role than tone and body language"],"blank_answer":1,"order_given_index":0,"order_blocks":[{"label":"B","sentence_indices":[1,2]},{"label":"C","sentence_indices":[3,4]},{"label":"D","sentence_indices":[5]}],"order_options":["(C)-(B)-(A)","(A)-(C)-(B)","(B)-(C)-(A)","(C)-(A)-(B)","(A)-(B)-(C)"],"order_answer":5,"insert_sentence":null,"insert_answer":null,"summary_template":"Negative words trigger stronger ________(A)________ responses in children's brains than positive words, meaning that critical communication places children in a ________(B)________ state that impairs their ability to learn and engage.","summary_A_options":["emotional","cognitive","critical","stress","communication"],"summary_A_answer":4,"summary_B_options":["passive","receptive","effective","defensive","stable"],"summary_B_answer":4,"implication_sentence_index":4,"implication_keyword":"negative words like no and don't have a more powerful effect on kids than positive words","implication_options":["children respond more strongly to language that triggers stress than to encouraging words","positive communication is equally effective as negative language in shaping behavior","children are largely unaffected by the emotional tone of the words adults use","the impact of language on children depends entirely on the context in which it is used","adults and children respond identically to both positive and negative verbal communication"],"implication_answer":1,"irrelevant_sentence_index":3},{"id":"27ST_E_25_03","difficulty":"높음","title":"자동화된 기술과 의식적 사고","sentences":["The experiences of learning to ride a bicycle or drive a car illustrate well how the 'what' and 'how' systems — those involved in object identification and practical action — might interact during development.","When we learn to drive a car, we go through a first stage where each required action and sequence of actions — such as looking in the mirror, signaling with the blinker, pressing the clutch prior to shifting into gear, and so forth — are explicitly thought of and double-checked while monitoring our situation in the environment.","Once learned and after a few hours of practice, the required actions for driving become second nature, transferable to almost any vehicle and performed without explicit thinking.","Information appears to be perceived directly; the affordances of the road, the car, and the traffic implicitly detected.","If you start to think too much about your driving, you actually increase your chances of having an accident.","People in sport competitions confirm that self-consciousness is one's worst enemy: tennis, golf, or billiard players commonly report that they lose their 'touch' by thinking too much about their moves."],"abstract":"Skilled performance depends on the automatization of learned actions, and reintroducing conscious attention to those actions disrupts the fluency that practice has established.","topic_options":["the paradox that reintroducing conscious awareness into automatized skills disrupts rather than improves their execution","the developmental stages through which learners progress when acquiring complex physical or procedural skills","the neurological differences between the brain systems responsible for conscious and unconscious motor control","the advantages of implicit learning over explicit instruction in acquiring skills that require fluid performance","the ways in which experienced practitioners in sports and driving maintain peak performance under pressure"],"topic_answer":1,"blank_sentence_index":2,"blank_target":"second nature, transferable to almost any vehicle and performed without explicit thinking","blank_options":["second nature, transferable to almost any vehicle and performed without explicit thinking","a conscious process that requires constant monitoring and deliberate control","a set of isolated skills that must be relearned for each new vehicle","increasingly complex as drivers encounter more challenging road conditions","an automatic routine that still requires focused attention and careful judgment"],"blank_answer":1,"order_given_index":0,"order_blocks":[{"label":"B","sentence_indices":[1,2]},{"label":"C","sentence_indices":[3]},{"label":"D","sentence_indices":[4,5]}],"order_options":["(C)-(A)-(B)","(C)-(B)-(A)","(B)-(C)-(A)","(A)-(B)-(C)","(A)-(C)-(B)"],"order_answer":4,"insert_sentence":"If you start to think too much about your driving, you actually increase your chances of having an accident.","insert_answer":4,"summary_template":"Skilled performance relies on the ________(A)________ of learned actions, and consciously attending to those actions once they have become automatic ________(B)________ their smooth execution.","summary_A_options":["repetition","memorization","automatization","actions","skilled"],"summary_A_answer":3,"summary_B_options":["improves","stabilizes","disrupts","effective","stable"],"summary_B_answer":3,"implication_sentence_index":5,"implication_keyword":"lose their 'touch'","implication_options":["experience a breakdown in the fluid, automatic quality of their performance when they become overly self-conscious","gradually lose the physical sensitivity required for precision movements through lack of regular practice","find that their competitive instinct diminishes as they become too analytically focused on technical details","discover that their previous training becomes irrelevant when they are placed under extreme competitive pressure","report a decline in confidence that spreads from one aspect of their performance to all others"],"implication_answer":1,"irrelevant_sentence_index":4},{"id":"27ST_E_26_01","difficulty":"높음","title":"맥락이 예술 작품에 부여하는 의미","sentences":["In the context of a studio visit, the viewer might notice several clipped newspaper articles pinned to the wall, a wax-coated hotplate, walls with paint marks, resin-drizzled floors and several sculptures barely visible through their plastic wrap.","Such real-world clues offer the visitor a foothold onto the artist's oeuvre.","Similarly, guests experiencing artworks in some homes notice art positioned next to furnishings, family photographs displayed on the piano and coffee-table books stacked to demonstrate preferences.","Together, these components affect particular experiences.","Within the artist's studio or collector's home, residue from studio activities or the collector's personal belongings help to connect the artworks to the world.","By contrast, artworks displayed in exhibitions feel comparatively isolated, practically clipped from the world where they originated.","This could explain why aestheticians tend to treat artworks as singletons, rather than as members of some set."],"abstract":"The meaning of an artwork is shaped by the contextual environment surrounding it — studio clues, domestic objects, personal belongings — and artworks displayed in isolation lose the relational richness that gives them their fullest significance.","topic_options":["the way contextual surroundings enrich the meaning of artworks and how their removal into exhibitions impoverishes that meaning","the role of studio visits in helping art collectors develop a deeper appreciation of an artist's creative process","the difference between the private experience of art in homes and the public experience in galleries and museums","the tendency of aestheticians to study artworks in isolation rather than in relation to the environments that produced them","the ways in which personal objects and domestic furnishings influence how visitors interpret the artworks near them"],"topic_answer":1,"blank_sentence_index":5,"blank_target":"practically clipped from the world where they originated","blank_options":["practically clipped from the world where they originated","deeply connected to the cultural context of their creation","enriched by the diverse interpretations of museum visitors","carefully preserved within their original historical setting","presented in a way that reveals their full artistic meaning"],"blank_answer":1,"order_given_index":0,"order_blocks":[{"label":"B","sentence_indices":[1,2]},{"label":"C","sentence_indices":[3]},{"label":"D","sentence_indices":[4,5,6]}],"order_options":["(C)-(A)-(B)","(B)-(A)-(C)","(C)-(B)-(A)","(A)-(C)-(B)","(A)-(B)-(C)"],"order_answer":5,"insert_sentence":"Together, these components affect particular experiences.","insert_answer":3,"summary_template":"Artworks acquire richer meaning when surrounded by ________(A)________ context such as studio objects or personal belongings, whereas exhibition settings ________(B)________ them from the world that gave them significance.","summary_A_options":["biographical","decorative","meaning","contextual","artwork"],"summary_A_answer":4,"summary_B_options":["liberate","transform","effective","isolate","stable"],"summary_B_answer":4,"implication_sentence_index":1,"implication_keyword":"a foothold onto the artist's oeuvre","implication_options":["a concrete point of entry that allows the viewer to begin constructing an understanding of the artist's broader work","a physical support that helps visitors navigate the often disorienting spatial layout of a working studio","a privileged perspective available only to those who have direct personal access to the artist's private space","a visual anchor that stabilizes the viewer's attention amid the overwhelming quantity of objects in the studio","a clue left deliberately by the artist to guide visitors toward the correct interpretation of the displayed work"],"implication_answer":1,"irrelevant_sentence_index":3},{"id":"27ST_E_26_02","difficulty":"높음","title":"의사소통과 문화적 해석의 차이","sentences":["Linguists typically distinguish between signals that are communicative and those that are informative, depending on whether the information is conveyed intentionally or not.","For example, a deliberate wink is distinguished from an involuntary blink by the communicative intention that lies behind it.","Yet in intercultural interaction, information conveyed unintentionally may actually be interpreted as intentional; for instance, in some cultures, showing the soles of one's shoes can communicate an insult and when somebody does that, it is typically assumed to have communicative intent.","In other words, a given piece of behaviour may be communicative to some of the participants and only informative to others."],"abstract":"The distinction between communicative and informative signals breaks down in intercultural interaction, where behaviors that are unintentional for one cultural group may be interpreted as intentional and meaningful by another.","topic_options":["the breakdown of the communicative-informative distinction in intercultural contexts where unintentional acts are misread as deliberate","the linguistic principles used to classify signals as communicative or informative in theoretical models of language","the cultural conventions that determine which physical gestures are considered insulting in different social contexts","the challenges that intercultural misunderstandings pose for diplomatic and professional communication","the reasons why intercultural communication requires more conscious effort than communication within a single culture"],"topic_answer":1,"blank_sentence_index":0,"blank_target":"depending on whether the information is conveyed intentionally or not","blank_options":["depending on whether the information is conveyed intentionally or not","based on whether the message is expressed verbally or nonverbally","according to the cultural background of the person sending the signal","determined by whether the signal is understood by the receiver","classified by the emotional content of the information being shared"],"blank_answer":1,"order_given_index":0,"order_blocks":[{"label":"B","sentence_indices":[1]},{"label":"C","sentence_indices":[2]},{"label":"D","sentence_indices":[3]}],"order_options":["(B)-(C)-(A)","(C)-(B)-(A)","(B)-(A)-(C)","(A)-(B)-(C)","(C)-(A)-(B)"],"order_answer":4,"insert_sentence":null,"insert_answer":null,"summary_template":"In intercultural interaction, ________(A)________ behavior can be misread as deliberate communication, meaning that the same act may be ________(B)________ to one cultural group and merely informative to another.","summary_A_options":["offensive","ambiguous","distinction","between","unintentional"],"summary_A_answer":5,"summary_B_options":["insulting","meaningful","effective","stable","communicative"],"summary_B_answer":5,"implication_sentence_index":1,"implication_keyword":"a deliberate wink is distinguished from an involuntary blink by the communicative intention that lies behind it","implication_options":["the same physical action carries entirely different significance depending on whether it is performed with intent to convey a message","people are generally able to distinguish intentional from unintentional signals without conscious effort in familiar cultural contexts","the meaning of a gesture is determined more by social convention than by the physical form the gesture takes","intentional communication is always more effective than unintentional signals at conveying the speaker's true feelings","cultural training is necessary before individuals can reliably interpret the communicative signals of others"],"implication_answer":1,"irrelevant_sentence_index":2},{"id":"27ST_E_26_03","difficulty":"보통","title":"서사와 공감 능력의 발달","sentences":["Through stories we can explore the human condition and see how other people think.","This can affirm our own beliefs and perceptions, but it also challenges them.","Regardless of the language, there is something universal about what occurs in the brain at the point when we are processing narratives, triggering better self-awareness and empathy for others.","Psychologists scanned people listening to narratives in English, Farsi, and Mandarin, and found the same patterns of brain activation when people found meaning in the stories.","And the more absorbed in a story a reader is, the more empathetically they behave in real life.","For instance, if the researcher 'accidentally' dropped his pens, those participants who had previously reported being 'highly absorbed' in the story were about twice as likely to help pick up the pens.","Another study concluded that literary fiction 'uniquely engages the psychological processes needed to gain access to characters' subjective experiences.'","That is to say, if you read novels, you can probably read emotions, vital skills for forming cooperative societies."],"abstract":"Engaging with narrative fiction activates universal brain processes that enhance empathy and self-awareness, with deeper absorption in stories producing measurably more prosocial behavior in real life.","topic_options":["the universal neurological and behavioral effects of narrative engagement on empathy and prosocial conduct","the cross-cultural similarities in brain activation patterns observed when people process stories in different languages","the specific ways in which literary fiction differs from other forms of storytelling in developing emotional intelligence","the research methods psychologists use to measure the relationship between reading habits and empathetic behavior","the role of narrative absorption in determining how deeply a story influences a reader's real-world attitudes"],"topic_answer":1,"blank_sentence_index":6,"blank_target":"uniquely engages the psychological processes needed to gain access to characters' subjective experiences","blank_options":["uniquely engages the psychological processes needed to gain access to characters' subjective experiences","primarily serves as a source of entertainment with limited cognitive benefits","has a weaker effect on empathy than nonfiction or factual narratives","relies on superficial emotional responses rather than deep psychological engagement","focuses on plot development at the expense of character depth and interiority"],"blank_answer":1,"order_given_index":0,"order_blocks":[{"label":"B","sentence_indices":[1,2]},{"label":"C","sentence_indices":[3,4]},{"label":"D","sentence_indices":[5,6,7]}],"order_options":["(B)-(C)-(A)","(A)-(B)-(C)","(B)-(A)-(C)","(C)-(A)-(B)","(A)-(C)-(B)"],"order_answer":2,"insert_sentence":"And the more absorbed in a story a reader is, the more empathetically they behave in real life.","insert_answer":4,"summary_template":"Reading fiction universally activates brain processes that enhance ________(A)________, and the deeper a reader's absorption in a story, the more ________(B)________ their behavior becomes in real-life social situations.","summary_A_options":["empathy","creativity","self-awareness","engaging","narrative"],"summary_A_answer":1,"summary_B_options":["prosocial","cooperative","effective","stable","reflective"],"summary_B_answer":1,"implication_sentence_index":7,"implication_keyword":"read emotions","implication_options":["accurately perceive and interpret the feelings and inner states of other people in social interactions","analyze the emotional content of written texts with the same precision applied to factual information","identify the emotional tone of a conversation and adjust one's own response accordingly","recognize and label one's own emotional experiences with the vocabulary developed through literary exposure","detect hidden emotional signals in others' behavior that untrained observers would typically overlook"],"implication_answer":1,"irrelevant_sentence_index":6},{"id":"27ST_E_27_01","difficulty":"높음","title":"디지털 정치와 사회운동의 한계","sentences":["Over the past twenty years, with the arrival of digital politics, social and political protest movements have changed and become ever more prominent through what the sociologist Manuel Castells has called Networks of Outrage and Hope.","We now have a swirling world of 'online activism', digital rebellion, information politics and People's Platforms.","Smartphones and social networking now provide a more fluid, leaderless, participatory activism that arises more spontaneously.","The early examples like the Occupy Movement, the Arab Spring in Egypt, the Umbrella Movement in Hong Kong, the Gezi Park Movement in Turkey, and the Pussy Riots in Russia galvanized large numbers of people and attracted world attention.","While some suggest that these new politics are enhancing democracy, others maintain that they do not really challenge the dominant power groups.","There seems a limit to the power of new social movements."],"abstract":"Although digital technology has enabled more spontaneous and participatory forms of political activism, most of these movements have ultimately failed to challenge entrenched power structures, revealing the limits of networked protest.","topic_options":["the limitations of digitally enabled social movements in producing lasting political change against established power","the ways in which smartphones and social media have transformed the organizational structure of protest movements","the reasons why leaderless movements tend to attract greater public attention than those with centralized leadership","the role of state repression in determining the ultimate success or failure of popular protest movements","the theoretical debate between those who see digital activism as democratizing and those who see it as ineffective"],"topic_answer":1,"blank_sentence_index":2,"blank_target":"a more fluid, leaderless, participatory activism that arises more spontaneously","blank_options":["a more fluid, leaderless, participatory activism that arises more spontaneously","a more organized and hierarchical form of political resistance","a more cautious and legally compliant approach to political change","a more exclusive and elite-driven model of civic engagement","a more passive and individualistic response to political issues"],"blank_answer":1,"order_given_index":0,"order_blocks":[{"label":"B","sentence_indices":[1,2]},{"label":"C","sentence_indices":[3,4]},{"label":"D","sentence_indices":[5]}],"order_options":["(B)-(A)-(C)","(A)-(B)-(C)","(C)-(A)-(B)","(C)-(B)-(A)","(A)-(C)-(B)"],"order_answer":2,"insert_sentence":"There seems a limit to the power of new social movements.","insert_answer":5,"summary_template":"Digital technology has enabled more ________(A)________ and spontaneous forms of political activism, but most such movements have been ________(B)________ by the state without achieving lasting change.","summary_A_options":["visible","emotional","although","participatory","digital"],"summary_A_answer":4,"summary_B_options":["ignored","absorbed","effective","suppressed","stable"],"summary_B_answer":4,"implication_sentence_index":5,"implication_keyword":"There seems a limit to the power of new social movements","implication_options":["digital activism, despite its scale and visibility, has repeatedly failed to translate popular mobilization into structural political change","social movements that rely on online platforms are inherently less capable of sustaining engagement than those with physical presence","the novelty of digital protest tools eventually wears off, reducing their effectiveness with each successive wave of activism","governments have become so skilled at monitoring online activism that it is now impossible to organize effective resistance digitally","the decentralized nature of online movements prevents them from developing the coherent demands needed to negotiate with power"],"implication_answer":1,"irrelevant_sentence_index":2},{"id":"27ST_E_27_02","difficulty":"보통","title":"자동차와 교외화","sentences":["The advent of automobiles drastically altered urban landscapes by enabling the growth of suburbs.","Cars provided individuals the ability to live farther from city centers, where land was cheaper and more abundant.","This expansion created the modern suburb, characterized by residential zones separate from commercial and industrial areas, promoting a shift from high-density urban living to the spacious suburbs.","The flexibility cars offered meant people could commute daily, uniting work, leisure, and homelife in new ways.","In response, urban planning evolved, placing emphasis on roads and highways to accommodate increased travel.","The sprawling growth fueled demands for expanded infrastructure and services in these areas, bringing in new economic opportunities.","Cars were instrumental in shaping this living model by significantly detaching home locations from places of employment and recreation."],"abstract":"The automobile transformed urban geography by making it economically viable to live at a distance from city centers, giving rise to the modern suburb and fundamentally reshaping how people relate their homes to their workplaces and daily activities.","topic_options":["the automobile's role in enabling suburban expansion by separating residential life from workplaces and urban centers","the economic factors that made suburban land more attractive to families than expensive city-center housing","the ways in which road construction and highway development changed the physical layout of American cities","the relationship between car ownership rates and the rate of urban sprawl in twentieth-century Western societies","the environmental consequences of suburban expansion driven by widespread personal automobile ownership"],"topic_answer":1,"blank_sentence_index":0,"blank_target":"by enabling the growth of suburbs","blank_options":["by enabling the growth of suburbs","by reducing the population density of city centers","by improving the efficiency of public transportation systems","by creating new economic opportunities in rural areas","by encouraging the construction of high-rise urban housing"],"blank_answer":1,"order_given_index":0,"order_blocks":[{"label":"B","sentence_indices":[1,2]},{"label":"C","sentence_indices":[3,4]},{"label":"D","sentence_indices":[5,6]}],"order_options":["(A)-(B)-(C)","(C)-(A)-(B)","(B)-(C)-(A)","(B)-(A)-(C)","(C)-(B)-(A)"],"order_answer":1,"insert_sentence":"The sprawling growth fueled demands for expanded infrastructure and services in these areas, bringing in new economic opportunities.","insert_answer":5,"summary_template":"Automobiles enabled people to live at greater ________(A)________ from city centers, giving rise to the modern suburb and fundamentally reshaping urban ________(B)________ by separating home, work, and recreation.","summary_A_options":["costs","speeds","automobile","distances","transformed"],"summary_A_answer":4,"summary_B_options":["planning","economy","effective","geography","stable"],"summary_B_answer":4,"implication_sentence_index":3,"implication_keyword":"uniting work, leisure, and homelife in new ways","implication_options":["integrating the previously separate domains of daily existence into flexible arrangements made possible by personal mobility","allowing individuals to pursue professional, recreational, and domestic activities simultaneously without compromise","enabling families to distribute their time between urban and suburban environments according to daily needs","creating new social patterns in which the boundaries between professional and personal life became less defined","making it possible for individuals to maintain connections to urban culture while enjoying the space of suburban living"],"implication_answer":1,"irrelevant_sentence_index":3},{"id":"27ST_E_28_01","difficulty":"보통","title":"사바나 가설과 환경 선호","sentences":["People like pictures of the savanna, even if they have never been there.","In one study, people of different ages looked at images of tropical forests, deciduous forests, coniferous forests, deserts, and the East African savanna.","Eight-year-old children said that they would like to live in or visit the savanna more than any other environment.","After the age of 15, people also liked deciduous and coniferous forests.","Since none of these people had visited savannas, the implication is that this preference was programmed into their brains.","This programmed preference is called 'the savanna hypothesis.'","As people get older, this preference gets modified by where they have lived.","They showed that young children in Austria prefer landscapes thinly dotted with trees and with low mountains, scenes that resemble the savanna.","After puberty, their preferences shifted to areas with denser trees and higher mountains, again, presumably, because of more experience with these terrains."],"abstract":"Children across cultures show an innate preference for savanna-like landscapes that is genetically programmed, though this preference is gradually modified by personal experience of different environments as they grow older.","topic_options":["the innate preference for savanna landscapes that is genetically programmed in humans but modified by experience over time","the cross-cultural research methods used to identify universal patterns in human aesthetic preferences for natural environments","the role of evolutionary psychology in explaining why certain landscape types are more appealing than others","the ways in which childhood exposure to natural environments shapes long-term preferences for specific landscape types","the differences in landscape preferences between children and adults and the developmental reasons behind them"],"topic_answer":1,"blank_sentence_index":4,"blank_target":"programmed into their brains","blank_options":["programmed into their brains","learned through cultural transmission","shaped by individual childhood experiences","influenced by parental preferences and values","determined by geographic location and climate"],"blank_answer":1,"order_given_index":0,"order_blocks":[{"label":"B","sentence_indices":[1,2,3]},{"label":"C","sentence_indices":[4,5,6]},{"label":"D","sentence_indices":[7,8]}],"order_options":["(A)-(B)-(C)","(C)-(B)-(A)","(A)-(C)-(B)","(B)-(A)-(C)","(C)-(A)-(B)"],"order_answer":1,"insert_sentence":"They showed that young children in Austria prefer landscapes thinly dotted with trees and with low mountains, scenes that resemble the savanna.","insert_answer":7,"summary_template":"Humans appear to have an ________(A)________ preference for savanna-like landscapes, but this preference becomes ________(B)________ by personal environmental experience as individuals grow older.","summary_A_options":["learned","cultural","preference","children","innate"],"summary_A_answer":5,"summary_B_options":["reinforced","eliminated","effective","stable","modified"],"summary_B_answer":5,"implication_sentence_index":4,"implication_keyword":"this preference was programmed into their brains","implication_options":["the landscape preference is encoded in human biology independently of any personal or cultural experience","children's brains are more receptive to environmental stimuli than those of adults due to developmental plasticity","the preference for open spaces was deliberately cultivated through early childhood exposure to nature documentaries","genetic programming determines all aesthetic preferences including those for music, art, and natural scenery","the savanna preference is a direct product of formal education about human evolutionary origins"],"implication_answer":1,"irrelevant_sentence_index":4},{"id":"27ST_E_28_02","difficulty":"높음","title":"꿈 기억의 출처 모니터링","sentences":["Dreamers find it difficult to determine whether a memory is from a dream or some other source after time has passed, known as 'source monitoring.'","It is difficult to distinguish between memories of real dreams and made-up ones, imagination or stories someone else told us.","Dream source monitoring was found to be less accurate than other memory source monitoring.","A cognitive psychologist, Marcia K. Johnson and her colleagues' explanation is that 'real dreams are deficient in information about cognitive operations that help identify the self-generations we create when we are awake.'","Although dreams are usually more vivid than imagination, the cognitive operations that generate imagining are also remembered.","Dream generation, in contrast, is 'transparent' in that we don't experience the generation process, making it more difficult to source monitor."],"abstract":"Dreams are harder to source-monitor than waking thoughts because the cognitive process of generating them is invisible to the dreamer, leaving memories without the markers of intentionality that distinguish waking imagination from perception.","topic_options":["the difficulty of source-monitoring dream memories due to the invisible nature of the dream generation process","the neurological differences between the brain states associated with dreaming and those associated with imagination","the ways in which the vividness of dream imagery makes dream memories more compelling than those of waking thought","the research methods cognitive psychologists use to measure the accuracy of memory source monitoring in different contexts","the reasons why people are more likely to confuse dream memories with real events than with imagined ones"],"topic_answer":1,"blank_sentence_index":5,"blank_target":"'transparent' in that we don't experience the generation process","blank_options":["'transparent' in that we don't experience the generation process","'vivid' in that it produces stronger and clearer mental images than waking thought","'reliable' in that it provides accurate records of real emotional experiences","'controlled' in that the dreamer can direct the content and narrative of dreams","'structured' in that it follows a logical sequence similar to conscious reasoning"],"blank_answer":1,"order_given_index":0,"order_blocks":[{"label":"B","sentence_indices":[1,2]},{"label":"C","sentence_indices":[3,4]},{"label":"D","sentence_indices":[5]}],"order_options":["(B)-(C)-(A)","(C)-(A)-(B)","(C)-(B)-(A)","(A)-(B)-(C)","(B)-(A)-(C)"],"order_answer":4,"insert_sentence":"Dream generation, in contrast, is 'transparent' in that we don't experience the generation process, making it more difficult to source monitor.","insert_answer":5,"summary_template":"Dream memories are harder to ________(A)________ than waking memories because the generation of dreams is cognitively ________(B)________, leaving no markers of intentionality that would allow the dreamer to identify their origin.","summary_A_options":["recall","source-monitor","verify","waking","dreams"],"summary_A_answer":2,"summary_B_options":["vivid","transparent","automatic","effective","stable"],"summary_B_answer":2,"implication_sentence_index":5,"implication_keyword":"transparent","implication_options":["invisible to conscious awareness — the dreamer has no access to the process that produced the dream content","clear and easy to recall because the dream images are more vivid than ordinary waking perceptions","honest and undistorted in the sense that dreams reflect the dreamer's true feelings without conscious editing","straightforward to interpret because the symbolic content of dreams directly represents the dreamer's concerns","open to external observation in ways that waking thoughts are not due to their expression in physical behavior"],"implication_answer":1,"irrelevant_sentence_index":4},{"id":"27ST_E_28_03","difficulty":"높음","title":"자기 보호적 이야기와 성공·실패","sentences":["Much research in social psychology has documented some of the key strategies that people rely upon in defending the belief 'I am good.'","For example, when people perform poorly at something, they tend to trivialize their failures.","This trivialization disarms those failures and prevents them from overwriting their life stories.","Imagine, say, that someone fails a calculus test.","A common defensive response is to conclude that this test was just not that important to them.","They may say to themselves, 'Who cares about calculus anyway. I'm not going to become a mathematician.'","So if someone aces a calculus test, they may think to themselves about how crucial calculus is for their future career success.","By titrating how importantly people view their successes and failures, they can shape their emotional reactions to these events in a way that enables them to tell a more convincing story that 'I am good.'"],"abstract":"People protect their self-concept by systematically minimizing the importance of their failures and exaggerating the significance of their successes, constructing a self-serving narrative that sustains the belief that they are fundamentally good.","topic_options":["the self-serving strategy of minimizing failures and amplifying successes to sustain a positive self-narrative","the social psychological research methods used to measure how people respond to failure in academic settings","the ways in which defensive self-perception prevents individuals from learning effectively from their mistakes","the relationship between self-esteem and the tendency to attribute success to personal ability and failure to external causes","the role of storytelling in helping people construct coherent identities from the disjointed events of their lives"],"topic_answer":1,"blank_sentence_index":0,"blank_target":"defending the belief","blank_options":["defending the belief","challenging the notion","questioning the validity","undermining the concept","supporting the idea"],"blank_answer":1,"order_given_index":0,"order_blocks":[{"label":"B","sentence_indices":[1,2,3]},{"label":"C","sentence_indices":[4,5]},{"label":"D","sentence_indices":[6,7,8]}],"order_options":["(B)-(A)-(C)","(A)-(B)-(C)","(C)-(A)-(B)","(C)-(B)-(A)","(A)-(C)-(B)"],"order_answer":2,"insert_sentence":"So if someone aces a calculus test, they may think to themselves about how crucial calculus is for their future career success.","insert_answer":6,"summary_template":"People protect the belief that they are good by ________(A)________ their failures and exaggerating their successes, a strategy that allows them to construct a ________(B)________ self-narrative.","summary_A_options":["forgetting","trivializing","reframing","self","people"],"summary_A_answer":2,"summary_B_options":["accurate","self-serving","consistent","effective","stable"],"summary_B_answer":2,"implication_sentence_index":2,"implication_keyword":"prevents them from overwriting their life stories","implication_options":["stops failures from undermining the positive self-narrative the individual has constructed about who they are","protects the individual's memories from being distorted by the emotional intensity of disappointing outcomes","prevents a single failure from reducing a person's motivation to pursue goals that matter to them","blocks negative experiences from permanently altering the behavioral patterns the individual has established","keeps the individual from reinterpreting their past in ways that would make future effort seem pointless"],"implication_answer":1,"irrelevant_sentence_index":6},{"id":"27ST_E_29_01","difficulty":"높음","title":"법의 접근성과 일상적 이해","sentences":["Along with the mistaken notion that the law resides in the books goes the equally mistaken idea that law is secret, or at least inaccessible to the ordinary person.","To understand and apply the law at the advanced, technical level that lawyers do requires professional knowledge, but to understand the basic substance of the law does not.","Law reflects life.","The principles and issues embodied in the law are not different from those that we experience in other aspects of our lives.","Contract law, for example, is a commentary on the way people make, interpret, keep, and break their promises in commercial and noncommercial settings.","If you cross your fingers when you make a promise, does it mean that the promise doesn't count?","If your newly purchased television doesn't work, can you return it to the store?","And so on."],"abstract":"The belief that law is inaccessible to ordinary people is mistaken, because legal principles are grounded in the same everyday experiences of promises, fairness, and obligation that non-lawyers already understand intuitively.","topic_options":["the mistaken belief that law is inaccessible to ordinary people, and how legal principles reflect everyday human experience","the professional training required to apply legal knowledge at an advanced level in courtroom and advisory settings","the relationship between written legal codes and the informal social norms that govern everyday behavior","the ways in which contract law protects individuals from the consequences of broken promises in commercial transactions","the reasons why legal literacy is an important skill for citizens to develop in democratic societies"],"topic_answer":1,"blank_sentence_index":1,"blank_target":"to understand the basic substance of the law does not","blank_options":["to understand the basic substance of the law does not","to comply with legal requirements in everyday transactions is impossible","to navigate the court system without professional assistance is straightforward","to interpret complex legal documents requires advanced academic training","to access legal information requires expensive professional consultation"],"blank_answer":1,"order_given_index":0,"order_blocks":[{"label":"B","sentence_indices":[1,2]},{"label":"C","sentence_indices":[3,4]},{"label":"D","sentence_indices":[5,6,7]}],"order_options":["(B)-(C)-(A)","(C)-(A)-(B)","(A)-(B)-(C)","(C)-(B)-(A)","(B)-(A)-(C)"],"order_answer":3,"insert_sentence":"If you cross your fingers when you make a promise, does it mean that the promise doesn't count?","insert_answer":5,"summary_template":"The idea that law is ________(A)________ to ordinary people is false; legal principles are grounded in the same everyday experiences of promises and fairness that non-lawyers already ________(B)________ intuitively.","summary_A_options":["irrelevant","inaccessible","complex","belief","ordinary"],"summary_A_answer":2,"summary_B_options":["question","understand","effective","apply","stable"],"summary_B_answer":2,"implication_sentence_index":2,"implication_keyword":"Law reflects life","implication_options":["legal principles are derived from and remain grounded in the same experiences, values, and conflicts that shape everyday human existence","the legal system is designed to adapt to changing social conditions by incorporating new norms as they emerge","lawyers draw on personal life experience as much as formal training when making judgments in complex cases","the law is a mirror that reveals the moral values of the society that created it at any given historical moment","legal texts are written in language that is deliberately accessible so that ordinary citizens can understand their rights"],"implication_answer":1,"irrelevant_sentence_index":2},{"id":"27ST_E_29_02","difficulty":"높음","title":"인터넷과 패션 소비의 변화","sentences":["The internet has transformed the fashion marketplace, making it increasingly difficult to predict the demand for the selling season.","Consumers can browse for product information and prices and gain comparative information almost instantaneously, making them more informed than ever before, transferring the balance of power from the retailer to the customer.","This is exacerbated by open and real-time access to fashion shows, facilitated through livestreaming, coupled with social media access to celebrity looks and lifestyles.","The traditional two-season offer is no longer seen as enough, with consumers demanding new products throughout the whole year.","This creates a problem for fashion retailers as many consumers are looking for more exclusive pieces to differentiate themselves, forcing up the desire for trend-led ever more rapidly changing styles, while still demanding affordable prices."],"abstract":"The internet has shifted power from fashion retailers to consumers by enabling instant access to information and trend content, driving demand for continuous novelty and personalized style at affordable prices that retailers struggle to meet.","topic_options":["the internet's role in shifting power from fashion retailers to consumers by enabling instant information access and fueling demand for constant novelty","the ways in which social media celebrities have replaced traditional fashion authorities as the primary influencers of consumer taste","the economic pressures that force fast fashion retailers to accelerate production cycles to meet continuously shifting consumer demands","the tension between consumers' desire for exclusive, trend-led pieces and their simultaneous expectation of affordable pricing","the impact of livestreamed fashion shows on the speed at which new trends reach mainstream consumer markets"],"topic_answer":1,"blank_sentence_index":0,"blank_target":"increasingly difficult to predict the demand for the selling season","blank_options":["increasingly difficult to predict the demand for the selling season","more profitable due to the rise of global e-commerce platforms","more transparent as consumers gain access to supply chain information","increasingly dominated by a small number of luxury fashion houses","more sustainable as ethical consumption becomes a mainstream trend"],"blank_answer":1,"order_given_index":0,"order_blocks":[{"label":"B","sentence_indices":[1]},{"label":"C","sentence_indices":[2]},{"label":"D","sentence_indices":[3,4]}],"order_options":["(B)-(A)-(C)","(C)-(B)-(A)","(B)-(C)-(A)","(A)-(B)-(C)","(C)-(A)-(B)"],"order_answer":4,"insert_sentence":null,"insert_answer":null,"summary_template":"The internet has ________(A)________ power from retailers to consumers by providing instant access to trend information, driving demand for continuous novelty and creating a ________(B)________ that retailers struggle to satisfy profitably.","summary_A_options":["removed","distributed","retailers","internet","transferred"],"summary_A_answer":5,"summary_B_options":["opportunity","competition","effective","stable","dilemma"],"summary_B_answer":5,"implication_sentence_index":2,"implication_keyword":"livestreaming","implication_options":["real-time online broadcasting that gives consumers instant access to fashion events","the traditional practice of displaying new fashion collections in physical stores","a system for delivering clothing purchases directly to consumers' homes","a method of creating fashion content exclusively for professional designers","the process of manufacturing garments in facilities located near consumers"],"implication_answer":1,"irrelevant_sentence_index":3},{"id":"27ST_E_29_03","difficulty":"보통","title":"환경적 인종차별과 레드라이닝","sentences":["What deeply affected so many Black communities globally was not only that they could not metaphorically breathe because of the oppressive forms and limits of white supremacy, but also that so many Black communities literally cannot breathe because of environmental racism.","Similarly to Black communities in the UK, Black Americans are also more likely to live near landfills, industrial plants and fossil-fuel infrastructure.","This process means that fossil-fuelled power plants and hazardous-waste facilities are disproportionately and deliberately situated in Black or ethnic-minority neighbourhoods.","As a result of this, Black Americans are three times more likely to die from exposure to air pollutants than their white counterparts."],"abstract":"Environmental racism, specifically the practice of redlining, deliberately concentrates hazardous infrastructure in Black and minority communities, producing severe and measurable health disparities that compound the broader impacts of racial inequality.","topic_options":["the deliberate placement of hazardous infrastructure in Black communities through redlining and its deadly health consequences","the historical origins of redlining as a financial practice and its subsequent expansion into environmental policy","the international dimensions of environmental racism and the similarities between Black communities in different countries","the legal frameworks that have been developed to address the disproportionate environmental burdens borne by minority communities","the relationship between air pollution exposure and mortality rates across different racial and socioeconomic groups"],"topic_answer":1,"blank_sentence_index":3,"blank_target":"three times more likely to die from exposure to air pollutants","blank_options":["three times more likely to die from exposure to air pollutants","equally affected by environmental hazards regardless of income level","better protected by federal regulations than other minority communities","less likely to suffer long-term health consequences from industrial pollution","more aware of environmental risks than the general population"],"blank_answer":1,"order_given_index":0,"order_blocks":[],"order_options":["(C)-(A)-(B)","(B)-(A)-(C)","(C)-(B)-(A)","(A)-(B)-(C)","(A)-(C)-(B)"],"order_answer":4,"insert_sentence":null,"insert_answer":null,"summary_template":"Redlining is the deliberate practice of placing ________(A)________ infrastructure near Black and minority communities, resulting in disproportionate exposure to pollutants and making environmental racism a direct contributor to racial ________(B)________.","summary_A_options":["industrial","fossil-fuel","hazardous","environmental","racism"],"summary_A_answer":3,"summary_B_options":["injustice","segregation","inequality","effective","stable"],"summary_B_answer":3,"implication_sentence_index":0,"implication_keyword":"could not metaphorically breathe","implication_options":["experienced the suffocating oppression of systemic racial inequality that denied them freedom and dignity","felt overwhelmed by the psychological burden of living under constant surveillance and social exclusion","were unable to express their cultural identity freely due to the restrictions imposed by white-dominated institutions","struggled to survive economically in environments where opportunities were systematically withheld from them","found it impossible to participate in civic life due to legal barriers that denied them basic rights"],"implication_answer":1,"irrelevant_sentence_index":2},{"id":"27ST_E_30_01","difficulty":"보통","title":"식이 절제의 원칙","sentences":["Not too much or too little — that's what moderation means.","Moderation does not mean that you have to eliminate low-nutrient-density foods from your diet, such as soft drinks and candy, but rather that you can include them occasionally.","Moderation entails not taking anything to extremes.","You probably have heard that vitamin C has positive effects, but that doesn't mean huge doses of this essential nutrient are appropriate for you.","For example, the body needs zinc for hundreds of chemical reactions, including those that support normal growth, development, and immune function.","Too much zinc, however, can cause deficiency of copper, another essential mineral, which can lead to damaged immune function.","Being moderate in your diet means that you do not restrict or completely eliminate any one type of food, but rather that all types of food can fit into a healthful diet."],"abstract":"Dietary moderation means neither eliminating any food entirely nor consuming any in excess, since even nutritionally beneficial substances can become harmful when taken in extreme quantities.","topic_options":["the principle of dietary moderation as avoiding all extremes, since even beneficial substances become harmful in excess","the specific nutritional guidelines that define appropriate portion sizes for different categories of food and drink","the reasons why restricting entire food groups from one's diet is counterproductive to achieving long-term health goals","the scientific evidence showing that vitamins and minerals produce diminishing returns when consumed above recommended levels","the ways in which the concept of moderation applies to lifestyle choices beyond diet, including exercise and sleep"],"topic_answer":1,"blank_sentence_index":1,"blank_target":"you can include them occasionally","blank_options":["you can include them occasionally","you must completely avoid all processed foods","you should track every calorie you consume daily","you are required to substitute them with healthier options","you need to limit all sources of added sugar and salt"],"blank_answer":1,"order_given_index":0,"order_blocks":[{"label":"B","sentence_indices":[1,2]},{"label":"C","sentence_indices":[3]},{"label":"D","sentence_indices":[4,5,6]}],"order_options":["(C)-(B)-(A)","(A)-(B)-(C)","(C)-(A)-(B)","(B)-(A)-(C)","(B)-(C)-(A)"],"order_answer":2,"insert_sentence":"For example, the body needs zinc for hundreds of chemical reactions, including those that support normal growth, development, and immune function.","insert_answer":4,"summary_template":"Dietary ________(A)________ means avoiding all extremes — neither eliminating any food entirely nor consuming any substance excessively — because even ________(B)________ nutrients can become harmful when taken in large quantities.","summary_A_options":["moderation","balance","restriction","dietary","means"],"summary_A_answer":1,"summary_B_options":["beneficial","essential","natural","effective","stable"],"summary_B_answer":1,"implication_sentence_index":0,"implication_keyword":"Not too much or too little","implication_options":["the optimal approach to diet lies in maintaining a balanced middle ground that avoids both excess and deprivation","the quality of food is less important than ensuring that intake falls within a narrow range of recommended quantities","dietary health is achieved by carefully measuring all food intake against standardized nutritional benchmarks","both overeating and undereating are equally harmful and should be treated as medical conditions requiring intervention","a healthy diet requires constant adjustment to ensure that no single nutrient ever exceeds its recommended daily allowance"],"implication_answer":1,"irrelevant_sentence_index":3},{"id":"27ST_E_30_02","difficulty":"보통","title":"식이 행동의 자동적 반응","sentences":["Dietary behaviors are, in large part, the consequence of automatic responses to a particular situation with food, many of which lead to increased caloric consumption and poor dietary choices.","Individuals are subject to inherent cognitive limitations and mostly lack the capacity to consistently recognize, ignore, or resist contextual cues that encourage eating.","Take, for example, going to the movies.","For many, a night at the movies also means sharing popcorn, candy, and soda.","People often cannot resist this learned indulgence and are encouraged by the environment to eat a particular food.","Another example is eating potato chips or peanuts that have been set out during a friendly card game or conversation with others.","Individuals often consume snacks not because they are hungry, but because they are prompted by the social environment, which encourages them to eat.","Grocery stores often use placement of items to encourage impulse buying."],"abstract":"Most eating behavior is driven not by hunger but by automatic responses to environmental and social cues that individuals lack the cognitive capacity to consistently recognize or resist.","topic_options":["the automatic nature of eating behavior driven by environmental and social cues that people lack the capacity to consistently resist","the marketing strategies used by food retailers to exploit consumers' cognitive limitations and encourage impulse buying","the role of social context in determining when and how much people eat regardless of their actual hunger levels","the cognitive mechanisms that allow environmental cues to override deliberate dietary intentions in everyday situations","the ways in which food environments can be redesigned to reduce automatic overeating and support healthier choices"],"topic_answer":1,"blank_sentence_index":0,"blank_target":"automatic responses to a particular situation with food","blank_options":["automatic responses to a particular situation with food","conscious and deliberate nutritional choices made after careful consideration","rational decisions based on hunger levels and caloric needs","learned behaviors that are easily changed through education and willpower","instinctive reactions that are entirely determined by genetic factors"],"blank_answer":1,"order_given_index":0,"order_blocks":[{"label":"B","sentence_indices":[1,2]},{"label":"C","sentence_indices":[3,4,5]},{"label":"D","sentence_indices":[6,7]}],"order_options":["(C)-(B)-(A)","(A)-(B)-(C)","(B)-(A)-(C)","(B)-(C)-(A)","(C)-(A)-(B)"],"order_answer":2,"insert_sentence":"Grocery stores often use placement of items to encourage impulse buying.","insert_answer":7,"summary_template":"Most dietary behavior results from ________(A)________ responses to environmental and social cues rather than genuine hunger, because people lack the cognitive capacity to consistently ________(B)________ these triggers.","summary_A_options":["learned","automatic","conditioned","most","eating"],"summary_A_answer":2,"summary_B_options":["recognize","resist","effective","stable","override"],"summary_B_answer":2,"implication_sentence_index":6,"implication_keyword":"prompted by the social environment","implication_options":["driven to eat by the cues and expectations embedded in the social situation rather than by any internal need","encouraged by peers who actively suggest or offer food as a way of expressing hospitality or inclusion","influenced by the eating behavior of others around them through a process of unconscious social imitation","pressured by social norms that treat refusing offered food as impolite or socially disruptive","motivated by the desire to conform to the eating patterns of the group in order to maintain social acceptance"],"implication_answer":1,"irrelevant_sentence_index":7},{"id":"27ST_E_30_03","difficulty":"보통","title":"초기 미각 경험과 식습관 형성","sentences":["Science shows that, when compared to adults, children naturally prefer higher levels of sweet and salty tastes and reject bitter tastes.","This might help explain why children are drawn to more unhealthy food choices within our current food environment — an environment composed of high-salt, high-refined-sugar foods.","In support of this idea, studies have found that sensory experiences, beginning early in life, can shape preferences in both a positive and a negative way.","For example, expecting mothers who consume diets rich in healthy foods can help develop their child's taste preferences in a positive way because flavors from foods that the mother eats are transmitted to amniotic fluid and to mother's milk.","Having healthy food experiences early in life may go a long way toward promoting healthy eating throughout a person's life span."],"abstract":"Children's innate preference for sweet and salty flavors makes them vulnerable to unhealthy food environments, but early sensory experiences — from prenatal exposure to postnatal feeding — can shape taste preferences in lasting ways.","topic_options":["the lasting influence of early sensory food experiences on taste preferences and the potential for both positive and negative outcomes","the biological reasons why children prefer sweet and salty foods and how these preferences can be managed through parenting","the role of prenatal nutrition in determining the flavor preferences that infants develop in the first months of life","the ways in which formula feeding creates taste preferences that make it harder for infants to accept healthy solid foods","the nutritional interventions available to parents who wish to counteract children's innate preference for unhealthy foods"],"topic_answer":1,"blank_sentence_index":0,"blank_target":"naturally prefer higher levels of sweet and salty tastes and reject bitter tastes","blank_options":["naturally prefer higher levels of sweet and salty tastes and reject bitter tastes","develop highly individualized taste preferences from the moment of birth","show no consistent pattern in food preferences during early childhood","respond primarily to texture and temperature rather than flavor when eating","gradually develop a preference for bitter and sour foods as they mature"],"blank_answer":1,"order_given_index":0,"order_blocks":[{"label":"B","sentence_indices":[1]},{"label":"C","sentence_indices":[2,3]},{"label":"D","sentence_indices":[4]}],"order_options":["(B)-(C)-(A)","(C)-(A)-(B)","(C)-(B)-(A)","(A)-(B)-(C)","(B)-(A)-(C)"],"order_answer":4,"insert_sentence":null,"insert_answer":null,"summary_template":"Children's innate preference for sweet and salty flavors makes them susceptible to unhealthy diets, but early ________(A)________ experiences can shape taste preferences in lasting ways, with prenatal and postnatal food exposure serving as a foundation for ________(B)________ eating habits.","summary_A_options":["dietary","sensory","nutritional","children","innate"],"summary_A_answer":2,"summary_B_options":["healthy","lifelong","consistent","effective","stable"],"summary_B_answer":2,"implication_sentence_index":1,"implication_keyword":"an environment composed of high-salt, high-refined-sugar foods","implication_options":["a food landscape specifically designed in ways that align with and therefore amplify children's innate unhealthy preferences","a nutritional context in which processed foods have become so dominant that healthy options are difficult to access","a cultural environment in which food advertising targets children's known preference for sweet and salty flavors","a commercial ecosystem driven by the food industry's interest in cultivating lifelong consumers of processed products","a social setting in which peer pressure and media influence reinforce children's natural attraction to unhealthy foods"],"implication_answer":1,"irrelevant_sentence_index":4},{"id":"27ST_E_21_GATE","difficulty":"높음","title":"지리학의 공간적 사고","sentences":["One word is inextricably associated with geography: where.","That is because geography starts from the premise that it matters where something is located.","The key questions are not simply 'where' questions, though; they are 'why there' and 'why not somewhere else' questions.","Getting to such questions means taking spatial arrangements, variations, and interactions seriously.","Engaging in even the simplest day-to-day activity requires some appreciation of spatial arrangement.","Locating a new store or public service requires taking into consideration population distribution.","Understanding why and where migration happens requires consideration of the political, economic, and social circumstances of different places."],"abstract":"Geography's defining contribution is to ask not merely where things are but why they are there and not elsewhere, making spatial context and arrangement central to understanding all human and natural phenomena.","topic_options":["geography's distinctive focus on why things are located where they are rather than simply recording their positions","the practical applications of geographic knowledge in business location decisions and public service planning","the relationship between geographic scale and the complexity of the questions geographers are able to ask","the ways in which spatial awareness shapes everyday decision-making without people being consciously aware of it","the role of geography in integrating political, economic, and social factors into a unified analytical framework"],"topic_answer":1,"blank_sentence_index":2,"blank_target":"'why there' and 'why not somewhere else'","blank_options":["'why there' and 'why not somewhere else'","'when' and 'how long ago'","'who' and 'how many'","'what' and 'how much'","'which way' and 'how far'"],"blank_answer":1,"order_given_index":0,"order_blocks":[{"label":"B","sentence_indices":[1,2]},{"label":"C","sentence_indices":[3,4]},{"label":"D","sentence_indices":[5,6]}],"order_options":["(C)-(A)-(B)","(A)-(C)-(B)","(C)-(B)-(A)","(B)-(A)-(C)","(A)-(B)-(C)"],"order_answer":5,"insert_sentence":"Locating a new store or public service requires taking into consideration population distribution.","insert_answer":5,"summary_template":"Geography goes beyond asking ________(A)________ something is located to asking why it is there, making ________(B)________ context the foundation of geographic understanding.","summary_A_options":["when","how","where","geography","defining"],"summary_A_answer":3,"summary_B_options":["historical","cultural","spatial","effective","stable"],"summary_B_answer":3,"implication_sentence_index":2,"implication_keyword":"'why not somewhere else' questions","implication_options":["inquiries into the conditions and forces that make one location more suitable or significant than any alternative","questions that challenge the assumption that the current distribution of phenomena is natural or inevitable","analyses that compare different locations in order to identify which offers the greatest strategic advantage","investigations into the historical decisions that placed particular features in their current positions","explorations of how the absence of something in a place can be as informative as its presence"],"implication_answer":1,"irrelevant_sentence_index":3},{"id":"27ST_E_22_GATE","difficulty":"높음","title":"소프트패스 하천 공학","sentences":["What is soft-path river engineering?","One way to visualize its spirit is to liken it to a footpath in the forest.","Suppose a tree falls across a footpath.","A soft-path response would be simply to redirect the trail around the fallen tree.","A more interventionist response would be to remove the tree and restore the original path.","A still more interventionist response might be to straighten and pave the path to prevent future obstructions.","The true high-modernist step would, of course, be to create a superhighway that bypasses nature altogether.","In contrast to hard-path engineering, soft-path engineering accepts variability and uncertainty as natural features of river systems.","Backwaters, short-lived wetlands, braids and channels, swamps — all undesirable from the perspective of a navigation engineer — are features to be accommodated in the soft-path approach."],"abstract":"Soft-path river engineering works with natural variability rather than against it, accepting uncertainty and temporary features as legitimate components of healthy river systems rather than obstacles to be eliminated.","topic_options":["the philosophy of soft-path river engineering as one that accommodates rather than eliminates natural variability","the technical differences between soft-path and hard-path approaches to managing obstructions in river channels","the historical development of river engineering from minimally interventionist to highly modernist approaches","the environmental benefits of preserving wetlands and backwaters rather than engineering them out of river systems","the reasons why soft-path engineering is considered intellectually modest in its approach to natural systems"],"topic_answer":1,"blank_sentence_index":7,"blank_target":"accepts variability and uncertainty as natural features of river systems","blank_options":["accepts variability and uncertainty as natural features of river systems","prioritizes economic efficiency over ecological considerations","aims to eliminate all unpredictable elements from river management","relies on advanced technology to control and redirect water flow","seeks to maximize the navigational and commercial use of waterways"],"blank_answer":1,"order_given_index":0,"order_blocks":[{"label":"B","sentence_indices":[1,2,3]},{"label":"C","sentence_indices":[4,5,6]},{"label":"D","sentence_indices":[7,8]}],"order_options":["(A)-(B)-(C)","(C)-(B)-(A)","(B)-(A)-(C)","(C)-(A)-(B)","(B)-(C)-(A)"],"order_answer":1,"insert_sentence":"In contrast to hard-path engineering, soft-path engineering accepts variability and uncertainty as natural features of river systems.","insert_answer":7,"summary_template":"Soft-path engineering ________(A)________ natural variability rather than eliminating it, treating uncertainty and temporary features as ________(B)________ components of healthy river systems.","summary_A_options":["studies","monitors","accommodates","river","rather"],"summary_A_answer":3,"summary_B_options":["inevitable","problematic","legitimate","effective","stable"],"summary_B_answer":3,"implication_sentence_index":3,"implication_keyword":"redirect the trail around the fallen tree","implication_options":["adapt to an obstacle by working around it rather than expending effort to remove or overcome it entirely","find a temporary detour while waiting for conditions to return to their original state","choose the path of least resistance in order to minimize the energy required to reach a destination","preserve the original route by protecting it from future interference by natural forces","design a new permanent route that is more resilient to the kind of obstruction that caused the original problem"],"implication_answer":1,"irrelevant_sentence_index":7},{"id":"27ST_E_23_GATE","difficulty":"높음","title":"혼돈 시스템의 예측 불가능성","sentences":["A good example of chaos is the magnetic pendulum sold as an executive toy.","It has four magnets arranged in a square at the base and a pendulum that swings over them.","Release the pendulum and note the magnets that it visits, and in what order.","If the pendulum is released from the same position a second time, the pattern of its movement will be different.","In fact, the pattern of its movement is chaotic.","No matter how much care is taken to start the pendulum in the same position, it will always behave differently.","Chaotic systems are generated by iteration, though not all iteration leads to chaos.","In order to produce chaos, the iteration has to be within what is called a nonlinear system.","Before that point is reached they may behave in a quite orderly fashion."],"abstract":"Chaotic systems are characterized by extreme sensitivity to initial conditions that makes their long-term behavior unpredictable even when the underlying processes are fully understood, as illustrated by the magnetic pendulum.","topic_options":["the defining characteristic of chaotic systems as extreme sensitivity to initial conditions that makes prediction impossible","the mathematical conditions required for a nonlinear iterative system to generate genuinely chaotic behavior","the practical uses of chaos theory in understanding complex natural and social systems","the distinction between systems that appear random and those that are genuinely chaotic in a mathematical sense","the ways in which the magnetic pendulum serves as a model for understanding broader principles of complex systems"],"topic_answer":1,"blank_sentence_index":4,"blank_target":"the pattern of its movement is chaotic","blank_options":["the pattern of its movement is chaotic","the pendulum always returns to its starting position","the magnets determine a predictable and repeatable path","the movement gradually slows down and becomes regular","the pattern becomes more stable with each successive release"],"blank_answer":1,"order_given_index":0,"order_blocks":[{"label":"B","sentence_indices":[1,2,3]},{"label":"C","sentence_indices":[4,5,6]},{"label":"D","sentence_indices":[7,8]}],"order_options":["(A)-(B)-(C)","(C)-(A)-(B)","(B)-(A)-(C)","(B)-(C)-(A)","(C)-(B)-(A)"],"order_answer":1,"insert_sentence":"Before that point is reached they may behave in a quite orderly fashion.","insert_answer":8,"summary_template":"Chaotic systems exhibit extreme ________(A)________ to initial conditions, making their behavior fundamentally ________(B)________ even when the rules governing them are completely known.","summary_A_options":["sensitivity","responsiveness","vulnerability","chaotic","systems"],"summary_A_answer":1,"summary_B_options":["unpredictable","nonlinear","effective","stable","complex"],"summary_B_answer":1,"implication_sentence_index":4,"implication_keyword":"the pattern of its movement is chaotic","implication_options":["the sequence of positions the pendulum visits cannot be predicted even with complete knowledge of its starting conditions","the pendulum's movement follows no recognizable pattern that could be detected by an observer watching it over time","the forces acting on the pendulum are too numerous and variable for any mathematical model to capture accurately","the pendulum's behavior changes unpredictably because the magnets exert forces that fluctuate randomly over time","the system produces different outputs each time because it incorporates an element of genuine randomness at the quantum level"],"implication_answer":1,"irrelevant_sentence_index":6},{"id":"27ST_E_24_GATE","difficulty":"보통","title":"낚시터의 극적인 반전","sentences":["The shoreline was known for having the best fishing spots on the lake.","Jessie was sitting at one of those spots, but her fishing line still hadn't moved.","With a deep sigh, Jessie pulled out the line and cast it back into the water.","Just as she was about to give up and leave, the fishing line suddenly became tense.","Jessie excitedly held onto the fishing pole as it began to move around wildly.","Her eyes widened and her heart began to beat faster with excitement.","With a big smile, she could feel that this was the biggest fish she had ever caught."],"abstract":"Jessie's long wait at a promising fishing spot ends in dramatic reversal when, just as she is on the verge of giving up, she hooks what feels like the biggest catch of her life.","topic_options":["the dramatic shift from near-despair to exhilaration experienced by a fisher whose patience is finally rewarded","the importance of choosing the right fishing location when attempting to catch large fish in a lake","the emotional journey of a young person learning to persist through disappointment in pursuit of a goal","the contrast between the peaceful atmosphere of a fishing spot and the excitement of an unexpected catch","the physical and emotional sensations associated with the moment of hooking a large fish"],"topic_answer":1,"blank_sentence_index":3,"blank_target":"the fishing line suddenly became tense","blank_options":["the fishing line suddenly became tense","a small fish appeared near the surface of the water","Jessie heard a loud splash from across the lake","the wind began to blow more strongly across the water","another fisherman called out a warning from the shore"],"blank_answer":1,"order_given_index":0,"order_blocks":[{"label":"B","sentence_indices":[1,2]},{"label":"C","sentence_indices":[3]},{"label":"D","sentence_indices":[4,5,6]}],"order_options":["(A)-(C)-(B)","(A)-(B)-(C)","(B)-(A)-(C)","(C)-(B)-(A)","(C)-(A)-(B)"],"order_answer":2,"insert_sentence":"Just as she was about to give up and leave, the fishing line suddenly became tense.","insert_answer":3,"summary_template":"After a long period of ________(A)________ and near-defeat at a promising fishing spot, Jessie experiences a dramatic reversal when the fishing line suddenly ________(B)________, transforming despair into excitement.","summary_A_options":["hoping","waiting","struggling","jessie","long"],"summary_A_answer":2,"summary_B_options":["moves","tightens","effective","responds","stable"],"summary_B_answer":2,"implication_sentence_index":4,"implication_keyword":"began to move around wildly","implication_options":["showed signs that a large and powerful fish was attached to the line","indicated that the fishing equipment was malfunctioning due to strong currents","suggested that Jessie had accidentally tangled the line with another fisherman","revealed that the fishing spot was too shallow to contain any large fish","demonstrated that the weather conditions were unsuitable for fishing that day"],"implication_answer":1,"irrelevant_sentence_index":3},{"id":"27ST_E_25_GATE","difficulty":"보통","title":"토론 중 노트 필기의 가치","sentences":["The purpose of class discussions is to encourage you to be an active participant in your own learning.","Much of the emphasis in a discussion is on getting students involved in thinking out loud, testing ideas, and responding to ideas.","These are important intellectual activities in the learning process, for through them, students begin to clarify their thinking.","Writing is an invaluable tool for accomplishing these tasks.","Unfortunately, too many times, when class discussion begins, pens and pencils go down.","Admittedly, it is considerably more difficult to take notes from discussions than from lectures.","And if you are an active participant, it is not easy to take notes and formulate responses at the same time.","But note taking in discussions is not only manageable, it is also important.","Note taking helps to keep you active and alert; it allows you to impose some organization on what is being said."],"abstract":"Despite the challenges of note-taking during class discussions, writing actively during these sessions is both possible and valuable as a tool for organizing thought and sustaining engagement.","topic_options":["the importance and feasibility of note-taking during class discussions as a tool for active engagement and intellectual organization","the differences between the note-taking strategies appropriate for lectures and those suitable for open discussions","the role of verbal participation in helping students develop and refine their thinking in educational settings","the reasons why students tend to stop writing when class discussion begins and how this habit can be changed","the relationship between active listening and effective note-taking in collaborative learning environments"],"topic_answer":1,"blank_sentence_index":3,"blank_target":"an invaluable tool for accomplishing these tasks","blank_options":["an invaluable tool for accomplishing these tasks","a distraction that prevents active participation in discussions","a skill that only benefits students with strong academic backgrounds","a passive activity that reduces engagement with course material","an outdated practice replaced by digital recording technology"],"blank_answer":1,"order_given_index":0,"order_blocks":[{"label":"B","sentence_indices":[1,2,3]},{"label":"C","sentence_indices":[4,5]},{"label":"D","sentence_indices":[6,7,8]}],"order_options":["(B)-(C)-(A)","(C)-(B)-(A)","(B)-(A)-(C)","(A)-(B)-(C)","(C)-(A)-(B)"],"order_answer":4,"insert_sentence":"And if you are an active participant, it is not easy to take notes and formulate responses at the same time.","insert_answer":6,"summary_template":"Although note-taking during discussions is more ________(A)________ than during lectures, it remains a valuable practice because writing actively helps students organize ideas and sustain ________(B)________ in the learning process.","summary_A_options":["time-consuming","demanding","during","challenging","despite"],"summary_A_answer":4,"summary_B_options":["attention","participation","effective","engagement","stable"],"summary_B_answer":4,"implication_sentence_index":4,"implication_keyword":"pens and pencils go down","implication_options":["students stop recording ideas at the very moment when active writing could most help them organize their thinking","learners shift from passive reception to active verbal participation as soon as the format changes from lecture to discussion","the physical act of writing is abandoned because students prefer to rely on memory during fast-moving exchanges","note-taking tools are set aside because students feel the informal nature of discussion makes writing seem unnecessary","the transition from lecture to discussion signals to students that the content being shared is less academically important"],"implication_answer":1,"irrelevant_sentence_index":3},{"id":"27ST_E_26_GATE","difficulty":"높음","title":"문학 캐릭터의 재등장과 변화","sentences":["In most fiction, characters' lives are limited to the individual work.","Readers may disagree on the characteristics and traits of fictional figures, and critics argue about their significance.","However, it is less common for characters in literary fiction to reappear in subsequent works.","This is even more pronounced in comics, which are typically serialized in newspapers or periodicals.","Thus characters introduced in the 1930s, like Superman and Batman, may still enjoy ongoing stories.","During these characters' long histories, they change in various ways for a variety of reasons.","On the other hand, if characters are the work of several hands over decades, they may change more dramatically."],"abstract":"Unlike literary fiction characters who are largely confined to a single work, serialized characters in comics can evolve across decades and multiple authors, resulting in far more significant transformation over time.","topic_options":["the contrast between the fixed nature of literary fiction characters and the ongoing evolution of serialized comic characters across multiple authors","the ways in which reader interpretation and critical debate shape the perceived characteristics of fictional figures","the commercial pressures that drive publishers to continue serializing popular characters beyond their original creators' intentions","the relationship between authorial continuity and character consistency in both literary fiction and comic book series","the historical development of superhero characters from their introduction in the 1930s to their contemporary forms"],"topic_answer":1,"blank_sentence_index":3,"blank_target":"even more pronounced in comics, which are typically serialized in newspapers or periodicals","blank_options":["even more pronounced in comics, which are typically serialized in newspapers or periodicals","less noticeable in literary fiction where characters rarely reappear","more common in novels where authors have complete creative control","especially evident in film adaptations of classic literary characters","most clearly seen in stage productions of well-known theatrical works"],"blank_answer":1,"order_given_index":0,"order_blocks":[{"label":"B","sentence_indices":[1,2]},{"label":"C","sentence_indices":[3,4]},{"label":"D","sentence_indices":[5,6]}],"order_options":["(B)-(C)-(A)","(C)-(B)-(A)","(A)-(B)-(C)","(C)-(A)-(B)","(B)-(A)-(C)"],"order_answer":3,"insert_sentence":"On the other hand, if characters are the work of several hands over decades, they may change more dramatically.","insert_answer":6,"summary_template":"While literary fiction characters are typically ________(A)________ to a single work, serialized comic characters can evolve across decades, with the degree of change depending on whether the character is the work of one or ________(B)________ authors.","summary_A_options":["limited","confined","restricted","characters","unlike"],"summary_A_answer":2,"summary_B_options":["successive","multiple","effective","collaborative","stable"],"summary_B_answer":2,"implication_sentence_index":4,"implication_keyword":"may still enjoy ongoing stories","implication_options":["continue to appear in new narratives long after their original creation","are recognized as historically significant figures in the development of comics","have been adapted into films that are more popular than the original comics","represent the artistic standards that all modern comic characters must meet","were created specifically to entertain children in the early twentieth century"],"implication_answer":1,"irrelevant_sentence_index":3},{"id":"27ST_E_27_GATE","difficulty":"높음","title":"정보와 의미의 구별","sentences":["Information and meaning are, clearly, not the same thing.","The former refers to uninterpreted data or sensory states whose probability in a given context can be calculated.","Take, for instance, a coin-tossing game in which it is decided that throwing three heads in a row wins the game.","If a certain player ends up consistently with the desired outcome, defeating all others, this should indicate that something more than chance is at work.","Interpretation is at the core of everything we do, think about, and feel."],"abstract":"Information and meaning are fundamentally distinct: information consists of raw data whose probability can be calculated, while meaning emerges only through interpretation, which underlies all human thought and experience.","topic_options":["the fundamental distinction between raw information as uninterpreted data and meaning as the product of active interpretation","the mathematical methods used to calculate the probability of events in games of chance and statistical analysis","the ways in which human beings use contextual interpretation to extract meaning from ambiguous sensory data","the role of pattern recognition in distinguishing meaningful signals from random noise in complex data sets","the philosophical debate about whether meaning exists independently of the minds that perceive and construct it"],"topic_answer":1,"blank_sentence_index":4,"blank_target":"Interpretation is at the core of everything we do, think about, and feel","blank_options":["Interpretation is at the core of everything we do, think about, and feel","Information can exist independently of any interpretive framework","The probability of a signal determines its ultimate significance and value","Meaning is always fixed and can be transmitted without any loss of precision","Statistical analysis provides the most reliable foundation for human understanding"],"blank_answer":1,"order_given_index":0,"order_blocks":[{"label":"B","sentence_indices":[1]},{"label":"C","sentence_indices":[2]},{"label":"D","sentence_indices":[3,4]}],"order_options":["(A)-(B)-(C)","(C)-(B)-(A)","(B)-(C)-(A)","(B)-(A)-(C)","(C)-(A)-(B)"],"order_answer":1,"insert_sentence":null,"insert_answer":null,"summary_template":"Information consists of ________(A)________ data whose probability can be calculated, while meaning only emerges through ________(B)________, which is central to all human thought and experience.","summary_A_options":["objective","uninterpreted","statistical","information","meaning"],"summary_A_answer":2,"summary_B_options":["analysis","interpretation","effective","reasoning","stable"],"summary_B_answer":2,"implication_sentence_index":3,"implication_keyword":"something more than chance is at work","implication_options":["a pattern that cannot be explained by random probability alone and therefore requires an interpretive explanation","a level of skill or strategy that distinguishes a successful player from those relying on luck alone","a systematic bias in the coin-tossing mechanism that makes certain outcomes more likely than others","an external force or intention that is deliberately influencing the outcome of each individual toss","a statistical anomaly significant enough to warrant further investigation under controlled experimental conditions"],"implication_answer":1,"irrelevant_sentence_index":4},{"id":"27ST_E_29_GATE","difficulty":"높음","title":"공정한 집단 선택과 무작위성","sentences":["When gathering the preferences of multiple agents into one collective choice, it is easily seen that certain cases call for randomization or other means of tiebreaking.","For example, if there are two alternatives and two agents such that one prefers one and the other prefers the other, there is no deterministic way of selecting a single alternative without violating one of two basic fairness conditions known as anonymity and neutrality.","Allowing lotteries as social outcomes hence seems like a necessity for impartial collective choice.","Indeed, most common deterministic social choice functions such as plurality rule are only deterministic as long as there is no tie, which is usually resolved by drawing a lot.","The use of lotteries for the selection of officials interestingly goes back to the world's first democracy in Athens, where it was widely regarded as a principal characteristic of democracy."],"abstract":"When collective decision-making produces a perfect tie, no deterministic method can satisfy both anonymity and neutrality simultaneously, making randomization a logically necessary feature of genuinely impartial social choice.","topic_options":["the logical necessity of randomization in collective decision-making when deterministic methods cannot satisfy both anonymity and neutrality","the historical use of lotteries in Athenian democracy and its relevance to contemporary debates about political representation","the mathematical properties of different social choice functions and the conditions under which each is most appropriate","the tension between the principles of anonymity and neutrality in designing fair systems for collective decision-making","the reasons why plurality rule and other standard voting systems break down in situations of perfect electoral ties"],"topic_answer":1,"blank_sentence_index":2,"blank_target":"a necessity for impartial collective choice","blank_options":["a necessity for impartial collective choice","a violation of democratic principles and individual rights","an inefficient method that produces unreliable outcomes","a theoretical concept with no practical application","a means of undermining the authority of elected officials"],"blank_answer":1,"order_given_index":0,"order_blocks":[{"label":"B","sentence_indices":[1]},{"label":"C","sentence_indices":[2]},{"label":"D","sentence_indices":[3,4]}],"order_options":["(C)-(A)-(B)","(A)-(B)-(C)","(B)-(A)-(C)","(A)-(C)-(B)","(C)-(B)-(A)"],"order_answer":2,"insert_sentence":null,"insert_answer":null,"summary_template":"When collective choices produce a tie, ________(A)________ methods cannot satisfy both anonymity and neutrality simultaneously, making ________(B)________ a logically necessary feature of truly impartial decision-making.","summary_A_options":["democratic","deterministic","majority","collective","decision"],"summary_A_answer":2,"summary_B_options":["compromise","randomization","delegation","effective","stable"],"summary_B_answer":2,"implication_sentence_index":1,"implication_keyword":"no deterministic way of selecting a single alternative","implication_options":["there is no fair rule that can produce a definitive outcome without bias","computers are unable to process collective decision-making efficiently","democratic systems always produce unpredictable and inconsistent results","individual preferences are too complex to be represented in any voting system","mathematical models cannot accurately predict the outcomes of group decisions"],"implication_answer":1,"irrelevant_sentence_index":4},{"id":"27ST_E_30_GATE","difficulty":"보통","title":"블렌디드 허니의 특성","sentences":["Honey can be eaten by itself or mixed with other ingredients.","Natural or pure honey has had no additives, preservatives or synthetic ingredients added.","Natural honey can also be called 'blended honey', in which honeys from various sources are blended together by human processors after collection.","Blending is frequently done for taste as well as marketing reasons, especially since some consumers find the darker honeys too strong.","Mixing different types of honey together can make it more palatable, and also gives a more uniform flavour.","Clover is one of the most popular honeys in the U.S., and its mild flavour and taste have become familiar to many Americans."],"abstract":"Blended honey is produced by combining honeys from different sources after collection to achieve a more consistent, palatable flavor that meets consumer expectations for mildness and uniformity.","topic_options":["the purpose and process of blending different honeys to achieve uniform flavor and meet consumer preferences for mildness","the distinctions between natural, pure, and diluted honeys and the price differences that reflect their varying quality","the marketing strategies that honey producers use to position blended products as preferable to single-source honeys","the reasons why darker honeys with stronger flavors are less popular among mainstream consumers in the United States","the role of clover honey in establishing the flavor profile that most American consumers associate with honey"],"topic_answer":1,"blank_sentence_index":2,"blank_target":"blended honey","blank_options":["blended honey","raw honey","organic honey","processed honey","filtered honey"],"blank_answer":1,"order_given_index":0,"order_blocks":[{"label":"B","sentence_indices":[1,2]},{"label":"C","sentence_indices":[3]},{"label":"D","sentence_indices":[4,5]}],"order_options":["(A)-(C)-(B)","(B)-(A)-(C)","(C)-(B)-(A)","(A)-(B)-(C)","(C)-(A)-(B)"],"order_answer":4,"insert_sentence":"Blending is frequently done for taste as well as marketing reasons, especially since some consumers find the darker honeys too strong.","insert_answer":3,"summary_template":"Blended honey is created by combining honeys from multiple ________(A)________ to produce a more ________(B)________ and palatable flavor that satisfies consumer preferences for consistency and mildness.","summary_A_options":["regions","varieties","blended","honey","sources"],"summary_A_answer":5,"summary_B_options":["mild","effective","refined","stable","uniform"],"summary_B_answer":5,"implication_sentence_index":3,"implication_keyword":"some consumers find the darker honeys too strong","implication_options":["the intense flavor of single-source dark honeys exceeds what mainstream consumers find acceptable or enjoyable","darker honeys contain higher concentrations of natural compounds that some people find medicinally unpleasant","the color of honey serves as a reliable indicator of flavor intensity that consumers use to guide their purchasing decisions","consumers who prefer mild flavors are unwilling to pay premium prices for artisanal dark honey varieties","the production of dark honeys is more expensive and time-consuming than that of lighter blended varieties"],"implication_answer":1,"irrelevant_sentence_index":3},{"id":"27STYD_01_001","difficulty":"상","title":"","sentences":[{"num":1,"text":"Research on the universality of facial expressions suggests that the socialization of affect involves interactions between situational variables and a finite repertoire of human emotions whose meanings are at least roughly synonymous among all members of the species.","symbol":"G","role":"얼굴 표정의 보편성과 감정의 사회화 주제 제시","keyWords":["universality","finite repertoire","synonymous"],"chunks":[{"en":"Research on the universality of facial expressions","ko":"얼굴 표정의 보편성에 관한 연구는"},{"en":"suggests that the socialization of affect","ko":"감정의 사회화가"},{"en":"involves interactions","ko":"상호작용을 포함한다고 시사한다"},{"en":"between situational variables","ko":"상황적 변수들과"},{"en":"and a finite repertoire of human emotions","ko":"한정된 인간 감정 목록 사이의"},{"en":"whose meanings are at least roughly synonymous","ko":"그 의미가 적어도 대략적으로 동의어인"},{"en":"among all members of the species","ko":"종의 모든 구성원들 사이에서"}]},{"num":2,"text":"At the same time, Izard's formulation of \"affective-cognitive structures\" shows that emotions are in reality not separable from the particular circumstances that are associated with them.","symbol":"↔","role":"감정은 특정 상황과 분리 불가능함을 대비적으로 제시","keyWords":["affective-cognitive structures","not separable","particular circumstances"],"chunks":[{"en":"At the same time,","ko":"동시에,"},{"en":"Izard's formulation of \"affective-cognitive structures\"","ko":"Izard의 '정서-인지 구조' 공식화는"},{"en":"shows that emotions are in reality","ko":"감정이 실제로는"},{"en":"not separable from the particular circumstances","ko":"특정 상황들로부터 분리될 수 없음을 보여준다"},{"en":"that are associated with them","ko":"그것들과 연관된"}]},{"num":3,"text":"The fact that it is possible to construct a list of \"basic,\" universally recognizable emotions derives not only from a species-specific repertoire of facial expressions, but perhaps more fundamentally from a larger set of human expressive behaviors, including laughter and crying as well as bodily movements and postures.","symbol":"+","role":"보편적 감정 목록의 근거가 얼굴 표정뿐 아니라 더 넓은 표현 행동에 있음을 부연","keyWords":["universally recognizable","species-specific repertoire","expressive behaviors"],"chunks":[{"en":"The fact that it is possible to construct a list of \"basic,\" universally recognizable emotions","ko":"'기본적'이고 보편적으로 인식 가능한 감정 목록을 구성하는 것이 가능하다는 사실은"},{"en":"derives not only from a species-specific repertoire of facial expressions,","ko":"종 특유의 얼굴 표정 목록에서만 비롯되는 것이 아니라,"},{"en":"but perhaps more fundamentally from a larger set of human expressive behaviors,","ko":"아마도 더 근본적으로는 더 광범위한 인간 표현 행동들에서 비롯된다,"},{"en":"including laughter and crying","ko":"웃음과 울음을 포함하여"},{"en":"as well as bodily movements and postures","ko":"신체 동작과 자세도 마찬가지로"}]},{"num":4,"text":"These behaviors, for which a universal capacity exists, are also, without exception, carried out in particular circumstances.","symbol":"==","role":"보편적 표현 행동도 예외 없이 특정 상황 속에서 수행됨을 재확인","keyWords":["universal capacity","without exception","particular circumstances"],"chunks":[{"en":"These behaviors,","ko":"이러한 행동들은,"},{"en":"for which a universal capacity exists,","ko":"그에 대한 보편적 능력이 존재하는,"},{"en":"are also, without exception,","ko":"또한, 예외 없이,"},{"en":"carried out in particular circumstances","ko":"특정 상황 속에서 수행된다"}]},{"num":5,"text":"As elements in the human communicative function, they create the necessity of response from the environment while also being shaped by it.","symbol":"→","role":"표현 행동이 환경과 쌍방향적 관계를 맺음을 인과적으로 설명","keyWords":["communicative function","necessity of response","shaped by"],"chunks":[{"en":"As elements in the human communicative function,","ko":"인간 소통 기능의 요소로서,"},{"en":"they create the necessity of response from the environment","ko":"그것들은 환경으로부터의 반응 필요성을 만들어내며"},{"en":"while also being shaped by it","ko":"동시에 환경에 의해 형성되기도 한다"}]},{"num":6,"text":"To use Lewis's terms, the contextual reality of emotional expression transforms \"state\" into \"experience.\"","symbol":"→","role":"감정 표현의 맥락적 현실이 '상태'를 '경험'으로 전환함을 결론으로 제시","keyWords":["contextual reality","state","experience"],"chunks":[{"en":"To use Lewis's terms,","ko":"Lewis의 용어를 사용하자면,"},{"en":"the contextual reality of emotional expression","ko":"감정 표현의 맥락적 현실은"},{"en":"transforms \"state\" into \"experience\"","ko":"'상태'를 '경험'으로 변환시킨다"}]}],"abstract":"","blank_sel":0,"insert_sel":0,"summary_sel":0,"irrel_sel":0,"irrel_insert_pos":4,"irrel_confirmed":true,"irrel_sentence":"However, research on facial expressions has demonstrated that the repertoire of human emotions is entirely culture-specific, meaning that the meanings of emotional displays differ so fundamentally across members of the species that no universal emotional vocabulary can be established.","grammar_sel":0,"grammar_answer":3,"vocab_sel":0,"vocab_answer":3,"flow":{"blocks":[{"id":1,"name":"보편성 제시","nameEn":"Universal Claim","color":"blue","sentenceNums":[1]},{"id":2,"name":"상황 맥락과의 불가분성","nameEn":"Inseparability from Context","color":"coral","sentenceNums":[2,3,4]},{"id":3,"name":"쌍방향적 소통과 결론","nameEn":"Bidirectional Communication & Conclusion","color":"teal","sentenceNums":[5,6]}],"interBlockConnectors":["↔","→"],"keyword":"감정 표현의 보편성과 맥락성","topicSummary":"얼굴 표정을 포함한 인간의 감정 표현은 보편적 목록을 가지지만, 동시에 특정 상황·맥락과 분리될 수 없으며, 환경과 상호작용하면서 단순한 '상태'가 아닌 '경험'으로 전환된다.","structureType":"보편성 제시 → 맥락 불가분성 대비·심화 → 결론"},"grammar":{},"blockSummaries":[{"blockId":1,"summary":"Research suggests that {facial expressions} reveal a {finite repertoire} of {human emotions} that are roughly synonymous across all members of the species.","keywords":["facial expressions","finite repertoire","human emotions"]},{"blockId":2,"summary":"Emotions are not separable from {particular circumstances}, as {basic} universally recognizable {behaviors} such as laughter and crying are always carried out in specific contexts.","keywords":["particular circumstances","basic","behaviors"]},{"blockId":3,"summary":"As elements in {human communicative function}, emotional {behaviors} are shaped by the environment while also creating a necessity of {response}, transforming state into experience.","keywords":["human communicative function","behaviors","response"]}],"topic_options":["the dual nature of emotional expression as both universal and shaped by particular contextual circumstances","the role of laughter and crying as universal expressive behaviors in human communication","the general influence of socialization and environment on all forms of human behavior","the universal repertoire of facial expressions as the basis for recognizing basic human emotions","the separability of basic emotions from the cognitive structures that define affective experience"],"topic_answer":1,"blank_sentence_index":0,"blank_target":"interactions between situational variables and a finite repertoire of human emotions","blank_options":["interactions between situational variables and a finite repertoire of human emotions","a universal repertoire of fixed emotional responses that operate independently of situational variables","a species-specific capacity for recognizing basic facial expressions","interactions between affective-cognitive structures and the contextual reality of emotional experience","exchanges between communicative functions and the biological mechanisms of laughter and crying"],"insert_sentence":"These behaviors, for which a universal capacity exists, are also, without exception, carried out in particular circumstances.","insert_answer":3,"summary_candidates":[{"template":"The passage argues that ________(A)________ leads to ________(B)________.","A_correct":"the interplay between universal expressive capacity and particular circumstances","A_distractors":["the complete independence of emotions from social context","the species-wide repertoire of facial expressions alone","the finite list of basic universally recognizable emotions","laughter and crying as isolated biological reflexes"],"B_correct":"emotional states being transformed into culturally shaped experiences","B_distractors":["emotions becoming entirely detached from cognitive structures","the suppression of affect in communicative environments","a uniform emotional response across all human cultures","the recognition of laughter as the primary expressive behavior"]},{"template":"Despite ________(A)________, the passage emphasizes ________(B)________.","A_correct":"a shared biological foundation for emotional expression across the species","A_distractors":["the complete absence of any universal emotional capacity","the universality of laughter and crying alone","a culturally constructed set of affective-cognitive labels","individual variation in facial musculature across populations"],"B_correct":"that emotional expression is always embedded in and shaped by specific situational contexts","B_distractors":["that emotions can be fully understood apart from their circumstances","that the environment plays no meaningful role in shaping affect","that bodily postures override facial expressions in communication","that basic emotions are reducible to neurological states alone"]},{"template":"True ________(A)________ requires ________(B)________ rather than mere appearance.","A_correct":"understanding of human emotional expression","A_distractors":["suppression of culturally variable affective responses","cataloguing of facial muscle movements","elimination of context from emotional analysis","measurement of laughter frequency across societies"],"B_correct":"recognition of how context transforms raw affective states into meaningful experience","B_distractors":["isolation of universal signals from their situational surroundings","prioritizing biological repertoire over cognitive interpretation","mapping each emotion onto a single corresponding facial expression","separating communicative function from environmental response"]},{"template":"X depends on ________(A)________ while Y depends on ________(B)________.","A_correct":"a species-universal repertoire that makes emotions broadly intelligible across cultures","A_distractors":["culturally exclusive codes that prevent cross-cultural emotional recognition","the specific facial expression of disgust as a prototype","affective-cognitive structures defined solely by individual memory","bodily posture as the sole determinant of emotional meaning"],"B_correct":"the contextual shaping of expression that gives emotion its particular lived meaning","B_distractors":["the biological hardwiring that operates independently of social environment","the communicative demand placed on the observer alone","the number of discrete states catalogued in a universal emotion list","the suppression of environmental feedback during emotional episodes"]},{"template":"The contrast between ________(A)________ and ________(B)________ reveals the central insight.","A_correct":"the fixed, universal capacity for emotional expression inherent in the species","A_distractors":["the complete cultural relativity of all affective responses","the learned suppression of instinctive facial signals","the dominance of cognitive structures over biological emotion","the infinite variety of human expressive behaviors"],"B_correct":"the context-dependent transformation that converts biological states into human experiences","B_distractors":["the purely instinctive reflex that bypasses social interaction entirely","the environmental demand for a single standardized emotional response","the reduction of all emotion to measurable facial muscle contractions","the communicative necessity that eliminates individual variation"]}],"summary_template":"The passage argues that ________(A)________ leads to ________(B)________.","summary_A_options":["the interplay between universal expressive capacity and particular circumstances","the complete independence of emotions from social context","the species-wide repertoire of facial expressions alone","the finite list of basic universally recognizable emotions","laughter and crying as isolated biological reflexes"],"summary_A_answer":1,"summary_B_options":["emotional states being transformed into culturally shaped experiences","emotions becoming entirely detached from cognitive structures","the suppression of affect in communicative environments","a uniform emotional response across all human cultures","the recognition of laughter as the primary expressive behavior"],"summary_B_answer":1,"implication_sentence_index":5,"implication_keyword":"transforms \"state\" into \"experience.\"","implication_options":["Emotional expression, shaped by and responsive to its social context, turns a raw biological reaction into a personally and culturally meaningful event","The act of expressing an emotion physically changes one's internal feeling state into a lived memory","Universal emotional states remain unchanged regardless of the particular circumstances in which they are expressed","Specific situational circumstances trigger the emergence of basic emotions from a species-wide repertoire","Repeated emotional experiences accumulate over time to gradually redefine an individual's core affective identity"],"implication_answer":1,"irrel_candidates":["However, research on facial expressions has demonstrated that the repertoire of human emotions is entirely culture-specific, meaning that the meanings of emotional displays differ so fundamentally across members of the species that no universal emotional vocabulary can be established.","The universally recognizable nature of basic emotions suggests that these species-specific expressive behaviors, such as laughter and crying, operate independently of particular circumstances, remaining constant regardless of the social or environmental context in which they occur.","Izard's affective-cognitive structures, along with the broader set of human expressive behaviors including laughter and bodily postures, have been most extensively studied not for their communicative function within the species, but rather for their role in distinguishing humans from other primates in evolutionary biology."],"irrelevant_sentence_index":4,"grammar_sets":[{"items":[{"sent":0,"word":"whose","original":"whose","correct":true,"note":"선행사 'a finite repertoire of human emotions'를 받는 관계대명사의 소유격으로, 'whose meanings'는 '그것의 의미들'을 뜻한다. 소유격 관계대명사 whose가 올바르게 쓰였다."},{"sent":1,"word":"associated","original":"associated","correct":true,"note":"'the particular circumstances that are associated with them'에서 associated는 수동태(be associated)의 과거분사로, circumstances가 감정과 '연관되는' 대상이므로 수동 표현이 문법적으로 적절하다."},{"sent":2,"word":"included","original":"including","correct":false,"note":"준동사(분사) 용법 오류. 'including'을 'included'로 바꾸면 어법 오류가 발생한다. 'including'은 능동의 전치사적 분사로 '~을 포함하여'의 의미이며, 뒤에 목적어(laughter and crying 등)를 취하므로 능동형 including이 올바른 형태이다. → including"},{"sent":3,"word":"carried","original":"carried","correct":true,"note":"'are also … carried out'은 수동태 구문으로, 주어 'These behaviors'가 '수행되는' 대상이므로 과거분사 carried가 be동사와 결합한 수동태 표현이 문법적으로 적절하다."},{"sent":4,"word":"shaped","original":"shaped","correct":true,"note":"'being shaped by it'은 수동의 동명사구로, 'they'(these behaviors)가 환경에 의해 '형성되는' 대상임을 나타낸다. 수동의 의미를 표현하기 위해 being + 과거분사 형태가 올바르게 사용되었다."}],"answer":3}],"grammar_items":[{"sent":0,"word":"whose","original":"whose","correct":true,"note":"선행사 'a finite repertoire of human emotions'를 받는 관계대명사의 소유격으로, 'whose meanings'는 '그것의 의미들'을 뜻한다. 소유격 관계대명사 whose가 올바르게 쓰였다."},{"sent":1,"word":"associated","original":"associated","correct":true,"note":"'the particular circumstances that are associated with them'에서 associated는 수동태(be associated)의 과거분사로, circumstances가 감정과 '연관되는' 대상이므로 수동 표현이 문법적으로 적절하다."},{"sent":2,"word":"included","original":"including","correct":false,"note":"준동사(분사) 용법 오류. 'including'을 'included'로 바꾸면 어법 오류가 발생한다. 'including'은 능동의 전치사적 분사로 '~을 포함하여'의 의미이며, 뒤에 목적어(laughter and crying 등)를 취하므로 능동형 including이 올바른 형태이다. → including"},{"sent":3,"word":"carried","original":"carried","correct":true,"note":"'are also … carried out'은 수동태 구문으로, 주어 'These behaviors'가 '수행되는' 대상이므로 과거분사 carried가 be동사와 결합한 수동태 표현이 문법적으로 적절하다."},{"sent":4,"word":"shaped","original":"shaped","correct":true,"note":"'being shaped by it'은 수동의 동명사구로, 'they'(these behaviors)가 환경에 의해 '형성되는' 대상임을 나타낸다. 수동의 의미를 표현하기 위해 being + 과거분사 형태가 올바르게 사용되었다."}],"vocab_sets":[{"items":[{"sent":0,"word":"finite","original":"finite","alt":"limited","correct":true},{"sent":1,"word":"separable","original":"separable","alt":"distinguishable","correct":true},{"sent":2,"word":"particular","original":"universal","alt":"universal","correct":false},{"sent":3,"word":"capacity","original":"capacity","alt":"ability","correct":true},{"sent":4,"word":"shaped","original":"shaped","alt":"influenced","correct":true}],"answer":3}],"vocab_items":[{"sent":0,"word":"finite","original":"finite","alt":"limited","correct":true},{"sent":1,"word":"separable","original":"separable","alt":"distinguishable","correct":true},{"sent":2,"word":"particular","original":"universal","alt":"universal","correct":false},{"sent":3,"word":"capacity","original":"capacity","alt":"ability","correct":true},{"sent":4,"word":"shaped","original":"shaped","alt":"influenced","correct":true}],"aGroup":["the interplay between universal expressive capacity and particular circumstances","the complete independence of emotions from social context","the species-wide repertoire of facial expressions alone"],"bGroup":["emotional states being transformed into culturally shaped experiences","emotions becoming entirely detached from cognitive structures","the suppression of affect in communicative environments"],"blank_candidates":[{"sentence_index":0,"keyword":"interactions between situational variables and a finite repertoire of human emotions","distractors":["a universal repertoire of fixed emotional responses that operate independently of situational variables","a species-specific capacity for recognizing basic facial expressions","interactions between affective-cognitive structures and the contextual reality of emotional experience","exchanges between communicative functions and the biological mechanisms of laughter and crying"]}],"blank_answer":1,"insert_candidates":[{"sentence":"These behaviors, for which a universal capacity exists, are also, without exception, carried out in particular circumstances.","pos":3}]},{"id":"27STYD_01_002","difficulty":"하","title":"","sentences":[{"num":1,"text":"Changes are often useful ─ people want to see new emails, better search results, and new news stories ─ but they can disrupt the user's ability to re-find information.","symbol":"G","role":"통념 제시 및 역접 도입","keyWords":["Changes","disrupt","re-find information"],"chunks":[{"en":"Changes are often useful","ko":"변화는 종종 유용하다"},{"en":"─ people want to see new emails, better search results, and new news stories ─","ko":"─ 사람들은 새 이메일, 더 나은 검색 결과, 새로운 뉴스 기사를 보고 싶어 한다 ─"},{"en":"but they can disrupt","ko":"하지만 그것들은 방해할 수 있다"},{"en":"the user's ability to re-find information","ko":"사용자가 정보를 다시 찾는 능력을"}]},{"num":2,"text":"As an example, dynamic menus were developed to help people access menu items faster by bubbling common items to the top of the menu.","symbol":"S","role":"첫 번째 구체 사례 도입","keyWords":["dynamic menus","bubbling common items"],"chunks":[{"en":"As an example,","ko":"예를 들어,"},{"en":"dynamic menus were developed","ko":"동적 메뉴가 개발되었다"},{"en":"to help people access menu items faster","ko":"사람들이 메뉴 항목에 더 빨리 접근하도록 돕기 위해"},{"en":"by bubbling common items to the top of the menu","ko":"자주 쓰는 항목을 메뉴 상단으로 띄워 올림으로써"}]},{"num":3,"text":"Rather than decreasing access time, research revealed dynamic menus actually slow their users down because commonly sought items no longer appear where expected.","symbol":"↔","role":"사례 결과: 기대와 반대되는 결과 제시","keyWords":["slow down","no longer appear where expected"],"chunks":[{"en":"Rather than decreasing access time,","ko":"접근 시간을 줄이기는커녕,"},{"en":"research revealed","ko":"연구는 밝혔다"},{"en":"dynamic menus actually slow their users down","ko":"동적 메뉴가 실제로 사용자를 더 느리게 만든다는 것을"},{"en":"because commonly sought items no longer appear where expected","ko":"자주 찾는 항목이 더 이상 예상되는 위치에 나타나지 않기 때문에"}]},{"num":4,"text":"As another example, some researchers tried to help people search better by giving them lists of relevant sentences that were dynamically reranked based on implicit feedback gathered during the search process.","symbol":"S","role":"두 번째 구체 사례 도입","keyWords":["dynamically reranked","implicit feedback"],"chunks":[{"en":"As another example,","ko":"또 다른 예로,"},{"en":"some researchers tried to help people search better","ko":"일부 연구자들은 사람들이 더 잘 검색하도록 돕고자 했다"},{"en":"by giving them lists of relevant sentences","ko":"관련 문장 목록을 제공함으로써"},{"en":"that were dynamically reranked","ko":"동적으로 재정렬된"},{"en":"based on implicit feedback gathered during the search process","ko":"검색 과정에서 수집된 암묵적 피드백을 기반으로"}]},{"num":5,"text":"To the researchers' surprise, people did not enjoy the search experience as much or perform as well as they did when the sentence list was static.","symbol":"↔","role":"두 번째 사례 결과: 기대와 반대되는 결과","keyWords":["surprise","static"],"chunks":[{"en":"To the researchers' surprise,","ko":"연구자들이 놀랍게도,"},{"en":"people did not enjoy the search experience as much","ko":"사람들은 검색 경험을 그만큼 즐기지 못했다"},{"en":"or perform as well","ko":"또는 그만큼 잘 수행하지도 못했다"},{"en":"as they did when the sentence list was static","ko":"문장 목록이 고정되어 있을 때만큼"}]},{"num":6,"text":"Similarly, a large-scale analysis of query logs revealed that when people repeat queries they are significantly less likely to click on a result they've clicked before if the result's rank has changed, and significantly slower to click when they do.","symbol":"+","role":"추가 근거: 쿼리 로그 분석으로 주제 강화","keyWords":["query logs","rank has changed","less likely to click"],"chunks":[{"en":"Similarly,","ko":"마찬가지로,"},{"en":"a large-scale analysis of query logs revealed","ko":"쿼리 로그에 대한 대규모 분석이 밝혔다"},{"en":"that when people repeat queries","ko":"사람들이 검색어를 반복할 때"},{"en":"they are significantly less likely to click on a result they've clicked before","ko":"그들은 이전에 클릭했던 결과를 클릭할 가능성이 훨씬 낮다"},{"en":"if the result's rank has changed,","ko":"결과의 순위가 바뀌었을 경우"},{"en":"and significantly slower to click when they do","ko":"그리고 클릭하더라도 훨씬 더 느리게 클릭한다"}]}],"abstract":"","blank_sel":0,"insert_sel":0,"summary_sel":0,"irrel_sel":0,"irrel_insert_pos":2,"irrel_confirmed":false,"irrel_sentence":"Dynamic menus have been widely praised by users for significantly improving navigation efficiency, as the automatic reordering of frequently accessed items allows people to locate what they need more quickly than with static menus.","grammar_sel":0,"grammar_answer":3,"vocab_sel":0,"vocab_answer":3,"flow":{"blocks":[{"id":1,"name":"통념 제시","nameEn":"General Claim","color":"blue","sentenceNums":[1]},{"id":2,"name":"사례 1: 동적 메뉴","nameEn":"Case 1: Dynamic Menus","color":"coral","sentenceNums":[2,3]},{"id":3,"name":"사례 2: 동적 재정렬","nameEn":"Case 2: Dynamic Reranking","color":"teal","sentenceNums":[4,5]},{"id":4,"name":"추가 근거: 쿼리 로그 분석","nameEn":"Supporting Evidence: Query Log Analysis","color":"purple","sentenceNums":[6]}],"interBlockConnectors":["↔","S","+"],"keyword":"동적 변화와 정보 재탐색 방해","topicSummary":"인터페이스의 동적 변화는 유용해 보이지만, 실제로는 사용자가 정보를 다시 찾는 능력을 방해한다.","structureType":"통념→반박 사례 나열→추가 근거"},"grammar":{},"topic_options":["the disruptive effect of dynamic content changes on users' ability to re-find information","the slowing effect of dynamic menus on users' access to menu items","the negative impact of technological changes on overall user experience","the unintended consequences of dynamic ranking systems in search engines","the role of implicit user feedback in improving search result performance"],"topic_answer":1,"blank_sentence_index":0,"blank_target":"re-find information","blank_options":["re-find information","adapt to new information quickly","access menu items more efficiently","search for relevant sentences dynamically","evaluate the credibility of online sources"],"insert_candidates":[{"sentence":"As another example, some researchers tried to help people search better by giving them lists of relevant sentences that were dynamically reranked based on implicit feedback gathered during the search process.","pos":3}],"insert_sentence":"As another example, some researchers tried to help people search better by giving them lists of relevant sentences that were dynamically reranked based on implicit feedback gathered during the search process.","insert_answer":3,"summary_candidates":[{"template":"The passage argues that ________(A)________ leads to ________(B)________.","A_correct":"dynamically altering interface layouts to boost efficiency","A_distractors":["keeping interface layouts fixed and predictable","updating only the visual design of menus","reranking search results based on user queries","introducing minor cosmetic changes to digital systems"],"B_correct":"degraded user performance due to violated spatial expectations","B_distractors":["improved user performance by meeting spatial expectations","slower loading times in menu and search systems","user frustration with irrelevant search results","reduced efficiency in a single type of navigation task"]},{"template":"Despite ________(A)________, the passage emphasizes ________(B)________.","A_correct":"the intention to improve users' speed and access through adaptive systems","A_distractors":["the proven success of dynamic interfaces in real-world settings","minor inconveniences caused by static interface designs","the developers' effort to gather implicit user feedback","occasional improvements in menu item accessibility"],"B_correct":"that consistency in information placement is essential for effective retrieval","B_distractors":["that novelty and change enhance long-term user engagement","that users prefer faster access over familiar layouts","that dynamic reranking helps users find relevant sentences","that predictability matters only in large-scale search systems"]},{"template":"True ________(A)________ requires ________(B)________ rather than mere appearance.","A_correct":"usability enhancement in information systems","A_distractors":["aesthetic improvement in digital interface design","reduction of irrelevant content in search results","acceleration of menu item loading speed","optimization of a single feature within an application"],"B_correct":"preserving the stable positional patterns users have already internalized","B_distractors":["abandoning all familiar structures to encourage adaptive behavior","supplying users with the most frequently accessed items only","dynamically reordering content based on implicit behavioral signals","maintaining static rankings on results from repeated queries"]},{"template":"X depends on ________(A)________ while Y depends on ________(B)________.","A_correct":"user trust built through predictable and stable interface structures","A_distractors":["user trust eroded by unpredictable changes in interface layout","user satisfaction derived from receiving faster search responses","user engagement driven by exposure to novel menu arrangements","user confidence limited to familiarity with a single menu system"],"B_correct":"adaptive algorithmic updates that prioritize efficiency over familiarity","B_distractors":["rigid adherence to original layouts regardless of usage patterns","implicit feedback mechanisms that track repetitive user behavior","incremental improvements that avoid disrupting existing structures","reranking logic applied exclusively to repeated search queries"]},{"template":"The contrast between ________(A)________ and ________(B)________ reveals the central insight.","A_correct":"designers' assumption that adaptive change improves user experience","A_distractors":["users' explicit preference for dynamically updated search lists","researchers' success in accelerating access through menu bubbling","the efficiency gains observed in static query log analyses","the minor benefits of reranking in narrow experimental contexts"],"B_correct":"users' actual reliance on spatial memory and positional consistency","B_distractors":["users' complete indifference to the position of interface elements","users' tendency to ignore previously clicked results entirely","designers' awareness of the cognitive costs of interface change","users' preference for visually prominent items over familiar ones"]}],"summary_template":"The passage argues that ________(A)________ leads to ________(B)________.","summary_A_options":["dynamically altering interface layouts to boost efficiency","keeping interface layouts fixed and predictable","updating only the visual design of menus","reranking search results based on user queries","introducing minor cosmetic changes to digital systems"],"summary_A_answer":1,"summary_B_options":["degraded user performance due to violated spatial expectations","improved user performance by meeting spatial expectations","slower loading times in menu and search systems","user frustration with irrelevant search results","reduced efficiency in a single type of navigation task"],"summary_B_answer":1,"implication_sentence_index":1,"implication_keyword":"bubbling common items to the top of the menu.","implication_options":["prioritizing frequently used options disrupts users' ability to locate them reliably","floating menu items upward like bubbles rising to the surface of a liquid","hiding less common menu items at the bottom to make the interface cleaner","making popular menu items more visible by moving them higher","sorting menu options automatically to reflect each user's personal preferences"],"implication_answer":1,"irrel_candidates":["Dynamic menus have been widely praised by users for significantly improving navigation efficiency, as the automatic reordering of frequently accessed items allows people to locate what they need more quickly than with static menus.","The development of dynamic interfaces was driven largely by user demand for personalization, and many search platforms continue to invest heavily in real-time reranking algorithms precisely because users report higher satisfaction when results adapt to their preferences.","When researchers analyzed implicit feedback gathered during search sessions, they found that dynamically updated result lists helped users build more accurate mental models of information hierarchies, ultimately improving their ability to re-find previously accessed content."],"grammar_sets":[{"items":[{"sent":0,"word":"disrupt","original":"disrupt","correct":true,"note":"주어 'they'(복수 대명사, Changes를 지칭)에 수일치한 복수 동사 형태로 적절하다."},{"sent":1,"word":"bubbling","original":"bubbling","correct":true,"note":"'by + -ing' 구조로 수단·방법을 나타내는 전치사 by의 목적어로 동명사가 사용된 것이며, 문맥상 메뉴 항목을 위로 올리는 동작을 표현하므로 능동적 의미의 현재분사(동명사)가 문법적으로 적절하다."},{"sent":2,"word":"seeking","original":"sought","correct":false,"note":"준동사(분사) 형태 오류. 'commonly sought items'에서 'sought'는 'seek'의 과거분사로 'items'를 수식하는 형용사적 용법의 과거분사이다. 앞에 수식어 'commonly'가 있으므로 부사가 동사를 수식하는 구조인데, 이를 능동 현재분사 'seeking'으로 바꾸면 '항목이 스스로 찾는다'는 의미가 되어 수동 관계를 나타내지 못하는 명백한 어법 오류가 된다. → sought"},{"sent":3,"word":"gathered","original":"gathered","correct":true,"note":"'implicit feedback'과 'gather' 사이의 관계가 수동(피드백이 수집되는 것)이므로 과거분사 'gathered'가 'implicit feedback'을 후치 수식하는 형태로 적절하다."},{"sent":4,"word":"as much","original":"as much","correct":true,"note":"'not as much'는 원급 비교 구조 'not as ~ as'의 일부로, 'enjoy the search experience as much (as they did when ~)'에서 동사 'enjoy'를 수식하는 부사 역할을 하므로 문법적으로 적절하다."}],"answer":3}],"grammar_items":[{"sent":0,"word":"disrupt","original":"disrupt","correct":true,"note":"주어 'they'(복수 대명사, Changes를 지칭)에 수일치한 복수 동사 형태로 적절하다."},{"sent":1,"word":"bubbling","original":"bubbling","correct":true,"note":"'by + -ing' 구조로 수단·방법을 나타내는 전치사 by의 목적어로 동명사가 사용된 것이며, 문맥상 메뉴 항목을 위로 올리는 동작을 표현하므로 능동적 의미의 현재분사(동명사)가 문법적으로 적절하다."},{"sent":2,"word":"seeking","original":"sought","correct":false,"note":"준동사(분사) 형태 오류. 'commonly sought items'에서 'sought'는 'seek'의 과거분사로 'items'를 수식하는 형용사적 용법의 과거분사이다. 앞에 수식어 'commonly'가 있으므로 부사가 동사를 수식하는 구조인데, 이를 능동 현재분사 'seeking'으로 바꾸면 '항목이 스스로 찾는다'는 의미가 되어 수동 관계를 나타내지 못하는 명백한 어법 오류가 된다. → sought"},{"sent":3,"word":"gathered","original":"gathered","correct":true,"note":"'implicit feedback'과 'gather' 사이의 관계가 수동(피드백이 수집되는 것)이므로 과거분사 'gathered'가 'implicit feedback'을 후치 수식하는 형태로 적절하다."},{"sent":4,"word":"as much","original":"as much","correct":true,"note":"'not as much'는 원급 비교 구조 'not as ~ as'의 일부로, 'enjoy the search experience as much (as they did when ~)'에서 동사 'enjoy'를 수식하는 부사 역할을 하므로 문법적으로 적절하다."}],"vocab_sets":[{"items":[{"sent":0,"word":"disrupt","original":"disrupt","alt":"hinder","correct":true},{"sent":1,"word":"common","original":"common","alt":"frequent","correct":true},{"sent":2,"word":"increasing","original":"decreasing","alt":"decreasing","correct":false},{"sent":3,"word":"relevant","original":"relevant","alt":"related","correct":true},{"sent":4,"word":"static","original":"static","alt":"unchanged","correct":true}],"answer":3}],"vocab_items":[{"sent":0,"word":"disrupt","original":"disrupt","alt":"hinder","correct":true},{"sent":1,"word":"common","original":"common","alt":"frequent","correct":true},{"sent":2,"word":"increasing","original":"decreasing","alt":"decreasing","correct":false},{"sent":3,"word":"relevant","original":"relevant","alt":"related","correct":true},{"sent":4,"word":"static","original":"static","alt":"unchanged","correct":true}],"aGroup":["dynamically altering interface layouts to boost efficiency","keeping interface layouts fixed and predictable","updating only the visual design of menus"],"bGroup":["degraded user performance due to violated spatial expectations","improved user performance by meeting spatial expectations","slower loading times in menu and search systems"]},{"id":"27STYD_01_003","difficulty":"중","title":"","sentences":[{"num":1,"text":"Verbal metaphors help make our language more colorful and expressive.","symbol":"G","role":"언어적 은유의 일반적 기능 소개","chunks":[{"en":"Verbal metaphors","ko":"언어적 은유는"},{"en":"help make our language","ko":"우리의 언어를 만드는 데 도움을 준다"},{"en":"more colorful and expressive","ko":"더 풍부하고 표현력 있게"}]},{"num":2,"text":"They influence how we think about something, but they do not change the thing itself.","symbol":"G","role":"언어적 은유의 한계 — 사고에만 영향, 실제 변화 없음","chunks":[{"en":"They influence","ko":"그것들은 영향을 미친다"},{"en":"how we think about something,","ko":"우리가 무언가를 생각하는 방식에"},{"en":"but they do not change","ko":"하지만 그것들은 바꾸지 않는다"},{"en":"the thing itself","ko":"그 사물 자체를"}]},{"num":3,"text":"Interface metaphors play a more fundamental role in how we experience and interact with the technological world, affecting function as well as feeling.","symbol":"↔","role":"인터페이스 은유는 감정뿐 아니라 기능까지 영향 — 언어적 은유와 대조","chunks":[{"en":"Interface metaphors","ko":"인터페이스 은유는"},{"en":"play a more fundamental role","ko":"더 근본적인 역할을 한다"},{"en":"in how we experience and interact","ko":"우리가 경험하고 상호작용하는 방식에"},{"en":"with the technological world,","ko":"기술적 세계와"},{"en":"affecting function as well as feeling","ko":"감정뿐만 아니라 기능에도 영향을 미치면서"}]},{"num":4,"text":"The metaphor that is chosen for an interface shapes how it can be used.","symbol":"→","role":"인터페이스 은유 선택 → 사용 방식 결정","chunks":[{"en":"The metaphor","ko":"은유는"},{"en":"that is chosen for an interface","ko":"인터페이스를 위해 선택된"},{"en":"shapes how it can be used","ko":"그것이 사용될 수 있는 방식을 형성한다"}]},{"num":5,"text":"When we put computer \"files\" into \"folders,\" these metaphoric constructs help us think about the way information is organized in our machine, but they also constrain what we can do with it.","symbol":"S","role":"파일/폴더 예시 — 은유가 사고를 돕는 동시에 행동을 제약함","chunks":[{"en":"When we put computer \"files\" into \"folders,\"","ko":"우리가 컴퓨터 '파일'을 '폴더'에 넣을 때"},{"en":"these metaphoric constructs","ko":"이러한 은유적 구조물들은"},{"en":"help us think about the way information is organized","ko":"정보가 정리되는 방식을 생각하도록 도와주지만"},{"en":"but they also constrain","ko":"동시에 제약하기도 한다"},{"en":"what we can do with it","ko":"우리가 그것으로 할 수 있는 것을"}]},{"num":6,"text":"Interface metaphors also influence the feel of the experience, the emotional and aesthetic response we have to our interactions with and via the machine.","symbol":"+","role":"기능뿐 아니라 정서적·미적 경험에도 영향","chunks":[{"en":"Interface metaphors also influence","ko":"인터페이스 은유는 또한 영향을 미친다"},{"en":"the feel of the experience,","ko":"경험의 느낌에"},{"en":"the emotional and aesthetic response","ko":"감정적·미적 반응"},{"en":"we have to our interactions","ko":"우리가 상호작용에 대해 갖는"},{"en":"with and via the machine","ko":"기계와 함께 그리고 기계를 통한"}]},{"num":7,"text":"The desktop metaphor calls to mind office work: secretaries, bosses, quarterly plans, and cubicles.","symbol":"S","role":"데스크탑 은유 — 사무실 이미지 연상","chunks":[{"en":"The desktop metaphor","ko":"데스크탑 은유는"},{"en":"calls to mind office work:","ko":"사무실 업무를 떠올리게 한다:"},{"en":"secretaries, bosses, quarterly plans, and cubicles","ko":"비서, 상사, 분기 계획, 그리고 칸막이 사무실"}]},{"num":8,"text":"It was developed in the late 1970s and early 1980s, when office work was seen as the primary use for personal computers.","symbol":"S","role":"데스크탑 은유의 역사적 맥락 — 당시 PC 주요 용도와 일치","chunks":[{"en":"It was developed","ko":"그것은 개발되었다"},{"en":"in the late 1970s and early 1980s,","ko":"1970년대 후반과 1980년대 초반에"},{"en":"when office work was seen as","ko":"그때 사무실 업무가 간주되었던"},{"en":"the primary use for personal computers","ko":"개인용 컴퓨터의 주요 사용 목적으로"}]},{"num":9,"text":"The desktop image certainly is appropriate for that setting.","symbol":"G","role":"데스크탑 은유가 사무 환경에는 적합함을 인정","chunks":[{"en":"The desktop image certainly is appropriate","ko":"데스크탑 이미지는 분명히 적합하다"},{"en":"for that setting","ko":"그 환경에는"}]},{"num":10,"text":"However, it is less appropriate when we use the computer as an entertainment center or as the locus of our social life.","symbol":"↔","role":"오락·사교 용도에는 데스크탑 은유가 부적합 — 한계 지적","chunks":[{"en":"However, it is less appropriate","ko":"그러나 그것은 덜 적합하다"},{"en":"when we use the computer","ko":"우리가 컴퓨터를 사용할 때"},{"en":"as an entertainment center","ko":"오락 센터로서"},{"en":"or as the locus of our social life","ko":"또는 우리 사회적 삶의 중심으로서"}]},{"num":11,"text":"Interface metaphors need to fit both the feel and function of the application.","symbol":"→","role":"결론 — 인터페이스 은유는 느낌과 기능 모두에 맞아야 함","chunks":[{"en":"Interface metaphors need to fit","ko":"인터페이스 은유는 맞아야 한다"},{"en":"both the feel and function","ko":"느낌과 기능 모두에"},{"en":"of the application","ko":"해당 응용 프로그램의"}]}],"abstract":"","blank_sel":0,"insert_sel":0,"summary_sel":0,"irrel_sel":0,"irrel_insert_pos":4,"irrel_confirmed":true,"irrel_sentence":"Verbal metaphors, like interface metaphors, can also reshape the underlying structure of the technologies they describe, altering both function and form.","grammar_sel":0,"grammar_answer":5,"vocab_sel":0,"vocab_answer":2,"flow":{"blocks":[{"id":1,"name":"언어적 은유 vs 인터페이스 은유","nameEn":"Verbal vs Interface Metaphors","color":"blue","sentenceNums":[1,2,3]},{"id":2,"name":"인터페이스 은유의 기능·감성적 영향","nameEn":"Functional & Emotional Impact","color":"teal","sentenceNums":[4,5,6]},{"id":3,"name":"데스크탑 은유의 적합성과 한계","nameEn":"Desktop Metaphor: Fit & Limitation","color":"coral","sentenceNums":[7,8,9,10]},{"id":4,"name":"결론: 은유의 적합성 요건","nameEn":"Conclusion: Requirements for Fit","color":"green","sentenceNums":[11]}],"interBlockConnectors":["↔","+","→"],"keyword":"인터페이스 은유(Interface Metaphor)","topicSummary":"인터페이스 은유는 언어적 은유와 달리 기능과 감성 모두에 근본적 영향을 미치므로, 해당 응용 프로그램의 느낌과 기능 양쪽에 부합해야 한다.","structureType":"비교·대조 → 사례 분석 → 결론"},"grammar":{"difficultSentences":[{"num":3,"text":"Interface metaphors play a more fundamental role in how we experience and interact with the technological world, affecting function as well as feeling.","structure":"주어(Interface metaphors) + 동사(play) + 목적어(a more fundamental role) / 분사구문(affecting function as well as feeling) — 앞 문장과 역접 관계","translation":"인터페이스 은유는 우리가 기술 세계를 경험하고 상호작용하는 방식에 더 근본적인 역할을 하며, 감정뿐만 아니라 기능에도 영향을 미친다.","point":"'as well as'로 기능(function)과 감정(feeling) 두 측면을 연결하며, 앞의 언어적 은유와 비교·대조되는 핵심 문장"},{"num":5,"text":"When we put computer \"files\" into \"folders,\" these metaphoric constructs help us think about the way information is organized in our machine, but they also constrain what we can do with it.","structure":"부사절(When ~) + 주절1(help us think ~) + but + 주절2(constrain what ~) — 역접 병렬 구조","translation":"우리가 컴퓨터 '파일'을 '폴더'에 넣을 때, 이러한 은유적 구조물들은 기기 내 정보 정리 방식을 이해하도록 돕지만, 동시에 우리가 그것으로 할 수 있는 것을 제약하기도 한다.","point":"'help + 목적어 + 동사원형' 구조와 'constrain what we can do with it'의 관계사절을 정확히 파악해야 하며, 은유의 양면성(도움 vs 제약)이 핵심 논지"},{"num":6,"text":"Interface metaphors also influence the feel of the experience, the emotional and aesthetic response we have to our interactions with and via the machine.","structure":"주어 + 동사(influence) + 목적어1(the feel) + , + 목적어1의 동격(the emotional and aesthetic response ~) — 동격 명사구 확장","translation":"인터페이스 은유는 또한 경험의 느낌, 즉 기계와 함께하고 기계를 통한 상호작용에 대해 우리가 갖는 감정적·미적 반응에도 영향을 미친다.","point":"'the emotional and aesthetic response we have to ~'가 앞의 'the feel of the experience'를 동격으로 부연 설명하는 구조를 인식해야 함"}]},"topic_options":["the dual role of interface metaphors in shaping both the function and feel of user experience","the limitation of the desktop metaphor for non-office uses of computers","the influence of all types of metaphors on human language and thought","the constraint that interface metaphors place on how information is organized","the importance of choosing appropriate metaphors in effective communication"],"topic_answer":1,"blank_sentence_index":2,"blank_target":"affecting function as well as feeling.","blank_options":["affecting function as well as feeling.","neglecting function in favor of feeling","shaping the feel of the experience alone","constraining what we can do with information","reflecting the historical context of office work"],"order_given_index":0,"order_blocks":[{"label":"B","sentence_indices":[1,2,3]},{"label":"C","sentence_indices":[4,5]},{"label":"D","sentence_indices":[6,7,8,9,10]}],"order_options":["(A)-(B)-(C)","(B)-(C)-(A)","(C)-(A)-(B)","(B)-(A)-(C)","(A)-(C)-(B)"],"order_answer":2,"insert_sentence":"However, it is less appropriate when we use the computer as an entertainment center or as the locus of our social life.","insert_answer":9,"summary_candidates":[{"template":"The passage argues that ________(A)________ leads to ________(B)________.","A_correct":"the choice of an interface metaphor","A_distractors":["the rejection of all interface metaphors","the visual design of an interface","the use of verbal metaphors in language","the desktop metaphor specifically"],"B_correct":"constraints on both usability and user experience","B_distractors":["unlimited freedom in how users interact with technology","changes in the emotional tone of an interface","colorful and expressive digital communication","difficulties only with office-related software"]},{"template":"Despite ________(A)________, the passage emphasizes ________(B)________.","A_correct":"the decorative appeal of verbal metaphors in everyday language","A_distractors":["the functional power of interface metaphors in shaping use","the complete absence of metaphor in technology design","the organizational role of file and folder labels","the historical dominance of the desktop metaphor"],"B_correct":"the deeper functional and emotional impact interface metaphors have on human-technology interaction","B_distractors":["the superficial and purely aesthetic nature of all metaphors","the emotional response users feel toward office software","the importance of developing new metaphors every decade","the effect metaphors have only on professional computing contexts"]},{"template":"True ________(A)________ requires ________(B)________ rather than mere appearance.","A_correct":"interface design effectiveness","A_distractors":["interface design failure","graphic attractiveness of a digital product","linguistic creativity in user manuals","the development of the desktop layout"],"B_correct":"alignment between the metaphor's implications and the application's actual purpose and feel","B_distractors":["complete independence of function from any guiding metaphor","matching the interface color scheme to user preferences","copying the organizational structure of physical office spaces","choosing metaphors drawn exclusively from entertainment culture"]},{"template":"X depends on ________(A)________ while Y depends on ________(B)________.","A_correct":"verbal metaphors, which shape only expression and thought without altering reality","A_distractors":["interface metaphors that restructure how technology functions","metaphors that simultaneously change both thought and physical objects","the use of folder and file terminology in computing","aesthetic responses triggered by screen layout"],"B_correct":"interface metaphors, which actively constrain function and color emotional experience","B_distractors":["verbal metaphors that remain limited to decorative linguistic effects","the desktop metaphor's suitability for entertainment applications","user preferences that override the influence of any metaphor","quarterly planning tools embedded in office software"]},{"template":"The contrast between ________(A)________ and ________(B)________ reveals the central insight.","A_correct":"metaphors that fit an application's context and purpose","A_distractors":["metaphors that are universally applicable across all digital uses","the visual style of a metaphor as perceived by users","the desktop metaphor's historical origins in office computing","verbal metaphors used to organize written communication"],"B_correct":"metaphors that are misaligned with users' actual functional and emotional needs","B_distractors":["metaphors that perfectly serve every computing context simultaneously","the aesthetic limitations of early personal computer interfaces","the organizational constraints imposed by file and folder systems","metaphors borrowed from entertainment rather than office settings"]}],"summary_template":"The passage argues that ________(A)________ leads to ________(B)________.","summary_A_options":["the choice of an interface metaphor","the rejection of all interface metaphors","the visual design of an interface","the use of verbal metaphors in language","the desktop metaphor specifically"],"summary_A_answer":1,"summary_B_options":["constraints on both usability and user experience","unlimited freedom in how users interact with technology","changes in the emotional tone of an interface","colorful and expressive digital communication","difficulties only with office-related software"],"summary_B_answer":1,"implication_sentence_index":4,"implication_keyword":"\"files\" into \"folders,\"","implication_options":["organizing information digitally both enables certain interactions and restricts others","physically placing documents inside storage containers on a desk","digital interfaces should avoid using metaphors drawn from the physical world","the way computer interfaces are designed shapes only the aesthetic experience of users","familiar metaphors from everyday life make technology easier to learn for beginners"],"implication_answer":1,"irrel_candidates":["Verbal metaphors, like interface metaphors, can also reshape the underlying structure of the technologies they describe, altering both function and form.","The desktop metaphor has proven so effective that it has been adopted across nearly all digital platforms, demonstrating how a single interface metaphor can unify rather than constrain the user experience.","While interface metaphors shape how users interact with technology, the most successful designs deliberately avoid relying on metaphors so that users can engage with digital systems in entirely new and unrestricted ways."],"irrelevant_sentence_index":4,"grammar_sets":[{"items":[{"sent":2,"word":"affecting","original":"affecting","correct":true,"note":"분사구문으로 쓰인 현재분사 affecting은 주절의 주어(Interface metaphors)가 능동적으로 '영향을 미치는' 행위자이므로 현재분사(-ing) 형태가 문법적으로 적절하다."},{"sent":3,"word":"chosen","original":"chosen","correct":true,"note":"관계절 내에서 선행사 The metaphor를 수식하는 과거분사 chosen은 '선택되어진' 수동의 의미를 나타내므로 과거분사(-ed) 형태가 문법적으로 적절하다."},{"sent":5,"word":"we have","original":"we have","correct":true,"note":"관계절에서 목적격 관계대명사가 이끄는 절의 동사 자리이므로 올바른 형태는 we have이지만, 이 자리를 주격 관계대명사절로 오인하여 삽입된 경우라면 구조가 맞지 않는다. — 실제 오류: 선행사 the emotional and aesthetic response를 받는 목적격 관계대명사절에서 'we have'는 적절하나, 이를 'having'으로 바꾸면 동사가 사라져 절 구조가 성립하지 않는다. → we have"},{"sent":7,"word":"seeing","original":"seen","correct":true,"note":"when절에서 office work가 '여겨지는' 대상이므로 수동태 was seen이 올바르며, 과거분사 seen은 be동사와 결합하여 수동의 의미를 적절히 나타낸다."},{"sent":9,"word":"entertainment","original":"entertainment","correct":false,"note":"전치사 as 뒤에서 명사 역할을 하는 자리이므로 명사 entertainment가 와야 한다. entertaining은 형용사/현재분사로, 명사 center를 수식하는 형용사로 오해될 수 있으나 'an entertaining center'는 '재미있는 센터'라는 의미가 되어 문맥상 맞지 않으며, 구조적으로도 'as + 명사(구)' 형태를 충족하지 못한다. → entertainment"}],"answer":5}],"grammar_items":[{"sent":2,"word":"affecting","original":"affecting","correct":true,"note":"분사구문으로 쓰인 현재분사 affecting은 주절의 주어(Interface metaphors)가 능동적으로 '영향을 미치는' 행위자이므로 현재분사(-ing) 형태가 문법적으로 적절하다."},{"sent":3,"word":"chosen","original":"chosen","correct":true,"note":"관계절 내에서 선행사 The metaphor를 수식하는 과거분사 chosen은 '선택되어진' 수동의 의미를 나타내므로 과거분사(-ed) 형태가 문법적으로 적절하다."},{"sent":5,"word":"we have","original":"we have","correct":true,"note":"관계절에서 목적격 관계대명사가 이끄는 절의 동사 자리이므로 올바른 형태는 we have이지만, 이 자리를 주격 관계대명사절로 오인하여 삽입된 경우라면 구조가 맞지 않는다. — 실제 오류: 선행사 the emotional and aesthetic response를 받는 목적격 관계대명사절에서 'we have'는 적절하나, 이를 'having'으로 바꾸면 동사가 사라져 절 구조가 성립하지 않는다. → we have"},{"sent":7,"word":"seeing","original":"seen","correct":true,"note":"when절에서 office work가 '여겨지는' 대상이므로 수동태 was seen이 올바르며, 과거분사 seen은 be동사와 결합하여 수동의 의미를 적절히 나타낸다."},{"sent":9,"word":"entertainment","original":"entertainment","correct":false,"note":"전치사 as 뒤에서 명사 역할을 하는 자리이므로 명사 entertainment가 와야 한다. entertaining은 형용사/현재분사로, 명사 center를 수식하는 형용사로 오해될 수 있으나 'an entertaining center'는 '재미있는 센터'라는 의미가 되어 문맥상 맞지 않으며, 구조적으로도 'as + 명사(구)' 형태를 충족하지 못한다. → entertainment"}],"vocab_sets":[{"items":[{"sent":0,"word":"expressive","original":"expressive","alt":"vivid","correct":true},{"sent":4,"word":"constrain","original":"constrain","alt":"restrict","correct":true},{"sent":2,"word":"superficial","original":"fundamental","alt":"fundamental","correct":false},{"sent":6,"word":"calls to mind","original":"calls to mind","alt":"evokes","correct":true},{"sent":9,"word":"appropriate","original":"appropriate","alt":"suitable","correct":true}],"answer":3}],"vocab_items":[{"sent":0,"word":"expressive","original":"expressive","alt":"vivid","correct":true},{"sent":2,"word":"superficial","original":"fundamental","alt":"fundamental","correct":false},{"sent":4,"word":"constrain","original":"constrain","alt":"restrict","correct":true},{"sent":6,"word":"calls to mind","original":"calls to mind","alt":"evokes","correct":true},{"sent":9,"word":"appropriate","original":"appropriate","alt":"suitable","correct":true}],"aGroup":["the choice of an interface metaphor","the rejection of all interface metaphors","the visual design of an interface"],"bGroup":["constraints on both usability and user experience","unlimited freedom in how users interact with technology","changes in the emotional tone of an interface"],"blockSummaries":[{"blockId":1,"summary":"While verbal {metaphors} help make language more colorful, interface metaphors play a more {fundamental} role in how we experience and interact with the {technological} world.","keywords":["metaphors","fundamental","technological"]},{"blockId":2,"summary":"The {metaphor} chosen for an interface shapes how it can be used and influences the {feel} of the experience, including the emotional and aesthetic {response} we have to our interactions with the machine.","keywords":["metaphor","feel","response"]},{"blockId":3,"summary":"The {desktop} metaphor was developed when office work was seen as the primary use for personal computers, making it {appropriate} for that setting but less appropriate when we use the computer as an {entertainment} center or as the locus of our social life.","keywords":["desktop","appropriate","entertainment"]},{"blockId":4,"summary":"Interface {metaphors} need to {fit} both the feel and {function} of the application.","keywords":["metaphors","fit","function"]}]},{"id":"27STYD_01_004","difficulty":"중","title":"","sentences":[{"num":1,"text":"Many news media studies use experimental designs to see whether citizens' opinions are influenced by different news content.","symbol":"G","role":"연구 목적 소개: 뉴스 내용이 시민 의견에 영향을 미치는지 실험적으로 검증","keyWords":[],"chunks":[{"en":"Many news media studies","ko":"많은 뉴스 미디어 연구들은"},{"en":"use experimental designs","ko":"실험적 설계를 사용한다"},{"en":"to see whether citizens' opinions are influenced","ko":"시민들의 의견이 영향을 받는지 알아보기 위해"},{"en":"by different news content","ko":"다양한 뉴스 내용에 의해"}]},{"num":2,"text":"For example, in one study, researchers created newspaper stories to frame the death penalty in different ways.","symbol":"S","role":"구체적 실험 사례 도입: 사형제도를 다르게 프레이밍한 신문 기사 제작","keyWords":[],"chunks":[{"en":"For example, in one study,","ko":"예를 들어, 한 연구에서"},{"en":"researchers created newspaper stories","ko":"연구자들은 신문 기사를 만들었다"},{"en":"to frame the death penalty","ko":"사형제도를 프레이밍하기 위해"},{"en":"in different ways","ko":"서로 다른 방식으로"}]},{"num":3,"text":"One story constructed the death penalty as an affront to moral values (the morality frame), whereas another story emphasized that the policy was fundamentally flawed because innocent people might be executed (the innocence frame).","symbol":"S","role":"두 프레임 대비: 도덕성 프레임 vs 무죄 프레임","keyWords":["frame"],"chunks":[{"en":"One story constructed the death penalty","ko":"한 기사는 사형제도를 구성했다"},{"en":"as an affront to moral values","ko":"도덕적 가치에 대한 모욕으로"},{"en":"(the morality frame),","ko":"(도덕성 프레임)"},{"en":"whereas another story emphasized","ko":"반면 다른 기사는 강조했다"},{"en":"that the policy was fundamentally flawed","ko":"그 정책이 근본적으로 결함이 있다고"},{"en":"because innocent people might be executed","ko":"무고한 사람들이 처형될 수 있기 때문에"},{"en":"(the innocence frame)","ko":"(무죄 프레임)"}]},{"num":4,"text":"Some subjects read the story with the morality frame, and others read the one with the innocence frame.","symbol":"S","role":"실험 집단 배분: 피험자들을 두 프레임 집단으로 나눔","keyWords":[],"chunks":[{"en":"Some subjects read the story","ko":"일부 피험자들은 기사를 읽었고"},{"en":"with the morality frame,","ko":"도덕성 프레임이 담긴"},{"en":"and others read the one","ko":"다른 피험자들은 읽었다"},{"en":"with the innocence frame","ko":"무죄 프레임이 담긴 기사를"}]},{"num":5,"text":"Subjects then completed a questionnaire that asked them to list the important factors they considered when determining their opinion on the death penalty.","symbol":"S","role":"측정 방법: 사형제도에 대한 의견 형성 시 고려 요인 설문","keyWords":[],"chunks":[{"en":"Subjects then completed a questionnaire","ko":"피험자들은 그 후 설문지를 작성했다"},{"en":"that asked them to list the important factors","ko":"중요한 요인들을 나열하도록 요청하는"},{"en":"they considered","ko":"그들이 고려한"},{"en":"when determining their opinion on the death penalty","ko":"사형제도에 대한 의견을 결정할 때"}]},{"num":6,"text":"It was found that subjects exposed to the innocence frame were more likely to mention innocence-related considerations as important factors in determining their attitudes toward the death penalty than subjects presented with the morality frame.","symbol":"S","role":"실험 결과: 무죄 프레임 노출 집단이 무죄 관련 요인을 더 많이 언급","keyWords":[],"chunks":[{"en":"It was found that","ko":"~인 것으로 밝혀졌다"},{"en":"subjects exposed to the innocence frame","ko":"무죄 프레임에 노출된 피험자들이"},{"en":"were more likely to mention","ko":"더 많이 언급할 가능성이 있었다"},{"en":"innocence-related considerations as important factors","ko":"무죄 관련 고려 사항을 중요한 요인으로"},{"en":"in determining their attitudes toward the death penalty","ko":"사형제도에 대한 태도를 결정하는 데 있어"},{"en":"than subjects presented with the morality frame","ko":"도덕성 프레임을 접한 피험자들보다"}]},{"num":7,"text":"Thus, the news frames shaped the ingredients of the subjects' death penalty attitudes.","symbol":"→","role":"결론 도출: 뉴스 프레임이 사형제도 태도의 구성 요소를 형성함","keyWords":[],"chunks":[{"en":"Thus,","ko":"따라서"},{"en":"the news frames shaped","ko":"뉴스 프레임은 형성했다"},{"en":"the ingredients","ko":"구성 요소들을"},{"en":"of the subjects' death penalty attitudes","ko":"피험자들의 사형제도 태도의"}]}],"abstract":"","blank_sel":0,"insert_sel":0,"summary_sel":0,"irrel_sel":0,"irrel_insert_pos":0,"irrel_confirmed":false,"irrel_sentence":"","grammar_sel":0,"grammar_answer":1,"vocab_sel":0,"vocab_answer":1,"flow":{"blocks":[{"id":1,"name":"연구 목적 제시","nameEn":"Research Purpose","color":"blue","sentenceNums":[1]},{"id":2,"name":"실험 설계 및 과정","nameEn":"Experimental Design & Procedure","color":"teal","sentenceNums":[2,3,4,5]},{"id":3,"name":"실험 결과 및 결론","nameEn":"Results & Conclusion","color":"coral","sentenceNums":[6,7]}],"interBlockConnectors":["S","→"],"keyword":"뉴스 프레임(news frame)","topicSummary":"뉴스 프레임은 시민들이 사형제도에 대한 태도를 형성할 때 고려하는 요소에 영향을 미친다.","structureType":"주제 제시→실험 사례→결론"},"grammar":{}},{"id":"27STYD_01_005","difficulty":"중","title":"","sentences":[{"num":1,"text":"The knowledge problem is most evident when we discuss our ability to predict that which has not yet been observed.","symbol":"G","role":"핵심 주제 제시: 관찰되지 않은 것을 예측하는 능력에서 지식의 한계가 드러남","keyWords":["knowledge problem"],"chunks":[{"en":"The knowledge problem","ko":"지식의 문제는"},{"en":"is most evident","ko":"가장 분명하게 드러난다"},{"en":"when we discuss our ability","ko":"우리의 능력을 논할 때"},{"en":"to predict that which has not yet been observed","ko":"아직 관찰되지 않은 것을 예측하는"}]},{"num":2,"text":"Most people would say that they \"know\" the Sun will rise tomorrow.","symbol":"S","role":"일반적 통념의 구체 사례: 내일 해가 뜰 것을 '안다'고 말하는 사람들","keyWords":[],"chunks":[{"en":"Most people would say","ko":"대부분의 사람들은 말할 것이다"},{"en":"that they \"know\"","ko":"자신들이 '안다'고"},{"en":"the Sun will rise tomorrow","ko":"내일 태양이 뜰 것이라고"}]},{"num":3,"text":"However, can we call this a certainty?","symbol":"↔","role":"통념에 대한 의문 제기: 과연 이것이 확실한가?","keyWords":[],"chunks":[{"en":"However,","ko":"그러나"},{"en":"can we call this a certainty?","ko":"우리는 이것을 확실성이라고 부를 수 있는가?"}]},{"num":4,"text":"It seems very likely, but it has also been predicted that the time will come when the Sun runs out of fuel, swells massively, and consumes the Earth.","symbol":"↔","role":"역접 전개: 그럴 것 같지만, 태양이 연료를 소진하고 지구를 삼킬 수도 있다는 예측 존재","keyWords":[],"chunks":[{"en":"It seems very likely,","ko":"매우 그럴 것 같지만"},{"en":"but it has also been predicted","ko":"또한 예측되어 왔다"},{"en":"that the time will come","ko":"그 때가 올 것이라고"},{"en":"when the Sun runs out of fuel,","ko":"태양이 연료를 다 소진하고"},{"en":"swells massively,","ko":"엄청나게 팽창하여"},{"en":"and consumes the Earth","ko":"지구를 집어삼킬"}]},{"num":5,"text":"We don't know if this prediction is true, but it is consistent with our best understanding and we cannot rule it out.","symbol":"→","role":"결론 보조: 예측의 진위는 모르지만 배제할 수 없음 — 지식의 한계","keyWords":[],"chunks":[{"en":"We don't know if this prediction is true,","ko":"우리는 이 예측이 사실인지 모르지만"},{"en":"but it is consistent with our best understanding","ko":"그것은 우리의 최선의 이해와 일치하며"},{"en":"and we cannot rule it out","ko":"우리는 그것을 배제할 수 없다"}]},{"num":6,"text":"It is also possible that the Earth will explode due to some internal process with its molten core, which we had not anticipated.","symbol":"S","role":"추가 사례: 예상치 못한 내부 과정으로 지구가 폭발할 가능성","keyWords":[],"chunks":[{"en":"It is also possible","ko":"또한 가능하다"},{"en":"that the Earth will explode","ko":"지구가 폭발할 것이"},{"en":"due to some internal process with its molten core,","ko":"용융 핵의 어떤 내부 과정으로 인해"},{"en":"which we had not anticipated","ko":"우리가 예상하지 못했던"}]},{"num":7,"text":"A massive comet that our telescopes have not observed may crash into the Earth and destroy the planet.","symbol":"S","role":"추가 사례: 망원경으로 관측되지 않은 혜성의 충돌 가능성","keyWords":[],"chunks":[{"en":"A massive comet","ko":"거대한 혜성이"},{"en":"that our telescopes have not observed","ko":"우리의 망원경이 관측하지 못한"},{"en":"may crash into the Earth","ko":"지구에 충돌하여"},{"en":"and destroy the planet","ko":"행성을 파괴할 수도 있다"}]},{"num":8,"text":"These examples seem a bit extreme, but consider the 230,000 people who died in the tsunami in Sumatra in 2004, which resulted from an undersea megathrust earthquake that had not been anticipated.","symbol":"S","role":"현실적 사례 전환: 예상 못한 지진해일로 23만 명 사망 — 극단적 예시에서 실제 사례로","keyWords":[],"chunks":[{"en":"These examples seem a bit extreme,","ko":"이 예들은 다소 극단적으로 보이지만"},{"en":"but consider the 230,000 people who died","ko":"하지만 사망한 23만 명을 생각해 보라"},{"en":"in the tsunami in Sumatra in 2004,","ko":"2004년 수마트라 쓰나미에서"},{"en":"which resulted from an undersea megathrust earthquake","ko":"해저 대규모 단층 지진에서 비롯된"},{"en":"that had not been anticipated","ko":"예상되지 않았던"}]},{"num":9,"text":"The most reasonable prediction on that day was that it would be an average day, like so many days before it, not that a massive wave was going to destroy many thousands of lives; tragically, such was the case.","symbol":"→","role":"결론 강화: 평범한 날일 것이라는 합리적 예측이 비극으로 끝남 — 예측 불가능성의 비극적 결말","keyWords":[],"chunks":[{"en":"The most reasonable prediction on that day","ko":"그날 가장 합리적인 예측은"},{"en":"was that it would be an average day,","ko":"평범한 날이 될 것이라는 것이었다"},{"en":"like so many days before it,","ko":"그 이전의 수많은 날들처럼"},{"en":"not that a massive wave was going to destroy many thousands of lives;","ko":"거대한 파도가 수천 명의 생명을 앗아갈 것이라는 게 아니라"},{"en":"tragically, such was the case","ko":"비극적으로도, 그런 일이 실제로 일어났다"}]}],"abstract":"","blank_sel":0,"insert_sel":0,"summary_sel":0,"irrel_sel":0,"irrel_insert_pos":0,"irrel_confirmed":false,"irrel_sentence":"","grammar_sel":0,"grammar_answer":1,"vocab_sel":0,"vocab_answer":1,"flow":{"blocks":[{"id":1,"name":"주제 및 통념 제시","nameEn":"Topic & Common Belief","color":"blue","sentenceNums":[1,2]},{"id":2,"name":"지식의 한계 반박 (추상적 사례)","nameEn":"Abstract Counterexamples","color":"coral","sentenceNums":[3,4,5,6,7]},{"id":3,"name":"현실 사례와 결론","nameEn":"Real-world Example & Conclusion","color":"teal","sentenceNums":[8,9]}],"interBlockConnectors":["↔","→"],"keyword":"지식의 한계(예측 불가능성)","topicSummary":"관찰되지 않은 것에 대한 예측은 결코 확실하지 않으며, 우리의 지식에는 근본적인 한계가 있다.","structureType":"주제 제시 → 반박(사례 열거) → 현실 사례로 결론 강화"},"grammar":{}},{"id":"27STYD_01_006","difficulty":"상","title":"","sentences":[{"num":1,"text":"Accepting or being at peace with things isn't easy.","symbol":"G","role":"주제 도입: 수용이 쉽지 않음을 인정","chunks":[{"en":"Accepting or being at peace with things","ko":"무언가를 받아들이거나 그것과 평화롭게 지내는 것은"},{"en":"isn't easy.","ko":"쉽지 않다."}]},{"num":2,"text":"It takes time, patience and a fair dose of courage.","symbol":"=","role":"1번 문장 재진술: 수용에 필요한 요소 열거","chunks":[{"en":"It takes","ko":"그것은 필요로 한다"},{"en":"time, patience","ko":"시간, 인내"},{"en":"and a fair dose of courage.","ko":"그리고 상당한 용기를."}]},{"num":3,"text":"True acceptance isn't about trying to make something go away, as in, 'If I accept this then it will go away'.","symbol":"↔","role":"통념 반박: 진정한 수용의 잘못된 정의 제시","chunks":[{"en":"True acceptance isn't about","ko":"진정한 수용은 ~에 관한 것이 아니다"},{"en":"trying to make something go away,","ko":"무언가를 사라지게 만들려는 시도,"},{"en":"as in,","ko":"즉,"},{"en":"'If I accept this then it will go away'.","ko":"'이것을 받아들이면 그것이 사라질 것이다'라는 식의."}]},{"num":4,"text":"That's a good way to get dispirited when the problem, the thing, doesn't go away.","symbol":"→","role":"잘못된 수용의 결과: 낙담으로 이어짐","chunks":[{"en":"That's a good way to get dispirited","ko":"그것은 낙담하기 딱 좋은 방법이다"},{"en":"when the problem, the thing, doesn't go away.","ko":"문제, 그 대상이 사라지지 않을 때."}]},{"num":5,"text":"Using acceptance to make something go away is actually non-acceptance masquerading as acceptance in order to get rid of that towards which you have a negative attitude.","symbol":"=","role":"핵심 정의: 가짜 수용의 본질 규정","chunks":[{"en":"Using acceptance to make something go away","ko":"무언가를 사라지게 하기 위해 수용을 이용하는 것은"},{"en":"is actually non-acceptance","ko":"사실 비수용이다"},{"en":"masquerading as acceptance","ko":"수용인 척 위장하는"},{"en":"in order to get rid of that","ko":"제거하기 위해 그것을"},{"en":"towards which you have a negative attitude.","ko":"당신이 부정적인 태도를 가지고 있는."}]},{"num":6,"text":"Rather than getting dispirited we would be better to notice what happens when we fight with a situation or experience.","symbol":"↔","role":"대안 제시: 낙담 대신 싸움의 결과 관찰 권유","chunks":[{"en":"Rather than getting dispirited","ko":"낙담하는 것보다"},{"en":"we would be better to notice","ko":"우리는 알아채는 것이 더 낫다"},{"en":"what happens when we fight with a situation or experience.","ko":"우리가 어떤 상황이나 경험과 싸울 때 무슨 일이 일어나는지를."}]},{"num":7,"text":"It escalates!","symbol":"→","role":"싸움의 결과: 문제가 악화됨","chunks":[{"en":"It escalates!","ko":"그것은 악화된다!"}]},{"num":8,"text":"We could then wonder what would happen if we stopped fighting with it.","symbol":"+","role":"사고 전환 유도: 싸움을 멈추면 어떨지 질문","chunks":[{"en":"We could then wonder","ko":"그러면 우리는 궁금해할 수 있다"},{"en":"what would happen","ko":"무슨 일이 일어날지를"},{"en":"if we stopped fighting with it.","ko":"우리가 그것과 싸우기를 멈춘다면."}]},{"num":9,"text":"Through true acceptance, the impact of such experiences starts to diminish and in their own time these experiences impact us less often.","symbol":"G","role":"진정한 수용의 효과: 경험의 영향이 줄어듦","chunks":[{"en":"Through true acceptance,","ko":"진정한 수용을 통해,"},{"en":"the impact of such experiences starts to diminish","ko":"그러한 경험들의 영향이 줄어들기 시작하고"},{"en":"and in their own time","ko":"그리고 자연스러운 시간이 지나면"},{"en":"these experiences impact us less often.","ko":"이러한 경험들은 우리에게 덜 자주 영향을 미친다."}]},{"num":10,"text":"It's as if we've been visited by a stray dog that keeps coming back because we keep feeding it, but soon it loses interest and goes away when it is not being fed.","symbol":"S","role":"비유: 주의를 주는 것이 경험을 되살린다는 비유","chunks":[{"en":"It's as if we've been visited by a stray dog","ko":"마치 우리가 떠돌이 개의 방문을 받은 것과 같다"},{"en":"that keeps coming back because we keep feeding it,","ko":"우리가 계속 먹이를 주기 때문에 계속 돌아오는,"},{"en":"but soon it loses interest and goes away","ko":"하지만 곧 그 개는 흥미를 잃고 떠난다"},{"en":"when it is not being fed.","ko":"먹이를 받지 못할 때."}]},{"num":11,"text":"Attention is the food that keeps it coming back.","symbol":"→","role":"결론: 주의(관심)가 경험을 지속시키는 원인","chunks":[{"en":"Attention is the food","ko":"주의(관심)는 먹이이다"},{"en":"that keeps it coming back.","ko":"그것을 계속 돌아오게 만드는."}]}],"abstract":"","blank_sel":0,"insert_sel":0,"summary_sel":0,"irrel_sel":0,"irrel_insert_pos":0,"irrel_confirmed":false,"irrel_sentence":"","grammar_sel":0,"grammar_answer":1,"vocab_sel":0,"vocab_answer":1,"flow":{"blocks":[{"id":1,"name":"수용의 어려움과 잘못된 정의","nameEn":"Misconception of Acceptance","color":"blue","sentenceNums":[1,2,3,4,5]},{"id":2,"name":"싸움 vs 수용: 대조와 효과","nameEn":"Fighting vs. True Acceptance","color":"coral","sentenceNums":[6,7,8,9]},{"id":3,"name":"비유와 결론: 주의가 경험을 유지시킴","nameEn":"Analogy & Conclusion","color":"teal","sentenceNums":[10,11]}],"interBlockConnectors":["↔","→"],"keyword":"true acceptance (진정한 수용)","topicSummary":"진정한 수용은 문제를 사라지게 하려는 수단이 아니며, 경험에 맞서 싸우지 않고 주의를 거둘 때 그 영향이 자연스럽게 줄어든다.","structureType":"통념 제시→반박·재정의→결론(비유)"},"grammar":{},"disabled_types":["order"]},{"id":"27STYD_01_007","difficulty":"중","title":"","sentences":[{"num":1,"text":"There are two classic problems that give us mathematically proper ways to evaluate coincidences.","symbol":"G","role":"핵심 소재 도입: 우연의 일치를 수학적으로 평가하는 두 가지 고전적 문제 제시","chunks":[{"en":"There are two classic problems","ko":"두 가지 고전적 문제가 있다"},{"en":"that give us","ko":"우리에게 제공하는"},{"en":"mathematically proper ways","ko":"수학적으로 적절한 방법들을"},{"en":"to evaluate coincidences","ko":"우연의 일치를 평가하기 위한"}]},{"num":2,"text":"One is a counterintuitive poser: the birthday problem, which tells us that in any group of twenty-three people the odds are better than even that two people in the group will have the same birthday.","symbol":"S","role":"첫 번째 문제(생일 문제) 구체적 설명 — 반직관적 결과 제시","chunks":[{"en":"One is a counterintuitive poser:","ko":"하나는 반직관적인 난제이다:"},{"en":"the birthday problem,","ko":"생일 문제,"},{"en":"which tells us that","ko":"이것은 우리에게 말해준다"},{"en":"in any group of twenty-three people","ko":"23명의 어떤 그룹에서든"},{"en":"the odds are better than even","ko":"확률이 50% 이상이라고"},{"en":"that two people in the group","ko":"그 그룹 안의 두 사람이"},{"en":"will have the same birthday","ko":"같은 생일을 가질"}]},{"num":3,"text":"The other is the monkey problem, which asks: if given a large enough amount of time, could a monkey, randomly hitting the keys of a computer keyboard, write the first line of a Shakespeare sonnet?","symbol":"S","role":"두 번째 문제(원숭이 문제) 구체적 설명 — 무한 시간 속 무작위 사건의 가능성","chunks":[{"en":"The other is the monkey problem,","ko":"다른 하나는 원숭이 문제이다,"},{"en":"which asks:","ko":"이것은 묻는다:"},{"en":"if given a large enough amount of time,","ko":"충분히 긴 시간이 주어진다면,"},{"en":"could a monkey,","ko":"원숭이가 할 수 있을까,"},{"en":"randomly hitting the keys of a computer keyboard,","ko":"컴퓨터 자판을 무작위로 두드려서,"},{"en":"write the first line of a Shakespeare sonnet?","ko":"셰익스피어 소네트의 첫 행을 쓸 수 있을까?"}]},{"num":4,"text":"These two problems, along with the law of large numbers, the theory of hidden variables, and the law of truly large numbers, give us a reasonable understanding of why coincidences happen far more frequently than we expect.","symbol":"→","role":"두 문제 + 수학 법칙들의 결론: 우연의 일치가 예상보다 훨씬 자주 발생하는 이유 설명","chunks":[{"en":"These two problems,","ko":"이 두 가지 문제는,"},{"en":"along with the law of large numbers,","ko":"큰 수의 법칙과 함께,"},{"en":"the theory of hidden variables,","ko":"숨겨진 변수 이론,"},{"en":"and the law of truly large numbers,","ko":"그리고 진정으로 큰 수의 법칙과 함께,"},{"en":"give us a reasonable understanding","ko":"우리에게 합리적인 이해를 제공한다"},{"en":"of why coincidences happen","ko":"왜 우연의 일치가 발생하는지에 대한"},{"en":"far more frequently than we expect","ko":"우리가 예상하는 것보다 훨씬 더 자주"}]},{"num":5,"text":"This last law, the law of truly large numbers, is a philosophical adage.","symbol":"G","role":"진정으로 큰 수의 법칙을 철학적 격언으로 규정 — 핵심 법칙 심화 설명 시작","chunks":[{"en":"This last law,","ko":"이 마지막 법칙,"},{"en":"the law of truly large numbers,","ko":"진정으로 큰 수의 법칙은,"},{"en":"is a philosophical adage","ko":"철학적 격언이다"}]},{"num":6,"text":"In a nutshell, it tells us that if there is any likelihood that something could happen, no matter how small, it's bound to happen at some time.","symbol":"==","role":"진정으로 큰 수의 법칙 핵심 내용 요약: 아무리 작은 확률도 결국 실현됨","chunks":[{"en":"In a nutshell,","ko":"간단히 말해서,"},{"en":"it tells us that","ko":"이것은 우리에게 말해준다"},{"en":"if there is any likelihood that something could happen,","ko":"어떤 일이 일어날 가능성이 있다면,"},{"en":"no matter how small,","ko":"아무리 작더라도,"},{"en":"it's bound to happen at some time","ko":"그것은 언젠가 반드시 일어나게 되어 있다"}]},{"num":7,"text":"It's not a theorem that can be proven.","symbol":"↔","role":"법칙의 한계 인정: 수학적으로 증명 가능한 정리가 아님을 인정","chunks":[{"en":"It's not a theorem","ko":"이것은 정리가 아니다"},{"en":"that can be proven","ko":"증명될 수 있는"}]},{"num":8,"text":"After all, I used the phrase \"bound to happen,\" which is as ambiguous as any phrase can be.","symbol":"+","role":"표현의 모호성 인정: '반드시 일어난다'는 표현 자체의 불명확성 보완 설명","chunks":[{"en":"After all,","ko":"결국,"},{"en":"I used the phrase \"bound to happen,\"","ko":"나는 '반드시 일어나게 되어 있다'는 표현을 사용했는데,"},{"en":"which is as ambiguous","ko":"이것은 매우 모호하다"},{"en":"as any phrase can be","ko":"어떤 표현이 그럴 수 있는 만큼이나"}]},{"num":9,"text":"But it gives a sense of just how common coincidences are.","symbol":"↔","role":"최종 결론: 한계에도 불구하고 이 법칙은 우연의 일치가 얼마나 흔한지 직관적으로 알려줌","chunks":[{"en":"But it gives a sense","ko":"하지만 이것은 감각을 준다"},{"en":"of just how common coincidences are","ko":"우연의 일치가 얼마나 흔한지에 대한"}]}],"abstract":"","blank_sel":0,"insert_sel":0,"summary_sel":0,"irrel_sel":0,"irrel_insert_pos":0,"irrel_confirmed":false,"irrel_sentence":"","grammar_sel":0,"grammar_answer":1,"vocab_sel":0,"vocab_answer":1,"flow":{"blocks":[{"id":1,"name":"두 고전적 문제 소개","nameEn":"Two Classic Problems","color":"blue","sentenceNums":[1,2,3]},{"id":2,"name":"우연의 일치가 잦은 이유 — 법칙들의 역할","nameEn":"Mathematical Laws Explaining Coincidences","color":"teal","sentenceNums":[4]},{"id":3,"name":"진정으로 큰 수의 법칙 심화","nameEn":"Law of Truly Large Numbers","color":"coral","sentenceNums":[5,6]},{"id":4,"name":"법칙의 한계와 의의","nameEn":"Limitation and Value of the Law","color":"amber","sentenceNums":[7,8,9]}],"interBlockConnectors":["→","+","↔"],"keyword":"우연의 일치(coincidences) / 진정으로 큰 수의 법칙","topicSummary":"생일 문제·원숭이 문제 등 수학적 도구와 '진정으로 큰 수의 법칙'은, 비록 엄밀히 증명되지 않더라도, 우연의 일치가 우리 예상보다 훨씬 자주 일어나는 이유를 이해하게 해준다.","structureType":"사례 나열 → 원리 도출 → 핵심 법칙 심화 → 한계 인정 후 의의 강조"},"grammar":{}},{"id":"27STYD_01_008","difficulty":"중","title":"","sentences":[{"num":1,"text":"The phrase 'image scanning' refers to the cognitive processes that operate on visual mental images when a person moves his or her attention across imagined objects.","symbol":"G","role":"'이미지 스캐닝'의 개념 정의","chunks":[{"en":"The phrase 'image scanning'","ko":"'이미지 스캐닝'이라는 용어는"},{"en":"refers to the cognitive processes","ko":"인지 과정을 가리킨다"},{"en":"that operate on visual mental images","ko":"시각적 심상에 작용하는"},{"en":"when a person moves his or her attention","ko":"사람이 주의를 이동할 때"},{"en":"across imagined objects","ko":"상상된 대상들 전반에 걸쳐"}]},{"num":2,"text":"The first image scanning paradigm was designed to investigate the spatial properties of images.","symbol":"G","role":"실험의 목적 소개","chunks":[{"en":"The first image scanning paradigm","ko":"최초의 이미지 스캐닝 패러다임은"},{"en":"was designed to investigate","ko":"조사하기 위해 설계되었다"},{"en":"the spatial properties of images","ko":"심상의 공간적 속성을"}]},{"num":3,"text":"In the original experiment, participants memorized drawings of elongated objects (such as a tower).","symbol":"S","role":"실험 절차 1단계: 자극 암기","chunks":[{"en":"In the original experiment","ko":"원래의 실험에서"},{"en":"participants memorized","ko":"참가자들은 암기했다"},{"en":"drawings of elongated objects","ko":"길쭉한 물체들의 그림을"},{"en":"(such as a tower)","ko":"(예: 탑)"}]},{"num":4,"text":"They were then asked to visualize one of the objects and to focus at one of its ends (for example, the bottom of the tower).","symbol":"S","role":"실험 절차 2단계: 심상 형성 및 특정 끝점 집중","chunks":[{"en":"They were then asked","ko":"그런 다음 참가자들은 요청받았다"},{"en":"to visualize one of the objects","ko":"물체들 중 하나를 시각화하도록"},{"en":"and to focus at one of its ends","ko":"그리고 그 끝 중 하나에 집중하도록"},{"en":"(for example, the bottom of the tower)","ko":"(예: 탑의 바닥)"}]},{"num":5,"text":"Lastly, participants heard the name of a feature on the object (e.g., a flag), and they had to look for it.","symbol":"S","role":"실험 절차 3단계: 탐침 자극 제시","chunks":[{"en":"Lastly, participants heard","ko":"마지막으로, 참가자들은 들었다"},{"en":"the name of a feature on the object","ko":"물체의 특정 부위 이름을"},{"en":"(e.g., a flag)","ko":"(예: 깃발)"},{"en":"and they had to look for it","ko":"그리고 그것을 찾아야 했다"}]},{"num":6,"text":"Participants were not instructed to scan their image, but were simply told to focus on the original location until the probe was delivered, and then to focus on the named part or feature.","symbol":"S","role":"실험 조건의 핵심: 스캔 지시 없음","chunks":[{"en":"Participants were not instructed to scan their image","ko":"참가자들은 심상을 스캔하라는 지시를 받지 않았다"},{"en":"but were simply told","ko":"단지 지시받았을 뿐이다"},{"en":"to focus on the original location","ko":"원래 위치에 집중하도록"},{"en":"until the probe was delivered","ko":"탐침이 제시될 때까지"},{"en":"and then to focus on the named part or feature","ko":"그런 다음 언급된 부위나 특징에 집중하도록"}]},{"num":7,"text":"They pressed one button when they had focused on the named part, and another button if they failed to find it.","symbol":"S","role":"반응 측정 방법","chunks":[{"en":"They pressed one button","ko":"참가자들은 하나의 버튼을 눌렀다"},{"en":"when they had focused on the named part","ko":"언급된 부위에 집중했을 때"},{"en":"and another button","ko":"또 다른 버튼을"},{"en":"if they failed to find it","ko":"찾지 못했을 경우"}]},{"num":8,"text":"The critical finding was that response times increased linearly with increasing distances from the focus point to the named part of the object.","symbol":"→","role":"핵심 실험 결과: 거리와 반응 시간의 선형 관계","chunks":[{"en":"The critical finding was that","ko":"핵심적인 발견은 ~이었다"},{"en":"response times increased linearly","ko":"반응 시간이 선형적으로 증가했다는 것"},{"en":"with increasing distances","ko":"거리가 증가함에 따라"},{"en":"from the focus point","ko":"집중 지점으로부터"},{"en":"to the named part of the object","ko":"물체의 언급된 부위까지"}]},{"num":9,"text":"This finding was taken as evidence that distance, as traversed by image scanning, is genuinely represented in visual mental images.","symbol":"→","role":"결론: 시각적 심상의 공간적 거리가 실제로 표상됨","chunks":[{"en":"This finding was taken as evidence","ko":"이 발견은 증거로 받아들여졌다"},{"en":"that distance","ko":"거리가"},{"en":"as traversed by image scanning","ko":"이미지 스캐닝에 의해 가로질러지는"},{"en":"is genuinely represented","ko":"실제로 표상된다는"},{"en":"in visual mental images","ko":"시각적 심상 안에"}]}],"abstract":"","blank_sel":0,"insert_sel":0,"summary_sel":0,"irrel_sel":0,"irrel_insert_pos":0,"irrel_confirmed":false,"irrel_sentence":"","grammar_sel":0,"grammar_answer":1,"vocab_sel":0,"vocab_answer":1,"flow":{"blocks":[{"id":1,"name":"개념 정의 및 실험 목적","nameEn":"Definition & Purpose","color":"blue","sentenceNums":[1,2]},{"id":2,"name":"실험 절차","nameEn":"Experimental Procedure","color":"teal","sentenceNums":[3,4,5,6,7]},{"id":3,"name":"결과 및 결론","nameEn":"Findings & Conclusion","color":"coral","sentenceNums":[8,9]}],"interBlockConnectors":["→","→"],"keyword":"image scanning","topicSummary":"이미지 스캐닝 실험을 통해 시각적 심상 속 거리가 실제로 공간적으로 표상됨을 증명함","structureType":"개념정의→실험절차→결과/결론"},"grammar":{}},{"id":"27STYD_01_009","difficulty":"하","title":"","sentences":[{"num":1,"text":"Social media's transformation into an e-commerce platform is a significant milestone that enabled it to become a platform for organizations.","symbol":"G","role":"주제 제시: 소셜 미디어의 전자상거래 플랫폼으로의 변화","chunks":[{"en":"Social media's transformation","ko":"소셜 미디어의 변화는"},{"en":"into an e-commerce platform","ko":"전자상거래 플랫폼으로의"},{"en":"is a significant milestone","ko":"중요한 이정표이다"},{"en":"that enabled it to become","ko":"그것이 ~이 될 수 있게 한"},{"en":"a platform for organizations","ko":"조직들을 위한 플랫폼"}]},{"num":2,"text":"Social media was initially and mainly used for communication with friends and family.","symbol":"G","role":"초기 통념: 소셜 미디어는 원래 소통 도구였음","chunks":[{"en":"Social media","ko":"소셜 미디어는"},{"en":"was initially and mainly used","ko":"처음에는 주로 사용되었다"},{"en":"for communication","ko":"소통을 위해"},{"en":"with friends and family","ko":"친구 및 가족과의"}]},{"num":3,"text":"But with the popularity of some platforms, social media has turned into a vital tool for businesses seeking to sell their products online.","symbol":"↔","role":"역접/전환: 현재는 기업의 판매 도구로 변화","chunks":[{"en":"But with the popularity","ko":"그러나 인기에 힘입어"},{"en":"of some platforms","ko":"일부 플랫폼들의"},{"en":"social media has turned into","ko":"소셜 미디어는 변했다"},{"en":"a vital tool","ko":"필수적인 도구로"},{"en":"for businesses seeking","ko":"기업들을 위한 (찾는)"},{"en":"to sell their products online","ko":"온라인으로 제품을 판매하려는"}]},{"num":4,"text":"Social media is now used by businesses to promote their products and offerings as well as provide a direct shopping option for buyers.","symbol":"==","role":"재진술: 기업이 소셜 미디어를 활용하는 구체적 방식","chunks":[{"en":"Social media is now used","ko":"소셜 미디어는 이제 사용된다"},{"en":"by businesses","ko":"기업들에 의해"},{"en":"to promote their products and offerings","ko":"제품과 서비스를 홍보하기 위해"},{"en":"as well as provide","ko":"제공하는 것뿐만 아니라"},{"en":"a direct shopping option","ko":"직접 구매 옵션을"},{"en":"for buyers","ko":"구매자들을 위한"}]},{"num":5,"text":"Influencer marketing is another way that social media has evolved into a platform for businesses.","symbol":"+","role":"추가 사례 도입: 인플루언서 마케팅이라는 또 다른 방식","chunks":[{"en":"Influencer marketing","ko":"인플루언서 마케팅은"},{"en":"is another way","ko":"또 다른 방식이다"},{"en":"that social media has evolved","ko":"소셜 미디어가 발전해 온"},{"en":"into a platform for businesses","ko":"기업을 위한 플랫폼으로"}]},{"num":6,"text":"Influencers are those users who have a sizable social media following and are recognized as authorities or thought leaders in their specialized field.","symbol":"S","role":"개념 정의: 인플루언서가 누구인지 설명","chunks":[{"en":"Influencers are those users","ko":"인플루언서는 그런 사용자들이다"},{"en":"who have a sizable social media following","ko":"상당한 소셜 미디어 팔로워를 가진"},{"en":"and are recognized","ko":"그리고 인정받는"},{"en":"as authorities or thought leaders","ko":"권위자 또는 의견 선도자로"},{"en":"in their specialized field","ko":"자신의 전문 분야에서"}]},{"num":7,"text":"Influencer marketing allows businesses to reach the users' followers, who are more likely to trust suggestions from people they follow on social media.","symbol":"→","role":"결론/인과: 인플루언서 마케팅의 효과와 신뢰 메커니즘","chunks":[{"en":"Influencer marketing allows businesses","ko":"인플루언서 마케팅은 기업이 ~할 수 있게 한다"},{"en":"to reach the users' followers","ko":"해당 사용자의 팔로워들에게 도달하도록"},{"en":"who are more likely to trust","ko":"더 신뢰하는 경향이 있는"},{"en":"suggestions from people they follow","ko":"자신이 팔로우하는 사람들의 제안을"},{"en":"on social media","ko":"소셜 미디어에서"}]}],"abstract":"","blank_sel":0,"insert_sel":0,"summary_sel":0,"irrel_sel":0,"irrel_insert_pos":0,"irrel_confirmed":false,"irrel_sentence":"","grammar_sel":0,"grammar_answer":1,"vocab_sel":0,"vocab_answer":1,"flow":{"blocks":[{"id":1,"name":"초기 통념","nameEn":"Initial Role of Social Media","color":"blue","sentenceNums":[2]},{"id":2,"name":"전환: 기업 플랫폼으로 변화","nameEn":"Transformation into Business Platform","color":"coral","sentenceNums":[1,3,4]},{"id":3,"name":"심화 사례: 인플루언서 마케팅","nameEn":"Influencer Marketing as Further Evidence","color":"teal","sentenceNums":[5,6,7]}],"interBlockConnectors":["↔","+"],"keyword":"소셜 미디어의 전자상거래·기업 플랫폼화","topicSummary":"소셜 미디어는 본래 개인 소통 수단이었으나, 현재는 제품 홍보·직접 판매·인플루언서 마케팅 등을 통해 기업을 위한 전자상거래 플랫폼으로 진화하였다.","structureType":"통념→전환(역접)→구체예시→결론"},"grammar":{}},{"id":"27STYD_01_010","difficulty":"중","title":"","sentences":[{"num":1,"text":"One way we stop listening is when we start preparing a response to what the other person has just said, often immediately after they have started speaking.","symbol":"G","role":"핵심 주제 제시: 듣기를 멈추는 방식 - 상대방 말에 응답을 준비할 때","chunks":[{"en":"One way we stop listening","ko":"우리가 듣기를 멈추는 한 가지 방식은"},{"en":"is when we start preparing a response","ko":"응답을 준비하기 시작할 때이다"},{"en":"to what the other person has just said,","ko":"상대방이 방금 말한 것에 대해"},{"en":"often immediately after they have started speaking.","ko":"흔히 그들이 말을 시작한 직후에"}]},{"num":2,"text":"For example, imagine you are in a meeting with your manager, who tells you that a reorganization is coming soon, and you and your team are going to be moved under a lower-level manager.","symbol":"S","role":"구체적 상황 예시 도입: 회의 중 조직개편 소식을 듣는 장면","chunks":[{"en":"For example,","ko":"예를 들어,"},{"en":"imagine you are in a meeting with your manager,","ko":"당신이 상사와 회의 중이라고 상상해보라,"},{"en":"who tells you that a reorganization is coming soon,","ko":"그 상사가 곧 조직개편이 있을 거라고 말하고,"},{"en":"and you and your team are going to be moved","ko":"당신과 팀이 이동하게 될 것이라고 한다"},{"en":"under a lower-level manager.","ko":"더 낮은 직급의 관리자 밑으로"}]},{"num":3,"text":"As soon as you hear that news, you stop listening, and your mind goes into high gear.","symbol":"S","role":"예시 전개: 소식을 듣자마자 듣기를 멈추고 머릿속이 바빠지는 반응","chunks":[{"en":"As soon as you hear that news,","ko":"그 소식을 듣자마자,"},{"en":"you stop listening,","ko":"당신은 듣기를 멈추고,"},{"en":"and your mind goes into high gear.","ko":"머릿속은 빠르게 돌아가기 시작한다."}]},{"num":4,"text":"You start thinking of ways to convince your manager not to let that happen.","symbol":"S","role":"예시 전개: 상사를 설득할 방법을 생각하기 시작함","chunks":[{"en":"You start thinking of ways","ko":"당신은 방법들을 생각하기 시작한다"},{"en":"to convince your manager","ko":"상사를 설득하기 위한"},{"en":"not to let that happen.","ko":"그 일이 일어나지 않도록"}]},{"num":5,"text":"You think of how much you don't like the manager you are about to be moved under, and you prepare to tell your manager that you are incompatible with the new person.","symbol":"S","role":"예시 심화: 새 상사에 대한 불만과 반박 논리를 준비하는 내면 상태","chunks":[{"en":"You think of how much you don't like","ko":"당신은 얼마나 싫어하는지를 생각하고"},{"en":"the manager you are about to be moved under,","ko":"새로 배치될 관리자를,"},{"en":"and you prepare to tell your manager","ko":"그리고 상사에게 말할 준비를 한다"},{"en":"that you are incompatible with the new person.","ko":"새 사람과 자신이 맞지 않는다고"}]},{"num":6,"text":"You fear your career is starting a downward spiral.","symbol":"S","role":"예시 심화: 경력에 대한 불안감으로 이어지는 내면의 흐름","chunks":[{"en":"You fear","ko":"당신은 두려워한다"},{"en":"your career is starting a downward spiral.","ko":"자신의 경력이 하향 곡선을 그리기 시작한다고"}]},{"num":7,"text":"Meanwhile, your manager has continued talking, laying out the rationale for the decision, and explaining why this is a good move for both you and your team.","symbol":"↔","role":"역접 전환: 그 사이 상사는 계속 말하며 결정의 이유와 긍정적 측면을 설명하고 있었음","chunks":[{"en":"Meanwhile,","ko":"그러는 동안,"},{"en":"your manager has continued talking,","ko":"상사는 계속 말을 이어가고 있었고,"},{"en":"laying out the rationale for the decision,","ko":"결정에 대한 근거를 제시하면서,"},{"en":"and explaining why this is a good move","ko":"그리고 왜 이것이 좋은 변화인지 설명하면서"},{"en":"for both you and your team.","ko":"당신과 팀 모두에게"}]},{"num":8,"text":"Unfortunately, you stopped listening, so you missed everything beyond \"you are going to be moved to ...\"","symbol":"→","role":"결과 제시: 듣기를 멈췄기 때문에 중요한 정보를 모두 놓침","chunks":[{"en":"Unfortunately,","ko":"안타깝게도,"},{"en":"you stopped listening,","ko":"당신은 듣기를 멈췄고,"},{"en":"so you missed everything","ko":"그래서 모든 것을 놓쳤다"},{"en":"beyond \"you are going to be moved to ...\"","ko":"\"당신은 ~로 이동하게 될 것입니다\" 이후의 모든 내용을"}]},{"num":9,"text":"When you prepare your response as the other person is talking, you are missing out on hearing what the other person is sharing with you.","symbol":"==","role":"주제 재진술 및 결론: 응답 준비가 상대방의 말을 놓치게 만든다는 핵심 메시지 반복","chunks":[{"en":"When you prepare your response","ko":"당신이 응답을 준비할 때"},{"en":"as the other person is talking,","ko":"상대방이 말하는 동안"},{"en":"you are missing out on hearing","ko":"당신은 듣지 못하게 된다"},{"en":"what the other person is sharing with you.","ko":"상대방이 당신과 나누고 있는 것을"}]}],"abstract":"","blank_sel":0,"insert_sel":0,"summary_sel":0,"irrel_sel":0,"irrel_insert_pos":0,"irrel_confirmed":false,"irrel_sentence":"","grammar_sel":0,"grammar_answer":1,"vocab_sel":0,"vocab_answer":1,"flow":{"blocks":[{"id":1,"name":"주제 제시","nameEn":"Topic Introduction","color":"blue","sentenceNums":[1]},{"id":2,"name":"구체적 예시 전개","nameEn":"Concrete Example","color":"teal","sentenceNums":[2,3,4,5,6]},{"id":3,"name":"역접 및 결과","nameEn":"Contrast & Consequence","color":"coral","sentenceNums":[7,8]},{"id":4,"name":"결론 및 재진술","nameEn":"Conclusion & Restatement","color":"purple","sentenceNums":[9]}],"interBlockConnectors":["+","↔","→"],"keyword":"listening / preparing a response","topicSummary":"상대방이 말하는 도중 응답을 준비하면 정작 중요한 내용을 듣지 못하게 된다.","structureType":"주제 제시 → 구체 예시 → 역접·결과 → 결론 재진술"},"grammar":{}},{"id":"27STYD_01_011","difficulty":"중","title":"","sentences":[{"num":1,"text":"Many marketers believe that buying should be regarded as a process whereby buyers attempt to reduce the risk of a purchase decision, rather than maximising their gain.","symbol":"G","role":"핵심 주장 제시: 구매는 이익 극대화가 아닌 위험 감소 과정","chunks":[{"en":"Many marketers believe","ko":"많은 마케터들은 믿는다"},{"en":"that buying should be regarded as a process","ko":"구매가 하나의 과정으로 여겨져야 한다고"},{"en":"whereby buyers attempt to reduce the risk","ko":"구매자들이 위험을 줄이려 시도하는"},{"en":"of a purchase decision,","ko":"구매 결정의"},{"en":"rather than maximising their gain.","ko":"이익을 극대화하는 것이 아니라"}]},{"num":2,"text":"When a person is faced with competing brands in a new product field, they feel risk ─ for example, uncertainty about whether the brand will work, whether they will be wasting money, whether their peer group will disagree with their choice, or whether they will feel comfortable with the purchase, etc.","symbol":"S","role":"구체 예시: 구매자가 느끼는 다양한 위험 유형 열거","chunks":[{"en":"When a person is faced with competing brands","ko":"사람이 경쟁 브랜드들에 직면했을 때"},{"en":"in a new product field,","ko":"새로운 제품 분야에서"},{"en":"they feel risk ─","ko":"그들은 위험을 느낀다 ─"},{"en":"uncertainty about whether the brand will work,","ko":"브랜드가 효과가 있을지에 대한 불확실성"},{"en":"whether they will be wasting money,","ko":"돈을 낭비하게 될지"},{"en":"whether their peer group will disagree with their choice,","ko":"동료 집단이 선택에 반대할지"},{"en":"or whether they will feel comfortable with the purchase,","ko":"또는 구매에 편안함을 느낄지"}]},{"num":3,"text":"Successful brand marketing should therefore be concerned with understanding buyers' perceptions of risk, followed by developing and presenting the brand in such a way that buyers feel minimal risk.","symbol":"→","role":"결론 도출: 성공적 마케팅은 위험 인식 최소화에 집중해야 함","chunks":[{"en":"Successful brand marketing should therefore be concerned with","ko":"따라서 성공적인 브랜드 마케팅은 ~에 관심을 가져야 한다"},{"en":"understanding buyers' perceptions of risk,","ko":"구매자의 위험 인식을 이해하는 것"},{"en":"followed by developing and presenting the brand","ko":"그 다음으로 브랜드를 개발하고 제시하는 것"},{"en":"in such a way that buyers feel minimal risk.","ko":"구매자가 최소한의 위험을 느끼도록 하는 방식으로"}]},{"num":4,"text":"An example of an industry appreciating perceived risk is the pharmaceutical industry.","symbol":"S","role":"사례 전환: 지각된 위험을 인식하는 산업으로 제약업계 소개","chunks":[{"en":"An example of an industry","ko":"하나의 산업 사례"},{"en":"appreciating perceived risk","ko":"지각된 위험을 중시하는"},{"en":"is the pharmaceutical industry.","ko":"는 제약 산업이다"}]},{"num":5,"text":"A company marketing a new drug suitable for children needs to consider the parent's concerns about risk.","symbol":"S","role":"세부 사례: 아동용 신약 마케팅 시 부모의 위험 우려 고려 필요","chunks":[{"en":"A company marketing a new drug","ko":"새로운 약을 마케팅하는 회사는"},{"en":"suitable for children","ko":"어린이에게 적합한"},{"en":"needs to consider the parent's concerns about risk.","ko":"위험에 대한 부모의 우려를 고려해야 한다"}]},{"num":6,"text":"One company launching such a product worked with a series of pain specialists in pediatric hospitals, providing clinical data and product trials, so that specialist endorsement of the brand would reassure parents and help to minimise their perception of risk.","symbol":"S","role":"구체적 실행 사례: 전문가 보증으로 부모의 위험 인식 최소화","chunks":[{"en":"One company launching such a product","ko":"그러한 제품을 출시한 한 회사는"},{"en":"worked with a series of pain specialists","ko":"여러 통증 전문가들과 협력했다"},{"en":"in pediatric hospitals,","ko":"소아과 병원의"},{"en":"providing clinical data and product trials,","ko":"임상 데이터와 제품 시험을 제공하면서"},{"en":"so that specialist endorsement of the brand","ko":"그래서 브랜드에 대한 전문가 보증이"},{"en":"would reassure parents","ko":"부모를 안심시키고"},{"en":"and help to minimise their perception of risk.","ko":"위험 인식을 최소화하는 데 도움이 되도록"}]}],"abstract":"","blank_sel":0,"insert_sel":0,"summary_sel":0,"irrel_sel":0,"irrel_insert_pos":0,"irrel_confirmed":false,"irrel_sentence":"","grammar_sel":0,"grammar_answer":1,"vocab_sel":0,"vocab_answer":1,"flow":{"blocks":[{"id":1,"name":"핵심 주장","nameEn":"Core Claim","color":"blue","sentenceNums":[1,2]},{"id":2,"name":"마케팅 전략 결론","nameEn":"Marketing Strategy Conclusion","color":"teal","sentenceNums":[3]},{"id":3,"name":"구체적 산업 사례","nameEn":"Industry Case Study","color":"amber","sentenceNums":[4,5,6]}],"interBlockConnectors":["→","S"],"keyword":"perceived risk (지각된 위험)","topicSummary":"구매는 이익 극대화가 아닌 위험 감소 과정이므로, 성공적인 브랜드 마케팅은 구매자의 위험 인식을 이해하고 최소화하는 데 집중해야 한다.","structureType":"주장→근거→결론→사례"},"grammar":{}},{"id":"27STYD_01_012","difficulty":"중","title":"","sentences":[{"num":1,"text":"For the longest time, it was debated how bees computed the distance to their nectar, but we have now figured it out.","symbol":"G","role":"오랫동안 논쟁이 되어온 벌의 거리 계산 방식 - 현재는 해명됨","chunks":[{"en":"For the longest time,","ko":"아주 오랫동안"},{"en":"it was debated","ko":"논쟁이 있었다"},{"en":"how bees computed the distance","ko":"벌이 거리를 어떻게 계산하는지에 대해"},{"en":"to their nectar,","ko":"꿀까지의"},{"en":"but we have now figured it out.","ko":"하지만 우리는 이제 그것을 알아냈다"}]},{"num":2,"text":"The bee is actually approximating distance by measuring the amount of visual stimuli it receives on the trip.","symbol":"==","role":"벌의 거리 계산 방식 핵심 메커니즘 제시","chunks":[{"en":"The bee is actually","ko":"벌은 사실"},{"en":"approximating distance","ko":"거리를 어림잡는다"},{"en":"by measuring","ko":"측정함으로써"},{"en":"the amount of visual stimuli","ko":"시각적 자극의 양을"},{"en":"it receives on the trip.","ko":"이동 중에 받는"}]},{"num":3,"text":"Imagine this setup.","symbol":"S","role":"실험 설명 도입","chunks":[{"en":"Imagine this setup.","ko":"이 실험 장치를 상상해보라"}]},{"num":4,"text":"You take a paper towel tube, split it open, and paint a bunch of tiny trees all along the inside.","symbol":"S","role":"실험 장치 제작 과정 1단계","chunks":[{"en":"You take a paper towel tube,","ko":"종이 타월 튜브를 가져다가"},{"en":"split it open,","ko":"쪼개 펼친 다음"},{"en":"and paint a bunch of tiny trees","ko":"작은 나무들을 잔뜩 그린다"},{"en":"all along the inside.","ko":"안쪽 전체에"}]},{"num":5,"text":"Then you tape it back up and put the tube at the door of the hive so that the bees must fly through it to exit.","symbol":"S","role":"실험 장치 제작 과정 2단계 - 벌집 출구에 설치","chunks":[{"en":"Then you tape it back up","ko":"그런 다음 다시 테이프로 붙이고"},{"en":"and put the tube at the door of the hive","ko":"튜브를 벌집 입구에 놓는다"},{"en":"so that the bees must fly through it","ko":"벌들이 반드시 그것을 통과해 날아야"},{"en":"to exit.","ko":"나갈 수 있도록"}]},{"num":6,"text":"Bug scientists discovered that while the bee only flies ten inches through the tube, from its point of view, it just flew through an entire forest.","symbol":"S","role":"실험 결과 - 벌의 시각적 착각 발생","chunks":[{"en":"Bug scientists discovered that","ko":"곤충학자들은 발견했다"},{"en":"while the bee only flies ten inches through the tube,","ko":"벌이 튜브를 통해 불과 10인치를 날았지만"},{"en":"from its point of view,","ko":"벌의 관점에서는"},{"en":"it just flew through an entire forest.","ko":"숲 전체를 날아온 것이었다"}]},{"num":7,"text":"If the scientists put a nectar source right at the end of the tube, the bee would fly ten inches to it, but go back and report that there is nectar a whole forest away.","symbol":"S","role":"시각 착각이 거리 보고에 미치는 영향 - 과장된 거리 보고","chunks":[{"en":"If the scientists put a nectar source","ko":"과학자들이 꿀 공급원을 놓으면"},{"en":"right at the end of the tube,","ko":"튜브 끝 바로 앞에"},{"en":"the bee would fly ten inches to it,","ko":"벌은 10인치를 날아가지만"},{"en":"but go back and report","ko":"돌아와서 보고한다"},{"en":"that there is nectar a whole forest away.","ko":"꿀이 숲 하나를 건너에 있다고"}]},{"num":8,"text":"This was confirmed by removing the tube, then putting tiny little RPIDs on the backs of the bees that saw the dance of the tricked bee and went on to overshoot the location by a mile.","symbol":"S","role":"추적 실험으로 결과 재확인 - 다른 벌들도 과장된 거리로 이동","chunks":[{"en":"This was confirmed by removing the tube,","ko":"이것은 튜브를 제거하는 방식으로 확인됐다"},{"en":"then putting tiny little RPIDs on the backs of the bees","ko":"그런 다음 벌들의 등에 작은 RPID를 붙여"},{"en":"that saw the dance of the tricked bee","ko":"속은 벌의 춤을 본"},{"en":"and went on to overshoot the location by a mile.","ko":"그리고 실제 위치를 훨씬 넘어 날아간"}]},{"num":9,"text":"So the bee is really just a simple little robot driven by cunning algorithms.","symbol":"→","role":"결론 - 벌은 정교한 알고리즘으로 구동되는 단순 로봇","chunks":[{"en":"So the bee is really","ko":"따라서 벌은 사실"},{"en":"just a simple little robot","ko":"단순한 작은 로봇에 불과하다"},{"en":"driven by cunning algorithms.","ko":"교묘한 알고리즘으로 구동되는"}]}],"abstract":"","blank_sel":0,"insert_sel":0,"summary_sel":0,"irrel_sel":0,"irrel_insert_pos":0,"irrel_confirmed":false,"irrel_sentence":"","grammar_sel":0,"grammar_answer":1,"vocab_sel":0,"vocab_answer":1,"flow":{"blocks":[{"id":1,"name":"핵심 메커니즘 제시","nameEn":"Core Mechanism","color":"blue","sentenceNums":[1,2]},{"id":2,"name":"실험 장치 및 결과","nameEn":"Experiment & Results","color":"teal","sentenceNums":[3,4,5,6,7,8]},{"id":3,"name":"결론","nameEn":"Conclusion","color":"coral","sentenceNums":[9]}],"interBlockConnectors":["→","→"],"keyword":"시각적 자극 기반 거리 계산","topicSummary":"벌은 실제 비행 거리가 아닌 이동 중 받는 시각적 자극의 양으로 거리를 어림잡으며, 이는 교묘한 알고리즘으로 작동하는 단순한 메커니즘이다.","structureType":"원리 제시→실험 예시→결론"},"grammar":{}},{"id":"ABSO_TYPE_01_011","difficulty":"중","title":"","sentences":[{"num":1,"text":"Many marketers believe that buying should be regarded as a process whereby buyers attempt to reduce the risk of a purchase decision, rather than maximising their gain.","symbol":"G","role":"핵심 주장 제시: 구매는 이익 극대화가 아닌 위험 감소 과정","chunks":[{"en":"Many marketers believe","ko":"많은 마케터들은 믿는다"},{"en":"that buying should be regarded as a process","ko":"구매가 하나의 과정으로 여겨져야 한다고"},{"en":"whereby buyers attempt to reduce the risk","ko":"구매자들이 위험을 줄이려 시도하는"},{"en":"of a purchase decision,","ko":"구매 결정의"},{"en":"rather than maximising their gain.","ko":"이익을 극대화하는 것이 아니라"}]},{"num":2,"text":"When a person is faced with competing brands in a new product field, they feel risk ─ for example, uncertainty about whether the brand will work, whether they will be wasting money, whether their peer group will disagree with their choice, or whether they will feel comfortable with the purchase, etc.","symbol":"S","role":"구체 예시: 구매자가 느끼는 다양한 위험 유형 열거","chunks":[{"en":"When a person is faced with competing brands","ko":"사람이 경쟁 브랜드들에 직면했을 때"},{"en":"in a new product field,","ko":"새로운 제품 분야에서"},{"en":"they feel risk ─","ko":"그들은 위험을 느낀다 ─"},{"en":"uncertainty about whether the brand will work,","ko":"브랜드가 효과가 있을지에 대한 불확실성"},{"en":"whether they will be wasting money,","ko":"돈을 낭비하게 될지"},{"en":"whether their peer group will disagree with their choice,","ko":"동료 집단이 선택에 반대할지"},{"en":"or whether they will feel comfortable with the purchase,","ko":"또는 구매에 편안함을 느낄지"}]},{"num":3,"text":"Successful brand marketing should therefore be concerned with understanding buyers' perceptions of risk, followed by developing and presenting the brand in such a way that buyers feel minimal risk.","symbol":"→","role":"결론 도출: 성공적 마케팅은 위험 인식 최소화에 집중해야 함","chunks":[{"en":"Successful brand marketing should therefore be concerned with","ko":"따라서 성공적인 브랜드 마케팅은 ~에 관심을 가져야 한다"},{"en":"understanding buyers' perceptions of risk,","ko":"구매자의 위험 인식을 이해하는 것"},{"en":"followed by developing and presenting the brand","ko":"그 다음으로 브랜드를 개발하고 제시하는 것"},{"en":"in such a way that buyers feel minimal risk.","ko":"구매자가 최소한의 위험을 느끼도록 하는 방식으로"}]},{"num":4,"text":"An example of an industry appreciating perceived risk is the pharmaceutical industry.","symbol":"S","role":"사례 전환: 지각된 위험을 인식하는 산업으로 제약업계 소개","chunks":[{"en":"An example of an industry","ko":"하나의 산업 사례"},{"en":"appreciating perceived risk","ko":"지각된 위험을 중시하는"},{"en":"is the pharmaceutical industry.","ko":"는 제약 산업이다"}]},{"num":5,"text":"A company marketing a new drug suitable for children needs to consider the parent's concerns about risk.","symbol":"S","role":"세부 사례: 아동용 신약 마케팅 시 부모의 위험 우려 고려 필요","chunks":[{"en":"A company marketing a new drug","ko":"새로운 약을 마케팅하는 회사는"},{"en":"suitable for children","ko":"어린이에게 적합한"},{"en":"needs to consider the parent's concerns about risk.","ko":"위험에 대한 부모의 우려를 고려해야 한다"}]},{"num":6,"text":"One company launching such a product worked with a series of pain specialists in pediatric hospitals, providing clinical data and product trials, so that specialist endorsement of the brand would reassure parents and help to minimise their perception of risk.","symbol":"S","role":"구체적 실행 사례: 전문가 보증으로 부모의 위험 인식 최소화","chunks":[{"en":"One company launching such a product","ko":"그러한 제품을 출시한 한 회사는"},{"en":"worked with a series of pain specialists","ko":"여러 통증 전문가들과 협력했다"},{"en":"in pediatric hospitals,","ko":"소아과 병원의"},{"en":"providing clinical data and product trials,","ko":"임상 데이터와 제품 시험을 제공하면서"},{"en":"so that specialist endorsement of the brand","ko":"그래서 브랜드에 대한 전문가 보증이"},{"en":"would reassure parents","ko":"부모를 안심시키고"},{"en":"and help to minimise their perception of risk.","ko":"위험 인식을 최소화하는 데 도움이 되도록"}]}],"abstract":"","blank_sel":0,"blank_candidates":[],"insert_sel":0,"insert_candidates":[],"summary_sel":0,"summary_candidates":[],"irrel_sel":0,"irrel_candidates":[],"irrel_insert_pos":0,"irrel_confirmed":false,"irrel_sentence":"","grammar_sets":[],"grammar_sel":0,"grammar_items":[],"grammar_answer":1,"vocab_sets":[],"vocab_sel":0,"vocab_items":[],"vocab_answer":1,"aGroup":[],"bGroup":[],"flow":{"blocks":[{"id":1,"name":"핵심 주장","nameEn":"Core Claim","color":"blue","sentenceNums":[1,2]},{"id":2,"name":"마케팅 전략 결론","nameEn":"Marketing Strategy Conclusion","color":"teal","sentenceNums":[3]},{"id":3,"name":"구체적 산업 사례","nameEn":"Industry Case Study","color":"amber","sentenceNums":[4,5,6]}],"interBlockConnectors":["→","S"],"keyword":"perceived risk (지각된 위험)","topicSummary":"구매는 이익 극대화가 아닌 위험 감소 과정이므로, 성공적인 브랜드 마케팅은 구매자의 위험 인식을 이해하고 최소화하는 데 집중해야 한다.","structureType":"주장→근거→결론→사례"},"grammar":{"difficultSentences":[{"num":1,"text":"Many marketers believe that buying should be regarded as a process whereby buyers attempt to reduce the risk of a purchase decision, rather than maximising their gain.","structure":"believe [that절] / whereby 관계부사절 / rather than 대조","translation":"많은 마케터들은 구매가, 이익을 극대화하는 것이 아니라, 구매자들이 구매 결정의 위험을 줄이려 시도하는 과정으로 여겨져야 한다고 믿는다.","point":"whereby(= by which)는 관계부사로 선행사 process를 수식. rather than이 핵심 대조 구조를 형성하며 글 전체 주제를 압축."},{"num":3,"text":"Successful brand marketing should therefore be concerned with understanding buyers' perceptions of risk, followed by developing and presenting the brand in such a way that buyers feel minimal risk.","structure":"be concerned with + 동명사 / followed by + 동명사 / in such a way that절","translation":"따라서 성공적인 브랜드 마케팅은 구매자의 위험 인식을 이해하는 것에 관심을 가져야 하고, 이어서 구매자가 최소한의 위험을 느끼도록 하는 방식으로 브랜드를 개발하고 제시해야 한다.","point":"followed by는 분사구문으로 '그 다음으로 ~하면서'의 순서를 표현. in such a way that은 결과/방식의 that절을 이끄는 관용 표현."},{"num":6,"text":"One company launching such a product worked with a series of pain specialists in pediatric hospitals, providing clinical data and product trials, so that specialist endorsement of the brand would reassure parents and help to minimise their perception of risk.","structure":"launching(현재분사 후치수식) / providing(분사구문, 동시동작) / so that(목적절)","translation":"그러한 제품을 출시한 한 회사는 소아과 병원의 여러 통증 전문가들과 협력하여, 임상 데이터와 제품 시험을 제공했는데, 이는 브랜드에 대한 전문가 보증이 부모를 안심시키고 위험 인식을 최소화하는 데 도움이 되도록 하기 위해서였다.","point":"launching은 company를 수식하는 현재분사, providing은 부대상황 분사구문, so that은 목적을 나타내는 접속사로 문장이 3단 구조로 압축되어 있어 독해 난이도가 높음."}]}},{"id":"ABSO_TYPE_01_012","difficulty":"중","title":"","sentences":[{"num":1,"text":"For the longest time, it was debated how bees computed the distance to their nectar, but we have now figured it out.","symbol":"G","role":"오랫동안 논쟁이 되어온 벌의 거리 계산 방식 - 현재는 해명됨","chunks":[{"en":"For the longest time,","ko":"아주 오랫동안"},{"en":"it was debated","ko":"논쟁이 있었다"},{"en":"how bees computed the distance","ko":"벌이 거리를 어떻게 계산하는지에 대해"},{"en":"to their nectar,","ko":"꿀까지의"},{"en":"but we have now figured it out.","ko":"하지만 우리는 이제 그것을 알아냈다"}]},{"num":2,"text":"The bee is actually approximating distance by measuring the amount of visual stimuli it receives on the trip.","symbol":"==","role":"벌의 거리 계산 방식 핵심 메커니즘 제시","chunks":[{"en":"The bee is actually","ko":"벌은 사실"},{"en":"approximating distance","ko":"거리를 어림잡는다"},{"en":"by measuring","ko":"측정함으로써"},{"en":"the amount of visual stimuli","ko":"시각적 자극의 양을"},{"en":"it receives on the trip.","ko":"이동 중에 받는"}]},{"num":3,"text":"Imagine this setup.","symbol":"S","role":"실험 설명 도입","chunks":[{"en":"Imagine this setup.","ko":"이 실험 장치를 상상해보라"}]},{"num":4,"text":"You take a paper towel tube, split it open, and paint a bunch of tiny trees all along the inside.","symbol":"S","role":"실험 장치 제작 과정 1단계","chunks":[{"en":"You take a paper towel tube,","ko":"종이 타월 튜브를 가져다가"},{"en":"split it open,","ko":"쪼개 펼친 다음"},{"en":"and paint a bunch of tiny trees","ko":"작은 나무들을 잔뜩 그린다"},{"en":"all along the inside.","ko":"안쪽 전체에"}]},{"num":5,"text":"Then you tape it back up and put the tube at the door of the hive so that the bees must fly through it to exit.","symbol":"S","role":"실험 장치 제작 과정 2단계 - 벌집 출구에 설치","chunks":[{"en":"Then you tape it back up","ko":"그런 다음 다시 테이프로 붙이고"},{"en":"and put the tube at the door of the hive","ko":"튜브를 벌집 입구에 놓는다"},{"en":"so that the bees must fly through it","ko":"벌들이 반드시 그것을 통과해 날아야"},{"en":"to exit.","ko":"나갈 수 있도록"}]},{"num":6,"text":"Bug scientists discovered that while the bee only flies ten inches through the tube, from its point of view, it just flew through an entire forest.","symbol":"S","role":"실험 결과 - 벌의 시각적 착각 발생","chunks":[{"en":"Bug scientists discovered that","ko":"곤충학자들은 발견했다"},{"en":"while the bee only flies ten inches through the tube,","ko":"벌이 튜브를 통해 불과 10인치를 날았지만"},{"en":"from its point of view,","ko":"벌의 관점에서는"},{"en":"it just flew through an entire forest.","ko":"숲 전체를 날아온 것이었다"}]},{"num":7,"text":"If the scientists put a nectar source right at the end of the tube, the bee would fly ten inches to it, but go back and report that there is nectar a whole forest away.","symbol":"S","role":"시각 착각이 거리 보고에 미치는 영향 - 과장된 거리 보고","chunks":[{"en":"If the scientists put a nectar source","ko":"과학자들이 꿀 공급원을 놓으면"},{"en":"right at the end of the tube,","ko":"튜브 끝 바로 앞에"},{"en":"the bee would fly ten inches to it,","ko":"벌은 10인치를 날아가지만"},{"en":"but go back and report","ko":"돌아와서 보고한다"},{"en":"that there is nectar a whole forest away.","ko":"꿀이 숲 하나를 건너에 있다고"}]},{"num":8,"text":"This was confirmed by removing the tube, then putting tiny little RPIDs on the backs of the bees that saw the dance of the tricked bee and went on to overshoot the location by a mile.","symbol":"S","role":"추적 실험으로 결과 재확인 - 다른 벌들도 과장된 거리로 이동","chunks":[{"en":"This was confirmed by removing the tube,","ko":"이것은 튜브를 제거하는 방식으로 확인됐다"},{"en":"then putting tiny little RPIDs on the backs of the bees","ko":"그런 다음 벌들의 등에 작은 RPID를 붙여"},{"en":"that saw the dance of the tricked bee","ko":"속은 벌의 춤을 본"},{"en":"and went on to overshoot the location by a mile.","ko":"그리고 실제 위치를 훨씬 넘어 날아간"}]},{"num":9,"text":"So the bee is really just a simple little robot driven by cunning algorithms.","symbol":"→","role":"결론 - 벌은 정교한 알고리즘으로 구동되는 단순 로봇","chunks":[{"en":"So the bee is really","ko":"따라서 벌은 사실"},{"en":"just a simple little robot","ko":"단순한 작은 로봇에 불과하다"},{"en":"driven by cunning algorithms.","ko":"교묘한 알고리즘으로 구동되는"}]}],"abstract":"","blank_sel":0,"blank_candidates":[],"insert_sel":0,"insert_candidates":[],"summary_sel":0,"summary_candidates":[],"irrel_sel":0,"irrel_candidates":[],"irrel_insert_pos":0,"irrel_confirmed":false,"irrel_sentence":"","grammar_sets":[],"grammar_sel":0,"grammar_items":[],"grammar_answer":1,"vocab_sets":[],"vocab_sel":0,"vocab_items":[],"vocab_answer":1,"aGroup":[],"bGroup":[],"flow":{"blocks":[{"id":1,"name":"핵심 메커니즘 제시","nameEn":"Core Mechanism","color":"blue","sentenceNums":[1,2]},{"id":2,"name":"실험 장치 및 결과","nameEn":"Experiment & Results","color":"teal","sentenceNums":[3,4,5,6,7,8]},{"id":3,"name":"결론","nameEn":"Conclusion","color":"coral","sentenceNums":[9]}],"interBlockConnectors":["→","→"],"keyword":"시각적 자극 기반 거리 계산","topicSummary":"벌은 실제 비행 거리가 아닌 이동 중 받는 시각적 자극의 양으로 거리를 어림잡으며, 이는 교묘한 알고리즘으로 작동하는 단순한 메커니즘이다.","structureType":"원리 제시→실험 예시→결론"},"grammar":{"difficultSentences":[{"num":2,"text":"The bee is actually approximating distance by measuring the amount of visual stimuli it receives on the trip.","structure":"[주어 The bee] + [동사 is approximating] + [목적어 distance] + [수단 by measuring the amount of visual stimuli (it receives on the trip)]","translation":"벌은 사실 이동 중에 받는 시각적 자극의 양을 측정함으로써 거리를 어림잡는다.","point":"'visual stimuli it receives'에서 목적격 관계대명사가 생략된 구조. by -ing(수단)가 핵심 메커니즘을 설명함."},{"num":7,"text":"If the scientists put a nectar source right at the end of the tube, the bee would fly ten inches to it, but go back and report that there is nectar a whole forest away.","structure":"[가정 If절] + [귀결 주절: would fly / go back and report] + [that절 명사절: there is nectar a whole forest away]","translation":"과학자들이 튜브 끝에 꿀 공급원을 놓으면, 벌은 10인치를 날아가지만 돌아와서 꿀이 숲 하나를 건너에 있다고 보고할 것이다.","point":"'a whole forest away'는 '숲 하나만큼 떨어진 거리에'를 의미하는 거리 표현. 가정법 현재(If+현재, would+동사원형)의 구조 파악이 중요."},{"num":8,"text":"This was confirmed by removing the tube, then putting tiny little RPIDs on the backs of the bees that saw the dance of the tricked bee and went on to overshoot the location by a mile.","structure":"[주어 This] + [수동태 was confirmed] + [by -ing 수단구] + [관계절 that saw ... and went on to overshoot]","translation":"이것은 튜브를 제거한 뒤, 속은 벌의 춤을 보고 실제 위치를 훨씬 지나쳐 날아간 벌들의 등에 작은 RPID를 붙이는 방식으로 확인됐다.","point":"'went on to overshoot the location by a mile'에서 'by a mile'은 '엄청나게, 훨씬'이라는 관용적 표현. 관계절(that)이 'bees'를 수식하는 구조 파악 필요."}]}}];